s/khalilurrrahmanridoykhan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/khalilurrrahmanridoykhan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/khalilurrrahmanridoykhan/public-health-repository-quality-auditor/commits/f099d2d8af310d4312332403ceaff48602ff682c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T15:26:33Z","email":"khalilurrahmanridoykhan@gmail.com","name":"khalilurrrahmanridoykhan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T15:26:33Z","email":"khalilurrahmanridoykhan@gmail.com","name":"khalilurrrahmanridoykhan"},"message":"feat: add the public live demo page\n\n/demo audits four real, independently-maintained global goods already\nverified against this auditor during Phases 2 and 4 — HL7/fhir-ips,\nHL7/US-Core, openmrs/openmrs-module-idgen, openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient\n-registration — not the maintainer''s own repos; the point is showing\nthe tool against widely-used digital health software.\n\nforce-dynamic, deliberately not a route-segment `revalidate` export: a\nrevalidate number without force-dynamic makes Next.js prerender the\npage (and run all four repos'' live GitHub calls) during `next build`\nitself — i.e. on every CI run and every deploy, not just real visits.\nCaching for real visitors instead comes from D1 (reuse a stored run\nunder an hour old before falling back to a live audit), which doesn''t\nrun at build time since the D1 binding isn''t available in a `next\nbuild` process — getDb() degrades to null there the same as any\ndeployment that hasn''t provisioned the database yet, so the live-fetch\npath runs once per cold cache, not once per build.\n\nAll four repos currently score low on the hygiene checklist specifically\n(a FHIR IG has no \"data dictionary\" in the research-reproducibility\nsense) — confirmed live via wrangler dev against real GitHub data, not\nassumed. The page explains why rather than presenting it as a tool bug.","tree":{"sha":"1d4c3d3f4c3994f8695b66946f47282ba6356