e,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/khalilurrrahmanridoykhan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/khalilurrrahmanridoykhan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/khalilurrrahmanridoykhan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/khalilurrrahmanridoykhan/public-health-repository-quality-auditor/commits/647e1b0a0e7e89dc93f38ed048fa416c2726ecbe/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T15:05:19Z","email":"khalilurrahmanridoykhan@gmail.com","name":"khalilurrrahmanridoykhan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T15:05:19Z","email":"khalilurrahmanridoykhan@gmail.com","name":"khalilurrrahmanridoykhan"},"message":"feat: add D1 binding + audit_runs schema for Phase 6 trend storage\n\nAdds the `DB` D1 binding to wrangler.jsonc (audit-run history: trend\nlines, org-wide fleet audits, badges) and its first migration\n(audit_runs: repository, commit_sha, ran_at, score, grade, passed,\nsource). The real database isn''t provisioned here — `wrangler d1 create\nph-repo-auditor-runs` needs a logged-in Cloudflare account, which this\nenvironment doesn''t have. `wrangler d1 migrations apply DB --local`\nneeds no login and was used to verify the schema end-to-end.\n\n`worker-configuration.d.ts` is generated by `wrangler types` (same\nconvention as `next-env.d.ts`) and gives D1Database/Env global types.\nPulling in the Workers runtime type library surfaced two pre-existing\nimplicit-`any` response.json() payloads in audit-dashboard.tsx as\nreal type errors (Response.json() resolves to `unknown` under workerd''s\ntypes, not `any`) — typed them properly rather than suppressing.","tree":{"sha":"b82a2abf87fbc43f28a24de0cbe2b638a76876a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/khalilurrrahmanridoykhan/public-health-repository-quality-auditor/git/trees/b82a2abf87fbc43f28a24de0cbe2b638a76876a8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/khalilurrrahmanridoykhan/public-health-reposit