://api.github.com/users/khalilurrrahmanridoykhan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/khalilurrrahmanridoykhan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/khalilurrrahmanridoykhan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/khalilurrrahmanridoykhan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/khalilurrrahmanridoykhan/public-health-repository-quality-auditor/commits/49544b9f66566d58f5718eb150be65c05a820151/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T05:42:39Z","email":"khalilurrahmanridoykhan@gmail.com","name":"khalilurrrahmanridoykhan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T05:42:39Z","email":"khalilurrahmanridoykhan@gmail.com","name":"khalilurrrahmanridoykhan"},"message":"feat(models,policy): disabled_packs and blocking findings\n\nAuditPolicy.disabled_packs mirrors disabled_checks but turns off a whole\npack (validated against the registered pack ids in policy.py). AuditReport\ngains has_blocking_findings: an error-severity Finding from *any* pack now\nfails passed, so a broken FHIR reference or a PII leak fails the Check Run\neven when the hygiene score alone clears the threshold. to_markdown() gains\na per-pack ''### `<pack>` pack findings'' section (severity-iconed) for\nnon-hygiene findings, since there''s now a second pack to actually group.","tree":{"sha":"cd9e4d5746961b294e40c4fe7212877f924aa212","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/khalilurrrahmanridoykhan/public-health-repository-quality-auditor/git/trees/cd9e4d5746961b294e40c4fe7212877f924aa212"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/khalilurrrahmanridoykhan/public-health-repository-quality-auditor/git/commits/49544b9f66566d58f5718eb150be65c05a820151","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/114473324?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kh