ttps://api.github.com/users/moshonk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/moshonk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/moshonk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/moshonk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IntelliSOFT-Consulting/liberia-emr/commits/3da52eb9143bc8588647c4c877b312858f8170a7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T17:31:23Z","email":"omondi.ken@gmail.com","name":"moshonk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T17:31:23Z","email":"omondi.ken@gmail.com","name":"moshonk"},"message":"fix(ci): name the generated E2E database passwords so no-secrets.sh reads them as references\n\nno-secrets.sh treats any *password* variable assigned a value as a hard-coded\ncredential, including $(openssl rand ...). The generated values are kept; only\nthe shell variables holding them are renamed (e2e_db_pw and so on), so the env\nfile lines are plain ${VAR} references.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01V44xbH5zsmcjXhiqxY1RVi","tree":{"sha":"a3bdc8d3ff423c575a3d4392c318681e24139625","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IntelliSOFT-Consulting/liberia-emr/git/trees/a3bdc8d3ff423c575a3d4392c318681e24139625"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IntelliSOFT-Consulting/liberia-emr/git/commits/3da52eb9143bc8588647c4c877b312858f8170a7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1963527?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/moshonk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/moshonk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/moshonk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/moshonk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/moshonk","id":1963527,"login":"moshonk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NjM1Mjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/moshonk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/moshonk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/moshonk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/moshonk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/moshonk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/moshonk","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IntelliSOFT-Consulting/liberia-emr/commit/3da52eb9143bc8588647c4c877b312858f8170a7","node_id":"C_kwDOTlxCMtoAKDNkYTUyZWI5MTQzYmM4NTg4NjQ3YzRjODc3YjMxMjg1OGY4MTcwYTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IntelliSOFT-Consulting/liberia-emr/commit/05c70fa1ed0959e811b936c42dcbda41dece36e4","sha":"05c70fa1ed0959e811b936c42dcbda41dece36e4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IntelliSOFT-Consulting/liberia-emr/commits/05c70fa1ed0959e811b936c42dcbda41dece36e4"}],"sha":"3da52eb9143bc8588647c4c877b312858f8170a7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IntelliSOFT-Consulting/liberia-emr/commits/3da52eb9143bc8588647c4c877b312858f8170a7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1963527?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/moshonk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/moshonk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/moshonk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/moshonk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/moshonk","id":1963527,"login":"moshonk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NjM1Mjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/moshonk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/moshonk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/moshonk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/moshonk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/moshonk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/moshonk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IntelliSOFT-Consulting/liberia-emr/commits/05c70fa1ed0959e811b936c42dcbda41dece36e4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T17:30:58Z","email":"omondi.ken@gmail.com","name":"moshonk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T17:30:58Z","email":"omondi.ken@gmail.com","name":"moshonk"},"message":"fix(sonar): clear the 31 issues the SonarQube upgrade raised on existing code\n\nThe SonarQube upgrade on 2026-10-04 widened what is analysed (YAML, and new Java\nrules), and every CI run since has failed the gate with new_violations=31 on\ncode that had not changed. This clears all 31.\n\nReports module (liberiaemrreports):\n- S1192: a private constant per repeated SQL literal in the five report\n  managers. The text is identical, so the registered SQL, which\n  RegisteredEtlDataSets compares character for character, is unchanged.\n- S6813: @Autowired moves from fields to the setters the tests already use\n  (setter injection), in the evaluator, the context service and the controller.\n- S6830: bean names camelCase (liberiaemrreportsLocationScopeResolver and so\n  on); the one lookup by name now uses LocationScopeResolver.BEAN_NAME.\n- S1168: getEtlLastRun() returns an empty map, not null. The REST response\n  still carries \"etlLastRun\": null, which the UI reads as \"no run yet\".\n- S6833/S4488: @RestController and @GetMapping.\n- S1604, S1640, S6353, S1128: a lambda, an EnumMap, \\w (the same as\n  [A-Za-z0-9_] without the Unicode flag), two unused imports.\n- S2143 and S2160 suppressed, each with its reason: java.util.Date is the\n  reporting module''s own parameter and value type and what JDBC returns, and a\n  definition''s identity is its uuid, which reporting relies on.\n\nci.yml (secrets:S6697): the E2E stack''s database passwords are generated per\nrun instead of committed as literals; they are only read back from its env file.\n\nThe module''s 92 tests pass.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01V44xbH5zsmcjXhiqxY1RVi","tree":{"sha":"970ce8f57f65d79fbdd4c4d6c673140cf5aec1e9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IntelliSOFT-Consulting/liberia-emr/git/trees/970ce8f57f65d79fbdd4c4d6c673140cf5aec1e9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IntelliSOFT-Consulting/liberia-emr/git/commits/05c70fa1ed0959e811b936c42dcbda41dece36e4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1963527?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/moshonk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/moshonk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/moshonk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/moshonk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/moshonk","id":1963527,"login":"moshonk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NjM1Mjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/moshonk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/moshonk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/moshonk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/moshonk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/moshonk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/moshonk","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IntelliSOFT-Consulting/liberia-emr/commit/05c70fa1ed0959e811b936c42dcbda41dece36e4","node_id":"C_kwDOTlxCMtoAKDA1YzcwZmExZWQwOTU5ZTgxMWI5MzZjNDJkY2JkYTQxZGVjZTM2ZTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IntelliSOFT-Consulting/liberia-emr/commit/ffe5e5aa1edfc647d8662f4043c202f7c757695c","sha":"ffe5e5aa1edfc647d8662f4043c202f7c757695c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IntelliSOFT-Consulting/liberia-emr/commits/ffe5e5aa1edfc647d8662f4043c202f7c757695c"}],"sha":"05c70fa1ed0959e811b936c42dcbda41dece36e4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IntelliSOFT-Consulting/liberia-emr/commits/05c70fa1ed0959e811b936c42dcbda41dece36e4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1963527?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/moshonk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/moshonk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/moshonk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/moshonk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/moshonk","id":1963527,"login":"moshonk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NjM1Mjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/moshonk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/moshonk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/moshonk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/moshonk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/moshonk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/moshonk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IntelliSOFT-Consulting/liberia-emr/commits/e8b2692b503b621c09ab50dd12f699ed6bddc1cb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T14:01:23Z","email":"omondi.ken@gmail.com","name":"moshonk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T14:01:23Z","email":"omondi.ken@gmail.com","name":"moshonk"},"message":"feat(LE-400): upgrade test upgrades from main and fails on rejected rows\n\nrun-upgrade.sh was a stub that could not run. Its tag glob matched no tag\n(the only one is the Maven tag liberiaemr-1.0.0), so it exited 0 as a \"first\nrelease\". No fixture existed and no distribution release ever has, so a\nrelease-based upgrade cannot run yet either.\n\nIt now upgrades from main. By default FROM is the newest liberia-emr-backend:<sha>\nthat main''s CI published at or before where this tree merges into main: the\nmain side of a PR merge commit, or the previous main commit on a push. Steps:\n\n- install FROM with run-clean-install.sh --keep-stack\n- seed-upgrade-data.py writes synthetic data over REST: obs on every Numeric,\n  Coded, Text, Boolean and Date concept in FROM''s concept CSVs, an encounter of\n  every type, an enrolment in every programme with a state per workflow\n- snapshot the counts and every piece of metadata the data references\n- recreate the backend at --to on the same database\n- fail on any row Initializer rejects on that boot (from the recreated\n  container''s log; initializer.log is not rewritten on a restart), an\n  unresolved ${var.*}, or any change to the snapshot\n\nCI runs it as upgrade-from-main on the clean install''s trigger; the gate accepts\nthe same skip. It warns when FROM''s architecture differs from the host.\n\nRun locally, with a native arm64 FROM built at main''s ee65a1d:\n- this branch: passed. 3 patients, 33 encounters, 254 obs, 4 enrolments; no row\n  rejected, snapshot unchanged. No states: production content defines workflows\n  but no workflow states.\n- a copy that gives the shipped concept \"Uterine Contraction Duration\" a new\n  UUID, the partograph pattern the dev servers hit: failed with\n  DuplicateConceptNameException on the upgrade boot. A clean install passes it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01V44xbH5zsmcjXhiqxY1RVi","tree":{"sha":"16bc12a435e6c7b3df41522adb063f38660cd9a9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IntelliSOFT-Consulting/liberia-emr/git/trees/16bc12a435e6c7b3df41522adb063f38660cd9a9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IntelliSOFT-Consulting/liberia-emr/git/commits/e8b2692b503b621c09ab50dd12f699ed6bddc1cb","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1963527?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.c