s/AndrejK666/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/bd0d6e64390023a49fc4cca4834b0577cda5c959/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T15:11:52Z","email":"Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech","name":"ANDREI KUCHMA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T15:11:52Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs(adr): one model for a project, and one story for async work (ADR-0037, ADR-0038) (#676)\n\nTwo proposed ADRs from the architecture review. Documentation only.\n\n**ADR-0037: one model for a project.** Today a project''s model is spread\nover five stores: the `studio_documents` tables, the artifact graph and\nits `studio_artifact_index` mirror, the domain model, the catalogue\nnodes, and the connector''s `cf.studio.kg.*` nodes. Repository, file,\nperson, project, document and gear each have two to five types, and no\nedge joins them. Authored documents have no node. Cross-store references\nare strings, and Spec Quality writes the same verdict twice. The ADR\nkeeps each fact in its owner''s store and makes the graph the link layer:\n- each concept gets one node type with one owner;\n- links are edges;\n- projections are best-effort, and a `<gear>.reproject` run repairs\nthem.\n\nIt also retires `kg`, and lets the domain model read the existing\nartifact and catalogue types instead of empty duplicates. The migration\nis ten steps, one PR each.\n\n**ADR-0038: one story for async work.** Scheduler and notify already\nride on `studio-tasks`. The `event-broker` sink is code no build\ncompiles. The ADR keeps two mechanisms and adds a rule for choosing\nbetween them: a run does the work, and an event says it happened. An\nevent is only a hint; the run row is the truth, so `followRun` also\nreads the run itself. It also proposes:\n- delete the broker sink, its feature and its dependency;\n- reach notify from the dispatcher through a port;\n- run the reports mirror as a task;\n- rename the `theia.*` kinds to rule E2.\n\nThe migration is six steps.\n\nEach ADR ends with its open questions.\n\n`node scripts/check-docs.mjs`: green.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","tree":{"sha":"9dd191ca1bcf58ab9369ae5e1a2347373847aab3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/trees/9dd191ca1bcf58ab9369ae5e1a2347373847aab3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/commits/bd0d6e64390023a49fc4cca4834b0577cda5c959","verification":{"payload":"tree 9dd191ca1bcf58ab9369ae5e1a2347373847aab3\nparent 5fd27ad1ed78a75def466653ae80a036f0fb6c3b\nauthor ANDREI KUCHMA <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech> 1791472312 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791472312 +0200\n\ndocs(adr): one model for a project, and one story for async work (ADR-0037, ADR-0038) (#676)\n\nTwo proposed ADRs from the architecture review. Documentation only.\n\n**ADR-0037: one model for a project.** Today a project''s model is spread\nover five stores: the `studio_documents` tables, the artifact graph and\nits `studio_artifact_index` mirror, the domain model, the catalogue\nnodes, and the connector''s `cf.studio.kg.*` nodes. Repository, file,\nperson, project, document and gear each have two to five types, and no\nedge joins them. Authored documents have no node. Cross-store references\nare strings, and Spec Quality writes the same verdict twice. The ADR\nkeeps each fact in its owner''s store and makes the graph the link layer:\n- each concept gets one node type with one owner;\n- links are edges;\n- projections are best-effort, and a `<gear>.reproject` run repairs\nthem.\n\nIt also retires `kg`, and lets the domain model read the existing\nartifact and catalogue types instead of empty duplicates. The migration\nis ten steps, one PR each.\n\n**ADR-0038: one story for async work.** Scheduler and notify already\nride on `studio-tasks`. The `event-broker` sink is code no build\ncompiles. The ADR keeps two mechanisms and adds a rule for choosing\nbetween them: a run does the work, and an event says it happened. An\nevent is only a hint; the run row is the truth, so `followRun` also\nreads the run itself. It also proposes:\n- delete the broker sink, its feature and its dependency;\n- reach notify from the dispatcher through a port;\n- run the reports mirror as a task;\n- rename the `theia.*` kinds to rule E2.\n\nThe migration is six steps.\n\nEach ADR ends with its open questions.\n\n`node scripts/check-docs.mjs`: green.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqx7K4CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAArnEQAC6fHu+O3zBMdr6pc6Whmxcx\naer/0F8JDkbGOfXl2yYt8rGNNWyOr3Idh8HtO2++o8EeexprFul9mUx0QXRleeW0\nqAlM/j3thYeoGG7qk7kh6sEcT2ZkGdtA5oivvveio4Y8E6irUP9nmbs2C6nVILMj\n//7TP5s/wmQpXm73bzk8JtbLwSYTdyTf3Rj+v1a+UzzSElvV2ho3StTD6iNXQsEO\nC5AtKe95mVlzOpf+ez+ncTeE/MjCz4ISG0yL/0IYzRHMuVaJE+bznXTnBwwTrgnY\nvEsyDMDJbCS5zx+xoNY3B+aBSx+SrIdk9HHP61LV5Ex1suqckMhvaS4B7gTkrpqY\nDm8kRd/27P5O9yjtY5rJPrX+0ThI+j2uTfDZqviQNKBVP6MVgRi85CioM7r1BuVF\n2BrSBtUcRo4uPPNa/Npg7i8G0Pl0X9May34T9F5AzCpo0vpMMvAHz9x6RDUb/P2F\n3aw9sSjPxI4EC5iquE4wl09hELl4HcQ6TidJXQZamfnksTUts4T8v+Oab+eJLD83\n/dW35WdSs/vCdvPcyJIO0nQBvw871rapz/6Swhmg8Fost3AG9WJQRzeyBXUL2mNw\njqBnWZolhleD3Ce5uVj+JyfhxDef8lURc0wOSXLKTbubKHwh9CZiRrWY2ixblm7B\nlb2VOfgszNBr7Nj0kX4N\n=cbI4\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-08T15:11:55Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/bd0d6e64390023a49fc4cca4834b0577cda5c959","node_id":"C_kwDOTl7dJtoAKGJkMGQ2ZTY0MzkwMDIzYTQ5ZmM0Y2NhNDgzNGIwNTc3Y2RhNWM5NTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/5fd27ad1ed78a75def466653ae80a036f0fb6c3b","sha":"5fd27ad1ed78a75def466653ae80a036f0fb6c3b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/5fd27ad1ed78a75def466653ae80a036f0fb6c3b"}],"sha":"bd0d6e64390023a49fc4cca4834b0577cda5c959","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/bd0d6e64390023a49fc4cca4834b0577cda5c959"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/301748190?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AndrejK666","id":301748190,"login":"AndrejK666","node_id":"U_kgDOEfxP3g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/5fd27ad1ed78a75def466653ae80a036f0fb6c3b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T11:35:11Z","email":"Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech","name":"ANDREI KUCHMA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T11:35:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(profile): the Profile page shows the person, with every identity attached to them (#674)\n\n## What\n\nThe Profile page showed the token''s claims: who signed in this time, not\nwho the person is. It now leads with the **Studio person** and shows\nevery identity **attached** to that person.\n\n- **You**: photo, name (with Rename → `POST /studio-user/v1/me`),\nprimary address, last seen, organizations and the role in each\n(`/me/memberships`).\n- **Identities**:\n- **How you sign in**: `/me/logins`, with the current session''s login\nmarked.\n- **Accounts elsewhere**: `/me/aliases`, each with its confidence. You\ncan claim an account, revoke one, or press \"Check my sign-ins and\nconnections\" (`/me/aliases/confirm`).\n  - **Addresses**: every address the person holds.\n- **This session**: the token''s claims, subject and home tenant, in a\nsmall card of their own.\n\n## Signing in through GitHub fills the profile\n\n`refresh_from_realm` already runs on `GET /me` (at most once a day per\nperson) and names a blank profile from the realm. Two additions:\n\n- **Brokered logins are recorded on the person.** Each account brokered\nonto a realm login is written as a `confirmed` alias, through the same\n`alias_policy` gate. A brokered login is already a proof of control\n(ADR-0015), so the person no longer has to press \"confirm\".\n- **A person with no photo gets their GitHub picture.** The URL is\n`https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/{numeric id}?v=4`. It is keyed\non the numeric id, which survives a rename, and a non-numeric id\nproduces no URL. An uploaded photo always wins.\n\n`docs/design/studio-user.md` is updated to match.\n\n## Checks\n\n- Backend: `backend-check.sh fmt` and `clippy` clean; `test\nuser_profile`: 74 passed, 2 of them new\n(`a_github_login_brings_its_picture`, `no_picture_is_made_up`).\n- Prototype: `tsc -b` clean; `vitest run`: 366 passed, with new cases in\n`people-profile.test.ts`.\n\n**Not verified live:** a real GitHub-brokered sign-in. The local\nKeycloak has no GitHub IdP, so this needs checking on Dev after deploy.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n* Expanded profile pages with organization memberships and a combined\nsession overview, including sign-in details and token expiry when\navailable.\n* Added profile display-name editing and an identities section for\nreviewing sign-in methods, linked accounts, and email addresses.\n* Users can claim or revoke linked accounts and check eligible sign-ins\nand connections for alias confirmations.\n* Profile photos now prioritize uploaded images; supported GitHub\naccounts can supply a fallback avatar when no photo is set.\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * Blank profile names refresh from the realm at most once per day.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","tree":{"sha":"40c703bfa08482662df087293eeee9f38245d5d2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/trees/40c703bfa08482662df087293eeee9f38245d5d2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/commits/5fd27ad1ed78a75def466653ae80a036f0fb6c3b","verification":{"payload":"tree 40c703bfa08482662df087293eeee9f38245d5d2\nparent 542a6688c741fadd7f9ee85693b4fb4f6122ebae\nauthor ANDREI KUCHMA <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech> 1791459311 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791459311 +0200\n\nfeat(profile): the Profile page shows the person, with every identity attached to them (#674)\n\n## What\n\nThe Profile page showed the token''s claims: who signed in this time, not\nwho the person is. It now leads with the **Studio person** and shows\nevery identity **attached** to that person.\n\n- **You**: photo, name (with Rename → `POST /studio-user/v1/me`),\nprimary address, last seen, organizations and the role in each\n(`/me/memberships`).\n- **Identities**:\n- **How you sign in**: `/me/logins`, with the current session''s login\nmarked.\n- **Accounts elsewhere**: `/me/aliases`, each with its confidence. You\ncan claim an account, revoke one, or press \"Check my sign-ins and\nconnections\" (`/me/aliases/confirm`).\n  - **Addresses**: every address the person holds.\n- **This session**: the token''s claims, subject and home tenant, in a\nsmall card of their own.\n\n## Signing in through GitHub fills the profile\n\n`refresh_from_realm` already runs on `GET /me` (at most once a day per\nperson) and names a blank profile from the realm. Two additions:\n\n- **Brokered logins are recorded on the person.** Each account brokered\nonto a realm login is written as a `confirmed` alias, through the same\n`alias_policy` gate. A brokered login is already a proof of control\n(ADR-0015), so the person no longer has to press \"confirm\".\n- **A person with no photo gets their GitHub picture.** The URL is\n`https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/{numeric id}?v=4`. It is keyed\non the numeric id, which survives a rename, and a non-numeric id\nproduces no URL. An uploaded photo always wins.\n\n`docs/design/studio-user.md` is updated to match.\n\n## Checks\n\n- Backend: `backend-check.sh fmt` and `clippy` clean; `test\nuser_profile`: 74 passed, 2 of them new\n(`a_github_login_brings_its_picture`, `no_picture_is_made_up`).\n- Prototype: `tsc -b` clean; `vitest run`: 366 passed, with new cases in\n`people-profile.test.ts`.\n\n**Not verified live:** a real GitHub-brokered sign-in. The local\nKeycloak has no GitHub IdP, so this needs checking on Dev after deploy.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n* Expanded profile pages with organization memberships and a combined\nsession overview, including sign-in details and token expiry when\navailable.\n* Added profile display-name editing and an identities section for\nreviewing sign-in methods, linked accounts, and email addresses.\n* Users can claim or revoke linked accounts and check eligible sign-ins\nand connections for alias confirmations.\n* Profile photos now prioritize uploaded images; supported GitHub\naccounts can supply a fallback avatar when no photo is set.\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * Blank profile names refresh from the realm at most once per day.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqx3/vCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAyecQAC5deC2xS0WT2SIOoSVH0Em4\nxsh6mTtAuQGFlXFOn2oeTNs+dhFEPUQhKl4JJ+VfQAg8hHsrQX+E0VyuoSdTqggg\n4E5VWvsAFo/bDvUa7gcM5JaiRJ/LpSG2oFy7+ku6aECSatmQ0ao9vpIyEdMRqTmQ\nEqBLyVYlPJzjf0cpJ3pUzyyM973niQShXf7erKkTRRtjWSVtnh+8VwNCN8PmrhRG\nK/MRvJdXYUIbBvjGnlPFAX2ykD2TVcazqUSqQQZ2jx8fsrKkGJBm6J3IUzDDb8DZ\nkHNRB0cJd5u3k8bqdrwE3iLEfbfRYKjGEfGFdOSxSIQ6HtU1/V+9uhVbe3b53vfO\nAzlOyGaxoehWIQT24V+l/MZNEOYBjNWC3YZRNTsTHiEqJ6RU+IHOLuNefVK5uO+/\naRiaBGmh0tXzHXLJDYm4qX5JBqltW42JKHTYQzkO+BjBjAyQXwQ/R0U3sA96x1VJ\nktDoBOqRIOZGTjPOdLh2C7EfRJqlZz/0fv3R79PYUivGol3I3+ZgnumM5ggUj+b8\nTILyol5RZiHgmhaBvQwBvLoLW4E8QfCxV2wi9kvnFHqChA84te8Kn2zscJrlEAYk\nOF32I/A13gWoE6tLf4Vw2Rz6pHBiJ9IAqxgQ64fCu131WJBEiXM7m9apGIV/2AAh\nXA9rQjP4astRsFXj8G4L\n=KBgl\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":