d}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AndrejK666","id":301748190,"login":"AndrejK666","node_id":"U_kgDOEfxP3g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/542a6688c741fadd7f9ee85693b4fb4f6122ebae/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T11:22:02Z","email":"Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech","name":"ANDREI KUCHMA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T11:22:02Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(gearbox, catalog): a product lives at products/<id>/product.gdl, and a gear''s PRD and DESIGN are found by name (#675)\n\nTwo places where building a product from a repository depended on one\nfixed file name.\n\n### The product description\n- The portal wrote `product.gdl` at the repository root; the desktop''s\nNew Product suggests `products/<id>/product.gdl`. A new product is now\nwritten at **`products/<id>/product.gdl`**, the layout the IDE''s Gearbox\nalready finds. The file keeps the name the engine and the `.gdl`\nlanguage look for; the product''s id names its directory, and a\nrepository can hold more than one product.\n- A description already written **stays where it is** (`written.path` on\nthe record). Projects created with a root `product.gdl` keep one file,\nand changing a product''s id does not leave a second one.\n- The sibling corpus is reached from where the file sits:\n`path(\"../../../gears-rust\")` from `products/<id>/`. The preview runs\nthe engine on the same layout, so it resolves as it will in the IDE.\n- The path is validated: relative, no `.`/`..` segment, ends in\n`product.gdl`.\n\n### A gear''s documents\n- The repository scan read `docs/PRD.md` and `docs/DESIGN.md` only.\n`principal_doc` now finds a gear''s PRD, DESIGN, DECOMPOSITION and\nUPSTREAM_REQS **by name** under its `docs/`: `PRD.md`,\n`PERMISSION_PRD.md`, `permission-design.md`, `prd/overview.md`. Nearest\nto `docs/` wins, so a gear''s own `docs/PRD.md` beats a feature''s\n`docs/specs/alerts/PRD.md`.\n- Feeds the doc states, the mapping''s evidence step (`doc_text`), the\nstage of an unbuilt gear, and the diagrams.\n\n### Checked\n- `cargo fmt --check` and `cargo clippy --all-targets -D warnings` are\nclean.\n- `cargo test components_catalog`: 262 passed, including new tests for\nthe path, the corpus link, the keep-where-written rule and the document\nrule.\n- Not run on a stand yet: a preview with `write` on a real repository.\n\nDocs: `studio-components-catalog.md` and `studio-spec-mapping.md` say\nwhere the file goes and how a gear''s documents are found.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","tree":{"sha":"813626dd1b57016a7f5d68c007a242a038241577","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/trees/813626dd1b57016a7f5d68c007a242a038241577"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/commits/542a6688c741fadd7f9ee85693b4fb4f6122ebae","verification":{"payload":"tree 813626dd1b57016a7f5d68c007a242a038241577\nparent 3a87478d653de33f1255cd24bc78d7c6210f79a3\nauthor ANDREI KUCHMA <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech> 1791458522 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791458522 +0200\n\nfix(gearbox, catalog): a product lives at products/<id>/product.gdl, and a gear''s PRD and DESIGN are found by name (#675)\n\nTwo places where building a product from a repository depended on one\nfixed file name.\n\n### The product description\n- The portal wrote `product.gdl` at the repository root; the desktop''s\nNew Product suggests `products/<id>/product.gdl`. A new product is now\nwritten at **`products/<id>/product.gdl`**, the layout the IDE''s Gearbox\nalready finds. The file keeps the name the engine and the `.gdl`\nlanguage look for; the product''s id names its directory, and a\nrepository can hold more than one product.\n- A description already written **stays where it is** (`written.path` on\nthe record). Projects created with a root `product.gdl` keep one file,\nand changing a product''s id does not leave a second one.\n- The sibling corpus is reached from where the file sits:\n`path(\"../../../gears-rust\")` from `products/<id>/`. The preview runs\nthe engine on the same layout, so it resolves as it will in the IDE.\n- The path is validated: relative, no `.`/`..` segment, ends in\n`product.gdl`.\n\n### A gear''s documents\n- The repository scan read `docs/PRD.md` and `docs/DESIGN.md` only.\n`principal_doc` now finds a gear''s PRD, DESIGN, DECOMPOSITION and\nUPSTREAM_REQS **by name** under its `docs/`: `PRD.md`,\n`PERMISSION_PRD.md`, `permission-design.md`, `prd/overview.md`. Nearest\nto `docs/` wins, so a gear''s own `docs/PRD.md` beats a feature''s\n`docs/specs/alerts/PRD.md`.\n- Feeds the doc states, the mapping''s evidence step (`doc_text`), the\nstage of an unbuilt gear, and the diagrams.\n\n### Checked\n- `cargo fmt --check` and `cargo clippy --all-targets -D warnings` are\nclean.\n- `cargo test components_catalog`: 262 passed, including new tests for\nthe path, the corpus link, the keep-where-written rule and the document\nrule.\n- Not run on a stand yet: a preview with `write` on a real repository.\n\nDocs: `studio-components-catalog.md` and `studio-spec-mapping.md` say\nwhere the file goes and how a gear''s documents are found.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqx3zaCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA0BwQAF5MJ9xGHrMGrpddIeiKdBwi\nBD173XZ3H60vgE6aks/v7N8Qj8zKeIbztf/cSc/64W/mXptMr/Z+2ZiTP