hat and why\n\n<!-- What changes, and why — for a reviewer who was not in the\ndiscussion. -->\n\n## How it was verified\n\n<!-- The checks you ran, and what you saw in the running stack or on a\nstand. -->\n\n- [ ] Checks for every component touched (CONTRIBUTING.md → \"Check it\nbefore you push\")\n- [ ] Seen working: Compose stack / `dev` stand / not user-visible\n\n## Contracts and decisions\n\n- [ ] No API, event or error contract changes — or\n`docs/api-conventions.md`, the catalogs and the OpenAPI agree with them\n- [ ] No architectural change — or an ADR is added or linked\n- [ ] Documentation updated where the way to build, run or use something\nchanged\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] One topic; stacked on #___ if it depends on another pull request\n- [ ] Every commit signed off (DCO)\n- [ ] No secrets, `.env` files or real credentials\n\nCloses #\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n- **New Features**\n- Repository syncs display queued, running, completed, failed,\ncancelled, and lost states with live progress updates.\n- Cancel queued or running syncs and retry failed or cancelled syncs.\nRefusals are shown when an action cannot be completed.\n- Long-running syncs continue to receive updates, with fallback checks\nwhen the event stream is unavailable.\n- **Bug Fixes**\n- Repository artifact lists refresh when sync status changes, even if\nthe total stored count stays the same. Updates to stored counts are also\nreflected after a brief delay.\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Maryna Lituyeva <maryna.lituyeva@constructor.tech>\nCo-authored-by: Maryna Lituyeva <maryna.lituyeva@constructor.tech>","tree":{"sha":"2f0dc937a4ef7c9eb871ac345bae0244eded0113","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/trees/2f0dc937a4ef7c9eb871ac345bae0244eded0113"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studi