*\n- Repository artifact lists refresh when sync status changes, even if\nthe total stored count stays the same. Updates to stored counts are also\nreflected after a brief delay.\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Maryna Lituyeva <maryna.lituyeva@constructor.tech>\nCo-authored-by: Maryna Lituyeva <maryna.lituyeva@constructor.tech>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqx1fmCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAEnQQAJ/KXhE/4vVdrz3FTg86Ndj2\nrLnkmPZE7j3OJDLuJPnDrPNw5A6JtZ7xFQEdBoIPK02dkaxgaXSxHJ3IUoC8bkgP\nn77A5ao4ziG/WOfOd4k06kLETjg2q+yXLu7PeANo5F4mOEaWMaoms4dFgpdAHYeY\nPT4YLm7DFKzc551ONqvXT5AoMoK4gDIHAbXjZ6ksocSFjZiaaJmvsn4Tx8QS/x6L\nWL4esNf+1x69v1odKWPxHsMutZpm/JfUlamhGmxPy3L1X9oYEIhU4s3AaOLPNGua\nJL87FmSGvqP4uq7SS5LF/ybhLUax6vBzJE5+7KhlDummwaAyDyyz0nDVSA8u49cB\nhaYF2UWQXR9Wypa7QrQ2NpG+hZr3aiHpXp6Y0xFNivQRNejWcrPWSBXYPUnbR69C\n7GhOtNvTXiXESCvq60V3ZH4WSbFbsuNof6GOKP4zSECSKl9QNYbBFK5/WDkEv8zh\nn6iCQ3TtJoMcu1JU5lguO+5BdxqXLK9q3+7Sa6MKxMrP389mCjxuu+aeulRAAx9G\nBrTvxi+K6BOhD0TzHPRCtL6tnSkZ5roKKPLS5lAJTYFMbyjuBZV/5mgdUfg/iynI\nGDhLAmKvloDVoJvdRGj0inZd9yWm2n9nuC4o39jDfkEPkv+p2LerAamx1iEMG40A\nsu4k0u6dsbRKSPBtYHth\n=le7a\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-08T08:44:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/3a87478d653de33f1255cd24bc78d7c6210f79a3","node_id":"C_kwDOTl7dJtoAKDNhODc0NzhkNjUzZGUzM2YxMjU1Y2QyNGJjNzhkN2M2MjEwZjc5YTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/dbc9a270954a1ce5971b0d745f5a6e479f72e5be","sha":"dbc9a270954a1ce5971b0d745f5a6e479f72e5be","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/dbc9a270954a1ce5971b0d745f5a6e479f72e5be"}],"sha":"3a87478d653de33f1255cd24bc78d7c6210f79a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/3a87478d653de33f1255cd24bc78d7c6210f79a3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/301748190?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AndrejK666","id":301748190,"login":"AndrejK666","node_id":"U_kgDOEfxP3g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/dbc9a270954a1ce5971b0d745f5a6e479f72e5be/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T06:37:49Z","email":"Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech","name":"ANDREI KUCHMA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T06:37:49Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Pull requests on the project page, by who they''re waiting on (#671)\n\n## What this is for\n\nA manager opening a project wants to know whether anything is stuck, and\non whom, without knowing what a pull request is. This adds that answer\nto the project page: **\"Pull requests — who they''re waiting on\"**. Every\nopen pull request of the project''s repositories is listed under the\nperson it is waiting on right now, with how long it has been open and\nhow long it has been quiet.\n\nThe People view (the same queues across every project, per person) is\nthe next PR. It reads the same endpoint.\n\n## Where the data comes from\n\n- **Sync (artifact-ingest).** A `pull_request` node now also carries\n`draft`, `requested_reviewers`, `requested_teams`, `assignees`,\n`reviews` (each reviewer''s last word: `approved` / `changes_requested` /\n`commented`) and `review_decision`. New edges `reviewed_by` and\n`assigned_to` link pull_request → user, the same way `authored_by` does.\n- **No extra GitHub calls.** GitHub''s `/pulls` listing already returns\ndraft, requested reviewers and teams, and assignees. The reviews come\nfrom the GraphQL query the sync already ran for unresolved review\nthreads: two review lists were added to it (`latestOpinionatedReviews` +\n`latestReviews`). REST would have needed one call per pull request.\n- **Schema.** These are added to `pull_request.v1` as optional fields\n(ADR-0013 §5, additive). The type id stays the same, and a node written\nbefore this PR still reads, as \"reviews not read\". `review_decision` is\nour own derivation. GitHub''s `reviewDecision` is null on any repository\nwithout branch protection.\n- **Providers.** GitHub only. The GitLab and Bitbucket drivers do not\nfetch pull requests at all today\n(`cpt-studio-constraint-connector-github-depth`), so there is nothing to\nextend there. This is stated in the connector design. Nothing is faked\nfor them: such a project has no pull requests in the graph.\n- **People.** A login is shown as a person only when a member of the\nproject''s organization has **confirmed** that account as theirs\n(ADR-0012 aliases). This goes through a new narrow studio-user port,\n`MemberAliases`: confirmed attributions only, active members of that one\norganization, the member''s id and name, and no e-mail or role. The\norganization is resolved project → workspace → organization through\naccount-management *as the caller*. If the directory cannot be asked,\n`members_known: false` is returned and nobody is called an outsider.\n\n## The endpoint\n\n`GET\n/studio-artifact-ingest/v1/open-pull-requests?project_id=…&offset=&limit=`\n→ `{ items, total, members_known }`, sorted longest-quiet first.\n\nIt lives in artifact-ingest because that gear owns the `pull_request`\nnodes and already serves `/source-activity` and `/activity` from them\nthrough the index. Insight''s `/components/pull-requests` reads a\ndifferent system (Insight''s warehouse). Authorization is the same as the\nother project artifact reads: authenticated, the caller''s tenant graph,\nand the project as a payload scope (`?project_id=`, rule C2).\n\n## Classification: one bucket per pull request, checked in order\n\n`artifact_ingest/pull_request_waits.rs` is a pure function with unit\ntests:\n\n1. **draft** → the author. Nobody acts before they do.\n2. **author**: a request for changes still stands, from someone who has\nnot been asked to look again. Changes outrank a pending reviewer,\nbecause the code is about to change.\n3. **review**: logins or teams that still owe a review. GitHub keeps\nthis list current: a review removes the login and a re-request puts it\nback. So \"asked again after changes\" waits on the reviewer.\n4. **author**: review conversations are still open, or the pull request\nwas only commented on and nobody approved it.\n5. **merge**: approved and nothing outstanding. This is the author''s\nmove.\n6. **nobody**: open, not a draft, and nobody was ever asked. These are\nthe stuck ones, and the page shows them first.\n\nThe author''s own reviews do not count, and a dismissed review counts\nonly as a comment.\n\n## Prototype\n\nThe project Overview gets a new card (`pull-requests-waiting.tsx`). It\nhas one collapsible queue per person, or per team, plus a \"Nobody asked\"\nqueue first. Each queue shows counts per bucket and its pull requests:\nthe title links to the provider, then repo#number, the reason in one\nsentence, \"open N days · quiet for N days\", and a \"quiet\" flag after a\nweek. The empty states are separate for \"no repositories\", \"not synced\nyet\" and \"nothing open\". All wording and grouping is in\n`pull-request-waits.ts`, with vitest tests.\n\n## Verified\n\n- **Backend gates** (rust 1.97, private target volume, rebuilt from\nscratch): `cargo fmt --check`, `cargo clippy --all-targets -D warnings`,\nand `cargo test`: 1376/1376 before the rebase onto #648/#649 and\n**1405/1405 after it**. `cargo test` includes the api_contract and\ngts_inventory snapshot tests. The new tests run: 21 in\n`pull_request_waits`, 2 in `gts`, and 1 GitHub driver test plus the\nextended review-threads fixture (self-reviews, deleted authors and\npending drafts are dropped; an approval outlives a later comment).\n`api-contract.json` and `gts-types.json` were regenerated. `check-docs`\nand `check-api-usage` pass.\n- **Live end to end**, on a standalone backend (`--no-default-features\n--features graph`, graph-postgres, static token). One project with four\nreal repositories: constructorfabric/studio-web, gears-frontx, studio,\nand gears-frontx-templates. The syncs ran read-only with my GitHub\ntoken: 1020 pull requests, open_review_threads reported for each\nrepository, and nothing written to GitHub. The stored `pull_request`\npayloads in `studio_artifact_index` carry `draft`,\n`requested_reviewers`, `requested_teams`, `assignees`, `reviews` and\n`review_decision`. The graph has 114 `reviewed_by` and 79 `assigned_to`\nedges.\n- **Endpoint**: 23 open pull requests: 1 nobody, 6 review, 6 author, 1\nmerge, 9 draft. Nine were spot-checked against `gh pr view --json\nreviewRequests,latestReviews,isDraft,reviewDecision,assignees`, and all\nmatch the rules:\n- gears-frontx#556 has reviewers GeraBart and tscbmstubp requested, and\nitechmeat has asked for changes. It lands in **author**, because\nstanding changes outrank a pending review.\n- gears-frontx#564 had a request for changes from itechmeat, and\nitechmeat was then asked to review again. It lands in **review** with\nthe reason \"asked again\". `approved` matches GitHub''s APPROVED.\n- studio#433: GitHub''s `latestReviews` shows ainetx only COMMENTED, but\nGitHub says CHANGES_REQUESTED. Ours says `changes_requested` too, which\nis why the query reads `latestOpinionatedReviews`.\n  - studio#435 is waiting on the **team** studio-maintainers.\n- studio-web#648 has an approval, but the approver was asked again. It\nlands in **review** and is `review_required`, the same as GitHub. The\nfirst live run said `approved`, and that is fixed in this PR.\n- studio-web#645 and gears-frontx-templates#27 have open conversations\nand nobody asked, so they land in **author**.\n- gears-frontx-templates#13 is a draft that was already approved. It\nlands in **draft**.\n  - gears-frontx#658 is waiting for review from GeraBart.\n- **People**: a GitHub account confirmed as the admin''s (alias\n`github:GeraBart`) shows as the member \"Stand Admin\" in every queue.\nEvery other login is marked \"not in this organization\", and\n`members_known: true`.\n- **The live run caught a boot panic that unit tests could not**:\n`OpenPullRequestDto` was already a schema name in the connector gear.\nThe DTOs are renamed (`WaitingPullRequest*`).\n- **Prototype**: tsc, vitest 363/363 after the rebase (15 new), and vite\nbuild all pass. I opened the real project page in headless Chrome\nagainst that backend and measured the DOM. The card is 754px wide at\n1440 with 12 queues, totals \"1 no reviewer · 6 to review · 6 to rework ·\n1 ready to merge · 9 draft\", and links to github.com. At 390px,\nscrollWidth equals clientWidth (390) in both light and dark, so there is\nno horizontal scroll. Dark theme renders on its tokens (card\nrgb(15,23,42)). The measurement also changed the queue order: six drafts\nof one author used to rank above someone owed three reviews, and now\ndrafts count last.\n\n## Not verified / known limits\n\n- GitLab and Bitbucket: their drivers fetch no pull requests at all, so\nthey have no data here. That is unchanged by this PR and is written in\nthe connector design.\n- Reviews are read for at most 200 open pull requests per repository\n(the existing threads cap). Past that cap, `reviews` is null and the\npage says the reviews could not be read.\n- Data is as fresh as the last sync. Edges only accumulate, so a\nreviewer who was removed keeps their `reviewed_by` edge. The node holds\nthe current state.\n- Member naming is only as good as the confirmed aliases. On Dev, few\npeople have confirmed a GitHub account yet, so most accounts will read\n\"not in this organization\" until they do. That is honest, but it looks\nbare.\n- Not checked against real Keycloak or on Dev. The DTO exposes members''\ndisplay names to anyone who can read the project''s artifacts. It does\nnot expose e-mail or role, and it covers only active members with\nconfirmed aliases.\n- The `merge` bucket assumes the author merges.\n\n## Next\n\nThe **People** view: the same queues across every project of the\norganization, per person (\"what is waiting on Bob\").\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n* Added a project overview section that groups open pull requests by who\nthey’re waiting on, with queue totals, reviewer and assignee details,\nand pull-request age.\n* Pull requests are ordered by how long they’ve been quiet, with items\nunchanged for seven or more days marked as quiet.\n* Added a loading view and distinct messages for projects without\nrepositories, repositories not yet synced, or no open pull requests.\n* Where organization membership is known, people are matched to\norganization members; otherwise, the interface indicates that membership\ninformation is unavailable.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","tree":{"sha":"ab6b34b867388e5f9db45810a8c5a77e613027e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/trees/ab6b34b867388e5f9db45810a8c5a77e613027e0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/commits/dbc9a270954a1ce5971b0d745f5a6e479f72e5be","verification":{"payload":"tree ab6b34b867388e5f9db45810a8c5a77e613027e0\nparent 9bc658dd61c951f9d5840c40593d96d9b2c93ce0\nauthor ANDREI KUCHMA <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech> 1791441469 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791441469 +0200\n\nPull requests on the project page, by who they''re waiting on (#671)\n\n## What this is for\n\nA manager opening a project wants to know whether anything is stuck, and\non whom, without knowing what a pull request is. This adds that answer\nto the project page: **\"Pull requests — who they''re waiting on\"**. Every\nopen pull request of the project''s repositories is listed under the\nperson it is waiting on right now, with how long it has been open and\nhow long it has been quiet.\n\nThe People view (the same queues across every project, per person) is\nthe next PR. It reads the same endpoint.\n\n## Where the data comes from\n\n- **Sync (artifact-ingest).** A `pull_request` node now also carries\n`draft`, `requested_reviewers`, `requested_teams`, `assignees`,\n`reviews