-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/9bc658dd61c951f9d5840c40593d96d9b2c93ce0","node_id":"C_kwDOTl7dJtoAKDliYzY1OGRkNjFjOTUxZjlkNTg0MGM0MDU5M2Q5NmQ5YjJjOTNjZTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/7a8eadc81bd3c27c60eadec616f23e3cd4ef159e","sha":"7a8eadc81bd3c27c60eadec616f23e3cd4ef159e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/7a8eadc81bd3c27c60eadec616f23e3cd4ef159e"}],"sha":"9bc658dd61c951f9d5840c40593d96d9b2c93ce0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/9bc658dd61c951f9d5840c40593d96d9b2c93ce0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/301748190?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AndrejK666","id":301748190,"login":"AndrejK666","node_id":"U_kgDOEfxP3g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/7a8eadc81bd3c27c60eadec616f23e3cd4ef159e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T15:56:12Z","email":"Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech","name":"ANDREI KUCHMA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T15:56:12Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(reports): the roadmap plan lives in Studio, linked to its people and projects, and mirrored into the domain model (#648)\n\n## Why\n\nThe roadmap report''s plan (the planning team''s `gears.yaml`: teams,\npeople, consumer projects, and when each project needs each gear) was a\nfile Studio only **read**, either from a repository through the GitHub\nconnection or as an upload. Changing who is on which team, or when a\nproject needs a gear, meant editing a file somewhere else and\nrefreshing. This makes Studio the place the plan is kept and edited.\n\n## What\n\n**Backend (`studio-reports`):**\n- `GET /studio-reports/v1/reports/{id}/plan` answers the plan in the\nsections the planning team edits: group lanes, units and their teams,\npeople (login, alias, team, power, email), consumer projects, and needs\n(per gear, per project: `Q3''26` / `YES` / `no` / `?`). Each is in the\ndocument''s order, which is the order the workbook draws. The answer also\ncarries the `revision` a save is made against.\n- `PUT …/plan/{lanes|units|people|projects|needs}` saves **one\nsection**, done in `plan_edit.rs`:\n- It replaces that one top-level key and nothing else. `board`,\n`branches`, an inline `report:` definition and any other key keep their\nvalue and their place. An entry keeps the fields the section does not\nname: a need written `{ needed: …, why: … }` keeps its `why`.\n- The whole plan must hold together afterwards (a person''s team exists,\na need''s project exists, a team tag is in one unit, colours are hex). If\nnot, nothing is saved and the **400 lists every reason**.\n- Every change bumps `revision`. A save at a stale revision is a **409**\n(`aborted`, `PLAN_REVISION_STALE`), so one editor cannot silently undo\nanother''s change.\n- The first save makes Studio the plan''s home (`from: studio`). The file\nit was read from is let go, and a refresh no longer reads it over the\nedit. An upload is still an import.\n- `GET …/plan/yaml` exports `gears.yaml` for the planning script or a\nbackup. `serde_yaml` writes YAML 1.2, but the script reads with PyYAML\n(1.1), so strings like `no`, `yes`, `on` are written quoted. Real\nbooleans (e.g. `per_group: true` in an inline definition) stay bare.\n- `PlanSnapshot` gains `revision` and `edited_by` (the subject id), with\nserde defaults so stored sources read as before.\n\n**Prototype:** the Reports card has \"Edit the plan…\" with a tab per\nsection:\n- Teams per unit, and people with a team picker and a filter.\n- Projects with ordering, which sets the column order.\n- The needs grid (gear × project) with `YES` / `no` / `?` and the coming\nquarters as suggestions.\n- Lanes.\n\nEach tab saves on its own, shows a dot when it has unsaved changes, can\nbe undone, and offers a reload on a 409. \"Load gears.yaml…\" is now\n\"Import gears.yaml…\", and there is \"Export gears.yaml\".\n\n**Docs:** `docs/design/studio-reports.md` gets a new principle\n(`cpt-studio-principle-reports-plan-edited-here`) and the endpoints.\n`api-contract-baseline.txt` adds the yaml export under `typed-response`\nbeside the workbook: it is a file, and `GET …/plan` is its typed shape.\n\n## Step 2: the plan''s people are linked to Studio''s\n\nSecond commit. A plan person is matched to a Studio person by their\nGitHub login, using **confirmed** GitHub aliases only (ADR-0012).\nMembership comes from `OrganizationRoster`. Nothing is stored: the match\nis computed on read, so a person who confirms their account is linked\nfrom then on.\n- `GET …/plan/people` answers three things:\n- each person in the plan, with the Studio `person_id` behind the login\nand `member` (an active member of this organization);\n- `unplanned`: members with a confirmed GitHub account the plan does not\nlist;\n- `members_without_github`: how many members have no confirmed GitHub\naccount.\n  \n  `identities_available: false` when studio-user is not running.\n- `user_profile::AliasResolver` gains `confirmed_identities(kind,\npeople)`, the reverse of `confirmed_owners`; confirmed only.\n- The People tab gets an \"In Studio\" column: ✓ name, \"not a member\",\n\"not in Studio\", or … for an unsaved row. Below the table:\n- \"Members of the organization the plan does not list\", each with **Add\nto the plan**;\n  - how many members cannot be named yet.\n  \nNames come from the members list (`people.view`); without it a person is\nshown by id.\n\n## Step 3: a consumer project can be a Studio project\n\nThird commit. A `gear_projects` entry may name the organization''s Studio\nproject it is, as `studio_project` (the tenant id), kept in the plan. A\nvalue that is not a UUID is refused with the project named. The Projects\ntab has a \"Studio project\" column with the organization''s projects, or\n\"outside Studio\". An id from elsewhere is shown, not dropped.\n\n## Step 4: the plan''s teams are mirrored into the domain model\n\nThe domain model already has the organization''s structure: `org-unit`,\n`team`, `person`, and `membership` with `allocation`. The plan now\nmirrors into it (`reports/mirror.rs`, through the new\n`domain_model::port::DomainObjects` in the ClientHub, which uses the\nsame path as `POST/GET /objects`: caller''s context, PDP, `warn`):\n- a unit becomes an `org-unit`;\n- a team becomes a `team` with `org_unit_ref`;\n- a person becomes a `person` keyed `github:<login>`, shared and never\nretired by one report;\n- a person in a team becomes a `membership` with `allocation` = power.\n\nAll are `mirrored`. Only what changed is written. What leaves the plan\nis **retired** with `valid_to`, never deleted, because a deleted graph\nkey cannot be written again. A save of units or people publishes in the\nbackground. `POST …/plan/sync` publishes now and reports what it did;\nthe editor has \"Publish teams to the domain model\".\n\n**The plan is the source of truth only until step 7 of the domain-query\nmigration** (version on read): until then a model write is\nlast-writer-wins, and a screen two planners edit must not sit on it.\nAfter step 7 the direction flips. This is marked in\n`docs/domain-query-migration.md` (step 7 and the \"into the graph\" line),\nthe reports design (`cpt-studio-principle-reports-teams-mirrored`) and\nthe domain-model design, with two model gaps: no team-to-unit relation,\nno team-members edge.\n\nMain is merged in (including #647 and #649); the API contract is\nregenerated.\n\n## Not in this PR\n- **Who may see and edit the plan.** The plan holds emails and\nper-person capacity. For now it is open to whoever can open the\norganization''s report, as the source and the workbook already are. Roles\n(ADR-0019) come later.\n- Making the domain model the source of truth for teams (after migration\nstep 7); pre-filling needs from `product.gdl`.\n- A file''s comments do not survive the first edit (`serde_yaml` writes\nthe text).\n\n## Checks\n- `cargo fmt --check` and `cargo clippy --all-targets -D warnings`:\nclean.\n- `cargo test` for `reports::`, `api_contract` and `org_scope`: 88\npassed (239 with steps 2–4 and main merged, over `reports`,\n`domain_model`, `user_profile`, `api_contract`, `org_scope`, `assembly`,\nwhich adds `user_profile::` and `people_links`). New: `plan_edit` (order\nkept, other keys untouched, entry fields kept, every reason listed,\nPyYAML-safe quoting, booleans kept, first section on an empty plan) and\nservice tests (Studio becomes home, stale revision refused, refresh\nstops reading the file, invalid edit leaves nothing).\n- `docs/api-contract.json` regenerated. `check-api-usage`: OK.\n`check-docs`: OK.\n- Prototype: `tsc -b` clean, vitest 348/348 (after merging main) (new\n`plan-model.test.ts`).\n- All fixtures are made up; no real plan data is in the repo.\n- Not verified on a running stand.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n- **New Features**\n- Edit report plans in Studio across teams, people, projects, needs, and\nlanes. Save sections independently while preserving unsaved edits\nelsewhere.\n- Add, remove, reorder, and undo plan entries; filter people; and export\nplans as `gears.yaml`.\n- View links between plan people and Studio accounts, including\norganization membership status.\n- See plan validation errors and reload after a conflicting edit. Saving\na file-based plan requires confirmation.\n\n- **Bug Fixes**\n- Prevent invalid plans and outdated edits from being saved, with\nfeedback when validation fails or the plan has changed.\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","tree":{"sha":"4e153c2bd6cafc001081429cc2852a568c453c3a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/trees/4e153c2bd6cafc001081429cc2852a568c453c3a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/commits/7a8eadc81bd3c27c60eadec616f23e3cd4ef159e","verification":{"payload":"tree 4e153c2bd6cafc001081429cc2852a568c453c3a\nparent 0eee79d7c7aba63d1cf1182cf167cc2fe3aed4eb\nauthor ANDREI KUCHMA <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech> 1791388572 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791388572 +0200\n\nfeat(reports): the roadmap plan lives in Studio, linked to its people and projects, and mirrored into the domain model (#648)\n\n## Why\n\nThe roadmap report''s plan (the planning team''s `gears.yaml`: teams,\npeople, consumer projects, and when each project needs each gear) was a\nfile Studio only **read**, either from a repository through the GitHub\nconnection or as an upload. Changing who is on which team, or when a\nproject needs a gear, meant editing a file somewhere else and\nrefreshing. This makes Studio the place the plan is kept and edited.\n\n## What\n\n**Backend (`studio-reports`):**\n- `GET /studio-reports/v1/reports/{id}/plan` answers the plan in the\nsections the planning team edits: group lanes, units and their teams,\npeople (login, alias, team, power, email), consumer projects, and needs\n(per gear, per project: `Q3''26` / `YES` / `no` / `?`). Each is in the\ndocument''s order, which is the order the workbook draws. The answer also\ncarries the `revision` a save is made against.\n- `PUT …/plan/{lanes|units|people|projects|needs}` saves **one\nsection**, done in `plan_edit.rs`:\n- It replaces that one top-level key and nothing else. `board`,\n`branches`, an inline `report:` definition and any other key keep their\nvalue and their place. An entry keeps the fields the section does not\nname: a need written `{ needed: …, why: … }` keeps its `why`.\n- The whole plan must hold together afterwards (a person''s team exists,\na need''s project exists, a team tag is in one unit, colours are hex). If\nnot, nothing is saved and the **400 lists every reason**.\n- Every change bumps `revision`. A save at a stale revision is a **409**\n(`aborted`, `PLAN_REVISION_STALE`), so one editor cannot silently undo\nanother''s change.\n- The first save makes Studio the plan''s home (`from: studio`). The file\nit was read from is let go, and a refresh no longer reads it over the\nedit. An upload is still an import.\n- `GET …/plan/yaml` exports `gears.yaml` for the planning script or a\nbackup. `serde_yaml` writes YAML 1.2, but the script reads with PyYAML\n(1.1), so strings like `no`, `yes`, `on` are written quoted. Real\nbooleans (e.g. `per_group: true` in an inline definition) stay bare.\n- `PlanSnapshot` gains `revision` and `edited_by` (the subject id), with\nserde defaults so stored sources read as before.\n\n**Prototype:** the Reports card has \"Edit the plan…\" with a tab per\nsection:\n- Teams per unit, and people with a team picker and a filter.\n- Projects with ordering, which sets the column order.\n- The needs grid (gear × project) with `YES` / `no` / `?` and the coming\nquarters as suggestions.\n- Lanes.\n\nEach tab saves on its own, shows a dot when it has unsaved changes, can\nbe undone, and offers a reload on a 409. \"Load gears.yaml…\" is now\n\"Import gears.yaml…\", and there is \"Export gears.yaml\".\n\n**Docs:** `docs/design/studio-reports.md` gets a new principle\n(`cpt-studio-principle-reports-plan-edited-here`) and the endpoints.\n`api-contract-baseline.txt` adds the yaml export under `typed-response`\nbeside the workbook: it is a file, and `GET …/plan` is its typed shape.\n\n## Step 2: the plan''s people are linked to Studio''s\n\nSecond commit. A plan person is matched to a Studio person by their\nGitHub login, using **confirmed** GitHub aliases only (ADR-0012).\nMembership comes from `OrganizationRoster`. Nothing is stored: the match\nis computed on read, so a person who confirms their account is linked\nfrom then on.\n- `GET …/plan/people` answers three things:\n- each person in the plan, with the Studio `person_id` behind the login\nand `member` (an active member of this organization);\n- `unplanned`: members with a confirmed GitHub account the plan does not\nlist;\n- `members_without_github`: how many members have no confirmed GitHub\naccount.\n  \n  `identities_available: false` when studio-user is not running.\n- `user_profile::AliasResolver` gains `confirmed_identities(kind,\npeople)`, the reverse of `confirmed_owners`; confirmed only.\n- The People tab gets an \"In Studio\" column: ✓ name, \"not a member\",\n\"not in Studio\", or … for an unsaved row. Below the table:\n- \"Members of the organization the plan does not list\", each with **Add\nto the plan**;\n  - how many members cannot be named yet.\n  \nNames come from the members list (`people.view`); without it a person is\nshown by id.\n\n## Step 3: a consumer project can be a Studio project\n\nThird commit. A `gear_projects` entry may name the organization''s Studio\nproject it is, as `studio_project` (the tenant id), kept in the plan. A\nvalue that is not a UUID is refused with the project named. The Projects\ntab has a \"Studio project\" column with the organization''s projects, or\n\"outside Studio\". An id from elsewhere is shown, not dropped.\n\n## Step 4: the plan''s teams are mirrored into the domain model\n\nThe domain model already has the organization''s structure: `org-unit`,\n`team`, `person`, and `membership` with `allocation`. The plan now\nmirrors into it (`reports/mirror.rs`, through the new\n`domain_model::port::DomainObjects` in the ClientHub, which uses the\nsame path as `POST/GET /objects`: caller''s context, PDP, `warn`):\n- a unit becomes an `org-unit`;\n- a team becomes a `team` with `org_unit_ref`;\n- a person becomes a `person` keyed `github:<login>`, shared and never\nretired by one report;\n- a person in a team becomes a `membership` with `allocation` = power.\n\nAll are `mirrored`. Only what changed is written. What leaves the plan\nis **retired** with `valid_to`, never deleted, because a deleted graph\nkey cannot be written again. A save of units or people publishes in the\nbackground. `POST …/plan/sync` publishes now and reports what it did;\nthe editor has \"Publish teams to the domain model\".\n\n**The plan is the source of truth only until step 7 of the domain-query\nmigration** (version on read): until then a model write is\nlast-writer-wins, and a screen two planners edit must not sit on it.\nAfter step 7 the direction flips. This is marked in\n`docs/domain-query-migration.md` (step 7 and the \"into the graph\" line),\nthe reports design (`cpt-studio-principle-reports-teams-mirrored`) and\nthe domain-model design, with two model gaps: no team-to-unit relation,\nno team-members edge.\n\nMain is merged in (including #647 and #649); the API contract is\nregenerated.\n\n## Not in this PR\n- **Who may see and edit the plan.** The plan holds emails and\nper-person capacity. For now it is open to whoever can open the\norganization''s report, as the source and the workbook already are. Roles\n(ADR-0019) come later.\n- Making the domain model the source of truth for teams (after migration\nstep 7); pre-filling needs from `product.gdl`.\n- A file''s comments do not survive the first edit (`serde_yaml` writes\nthe text).\n\n## Checks\n- `cargo fmt --check` and `cargo clippy --all-targets -D warnings`:\nclean.\n- `cargo test` for `reports::`, `api_contract` and `org_scope`: 88\npassed (239 with steps 2–4 and main merged, over `reports`,\n`domain_model`, `user_profile`, `api_contract`, `org_scope`, `assembly`,\nwhich adds `user_profile::` and `people_links`). New: `plan_edit` (order\nkept, other keys untouched, entry fields kept, every reason listed,\nPyYAML-safe quoting, booleans kept, first section on an empty plan) and\nservice tests (Studio becomes home, stale revision refused, refresh\nstops reading the file, invalid edit leaves nothing).\n- `docs/api-contract.json` regenerated. `check-api-usage`: OK.\n`check-docs`: OK.\n- Prototype: `tsc -b` clean, vitest 348/348 (after merging main) (new\n`plan-model.test.ts`).\n- All fixtures are made up; no real plan data is in the repo.\n- Not verified on a running stand.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n- **New Features**\n- Edit report plans in Studio across teams, people, projects, needs, and\nlanes. Save sections independently while preserving unsaved edits\nelsewhere.\n- Add, remove, reorder, and undo plan entries; filter people; and export\nplans as `gears.yaml`.\n- View links between plan people and Studio accounts, including\norganization membership status.\n- See plan validation errors and reload after a conflicting edit. Saving\na file-based plan requires confirmation.\n\n- **Bug Fixes**\n- Prevent invalid plans and outdated edits from being saved, with\nfeedback when validation fails or the plan has changed.\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxmucCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAllEQAHCT1b/YICEiMySk+cAjLcaT\nxdRagAW1qzht9KtpeKkSUo9l+Rg6KCoFv/EQBzPSECTc2SX3BvYB4+Z2toFv9nq1\n15GovDNzIJjMQf2n6JmSsZ/H8BqdYJO1+Fggw5XUv/Gq1StVr//thEHg/jnGouWe\nb1NsGN/Q+cZUqcS6jX8ejmeVhFaaF7bSNnY0PUMpb7aXYIOKriuOGYoIPMKng51c\n7KYqheVHZxAoCDoJILolskjsEmqq0luJ0Bkg3JYKNovwkc0Zp6+yRapz4TdNvBX+\nQRu++hGWjJ4WNUnN90KGNKh85w0BSvaQDeZlMWfqpc3vLhHvs/8lILHSNGjNRP+I\n4UKJEs7GD7bEMJwDccCRTcPseSY6x1t85hzkGuzNgpJBQbgI7pRR20dNzoPfogIl\n4vgXQ81AKgF81GcUIRHjXm5cpnuTpGO8MmTkPx0LDCuKY5e2AGsPSwgTMNv+1THq\nPs3LhTfMKPr9NCkKybRCYS7G6EZplqQEQLsjoZIDNr0IWei3uGnZL0UUh2fVFg4j\n81Z2VtF/Z7vtTzTo4lBpCCq1URnKxPrepdbvR5DW3Q0fZc1NX3XZ396FkHBsSu8L\nplHns4bne90PqpUXYrWmtCydvnBDOOEwtf1iH4D3pWq7t5pNfwDen2lqmyt5Z2nD\nzQVgbbAjl8VHU8ggszLr\n=HHNa\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T15:56:12Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/7a8eadc81bd3c27c60eadec616f23e3cd4ef159e","node_id":"C_kwDOTl7dJtoAKDdhOGVhZGM4MWJkM2MyN2M2MGVhZGVjNjE2ZjIzZTNjZDRlZjE1OWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/0eee79d7c7aba63d1cf1182cf167cc2fe3aed4eb","sha":"0eee79d7c7aba63d1cf1182cf167cc2fe3aed4eb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/0eee79d7c7aba63d1cf1182cf167cc2fe3aed4eb"}],"sha":"7a8eadc81bd3c27c60eadec616f23e3cd4ef159e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/7a8eadc81bd3c27c60eadec616f23e3cd4ef159e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/301748190?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AndrejK666","id":301748190,"login":"AndrejK666","node_id":"U_kgDOEfxP3g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/0eee79d7c7aba63d1cf1182cf167cc2fe3aed4eb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T14:52:28Z","email":"Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech","name":"ANDREI KUCHMA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T14:52:28Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(user): a person carries every address, a photo, when they were last seen, and how the organization describes them (#649)\n\n## What and why\n\nThe members screen showed ids, and nothing about a person beyond a role.\nThe Constructor Studio prototype shows each person''s photo, address,\nlast activity and how the organization describes them (company,\ndepartment, title, manager). Studio did not hold any of it.\n\n**Backend (studio-user):**\n\n- **Names are no longer ids.** A person first seen through a token had\nno name in Studio, because nothing asked the realm. The profile now\nfills its blanks from the identity provider the first time the person,\nor a members listing, reads it. It also records the address the provider\nholds for each login.\n- **Every address a person holds: `emails`.** It is on `/me` and on each\nmember. It lists the profile''s address, each sign-in''s, and attributed\n`email` aliases. Each address carries its `source`, `verified` and\n`primary`. One person with several logins has several addresses.\n`LoginDto` gains `email` and `email_verified`.\n- **A photo.**\n- `PUT /me/avatar` and `DELETE /me/avatar` store and remove it. It may\nbe a PNG, JPEG, WebP or GIF of at most 1 MiB. The type is sniffed from\nthe bytes, not taken from the declaration.\n- `GET /avatars/{user_id}/{digest}` serves it anonymously, because an\n`<img>` sends no token. The digest is learned only from a profile read\nthe caller may make, and anything but the current version is a 404. The\nresponse is cached immutable, with `nosniff` and a `sandbox` CSP.\n- **`last_seen_at_epoch_ms`.** It is written at most every five minutes,\nwhen the caller is resolved.\n- **The organization''s description of a member.** Company, department,\ntitle and manager are held on the membership, so each organization\ndescribes its own people (ADR-0023). They are set through an optional\n`directory` on the existing `PUT /users/{user_id}/memberships/{org_id}`.\nA new route would have put `{org_id}` in another path (C1). The input is\nchecked before anything is written. The manager must be a member of the\nsame organization.\n- Migration `m0005` adds the columns and the `identity_avatar` table.\nThe upserts every sign-in and role change already run leave the new\ncolumns alone.\n\n- **Every member sees who else is in the organization (ADR-0036,\nproposed in this PR).** New route `GET /me/colleagues`. For each\norganization the caller is an active member of, it returns every active\nmember: name, photo, role, the organization''s description of them, and\nlast seen. It carries no addresses, no sign-ins and no suspended\nmembers; those stay on the members listing behind `people.view`. The\norganizations come from the caller''s own memberships, so the route takes\nno organization and stays within rule C1.\n\n**Portal (`studio-frontend-prototype`):**\n\n- **Members:**\n  - photo instead of initials;\n  - the primary address plus a count of the others;\n  - a Position column and a Last seen column.\n- **An opened member row:**\n  - every address, with its source and whether it is verified;\n  - the address each sign-in carries;\n  - a form for the organization''s description.\n- **Profile:** a card to upload, replace or remove a photo, and to see\nevery address you hold.\n- **Account button:** shows the photo.\n- **People:** a \"Who is here\" card that any member sees. The description\nform notes that every member sees it.\n- Every new field is optional, so against an older backend the screens\nlook as they did.\n\n## How it was verified\n\n- [x] Checks for every component touched:\n- **Backend** (`scripts/backend-check.sh`, after a rebase on current\n`main`):\n    - `clippy` with `-D warnings`, `fmt` and `features` pass.\n- `test user_profile` passes: 72 tests, including 10 new Postgres tests.\nThey check that a role change keeps the description, a re-link keeps a\nsign-in''s address, a sign-in keeps last-seen, a photo is stored,\nreplaced and removed, a merge carries the photo and description, a\nlisting reads sign-ins and aliases in bulk, and a member sees only the\nactive people of their own active organizations.\n- `test identity_directory` and `test api_contract` pass. The snapshot\nis regenerated.\n  - **Portal:**\n    - `tsc -b` and `vite build` pass.\n- `vitest` passes: 339 tests, including new ones for the address,\ndescription and photo helpers.\n    - `scripts/check-api-usage.mjs` is clean.\n- [ ] Seen working: **not yet.** This has not been run in the Compose\nstack or on a stand. That is the next step, and anything it finds lands\non this PR.\n\nThe no-default-features build warns about an unused `pub use\nservice::normalize_key` in `user_profile/mod.rs`. That warning is\nalready on `main`. This PR does not touch that file.\n\n## Contracts and decisions\n\n- [x] API changes:\n- New fields on `UserProfileDto`, `OrganizationMemberDto`, `LoginDto`\nand `PutMembershipRequest`.\n- New operations `studio_user.upsert_my_avatar`,\n`studio_user.delete_my_avatar`, `studio_user.get_avatar` and\n`studio_user.list_my_colleagues`. `docs/api-contract.json` is\nregenerated.\n- One line is added to `api-contract-baseline.txt`: `typed-response` for\nthe photo route. A photo is image bytes and has no JSON schema, like the\nreports workbook.\n- [x] Architectural decision: **ADR-0036** (proposed), \"Every member\nsees who else is in the organization\". It extends ADR-0019 and applies\nADR-0023. The org-scoped description follows ADR-0023.\n- [x] `docs/design/studio-user.md` is updated: domain model, endpoints,\nnew columns and the `identity_avatar` table. The ADR index is updated\ntoo.\n\n**Settled in this PR** (`fix(user)` commit):\n\n- **Merge.** A merge now carries the source''s photo and its description\nin each organization, wherever the target has none of its own. Whoever\nreported to the source now reports to the target.\n- **Members listing.** It reads every member''s sign-ins and aliases in\none query each, instead of two queries per member.\n- **Realm reads.** What the realm says about a person is re-read after a\nday, not once per process.\n\nEach of these is covered by a Postgres test.\n\n**Who may read the People list** is decided in **ADR-0036** (proposed):\n\n- The full members listing (addresses, sign-ins, suspended members,\ninvitations) stays behind `people.view`.\n- Every active member reads the smaller colleague projection.\n- Two choices in the ADR are for review: colleagues see each other''s\nlast-seen time, to five minutes, and every member sees the\norganization''s description of each person.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] One topic: the people profile and who may see it, backend plus the\nportal that shows it\n- [x] Every commit signed off (DCO)\n- [x] No secrets, `.env` files or real credentials\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","tree":{"sha":"a2d2966c8256dce9470320b6b39a4a870631e23e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/trees/a2d2966c8256dce9470320b6b39a4a870631e23e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/commits/0eee79d7c7aba63d1cf1182cf167cc2fe3aed4eb","verification":{"payload":"tree a2d2966c8256dce9470320b6b39a4a870631e23e\nparent a91139654a990bc47244a626c61fb16a22059ee7\nauthor ANDREI KUCHMA <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech> 1791384748 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791384748 +0200\n\nfeat(user): a person carries every address, a photo, when they were last seen, and how the organization describes them (#649)\n\n## What and why\n\nThe members screen showed ids, and nothing about a person beyond a role.\nThe Constructor Studio prototype shows each person''s photo, address,\nlast activity and how the organization describes them (company,\ndepartment, title, manager). Studio did not hold any of it.\n\n**Backend (studio-user):**\n\n- **Names are no longer ids.** A person first seen through a token had\nno name in Studio, because nothing asked the realm. The profile now\nfills its blanks from the identity provider the first time the person,\nor a members listing, reads it. It also records the address the provider\nholds for each login.\n- **Every address a person holds: `emails`.** It is on `/me` and on each\nmember. It lists the profile''s address, each sign-in''s, and attributed\n`email` aliases. Each address carries its `source`, `verified` and\n`primary`. One person with several logins has several addresses.\n`LoginDto` gains `email` and `email_verified`.\n- **A photo.**\n- `PUT /me/avatar` and `DELETE /me/avatar` store and remove it. It may\nbe a PNG, JPEG, WebP or GIF of at most 1 MiB. The type is sniffed from\nthe bytes, not taken from the declaration.\n- `GET /avatars/{user_id}/{digest}` serves it anonymously, because an\n`<img>` sends no token. The digest is learned only from a profile read\nthe caller may make, and anything but the current version is a 404. The\nresponse is cached immutable, with `nosniff` and a `sandbox` CSP.\n- **`last_seen_at_epoch_ms`.** It is written at most every five minutes,\nwhen the caller is resolved.\n- **The organization''s description of a member.** Company, department,\ntitle and manager are held on the membership, so each organization\ndescribes its own people (ADR-0023). They are set through an optional\n`directory` on the existing `PUT /users/{user_id}/memberships/{org_id}`.\nA new route would have put `{org_id}` in another path (C1). The input is\nchecked before anything is written. The manager must be a member of the\nsame organization.\n- Migration `m0005` adds the columns and the `identity_avatar` table.\nThe upserts every sign-in and role change already run leave the new\ncolumns alone.\n\n- **Every member sees who else is in the organization (ADR-0036,\nproposed in this PR).** New route `GET /me/colleagues`. For each\norganization the caller is an active member of, it returns every active\nmember: name, photo, role, the organization''s description of them, and\nlast seen. It carries no addresses, no sign-ins and no suspended\nmembers; those stay on the members listing behind `people.view`. The\norganizations come from the caller''s own memberships, so the route takes\nno organization and stays within rule C1.\n\n**Portal (`studio-frontend-prototype`):**\n\n- **Members:**\n  - photo instead of initials;\n  - the primary address plus a count of the others;\n  - a Position column and a Last seen column.\n- **An opened member row:**\n  - every address, with its source and whether it is verified;\n  - the address each sign-in carries;\n  - a form for the organization''s description.\n- **Profile:** a card to upload, replace or remove a photo, and to see\nevery address you hold.\n- **Account button:** shows the photo.\n- **People:** a \"Who is here\" card that any member sees. The description\nform notes that every member sees it.\n- Every new field is optional, so against an older backend the screens\nlook as they did.\n\n## How it was verified\n\n- [x] Checks for every component touched:\n- **Backend** (`scripts/backend-check.sh`, after a rebase on current\n`main`):\n    - `clippy` with `-D warnings`, `fmt` and `features` pass.\n- `test user_profile` passes: 72 tests, including 10 new Postgres tests.\nThey check that a role change keeps the description, a re-link keeps a\nsign-in''s address, a sign-in keeps last-seen, a photo is stored,\nreplaced and removed, a merge carries the photo and description, a\nlisting reads sign-ins and aliases in bulk, and a member sees only the\nactive people of their own active organizations.\n- `test identity_directory` and `test api_contract` pass. The snapshot\nis regenerated.\n  - **Portal:**\n    - `tsc -b` and `vite build` pass.\n- `vitest` passes: 339 tests, including new ones for the address,\ndescription and photo helpers.\n    - `scripts/check-api-usage.mjs` is clean.\n- [ ] Seen working: **not yet.** This has not been run in the Compose\nstack or on a stand. That is the next step, and anything it finds lands\non this PR.\n\nThe no-default-features build warns about an unused `pub use\nservice::normalize_key` in `user_profile/mod.rs`. That warning is\nalready on `main`. This PR does not touch that file.\n\n## Contracts and decisions\n\n- [x] API changes:\n- New fields on `UserProfileDto`, `OrganizationMemberDto`, `LoginDto`\nand `PutMembershipRequest`.\n- New operations `studio_user.upsert_my_avatar`,\n`studio_user.delete_my_avatar`, `studio_user.get_avatar` and\n`studio_user.list_my_colleagues`. `docs/api-contract.json` is\nregenerated.\n- One line is added to `api-contract-baseline.txt`: `typed-response` for\nthe photo route. A photo is image bytes and has no JSON schema, like the\nreports workbook.\n- [x] Architectural decision: **ADR-0036** (proposed), \"Every member\nsees who else is in the organization\". It extends ADR-0019 and applies\nADR-0023. The org-scoped description follows ADR-0023.\n- [x] `docs/design/studio-user.md` is updated: domain model, endpoints,\nnew columns and the `identity_avatar` table. The ADR index is updated\ntoo.\n\n**Settled in this PR** (`fix(user)` commit):\n\n- **Merge.** A merge now carries the source''s photo and its description\nin each organization, wherever the target has none of its own. Whoever\nreported to the source now reports to the target.\n- **Members listing.** It reads every member''s sign-ins and aliases in\none query each, instead of two queries per member.\n- **Realm reads.** What the realm says about a person is re-read after a\nday, not once per process.\n\nEach of these is covered by a Postgres test.\n\n**Who may read the People list** is decided in **ADR-0036** (proposed):\n\n- The full members listing (addresses, sign-ins, suspended members,\ninvitations) stays behind `people.view`.\n- Every active member reads the smaller colleague projection.\n- Two choices in the ADR are for review: colleagues see each other''s\nlast-seen time, to five minutes, and every member sees the\norganization''s description of each person.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] One topic: the people profile and who may see it, backend plus the\nportal that shows it\n- [x] Every commit signed off (DCO)\n- [x] No secrets, `.env` files or real credentials\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxlysCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA0VUQAJbFF/jgJSIeG6RX7gMvGs47\nmEHy0hbwg2VX8DePuUtt+7J5lfaC7N6FblQjmuavQK7xDmM3psjuOfvZavCNriNK\naImUPmptbu+U9Y6HNdTFOGXytXKqL9joeLAvITpddjFN4dyGjGKoMaWe9mWtah1h\nkYU5Z18onsBiZ7CJ0WTUM7BZrno6/M63UnyMtiids4lfr70nHn56oYKpqDdsBoNd\nuzGObcUo/mjHg4ovnsz2BgaKqQVo6kFSeNvZajes1jfXZt2OChFLsTvPv3F4Tbag\nx6bK7PqAsoBg16/TKnPvRbIhU2Oqaa8YBx+fH5VTjNkPtroZL+JmQ4ZQzRDF1SW2\n/4SbLECKfTa1MKFfJi5U3nzMzoYwNwZCtJQNfD8R2nMsGEhQy8ShV1/x/RTG69DN\ndxIKLO6wd8BZICSpek9a3H9V1t/L9Ne9j6eyYzAR1dK29OMCf09RFZK7R/WL6FKB\n1TUNyaoDdVg12YJjv+owqJR98U81XkmKsbBZOYatuJij5/HrQudG05AEXZ5+TyJR\ngiH24GuvI8amvuGjsBWp3sWmU+SeSbewq0fzxXt779ahoYz3n4eJEdf5jQ/n/udl\ng833EvX9DYC3hF7X3GhtRSSp7Rq7/X648MaTEXgAEXH7OjRm6dxOV7vn5qJVTgeC\nOGpW6UUEM52xhqP+SsiX\n=lafy\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T14:52:29Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/0eee79d7c7aba63d1cf1182cf167cc2fe3aed4eb","node_id":"C_kwDOTl7dJtoAKDBlZWU3OWQ3YzdhYmE2M2QxY2YxMTgyY2YxNjdjYzJmZTNhZWQ0ZWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/a91139654a990bc47244a626c61fb16a22059ee7","sha":"a91139654a990bc47244a626c61fb16a22059ee7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/a91139654a990bc47244a626c61fb16a22059ee7"}],"sha":"0eee79d7c7aba63d1cf1182cf167cc2fe3aed4eb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/0eee79d7c7aba63d1cf1182cf167cc2fe3aed4eb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/301748190?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AndrejK666","id":301748190,"login":"AndrejK666","node_id":"U_kgDOEfxP3g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/a91139654a990bc47244a626c61fb16a22059ee7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T13:09:41Z","email":"Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech","name":"ANDREI KUCHMA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T13:09:41Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(architecture): a page that shows how the running backend and the prototype are built (#647)\n\n## What this is for\n\nPeople keep asking \"what is actually in the backend, and how does it fit\ntogether?\" The product menu on the wordmark gets a new entry,\n**Architecture**. It opens `/architecture/`, a page of its own next to\n`/api-docs/`. The page shows:\n\n- **a header**: the commit the backend was built from, the commit this\nprototype was built from, the IDE session image, and the cargo features.\nIf the two commits differ, a warning says so.\n- **a diagram of every gear running in the backend**, in rows by\ndependency. The first row needs nothing, and each later row needs only\nrows above it. Studio gears, platform gears, platform system gears and\nplugins each look different, and it reads in light and dark. Choose a\ngear and you see what it is for, a link to its design doc (at the\nbackend''s commit), what it needs and what needs it (with lines drawn),\nits REST prefixes with a link into Docs & API narrowed to that gear, and\nwhich prototype screens call it.\n- **a \"Prototype\" section**: each screen, grouped by file, and the gears\nit calls. It also lists the calls that no gear of this backend serves.\n\nThe text is plain language, written so a manager can follow it.\n\n## Where each piece of data comes from, and why it cannot drift\n\n| Data | Source | Why it cannot drift |\n|---|---|---|\n| Gears, start order, dependencies, capabilities | New gear\n**`studio-assembly`**, `GET /studio-assembly/v1/manifest`. It calls\n`toolkit::GearRegistry::discover_and_build()`, the same inventory walk\nand topo sort the runtime runs at boot. | It is read from the process.\nNothing in the gear names a gear. |\n| Studio vs platform, gear / plugin / system, which extension point a\nplugin fills | Pure rules in `assembly/manifest.rs`. Origin comes from\nthe name (`studio-…`) or from the plugin''s host. Role comes from the\nregistry''s `system` capability or a `-plugin` suffix. The extension\npoint comes from the plugin''s name, matched in 3 tiers, and an ambiguous\nmatch answers null. | Same as above. The IdP plugins honestly answer\n`extends: null`, because the GTS plugin instance does not name its host\ngear. |\n| What a Studio gear is for | `build.rs` compiles in the first paragraph\nof §1.1 of each `docs/design/<gear>.md`. | It ships inside the binary,\nso the text is that commit''s design. A test fails if a design loses its\n§1.1. |\n| Backend commit | `STUDIO_BUILD_COMMIT`, compiled in by `build.rs`.\nCI''s `Build (release)` step sets it from `git rev-parse HEAD`. | It is\nfixed at compile time. A local build says `null` rather than guessing\nfrom `.git`, because an incremental build would keep a stale SHA. |\n| Session image | `studio-session`''s own config section, parsed with its\nown `StudioSessionConfig`. | It is the image that gear will actually\nstart. |\n| A gear''s REST paths and tags | `/cf/openapi.json` of the same backend.\nEach path goes to the gear named by its first segment (rule A1), or to\nthe single gear whose name starts with it (`studio-identity` →\n`studio-identity-directory`). | The gateway builds it from what each\ngear registered. Another gear cannot reach the gateway''s registry, so\nthe manifest does not repeat it. |\n| Which screen calls which path | `architecture/prototype-map.json`. A\nvite plugin emits it at build time using\n`scripts/prototype-api-map.mjs`. That script follows names from a screen\nthrough hooks and helpers into `api.ts`''s members. It stops at other\ncomponents and ignores comments. | It belongs to the same build as the\nbundle. It uses the reader that `check-api-usage.mjs` now shares\n(`scripts/api-usage-lib.mjs`), so the page and the CI check agree about\nwhat the prototype calls. |\n\nThe manifest needs a signed-in caller, like other reads. It carries no\nsecrets, no tenant data, and no config value except the image reference.\nThe page renews the portal''s SSO session in the same browser. Without\none, it says \"sign in first\" and links back to the portal.\n\n## Other changes\n\n- `/api-docs/?component=<gear>` narrows Docs & API to one gear. This is\nthe target of the page''s \"Open in Docs & API\" link.\n- `check-api-usage.mjs` now imports its reader from `api-usage-lib.mjs`.\nIts output on `--list` was byte-identical before and after the refactor.\nGitHub shows the file as binary because the old version had a literal\nNUL as its wildcard; the shared lib spells it `''\\u0000''`.\n- The `Contract` CI job also runs `node --test\nscripts/prototype-api-map.test.mjs`.\n- `studio-backend/Dockerfile.src` copies `docs/design/` into the build\nstage after `cargo chef cook`, and accepts `STUDIO_BUILD_COMMIT`.\n`studio-frontend-prototype/Dockerfile.src` copies the two scripts.\n- Docs:\n- `docs/design/studio-assembly.md` (new) is indexed in `docs/README.md`.\n- `constructor-studio.md` gets the component\n`cpt-studio-component-assembly` and an endpoint row, and its\nprototype-portal entry now mentions both pages.\n  - The prototype README describes Docs & API and Architecture.\n- `studio-backend/docs/architecture/README.md` points at the live page.\n\n## Verified\n\n- **Backend gates.** I ran them in the CI image\n(`cf-studio-backend-check:1.97.0`) on a private target volume, and the\nlogs show `Compiling cf-studio-backend`. Results: `cargo fmt --check`\nOK, `cargo clippy --all-targets -D warnings` OK, `cargo test --locked`\n1334 passed. That includes 6 new `assembly::` tests and\n`api_contract::*`. `docs/api-contract.json` was regenerated from the\nbinary.\n- **Live backend.** I built with the release features\n`--no-default-features --features graph,theia-bridge` and\n`STUDIO_BUILD_COMMIT=<sha>`, and ran it on `studio-graph-postgres` with\nthe postgres profile and static tokens.\n- `GET /cf/studio-assembly/v1/manifest` without a token answers **401**.\n- With a token it answers 55 gears. That matches the 55 in the boot\nlog''s `Gear dependency order resolved (topo)` line.\n- Of those, 18 are plugins: the 12 connector drivers point at\n`studio-connector`, static/oidc authn at `authn-resolver`, both authz\nplugins at `authz-resolver`, static-credstore at `credstore`, and the\ntwo IdP plugins at null.\n- 24 Studio gears have a purpose. The `commit` matches HEAD, and the\nfeatures are `graph, theia-bridge`.\n- **Prototype.** `npx vitest run`: 37 files, 329 tests passed. `npm run\nbuild` (tsc -b + vite) passed, and `node scripts/check-api-usage.mjs`,\n`node scripts/check-docs.mjs` and `bash scripts/check-portal-nginx.sh`\nall pass. The image from `Dockerfile.src` builds. Its nginx serves\n`/architecture/` (text/html) and `/architecture/prototype-map.json`\n(application/json). In headless Chrome with no session, the page shows\nthe sign-in message.\n- **The page against the live backend.** I used headless Chrome over CDP\nwith a fresh profile and measured the real DOM:\n  - 55 gear chips in 5 layers (10/20/7/4/14).\n- Clicking `studio-tasks` shows its purpose, the design link at the\nbackend SHA, `/studio-tasks/v1` with 5 operations, 2 calling screens, 1\ndependency highlighted and 1 line drawn, and sets `#gear=studio-tasks`.\n- The Docs & API jump opens `/api-docs/?component=studio-tasks`. It\nshows only the Tasks paths, with no `/studio-presence`.\n- Dark theme: body `rgb(15,23,42)`. The deep link\n`#gear=gitlab-connector-plugin` shows \"Plugs into studio-connector\".\n- At 375px and 768px, `scrollWidth` equals `clientWidth` (no horizontal\nscroll).\n- The commit-mismatch warning appears when the map''s commit differs, and\nis absent when the commits match.\n\n## Not verified / known limits\n\n- I did not sign in through Keycloak. On the static-token stand, a\npreview proxy injected the bearer token. The SSO renewal path is the\nportal''s own `refreshSsoSession`, and I did not exercise it in this\npage.\n- I did not run the CI workflow changes (the `STUDIO_BUILD_COMMIT` lines\nand the new `node --test` step), and I did not run `cargo check\n--no-default-features` (the bootstrap seeder build). Nothing in the\nchange is feature-gated, but CI is the authority.\n- On a compose / `Dockerfile.src` build the commit shows as \"local\nbuild\". Compose does not pass `STUDIO_BUILD_COMMIT`, and that is\ndeliberate.\n- Two things are inferred from naming conventions:\n- **Plugin hosts** come from the plugin''s name. A plugin named against\nthe convention shows \"not said by its name\".\n- **Path owners** come from the path''s first segment. A path that names\nno single gear is listed as unowned rather than guessed.\n- The diagram draws lines only for the selected gear. Drawing all 100+\nedges at once was unreadable.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n* Added an Architecture page showing system components, dependencies,\nAPI coverage, and prototype screen mappings.\n  * Added build and deployment details, including commit comparisons.\n* Added API documentation filtering by component, with links to view all\ncomponents.\n* **Improvements**\n* Added an Architecture link to the product menu, matching the selected\nportal theme.\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","tree":{"sha":"1abce5d5c2a242cdfb9fdd049f707e7509604ad9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/trees/1abce5d5c2a242cdfb9fdd049f707e7509604ad9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/commits/a91139654a990bc47244a626c61fb16a22059ee7","verification":{"payload":"tree 1abce5d5c2a242cdfb9fdd049f707e7509604ad9\nparent 11ddb6f0c784ed102bfc8d4c36697c0df9fd2a69\nauthor ANDREI KUCHMA <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech> 1791378581 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791378581 +0200\n\nfeat(architecture): a page that shows how the running backend and the prototype are built (#647)\n\n## What this is for\n\nPeople keep asking \"what is actually in the backend, and how does it fi