he GTS plugin instance does not name its host\ngear. |\n| What a Studio gear is for | `build.rs` compiles in the first paragraph\nof §1.1 of each `docs/design/<gear>.md`. | It ships inside the binary,\nso the text is that commit''s design. A test fails if a design loses its\n§1.1. |\n| Backend commit | `STUDIO_BUILD_COMMIT`, compiled in by `build.rs`.\nCI''s `Build (release)` step sets it from `git rev-parse HEAD`. | It is\nfixed at compile time. A local build says `null` rather than guessing\nfrom `.git`, because an incremental build would keep a stale SHA. |\n| Session image | `studio-session`''s own config section, parsed with its\nown `StudioSessionConfig`. | It is the image that gear will actually\nstart. |\n| A gear''s REST paths and tags | `/cf/openapi.json` of the same backend.\nEach path goes to the gear named by its first segment (rule A1), or to\nthe single gear whose name starts with it (`studio-identity` →\n`studio-identity-directory`). | The gateway builds it from what each\ngear registered. Another gear cannot reach the gateway''s registry, so\nthe manifest does not repeat it. |\n| Which screen calls which path | `architecture/prototype-map.json`. A\nvite plugin emits it at build time using\n`scripts/prototype-api-map.mjs`. That script follows names from a screen\nthrough hooks and helpers into `api.ts`''s members. It stops at other\ncomponents and ignores comments. | It belongs to the same build as the\nbundle. It uses the reader that `check-api-usage.mjs` now shares\n(`scripts/api-usage-lib.mjs`), so the page and the CI check agree about\nwhat the prototype calls. |\n\nThe manifest needs a signed-in caller, like other reads. It carries no\nsecrets, no tenant data, and no config value except the image reference.\nThe page renews the portal''s SSO session in the same browser. Without\none, it says \"sign in first\" and links back to the portal.\n\n## Other changes\n\n- `/api-docs/?component=<gear>` narrows Docs & API to one gear. This is\nthe target of the page''s \"Open in Docs & API\" link.\n- `check-api-usage.mjs` now imports its reader from `api-usage-lib.mjs`.\nIts output on `--list` was byte-identical before and after the refactor.\nGitHub shows the file as binary because the old version had a literal\nNUL as its wildcard; the shared lib spells it `''\\u0000''`.\n- The `Contract` CI job also runs `node --test\nscripts/prototype-api-map.test.mjs`.\n- `studio-backend/Dockerfile.src` copies `docs/design/` into the build\nstage after `cargo chef cook`, and accepts `STUDIO_BUILD_COMMIT`.\n`studio-frontend-prototype/Dockerfile.src` copies the two scripts.\n- Docs:\n- `docs/design/studio-assembly.md` (new) is indexed in `docs/README.md`.\n- `constructor-studio.md` gets the component\n`cpt-studio-component-assembly` and an endpoint row, and its\nprototype-portal entry now mentions both pages.\n  - The prototype README describes Docs & API and Architecture.\n- `studio-backend/docs/architecture/README.md` points at the live page.\n\n## Verified\n\n- **Backend gates.** I ran them in the CI image\n(`cf-studio-backend-check:1.97.0`) on a private target volume, and the\nlogs show `Compiling cf-studio-backend`. Results: `cargo fmt --check`\nOK, `cargo clippy --all-targets -D warnings` OK, `cargo test --locked`\n1334 passed. That includes 6 new `assembly::` tests and\n`api_contract::*`. `docs/api-contract.json` was regenerated from the\nbinary.\n- **Live backend.** I built with the release features\n`--no-default-features --features graph,theia-bridge` and\n`STUDIO_BUILD_COMMIT=<sha>`, and ran it on `studio-graph-postgres` with\nthe postgres profile and static tokens.\n- `GET /cf/studio-assembly/v1/manifest` without a token answers **401**.\n- With a token it answers 55 gears. That matches the 55 in the boot\nlog''s `Gear dependency order resolved (topo)` line.\n- Of those, 18 are plugins: the 12 connector drivers point at\n`studio-connector`, static/oidc authn at `authn-resolver`, both authz\nplugins at `authz-resolver`,