 the commit shows as \"local\nbuild\". Compose does not pass `STUDIO_BUILD_COMMIT`, and that is\ndeliberate.\n- Two things are inferred from naming conventions:\n- **Plugin hosts** come from the plugin''s name. A plugin named against\nthe convention shows \"not said by its name\".\n- **Path owners** come from the path''s first segment. A path that names\nno single gear is listed as unowned rather than guessed.\n- The diagram draws lines only for the selected gear. Drawing all 100+\nedges at once was unreadable.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n* Added an Architecture page showing system components, dependencies,\nAPI coverage, and prototype screen mappings.\n  * Added build and deployment details, including commit comparisons.\n* Added API documentation filtering by component, with links to view all\ncomponents.\n* **Improvements**\n* Added an Architecture link to the product menu, matching the selected\nportal theme.\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxkSVCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA5/sQAIK/EYW107Os2c/Y+jmH+nbD\n+lXPLxl1IoW41HN9yiivpGvDSt11iR1AxyZxOrTcSpQHITr3ve/WwsLuAK2zXX77\nOpYj3LKIulTdqvtMq3J3jiROQoLe/X9qabaFEQTKQpobP2vPlKZhdmXTD2RJc0UO\nriTTIvLD8tpX7ZAcERg64kjWN8Bj7pLMSKB246OUVLSpmN8cSh5GhOepXYKfsgQJ\nMDOImBrjCrUwaqAX85Fwe0f+xTbDr0RtmQlKLZi888nDHGU1mFyyePABUThwyk7q\nPty61dnfBxrfvYhtBCctHZjaj8VglP1ou5Lirhxp5P/PETYLaB09gxRSVqTW9Nom\nGzmkSbPL8sAA6W3ZDQSEhvnmrJw1rYKIMkzpyRvRtm9J7kpOmntD97tXBasSQE3n\ndznsi7Dwk4sCRUXALU74VvLsXGXdgZU9yv5khQAXzNYYVmuZ0Mzxwwu/ajC/LYo8\noiyCH3a1IKS4+Am1uJwYDBt+u+QsDBXshoQOLf6EiXK0feCPnIJKdTEX/2gbn2tL\njco1XK6x4JBjmXtK7PP/MO5PDaHpBPmFHlxbSR0lf6pz/mBD3Svv/NkQFv9VsafS\nlRxXiZT7toy1rE0/jHUagieJ4/HUQtVNekbP+0epP7TckREVqmJWvF/ZVqwY/y9E\n1QIKtLvEGdSwINfmCwUu\n=7tcC\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T13:09:42Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/a91139654a990bc47244a626c61fb16a22059ee7","node_id":"C_kwDOTl7dJtoAKGE5MTEzOTY1NGE5OTBiYzQ3MjQ0YTYyNmM2MWZiMTZhMjIwNTllZTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/11ddb6f0c784ed102bfc8d4c36697c0df9fd2a69","sha":"11ddb6f0c784ed102bfc8d4c36697c0df9fd2a69","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/11ddb6f0c784ed102bfc8d4c36697c0df9fd2a69"}],"sha":"a91139654a990bc47244a626c61fb16a22059ee7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/a91139654a990bc47244a626c61fb16a22059ee7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/301748190?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AndrejK666","id":301748190,"login":"AndrejK666","node_id":"U_kgDOEfxP3g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/11ddb6f0c784ed102bfc8d4c36697c0df9fd2a69/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T12:50:45Z","email":"Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech","name":"ANDREI KUCHMA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T12:50:45Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Specs to gears: one gear reads a specification as written and maps it by contract, evidence and gap (#646)\n\nFrom a project''s specification to the gears that build it. This\nimplements the requirements fixed in #634:\n- `cpt-studio-fr-spec-gear-mapping`\n- `cpt-studio-fr-mapping-decisions`\n- `cpt-studio-fr-nfr-to-profile`\n\nAll of it is gathered in one new gear, **`studio-spec-mapping`**.\n\nRefs #205, #199, #206, #616.\n\n### Why\nOn Dev the Components tab of constructorfabric/insight said \"0\ncapabilities\". The project has 11 PRDs and 10 DESIGNs, but capabilities\ncame only from a `capabilities:` front-matter line, which no real spec\nhas. Only documents confirmed on the Specs tab counted, and nobody had\nconfirmed any. Matching was keywords over gear prose, so it could not\ntell a gear that provides a capability from one that mentions it.\n\n### What it does\n- **A specification is read as written. Nothing has to be added to it.**\n- Without a `capabilities:` line, capabilities are inferred from the\nFunctional Requirements, each with the requirement headings behind it.\n  - Unconfirmed (detected) documents count, marked as such.\n- **Contract first, evidence second, gap last.**\n- A *contract* is what the Gearbox engine reports a gear doing for\nothers: a `provides` contract (`<gear>/<Trait>@v<N>`), a hosted\nextension-point GTS spec, or the spec it implements. The catalogue sync\nwrites these into the profile as `gdl_contracts`.\n- The vocabulary maps a capability to contracts\n(`Capability.contracts`). The built-ins carry the platform''s\n`cf.core`/`cf.bss` points.\n- *Evidence* is the old term matching over the catalogue text, then over\nthe opening of the gear''s own PRD/DESIGN (`doc_text`, cited by link),\nalways with a quoted passage.\n  - Every evidence match ranks below every contract match.\n- **Decisions.**\n- A member confirms or rejects a candidate (✓/✗). The decision is a\n`mapping_decision` node with a `decision_on` edge.\n- It records who, when, the step, the gear version and the document\nrevision.\n- A confirmed gear ranks first within its step and a rejected one last.\n- When the gear version or the document changed, the decision is marked\n`needs_review` and ranks as undecided.\n- **Non-functional requirements choose the deployment profile, never a\ngear.**\n- Lines under NFR/operational/deployment headings are indexed and mapped\nto `dev`/`local`/`prod` (embedded/self_hosted/kubernetes).\n  - `deploy` is `nonfunctional` and offered no gear.\n- **One gear, `studio-spec-mapping`** (`src/spec_mapping/`): rules only,\nno data. It reads through ports:\n  - `documents::port::SpecNeeds`\n  - `components_catalog::port::ComponentCatalog`\n  - `artifact_ingest::port::MappingDecisionStore`\n- **One read for the Components tab:** `GET\n/studio-spec-mapping/v1/plan?project_id=`.\n\n### API\n| Removed | Now |\n|---|---|\n| `POST /studio-components-catalog/v1/compose` | `POST\n/studio-spec-mapping/v1/plan` |\n| `POST /studio-components-catalog/v1/conformance` | `POST\n/studio-spec-mapping/v1/conformance` |\n| `GET /studio-documents/v1/declared-capabilities` | `GET\n/studio-spec-mapping/v1/capabilities?project_id=` |\n| `GET /studio-documents/v1/declared-requirements` (added on this\nbranch) | `GET /studio-spec-mapping/v1/requirements?project_id=` |\n| `/studio-artifact-ingest/v1/mapping-decisions` (added on this branch)\n| `POST`/`GET /studio-spec-mapping/v1/decisions` |\n| — | `GET /studio-spec-mapping/v1/plan?project_id=` |\n\nThe only consumer of the removed routes is the prototype, which this PR\nupdates.\n\n### Also\n- Migrations in `studio_documents`:\n  - `m0012`: `contracts` on capabilities;\n- `m0013`: `requirements` on documents and bindings, `nonfunctional` on\ncapabilities;\n  - `m0014`: `inferred_capabilities` on documents and bindings.\n- Fix: editing a Studio document never wrote its re-indexed\n`capabilities` back. The upsert left the column out.\n- Docs:\n  - new `docs/design/studio-spec-mapping.md` and the gear README;\n  - the catalogue, documents and artifact-ingest designs updated;\n  - the component added to the product design;\n- the PRD says a specification is never changed for the mapping, and its\nglossary corrects \"Contract\", which is not a GTS id in `provide(...)`.\n\n### Checked\n- `cargo fmt`, `clippy -D warnings`, `cargo check\n--no-default-features`.\n- 1347 backend tests and 310 prototype tests pass, and `check-docs`\npasses.\n- **Local stand, real corpus** (gears-rust `feature/gearbox` 70a5354,\nengine ea964f9):\n  - the sync stored 55 gears, with engine facts for 47;\n  - contract matches for auth, authz, tenancy, billing and compliance;\n  - evidence quotes prose from the gear documents;\n  - on-premises statements give `local`;\n- decisions rank candidates, and a changed document marks a decision for\nreview;\n- after the move into the gear, it initialises, its routes answer\nthrough the ports, and the old routes are gone.\n- **Insight''s 11 real PRDs** (copied from the Dev checkout): every one\ninfers capabilities with the requirements behind them. There is noise\nfrom broad vocabulary terms (\"source\", \"connector\"); fix it in the\nvocabulary or with ✓/✗.\n\nNot checked: a full `GET /plan?project_id=` on a stand with a real\nproject and synced documents.\n\n### After merge\n1. Deploy the **backend and the prototype together**, because the old\nroutes are gone.\n2. **Re-sync** the Insight repository. The inferred capabilities are\ncomputed when a document is synced.\n\n### Not in this PR\n- Decisions shared across an organization: they are per project now.\n- `config` in `product.gdl` from requirements: only the profile is\nchosen.\n- A gearbox issue: the engine silently drops a `#[toolkit::provides]`\nwhose trait has no `#[toolkit::contract]` (bss-products''\n`ProductCatalogClientV1`).\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n* Added project-level specification-to-component plans, with suggestions\nranked by contract matches and supporting evidence.\n* Review and confirm or reject suggested mappings; see when saved\ndecisions may need review.\n* View capability sources, inferred capabilities, non-functional\nrequirements, and suggested deployment profiles.\n* Define contract identifiers and mark capabilities as non-functional in\nthe capability catalog.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","tree":{"sha":"b706eb4234a6a9edcf3ed388a0fb16576936e4c9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/trees/b706eb4234a6a9edcf3ed388a0fb16576936e4c9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/commits/11ddb6f0c784ed102bfc8d4c36697c0df9fd2a69","verification":{"payload":"tree b706eb4234a6a9edcf3ed388a0fb16576936e4c9\nparent f0d8e19fafa27b80ee69258ddbc661bde4e00008\nauthor A