s or rejects a candidate (✓/✗). The decision is a\n`mapping_decision` node with a `decision_on` edge.\n- It records who, when, the step, the gear version and the document\nrevision.\n- A confirmed gear ranks first within its step and a rejected one last.\n- When the gear version or the document changed, the decision is marked\n`needs_review` and ranks as undecided.\n- **Non-functional requirements choose the deployment profile, never a\ngear.**\n- Lines under NFR/operational/deployment headings are indexed and mapped\nto `dev`/`local`/`prod` (embedded/self_hosted/kubernetes).\n  - `deploy` is `nonfunctional` and offered no gear.\n- **One gear, `studio-spec-mapping`** (`src/spec_mapping/`): rules only,\nno data. It reads through ports:\n  - `documents::port::SpecNeeds`\n  - `components_catalog::port::ComponentCatalog`\n  - `artifact_ingest::port::MappingDecisionStore`\n- **One read for the Components tab:** `GET\n/studio-spec-mapping/v1/plan?project_id=`.\n\n### API\n| Removed | Now |\n|---|---|\n| `POST /studio-components-catalog/v1/compose` | `POST\n/studio-spec-mapping/v1/plan` |\n| `POST /studio-components-catalog/v1/conformance` | `POST\n/studio-spec-mapping/v1/conformance` |\n| `GET /studio-documents/v1/declared-capabilities` | `GET\n/studio-spec-mapping/v1/capabilities?project_id=` |\n| `GET /studio-documents/v1/declared-requirements` (added on this\nbranch) | `GET /studio-spec-mapping/v1/requirements?project_id=` |\n| `/studio-artifact-ingest/v1/mapping-decisions` (added on this branch)\n| `POST`/`GET /studio-spec-mapping/v1/decisions` |\n| — | `GET /studio-spec-mapping/v1/plan?project_id=` |\n\nThe only consumer of the removed routes is the prototype, which this PR\nupdates.\n\n### Also\n- Migrations in `studio_documents`:\n  - `m0012`: `contracts` on capabilities;\n- `m0013`: `requirements` on documents and bindings, `nonfunctional` on\ncapabilities;\n  - `m0014`: `inferred_capabilities` on documents and bindings.\n- Fix: editing a Studio document never wrote its re-indexed\n`capabilities` back. The upsert left the column out.\n- Docs:\n  - new `docs/design/studio-spec-mapping.md` and the gear README;\n  - the catalogue, documents and artifact-ingest designs updated;\n  - the component added to the product design;\n- the PRD says a specification is never changed for the mapping, and its\nglossary corrects \"Contract\", which is not a GTS id in `provide(...)`.\n\n### Checked\n- `cargo fmt`, `clippy -D warnings`, `cargo check\n--no-default-features`.\n- 1347 backend tests and 310 prototype tests pass, and `check-docs`\npasses.\n- **Local stand, real corpus** (gears-rust `feature/gearbox` 70a5354,\nengine ea964f9):\n  - the sync stored 55 gears, with engine facts for 47;\n  - contract matches for auth, authz, tenancy, billing and compliance;\n  - evidence quotes prose from the gear documents;\n  - on-premises statements give `local`;\n- decisions rank candidates, and a changed document marks a decision for\nreview;\n- after the move into the gear, it initialises, its routes answer\nthrough the ports, and the old routes are gone.\n- **Insight''s 11 real PRDs** (copied from the Dev checkout): every one\ninfers capabilities with the requirements behind them. There is noise\nfrom broad vocabulary terms (\"source\", \"connector\"); fix it in the\nvocabulary or with ✓/✗.\n\nNot checked: a full `GET /plan?project_id=` on a stand with a real\nproject and synced documents.\n\n### After merge\n1. Deploy the **backend and the prototype together**, because the old\nroutes are gone.\n2. **Re-sync** the Insight repository. The inferred capabilities are\ncomputed when a document is synced.\n\n### Not in this PR\n- Decisions shared across an organization: they are per project now.\n- `config` in `product.gdl` from requirements: only the profile is\nchosen.\n- A gearbox issue: the engine silently drops a `#[toolkit::provides]`\nwhose trait has no `#[toolkit::contract]` (bss-products''\n`ProductCatalogClientV1`).\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n* Added project-level specification-to-component plans, with suggestions\nranked by contract matches and supporting evidence.\n* Review and confirm or reject suggested mappings; see when saved\ndecisions may need review.\n* View capability sources, inferred capabilities, non-functional\nrequirements, and suggested deployment profiles.\n* Define contract identifiers and mark capabilities as non-functional in\nthe capability catalog.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxkAlCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAUrsQAAh9sqpTBmstwJju8Bp/OYnh\n3nhmL9HKNMwuh0yK88V9WMre0Yo2vkbQIiApfvqhp8ea8PYoV4BktTbhcSd0NwTD\nkT0n82viuNPc07l+k/u/F1cLlDNc7RuPj4vaMGOZw82pIIXUI1qmaIucldlqC77T\nChNwCj+wo3F5OIAIaYPlGAnZLbwj1C6XbCigMn+jI/I5Ia9qA0JC0iY7zcmwuP9q\n2F6Xu95fA0/njtCtXpFj7CSTMwDCDX1kj7VQY84shDlIQOP/NeZ1J61eXXVimrSM\n/BkSFzIaD0Uz3Kw8VM7xcEWqxoTWTeATAqFgdRtRC4VCp+r39dstsNOJ6LBFNgzC\npWSvqos4C0Jsbf6ijFBEWWSQ5BL2RmzIf262kfw4Xgt4jQYbs9DoLEpx3FJY4jvK\noi3NCisdXCrzpf1yNGEYle3RTxGzNCkgl2u+A7BtvMF7sDCPTEVepij8h6Ed1S3E\nrloqeJkL5EAAv+Yz+Rx05wEyJmp5rrLborjA15OsN6aTKz8urKYLXo8AqA7gzt6S\n+J89MDugutbq/rNX5PDtNENti4wRFN/PA5oBlG0brw8p/R0bKgNEFn84U0DtEZKJ\nSW/c+Az2r1/SpW9+oZkgT2336VQ2AeN8NMxryqYf/ZzA6D7TIeNpkBhvi/ueIn2E\n/FxhajK/fveBo2QSGCZj\n=Nya1\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T12:50:46Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/11ddb6f0c784ed102bfc8d4c36697c0df9fd2a69","node_id":"C_kwDOTl7dJtoAKDExZGRiNmYwYzc4NGVkMTAyYmZjOGQ0YzM2Njk3YzBkZjlmZDJhNjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/f0d8e19fafa27b80ee69258ddbc661bde4e00008","sha":"f0d8e19fafa27b80ee69258ddbc661bde4e00008","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/f0d8e19fafa27b80ee69258ddbc661bde4e00008"}],"sha":"11ddb6f0c784ed102bfc8d4c36697c0df9fd2a69","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/11ddb6f0c784ed102bfc8d4c36697c0df9fd2a69"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/301748190?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AndrejK666","id":301748190,"login":"AndrejK666","node_id":"U_kgDOEfxP3g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/f0d8e19fafa27b80ee69258ddbc661bde4e00008/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T12:27:49Z","email":"Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech","name":"ANDREI KUCHMA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T12:27:49Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Add Custom Agent Navigation Rules, Constructor Studio Kit: SDLC (`sdlc`), ADR (Architecture Decision Record) Expert Checklist and 42 more (#644)\n\nShared from Constructor Studio.\n\n- Custom Agent Navigation Rules (`.cf-studio/config/AGENTS.md`)\n- Constructor Studio Kit: SDLC (`sdlc`)\n(`.cf-studio/config/kits/sdlc/AGENTS.md`)\n- ADR (Architecture Decision Record) Expert Checklist\n(`.cf-studio/config/kits/sdlc/artifacts/ADR/checklist.md`)\n- ADR-0001: Use PostgreSQL for Task Storage\n(`.cf-studio/config/kits/sdlc/artifacts/ADR/examples/example.md`)\n- ADR Rules (`.cf-studio/config/kits/sdlc/artifacts/ADR/rules.md`)\n- {Short title describing problem and chosen solution}\n(`.cf-studio/config/kits/sdlc/artifacts/ADR/template.md`)\n- DECOMPOSITION Expert Checklist\n(`.cf-studio/config/kits/sdlc/artifacts/DECOMPOSITION/checklist.md`)\n- Decomposition: TaskFlow\n(`.cf-studio/config/kits/sdlc/artifacts/DECOMPOSITION/examples/example.md`)\n- DECOMPOSITION Rules\n(`.cf-studio/config/kits/sdlc/artifacts/DECOMPOSITION/rules.md`)\n- Decomposition: {PROJECT_NAME}\n(`.cf-studio/config/kits/sdlc/artifacts/DECOMPOSITION/template.md`)\n- DESIGN (Overall Design) Expert Checklist\n(`.cf-studio/config/kits/sdlc/artifacts/DESIGN/checklist.md`)\n- Technical Design: TaskFlow\n(`.cf-studio/config/kits/sdlc/artifacts/DESIGN/examples/example.md`)\n- DESIGN Rules (`.cf-studio/config/kits/sdlc/artifacts/DESIGN/rules.md`)\n- Technical Design — {Module Name}\n(`.cf-studio/config/kits/