tps://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AndrejK666","id":301748190,"login":"AndrejK666","node_id":"U_kgDOEfxP3g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/9203ad1bf23185cf2c4b4d96724063b65c82514a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T10:14:07Z","email":"Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech","name":"ANDREI KUCHMA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T10:14:07Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(domain-model): a query over the domain model, its authorization, and saved views (#641)\n\nThe domain model gets an API a screen can be built on, the authorization\nreal data needs, and a first feature that is a screen stored as data.\n\nReplaces the closed #637, #638 and #639: one branch, one PR.\n\n## What is in it\n\n**A query over domain objects:** `POST /studio-domain-model/v1/query`,\nexperimental.\n- One request reads a type''s objects with a Hasura-style `where`:\n  - operators `_eq _neq _gt _gte _lt _lte _in _nin _contains _is_null`;\n  - combinators `_and _or _not`.\n- It also takes `order_by`, `fields`, `offset`/`limit`, and `include`:\ndeclared relations, nested up to 3 levels.\n- Everything named is checked against the model. A wrong field or\nrelation is a 400 that lists what the type has.\n- Each relation level costs one typed graph-storage traversal for all\nparent rows together (`DomainStore::neighbours`).\n- Known limits, which the answer reports itself:\n- filtering runs in the gear over at most 5,000 objects, with `complete:\nfalse` past that;\n  - relations are followed from their declaring side only;\n  - relations that share an edge type come back with `warnings`.\n\n**A typed client generated from the model.**\n- `scripts/gen-domain-client.mjs` writes\n`studio-frontend-prototype/src/domain-model.gen.ts`:\n  - 140 entity interfaces, inherited fields included;\n  - per entity, the relations `include` accepts;\n  - the same field and relation maps at runtime.\n- `domain-query.ts` and `api.queryDomain` sit on top, so a wrong field\nor relation is a compile error.\n- CI runs the generator with `--check`.\n\n**Authorization:** ADR-0035, accepted.\n- New privileges: `domain.view`, `domain.edit`, `domain.model`.\n- The seeded ladder gives editor `view` and `edit`, admin all three,\nviewer `view`.\n- Objects are a row question for the PDP.\n- The gear is a PEP for `gts.cf.studio.domain.object.v1~`, with tenant\nhierarchy declared.\n- Constraints are evaluated per object: at the root, at every `include`\nlevel, and before `total`.\n  - Relating needs write on the source and read on the target.\n  - A refusal is 403, a PDP outage 503.\n- The model is administration. Field edits, import, sync and revert need\n`domain.model` through studio-user''s new `OrgAuthority`.\n- `GET /types` returns `can_edit_model`, and the prototype hides the\ncontrols when it is false.\n- PDP changes:\n  - `privilege_for` maps its first resource;\n- the role path''s access-config read is cached (10 s, plus a generation\nmoved by every allowed config write);\n  - the tripwire test is replaced, per ADR-0019 §8.\n- `project_id` on `POST /objects` and `/query`: a tenant id, so project\ngrants reach objects. `scope` stays as an alias.\n\n**Saved views:** the first feature built on the model.\n- The new **Views** section in the prototype. A view is a `view` object:\nits `query` is the `/query` body, and its `presentation` is what the\neditor reopens.\n- Pick a type, columns, conditions, related objects and an order.\n- The table is paged, sorted and searched by the backend.\n- Retiring sets `valid_to` rather than deleting a graph key.\n- **No backend change was needed for it.**\n\n**Graph views and the legacy-scope report.**\n- A view can be drawn as a graph (`view_kind: \"graph\"`): the same stored\nquery, with its included relations as edges, on the canvas the model\ngraph uses. That makes the Knowledge Graph surface a saved view as well.\n- `GET /objects/legacy-scopes` lists objects whose scope names no\nproject, so no project grant reaches them. It is also a **Check scopes**\nbutton on the System page.\n- `GET /types/{id}/conformance` read payloads with no read check and\nreturned samples of them. It now reads only what the caller may read.\n\n**Docs.**\n- `docs/domain-query-migration.md`: the plan. Steps 0–3 and 6 are done;\n4, 5 and 7 wait on gears-rust.\n- ADR-0035.\n- The gear design gains the query and access components.\n- `docs/upstream/graph-storage-requests.md` is re-checked against 0.1.4.\nThe new asks are filed as gears-rust#5239, #5240 and #5241, plus a\ncomment on #5021.\n\n## Behaviour changes\n\n- **Changing the domain model** (field edits, import, sync, revert) now\nneeds the organization''s owner or a platform administrator on the\n`tenant` model, or `domain.model` on the roles model. Until now any\nmember could.\n- **`GET /studio-domain-model/v1/objects`** is deprecated, with removal\nafter 2026-12-01. No portal calls it; `/query` covers it.\n- **Organizations already on the roles model** (none today) do not gain\nthe three privileges in their stored roles until they add them. Owners\nhold them by definition.\n\n## Verified\n\n- Backend:\n- `fmt`, `clippy -D warnings`, `build`, `check --features theia-bridge`\nand `check --no-default-features` are clean;\n  - `cargo test`: 1323/1323, on the branch merged with current `main`.\n- Prototype:\n  - `tsc -b` and `vite build` are clean;\n  - `vitest` 305/305.\n- Repository checks: `check-docs`, `check-api-usage`, `gen-domain-client\n--check`.\n- Stand with real graph-storage and the Studio PDP:\n- ADR-0035 matrix on a `roles` organization with two projects and five\nusers: every case as specified;\n- on the `tenant` model a member reads but cannot edit the model, and a\nplatform admin can;\n- Views: save, list, run with relations, search and retire through the\nscreen''s own code;\n- a graph view rendered (4 objects, 3 relations, two buckets), and the\nlegacy report found exactly the one free-form-scoped object;\n  - the screen rendered in headless Chrome against the stand.\n\n## After merge\n\nA merge to `main` builds images but does not deploy. Dispatch \"Deploy\nexisting images\" for **backend** and **prototype** with the merge''s\n`sha-…`.\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","tree":{"sha":"2b865b70a7d9ecdfe8d36da18288a4f780e3d2a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/trees/2b865b70a7d9ecdfe8d36da18288a4f780e3d2a2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/commits/9203ad1bf23185cf2c4b4d96724063b65c82514a","verification":{"payload":"tree 2b865b70a7d9ecdfe8d36da18288a4f780e3d2a2\nparent b695b5e89afe49ea7e8f60a64be445a0ee3bbf11\nauthor ANDREI KUCHMA <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech> 1791368047 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791368047 +0200\n\nfeat(domain-model): a query over the domain model, its authorization, and saved views (#641)\n\nThe domain model gets an API a screen can be built on, the authorization\nreal data needs, and a first feature that is a screen stored as data.\n\nReplaces the closed #637, #638 and #639: one branch, one PR.\n\n## What is in it\n\n**A query over domain objects:** `POST /studio-domain-model/v1/query`,\nexperimental.\n- One request reads a type''s objects with a Hasura-style `where`:\n  - operators `_eq _neq _gt _gte _lt _lte _in _nin _contains _is_null`;\n  - combinators `_and _or _not`.\n- It also takes `order_by`, `fields`, `offset`/`limit`, and `include`:\ndeclared relations, nested up to 3 levels.\n- Everything named is checked against the model. A wrong field or\nrelation is a 400 that lists what the type has.\n- Each relation level costs one typed graph-storage traversal for all\nparent rows together (`DomainStore::neighbours`).\n- Known limits, which the answer reports itself:\n- filtering runs in the gear over at most 5,000 objects, with `complete:\nfalse` past that;\n  - relations are followed from their declaring side only;\n  - relations that share an edge type come back with `warnings`.\n\n**A typed client generated from the model.**\n- `scripts/gen-domain-client.mjs` writes\n`studio-frontend-prototype/src/domain-model.gen.ts`:\n  - 140 entity interfaces, inherited fields included;\n  - per entity, the relations `include` accepts;\n  - the same field and relation maps at runtime.\n- `domain-query.ts` and `api.queryDomain` sit on top, so a wrong field\nor relation is a compile error.\n- CI runs the generator with `--check`.\n\n**Authorization:** ADR-0035, accepted.\n- New privileges: `domain.view`, `domain.edit`, `domain.model`.\n- The seeded ladder gives editor `view` and `edit`, admin all three,\nviewer `view`.\n- Objects are a row question for the PDP.\n- The gear is a PEP for `gts.cf.studio.domain.object.v1~`, with tenant\nhierarchy declared.\n- Constraints are evaluated per object: at the root, at every `include`\nlevel, and before `total`.\n  - Relating needs write on the source and read on the target.\n  - A refusal is 403, a PDP outage 503.\n- The model is administration. Field edits, import, sync and revert need\n`domain.model` through studio-user''s new `OrgAuthority`.\n- `GET /types` returns `can_edit_model`, and the prototype hides the\ncontrols when it is false.\n- PDP changes:\n  - `privilege_for` maps its first resource;\n- the role path''s access-config read is cached (10 s, plus a generation\nmoved by every allowed config write);\n  - the tripwire test is replaced, per ADR-0019 §8.\n- `project_id` on `POST /objects` and `/query`: a tenant id, so project\ngrants reach objects. `scope` stays as an alias.\n\n**Saved views:** the first feature built on the model.\n- The new **Views** section in the prototype. A view is a `view` object:\nits `query` is the `/query` body, and its `presentation` is what the\neditor reopens.\n- Pick a type, columns, conditions, related objects and an order.\n- The table is paged, sorted and searched by the backend.\n- Retiring sets `valid_to` rather than deleting a graph key.\n- **No backend change was needed for it.**\n\n**Graph views and the legacy-scope report.**\n- A view can be drawn as a graph (`view_kind: \"graph\"`): the same stored\nquery, with its included relations as edges, on the canvas the model\ngraph uses. That makes the Knowledge Graph surface a saved view as well.\n- `GET /objects/legacy-scopes` lists objects whose scope names no\nproject, so no project grant reaches them. It is also a **Check scopes**\nbutton on the System page.\n- `GET /types/{id}/conformance` read payloads with no read check and\nreturned samples of them. It now reads only what the caller may read.\n\n**Docs.**\n- `docs/domain-query-migration.md`: the plan. Steps 0–3 and 6 are done;\n4, 5 and 7 wait on gears-rust.\n- ADR-0035.\n- The gear design gains the query and access components.\n- `docs/upstream/graph-storage-requests.md` is re-checked against 0.1.4.\nThe new asks are filed as gears-rust#5239, #5240 and #5241, plus a\ncomment on #5021.\n\n## Behaviour changes\n\n- **Changing the domain model** (field edits, import, sync, revert) now\nneeds the organization''s owner or a platform administrator on the\n`tenant` model, or `domain.model` on the roles model. Until now any\nmember could.\n- **`GET /studio-domain-model/v1/objects`** is deprecated, with removal\nafter 2026-12-01. No portal calls it; `/query` covers it.\n- **Organizations already on the roles model** (none today) do not gain\nthe three privileges in their stored roles until they add them. Owners\nhold them by definition.\n\n## Verified\n\n- Backend:\n- `fmt`, `clippy -D warnings`, `build`, `check --features theia-bridge`\nand `check --no-default-features` are clean;\n  - `cargo test`: 1323/1323, on the branch merged with current `main`.\n- Prototype:\n  - `tsc -b` and `vite build` are clean;\n  - `vitest` 305/305.\n- Repository checks: `check-docs`, `check-api-usage`, `gen-domain-client\n--check`.\n- Stand with real graph-storage and the Studio PDP:\n- ADR-0035 matrix on a `roles` organization with two projects and five\nusers: every case as specified;\n- on the `tenant` model a member reads but cannot edit the model, and a\nplatform admin can;\n- Views: save, list, run with relations, search and retire through the\nscreen''s own code;\n- a graph view rendered (4 objects, 3 relations, two buckets), and the\nlegacy report found exactly the one free-form-scoped object;\n  - the screen rendered in headless Chrome against the stand.\n\n## After merge\n\nA merge to `main` builds images but does not deploy. Dispatch \"Deploy\nexisting images\" for **backend** and **prototype** with the merge''s\n`sha-…`.\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxhtvCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAUbIQAHSYHEdEGZGV+NbwipMPSydS\nah+C3Ckahk9xCcRFrUv1ccUc7+E1a9nWPaQmrdnUqB+QbrxuR7osoCvklllOkLd2\n9/2N2baT1bj2O7e/aFVYlpL+BfXCdLqAKt7s2T6a8ubfkWvwgUajnpPJfoii4J0N\naHXgntpRZxGO6/ShFDA/raK1IYo7UIpWRQkT8vVlueHfEO7rfVka172Vt6qWxmLv\nynLBti/ZQ60vE4XxDe/JIdVyNPR5Aem4mRkivzwBYWHcxW0tC02WGJHijPa1Hyyt\ngMiC/Qpgoq7ciATMI/VGPRsNbcwntgjzbV4aYhRLLAWHuojfxs2jpkDj6nqYJz5x\nlaVIBGdLdNk7bpHju7f5TDBhG+5ZN6KPOwLaLOpL/Ep468lhSKruAdvkGpVN5oG/\n01uxACku5laRA4V0Fba1SC1WQQKYuf4QQsneFlzKahJq8FJ++nHD0BSfoKWiF8z8\n1hctOD3m2vIxLuD/Xt0JA8x9bIMmqv3CEs1/fmMP+piGJWwgLWUDpziP6AnP4yL+\np0Gc9+gEq6h7QS0SLcQejs2ISmOATBSR9ixvdMPkxEHb0HtJTUYtUe0K7usvfY+/\nwOXuYeggJAyYpWO/NSmu8c1U7c8TCu7ren3rnUeCa1rF48Qv835MEpL3CQobbS7W\n6nX4dmfV4NSWlfgFMkKv\n=MRq5\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T10:14:08Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/9203ad1bf23185cf2c4b4d96724063b65c82514a","node_id":"C_kwDOTl7dJtoAKDkyMDNhZDFiZjIzMTg1Y2YyYzRiNGQ5NjcyNDA2M2I2NWM4MjUxNGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/b695b5e89afe49ea7e8f60a64be445a0ee3bbf11","sha":"b695b5e89afe49ea7e8f60a64be445a0ee3bbf11","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/b695b5e89afe49ea7e8f60a64be445a0ee3bbf11"}],"sha":"9203ad1bf23185cf2c4b4d96724063b65c82514a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/9203ad1bf23185cf2c4b4d96724063b65c82514a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/301748190?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AndrejK666","id":301748190,"login":"AndrejK666","node_id":"U_kgDOEfxP3g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/b695b5e89afe49ea7e8f60a64be445a0ee3bbf11/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T10:11:43Z","email":"Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech","name":"ANDREI KUCHMA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T10:11:43Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(reports, catalog): reports and the components catalogue work in the organization on screen, and an unread board is said (#642)\n\n## What happened on Dev\n\nThe roadmap report showed **0 gears** with no error. The source was set\nup on the Reports screen with connection \"1111\" (`ddff5557`). That\nconnection is one of the organization''s (Constructor Fabric `c31da936`),\nand the screen lists connections from the selected organization. But\nevery `studio-reports` route, like every `studio-components-catalog`\nroute, keys on the caller''s **home tenant**. For a platform\nadministrator that is the platform root, so:\n\n- the source was saved on the root, and `reports.refresh` /\n`catalog.sync` ran in tenant `00000000-…-0001`;\n- the catalogue looked for the connection in the root and logged\n`components-catalog: roadmap board unreadable error=connection ddff5557…\nnot found` as a WARN;\n- the sync **succeeded** (`gears: 0, stored: 54`), and the refresh\nrecorded `error: null`.\n\n## The fix\n\n**1. The organization is named, not assumed (`src/org_scope.rs`).**\n`OrgCtx` is one extractor for `?organization_id=`:\n- When the parameter is absent, it gives the caller''s own context,\nexactly as before.\n- When it is present, the caller must reach that organization. This is\nchecked by resolving the tenant under the caller''s own context, the\nguard documents, kits and sessions already use\n(`studio_session::access::TenantMembership`); a refusal answers 404. The\nhandler then gets the same caller (subject, scopes, token) acting in\nthat tenant.\n\nThe reports routes (9) and the catalogue''s context-taking routes (24)\ntake it and declare the parameter. Scheduled report runs already named\ntheir organization (#607); manual refreshes and catalogue syncs now\nqueue in it too.\n\n**2. An unread board is said, not swallowed.**\n- `refresh` checks that the board''s connection resolves before it queues\nthe sync (`PlanReader::connection`). The Dev case now fails right there,\nand the reason lands on `last_refresh.error`.\n- `catalog.sync` stays best-effort, because a board is one source of\nmany. Its result now carries `boards_unread: [{board, error}]`.\n- The report source answers `board_error`, read from its last sync run,\nfor failures only that run can see.\n\n**Prototype:**\n- `request()` adds the organization on screen (`orgAsSpace.id`, set by\nApp during render so the first fetch already has it) to every catalogue\nand reports call.\n- Runs are polled with `?tenant=`.\n- Refresh waits for the board sync before it redraws, and `board_error`\nis shown as an alert.\n\n## Checks\n- `cargo fmt --check`, `cargo clippy --all-targets -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo test` for `reports::`, `components_catalog::`, `org_scope` and\n`api_contract`: 360 passed. That includes the Dev case\n(`a_connection_this_tenant_does_not_hold_fails_the_refresh_before_any_sync`),\nthe org guard, `acting_in` and `board_error_of`.\n- `docs/api-contract.json` regenerated: `list_reports` gains a 404.\n`scripts/check-api-usage.mjs`: OK.\n- Prototype: `tsc -b` clean, vitest 296/296 (new cases for `orgScoped`,\nthe request it sends, and `board-unread`).\n- Not verified on a running stand.\n\n## Unchanged\nCallers that name no organization (Theia, desktop, scripts) get exactly\nwhat they got before. So does a member, whose home *is* the\norganization.\n\n## After deploy\nThe source saved during the Dev attempt lives on the platform root. Open\nReports in Constructor Fabric, set the source there once and refresh. A\nplatform administrator''s Components page now shows the organization''s\ncatalogue; if that organization was never synced, run a sync there.\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","tree":{"sha":"b1e97f77c223c5f4a4b94ea469d5f4083b3c9152","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/trees/b1e97f77c223c5f4a4b94ea469d5f4083b3c9152"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/commits/b695b5e89afe49ea7e8f60a64be445a0ee3bbf11","verification":{"payload":"tree b1e97f77c223c5f4a4b94ea469d5f4083b3c9152\nparent eb77caa2206d464b3e8957b6604d144fdc7bcb97\nauthor ANDREI KUCHMA <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech> 1791367903 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791367903 +0200\n\nfix(reports, catalog): reports and the components catalogue work in the organization on screen, and an unread board is said (#642)\n\n## What happened on Dev\n\nThe roadmap report showed **0 gears** with no error. The source was set\nup on the Reports screen with connection \"1111\" (`ddff5557`). That\nconnection is one of the organization''s (Constructor Fabric `c31da936`),\nand the screen lists connections from the selected organization. But\nevery `studio-reports` route, like every `studio-components-catalog`\nroute, keys on the caller''s **home tenant**. For a platform\nadministrator that is the platform root, so:\n\n- the source was saved on the root, and `reports.refresh` /\n`catalog.sync` ran in tenant `00000000-…-0001`;\n- the catalogue looked for the connection in the root and logged\n`components-catalog: roadmap board unreadable error=connection ddff5557…\nnot found` as a WARN;\n- the sync **succeeded** (`gears: 0, stored: 54`), and the refresh\nrecorded `error: null`.\n\n## The fix\n\n**1. The organization is named, not assumed (`src/org_scope.rs`).**\n`OrgCtx` is one extractor for `?organization_id=`:\n- When the parameter is absent, it gives the caller''s own context,\nexactly as before.\n- When it is present, the caller must reach that organization. This is\nchecked by resolving the tenant under the caller''s own context, the\nguard documents, kits and sessions already use\n(`studio_session::access::TenantMembership`); a refusal answers 404. The\nhandler then gets the same caller (subject, scopes, token) acting in\nthat tenant.\n\nThe reports routes (9) and the catalogue''s context-taking routes (24)\ntake it and declare the parameter. Scheduled report runs already named\ntheir organization (#607); manual refreshes and catalogue syncs now\nqueue in it too.\n\n**2. An unread board is said, not swallowed.**\n- `refresh` checks that the board''s connection resolves before it queues\nthe sync (`PlanReader::connection`). The Dev case now fails right there,\nand the reason lands on `last_refresh.error`.\n- `catalog.sync` stays best-effort, because a board is one source of\nmany. Its result now carries `boards_unread: [{board, error}]`.\n- The report source answers `board_error`, read from its last sync run,\nfor failures only that run can see.\n\n**Prototype:**\n- `request()` adds the organization on screen (`orgAsSpace.id`, set by\nApp during render so the first fetch already has it) to every catalogue\nand reports call.\n- Runs are polled with `?tenant=`.\n- Refresh waits for the board sync before it redraws, and `board_error`\nis shown as an alert.\n\n## Checks\n- `cargo fmt --check`, `cargo clippy --all-targets -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo test` for `reports::`, `components_catalog::`, `org_scope` and\n`api_contract`: 360 passed. That includes the Dev case\n(`a_connection_this_tenant_does_not_hold_fails_the_refresh_before_any_sync`),\nthe org guard, `acting_in` and `board_error_of`.\n- `docs/api-contract.json` regenerated: `list_reports` gains a 404.\n`scripts/check-api-usage.mjs`: OK.\n- Prototype: `tsc -b` clean, vitest 296/296 (new cases for `orgScoped`,\nthe request it sends, and `board-unread`).\n- Not verified on a running stand.\n\n## Unchanged\nCallers that name no organization (Theia, desktop, scripts) get exactly\nwhat they got before. So does a member, whose home *is* the\norganization.\n\n## After deploy\nThe source saved during the Dev attempt lives on the platform root. Open\nReports in Constructor Fabric, set the source there once and refresh. A\nplatform administrator''s Components page now shows the organization''s\ncatalogue; if that organization was never synced, run a sync there.\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxhrfCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA7YQQAJV0LCsHcveu9VpSwqHr6rOa\noAWhxOZ+WYux00OKpQEL/6OpySowDOwBbEUss0vC342D9q3mDUTEQYXZp26sVZLi\nHERoKKMCjshCFWY9CAIsUEhL98v/nVc3Da1aYKMr/hZoOPe1ZnyeeMI3X2tHhbBQ\nrdpeFOCiBGQk0lq7EwHKP3ChPyWV6HcI1ZRmAoTxqEuP8EtQXdOL/aHi9ONzKXxC\nN1LTIkbW5kDCZmsM0uGKzrU6ltXNSWh3sMkse5/0ajF1qxa3KG23jUGiR9bk2Nq/\ntBbEtAXABuCaYb/pgh3SGt7YYEwnk1chwaNhg5xWlivGYqrxg+axRAZMaZVD0lvt\nVfbm0H0hN17e18blaOQDUTFThRkbmYB4h2HCCfPBgIs+T5UfDvyQ/HVsroq9doOv\nmth7qO9Nc69ekiHAB9a9SyjxShcx0GnT70fqeFCypzSbNcw0zhLlDanJzhTaNwaS\nM5BcLFH3pYfUkU4Mk6QxDtbNdN+zGm7aGcUdZIvDbt4jtlTn3VnGvlYDcdQDGPDW\n4/6sVVSfeMBM0J5ZM8OB/aaz4iYjW3cVW48vLgri8KlelrE1vS2FSw5mye4zYgl/\noUuZMZyLIEPEBgHi+zfgqwRqpRQ4e2cK3KgG3OBplH4YzSJ9j6FEPkofLbau2DTy\n4nflYC/6uXe3kcQK3tGd\n=VoT7\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T10:11:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/b695b5e89afe49ea7e8f60a64be445a0ee3bbf11","node_id":"C_kwDOTl7dJtoAKGI2OTViNWU4OWFmZTQ5ZWE3ZThmNjBhNjRiZTQ0NWEwZWUzYmJmMTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/eb77caa2206d464b3e8957b6604d144fdc7bcb97","sha":"eb77caa2206d464b3e8957b6604d144fdc7bcb97","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/eb77caa2206d464b3e8957b6604d144fdc7bcb97"}],"sha":"b695b5e89afe49ea7e8f60a64be445a0ee3bbf11","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/b695b5e89afe49ea7e8f60a64be445a0ee3bbf11"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/301748190?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AndrejK666","id":301748190,"login":"AndrejK666","node_id":"U_kgDOEfxP3g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/eb77caa2206d464b3e8957b6604d144fdc7bcb97/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T10:10:33Z","email":"Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech","name":"ANDREI KUCHMA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T10:10:33Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(share): send what was committed in Source Control, and show Share there with a count (#640)\n\n## What broke\n\nOn studio-web (`share_mode = pull_request`, and `main` protected by a\nruleset), a member edited a document, committed it in the stock Source\nControl panel (one commit had an empty message), and pressed **Sync\nChanges**. GitHub refused the push (`GH013 … Changes must be made\nthrough a pull request`), and the checkout was left two commits ahead of\n`origin/main`. Then the member opened **Share with the team**. The\ndialog said *A change you shared earlier has not reached the team yet*,\nbut **Send for review** was disabled. In review mode, Share proposed\nonly files that were not committed, so committed changes could never\nreach the team.\n\n## What changed\n\n**1. Share sends what was committed and not sent**\n(`document-share-service.ts`, `share-dialog.tsx`, `share-model.ts`)\n- `describe()` now also lists the documents changed by commits that are\nnot sent yet. These are the files in `@{upstream}...HEAD`, kept only\nwhile they still differ from `@{upstream}`, so something the team\nalready took another way (a squash merge) is not offered again. They\ncome with their `.studio` companions and are flagged `committed`. The\ndialog shows them as *committed here, not sent yet*, ticked when they\nare the person''s.\n- When the project takes changes by review, those files go to the\nperson''s pull request through the existing `propose()`/`commitOnto()`.\nThat builds one commit from the files as they are on disk in a scratch\nindex, so a document committed and then edited again is sent as it is\nnow. The commit message is the sentence typed in the dialog, so an empty\nSCM commit message does not matter. **The checkout''s commits and HEAD\nstay where they are**, which is important in a shared portal checkout.\n- After sending, the existing `markInReview` reads them as *In your pull\nrequest*, and they drop out of the count.\n- *See changes* compares with the team''s version when there are commits\nthat are not sent.\n- When the project commits straight to the branch, behaviour is\nunchanged. Committed documents are not listed for choosing, because the\nnext share pushes every commit that has not been sent, as before.\n\n**2. Share in Source Control, portal sessions only**\n(`share-contribution.ts`)\n- **Share with the Team** (`studio.share.openRepository`) appears in the\ntitle bar of Source Control''s *Changes* view, through a\n`TabBarToolbarContribution` item shown for `ScmWidget`. It also appears\nin a repository row''s `…` and right-click menus (`SCM_REPOSITORY_MENU`\nand `SCM_SOURCE_CONTROL_MENU`). It opens the existing dialog for that\nrepository.\n- It is shown only when `isDesktopHost()` says this is not a desktop,\nthe same check `desktop-git-contribution.ts` and the start pages use.\nThe desktop keeps its own Sync and Push.\n- Purely additive: no `git.*` command is overridden, and nothing is\nhooked, configured or hidden. Stock Commit, Sync, the status-bar sync\nand the *Sync Changes* button behave exactly as before.\n\n**3. A count on the ribbon''s Team › Share** (`ribbon-badges.ts`,\n`studio-mode-bar.tsx`)\n- A small `RibbonBadges` service holds a number per command. The mode\nbar draws it on the button, and `ShareContribution.showCount` sets it\nfrom the same count as the status line, unsent commits included.\n- The recount now also runs on each Source Control provider''s\n`onDidChange`. A stock commit touches only `.git`, which the existing\nfile-event recount deliberately ignores. No polling was added.\n\nDocs: `docs/sharing-documents-without-git.md` has a new *Committed from\nSource Control* section and a note on the button and badge.\n`docs/verifying-the-collaboration-work.md` has a new check **5k**.\n\n## How it was verified\n\n**Unit tests** were run in a container from the session image, since the\nhost has no `@theia` `node_modules`:\n- `npx tsc -p .` in `theia/studio`: exit 0.\n- `jest src/node/document-share-service.test.ts src/browser/share\nsrc/browser/ribbon-badges.test.ts src/browser/studio-mode-bar*`: **5\nsuites, 59 tests passed**.\n- New tests: committed documents are sent to the review branch as on\ndisk, with one empty-message commit and a further edit, leaving HEAD and\n`main` alone and reading *in review* afterwards; a document the team\nalready has is not offered again; the branch mode still pushes the\ncommits; `parseNameStatus`; `splitDocuments` with and without review;\ncounts; and the Source Control helpers and badge service.\n- Full studio suite: 1283 passed and 5 failed in 6 suites\n(`cfs-map-adapter`, `orca-service`, `kit-installer`,\n`portal-bridge-contribution`, `audit-controller`, `orca-live`). **The\nsame 6 suites and 5 tests fail on unmodified `main` in the same\ncontainer**, so these failures come from the environment and this PR\ndoes not cause them.\n- The container''s root needed a git identity for the three rebase tests.\nWithout it they fail on `main` as well.\n\n**Live, headless Chrome over CDP, on a real session** (the session image\nrebuilt with this branch, `/workspace` on a Docker volume):\n- **Stand.** A bare remote whose `pre-receive` hook refuses\n`refs/heads/main` with GitHub''s GH013 text. The IDE was embedded in a\nsame-origin test page that posts `studio.init` with a viewer. CDP\n`Fetch` answered the `studio-api` calls as a project whose source is\n`pull_request`, and accepted the PR POST.\n- **Before any commit.** I edited two documents. The ribbon badge read\n**2**, matching *2 documents not shared*.\n- **Stock commit and Sync.** I typed a message in Source Control and\nclicked **Commit** (stock prompt *stage all?* → Yes), then added a\nsecond commit with an empty message from the terminal. The badge read\n**3**, the status line said *3 documents not shared* and Source Control\nshowed *Sync Changes 2*. Clicking it gave vscode.git''s *Can''t push refs\nto remote*, and the checkout stayed `ahead 2`.\n- **Source Control''s title bar** read `git.refresh`, `git.commit`,\n`scm.viewmode.tree`, `studio.share.openRepository`. Clicking Share\n(after hovering the header, as a person does) opened the dialog at once.\nIt said *This project takes changes through review*, listed Notes (new),\nPlan and Spec findings, all ticked and marked *committed here, not sent\nyet*, and showed **Send 3 documents for review**, enabled.\n- **Send.** The dialog said *Your 3 documents are in your pull request*.\nThe remote got `studio/alice-example/share` with one commit by *Alice\nExample*, `Signed-off-by` present, containing `A docs/notes.md, M\ndocs/plan.md, M docs/spec.md` at their on-disk content. `main` on the\nremote was unchanged and the checkout''s HEAD was unchanged. The PR POST\ncarried head `studio/alice-example/share` and base `main`.\n- **After closing.** The badge and the *not shared* status line were\ngone. After one more edit to Plan the badge read **1**, and the dialog\nlisted Plan to send, with *In your pull request — Notes, Spec findings*.\n- **Branch mode** (standalone tab, so no Studio scope): the same\ncommitted state showed the old note and a plain Share button, and\ncommitted documents were not listed, as before.\n\n## Not verified\n\n- **A real GitHub ruleset and a real PR opened by `studio-connector`.**\nThe rejection came from a local hook with the GH013 text, and the PR\ncall was answered by a stub. Check 5k on Dev covers both.\n- **The repository-row menus** (`…` and right-click in the\n*Repositories* view) were not clicked. That view only shows with two or\nmore repositories, and the stand had one.\n- **The desktop.** I relied on `isDesktopHost()` to hide the button\nthere and did not run an electron-app.\n- **Pushing the review once more from an already-open dialog.** After a\nsuccessful send, the dialog keeps its list and **Send** stays enabled\nuntil it is closed, which is the existing behaviour for uncommitted\ndocuments too. A second click would add a commit with no changes.\n- **A checkout behind the team after a squash merge.** The local commits\nstay. Their documents stop being offered once the team''s branch matches,\nbut `unsent` stays above 0 until the checkout is reset or pulled. That\nis outside this change.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","tree":{"sha":"e1b4cc6e87f1b038a0b8cfa2f42e0dbb6022c66e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/trees/e1b4cc6e87f1b038a0b8cfa2f42e0dbb6022c66e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/commits/eb77caa2206d464b3e8957b6604d144fdc7bcb97","verification":{"payload":"tree e1b4cc6e87f1b038a0b8cfa2f42e0dbb6022c66e\nparent ac3e2c602a776ea73a8f2fda2a3b6f39324a33ed\nauthor ANDREI KUCHMA <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech> 1791367833 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791367833 +0200\n\nfix(share): send what was committed in Source Control, and show Share there with a count (#640)\n\n## What broke\n\nOn studio-web (`share_mode = pull_request`, and `main` protected by a\nruleset), a member edited a document, committed it in the stock Source\nControl panel (one commit had an empty message), and pressed **Sync\nChanges**. GitHub refused the push (`GH013 … Changes must be made\nthrough a pull request`), and the checkout was left two commits ahead of\n`origin/main`. Then the member opened **Share with the team**. The\ndialog said *A change you shared earlier has not reached the team yet*,\nbut **Send for review** was disabled. In review mode, Share proposed\nonly files that were not committed, so committed changes could never\nreach the team.\n\n## What changed\n\n**1. Share sends what was committed and not sent**\n(`document-share-service.ts`, `share-dialog.tsx`, `share-model.ts`)\n- `describe()` now also lists the documents changed by commits that are\nnot sent yet. These are the files in `@{upstream}...HEAD`, kept only\nwhile they still differ from `@{upstream}`, so something the team\nalready took another way (a squash merge) is not offered again. They\ncome with their `.studio` companions and are flagged `committed`. The\ndialog shows them as *committed here, not sent yet*, ticked when they\nare the person''s.\n- When the project takes changes by review, those files go to the\nperson''s pull request through the existing `propose()`/`commitOnto()`.\nThat builds one commit from the files as they are on disk in a scratch\nindex, so a document committed and then edited again is sent as it is\nnow. The commit message is the sentence typed in the dialog, so an empty\nSCM commit message does not matter. **The checkout''s commits and HEAD\nstay where they are**, which is important in a shared portal checkout.\n- After sending, the existing `markInReview` reads them as *In your pull\nrequest*, and they drop out of the count.\n- *See changes* compares with the team''s version when there are commits\nthat are not sent.\n- When the project commits straight to the branch, behaviour is\nunchanged. Committed documents are not listed for choosing, because the\nnext share pushes every commit that has not been sent, as before.\n\n**2. Share in Source Control, portal sessions only**\n(`share-contribution.ts`)\n- **Share with the Team** (`studio.share.openRepository`) appears in the\ntitle bar of Source Control''s *Changes* view, through a\n`TabBarToolbarContribution` item shown for `ScmWidget`. It also appears\nin a repository row''s `…` and right-click menus (`SCM_REPOSITORY_MENU`\nand `SCM_SOURCE_CONTROL_MENU`). It opens the existing dialog for that\nrepository.\n- It is shown only when `isDesktopHost()` says this is not a desktop,\nthe same check `desktop-git-contribution.ts` and the start pages use.\nThe desktop keeps its own Sync and Push.\n- Purely additive: no `git.*` command is overridden, and nothing is\nhooked, configured or hidden. Stock Commit, Sync, the status-bar sync\nand the *Sync Changes* button behave exactly as before.\n\n**3. A count on the ribbon''s Team › Share** (`ribbon-badges.ts`,\n`studio-mode-bar.tsx`)\n- A small `RibbonBadges` service holds a number per command. The mode\nbar draws it on the button, and `ShareContribution.showCount` sets it\nfrom the same count as the status line, unsent commits included.\n- The recount now also runs on each Source Control provider''s\n`onDidChange`. A stock commit touches only `.git`, which the existing\nfile-event recount deliberately ignores. No polling was added.\n\nDocs: `docs/sharing-documents-without-git.md` has a new *Committed from\nSource Control* section and a note on the button and badge.\n`docs/verifying-the-collaboration-work.md` has a new check **5k**.\n\n## How it was verified\n\n**Unit tests** were run in a container from the session image, since the\nhost has no `@theia` `node_modules`:\n- `npx tsc -p .` in `theia/studio`: exit 0.\n- `jest src/node/document-share-service.test.ts src/browser/share\nsrc/browser/ribbon-badges.test.ts src/browser/studio-mode-bar*`: **5\nsuites, 59 tests passed**.\n- New tests: committed documents are sent to the review branch as on\ndisk, with one empty-message commit and a further edit, leaving HEAD and\n`main` alone and reading *in review* afterwards; a document the team\nalready has is not offered again; the branch mode still pushes the\ncommits; `parseNameStatus`; `splitDocuments` with and without review;\ncounts; and the Source Control helpers and badge service.\n- Full studio suite: 1283 passed and 5 failed in 6 suites\n(`cfs-map-adapter`, `orca-service`, `kit-installer`,\n`portal-bridge-contribution`, `audit-controller`, `orca-live`). **The\nsame 6 suites and 5 tests fail on unmodified `main` in the same\ncontainer**, so these failures come from the environment and this PR\ndoes not cause them.\n- The container''s root needed a git identity for the three rebase tests.\nWithout it they fail on `main` as well.\n\n**Live, headless Chrome over CDP, on a real session** (the session image\nrebuilt with this branch, `/workspace` on a Docker volume):\n- **Stand.** A bare remote whose `pre-receive` hook refuses\n`refs/heads/main` with GitHub''s GH013 text. The IDE was embedded in a\nsame-origin test page that posts `studio.init` with a viewer. CDP\n`Fetch` answered the `studio-api` calls as a project whose source is\n`pull_request`, and accepted the PR POST.\n- **Before any commit.** I edited two documents. The ribbon badge read\n**2**, matching *2 documents not shared*.\n- **Stock commit and Sync.** I typed a message in Source Control and\nclicked **Commit** (stock prompt *stage all?* → Yes), then added a\nsecond commit with an empty message from the terminal. The badge read\n**3**, the status line said *3 documents not shared* and Source Control\nshowed *Sync Changes 2*. Clicking it gave vscode.git''s *Can''t push refs\nto remote*, and the checkout stayed `ahead 2`.\n- **Source Control''s title bar** read `git.refresh`, `git.commit`,\n`scm.viewmode.tree`, `studio.share.openRepository`. Clicking Share\n(after hovering the header, as a person does) opened the dialog at once.\nIt said *This project takes changes through review*, listed Notes (new),\nPlan and Spec findings, all ticked and marked *committed here, not sent\nyet*, and showed **Send 3 documents for review**, enabled.\n- **Send.** The dialog said *Your 3 documents are in your pull request*.\nThe remote got `studio/alice-example/share` with one commit by *Alice\nExample*, `Signed-off-by` present, containing `A docs/notes.md, M\ndocs/plan.md, M docs/spec.md` at their on-disk content. `main` on the\nremote was unchanged and the checkout''s HEAD was unchanged. The PR POST\ncarried head `studio/alice-example/share` and base `main`.\n- **After closing.** The badge and the *not shared* status line were\ngone. After one more edit to Plan the badge read **1**, and the dialog\nlisted Plan to send, with *In your pull request — Notes, Spec findings*.\n- **Branch mode** (standalone tab, so no Studio scope): the same\ncommitted state showed the old note and a plain Share button, and\ncommitted documents were not listed, as before.\n\n## Not verified\n\n- **A real GitHub ruleset and a real PR opened by `studio-connector`.**\nThe rejection came from a local hook with the GH013 text, and the PR\ncall was answered by a stub. Check 5k on Dev covers both.\n- **The repository-row menus** (`…` and right-click in the\n*Repositories* view) were not clicked. That view only shows with two or\nmore repositories, and the stand had one.\n- **The desktop.** I relied on `isDesktopHost()` to hide the button\nthere and did not run an electron-app.\n- **Pushing the review once more from an already-open dialog.** After a\nsuccessful send, the dialog keeps its list and **Send** stays enabled\nuntil it is closed, which is the existing behaviour for uncommitted\ndocuments too. A second click would add a commit with no changes.\n- **A checkout behind the team after a squash merge.** The local commits\nstay. Their documents stop being offered once the team''s branch matches,\nbut `unsent` stays above 0 until the checkout is reset or pulled. That\nis outside this change.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxhqZCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAbJIQAEXX7Ad3Gq1/9FnREo5P/wU5\n1B4/976UqCVG3Wcyk7OvSYsJBd5mHyU9P2iYMJlTCPZmnGJkXjJ9STpfNtWfX3rX\nET5BgLwQpydORnx2CswsEqinAoMkqKB/59iR5TQLcoP6zc6JshVb65q/5/3O57qA\nbRPaiuPu5kYe11RJxYwxaQZx/1iLyu+7zS7cHdG7pW6Eol0+s12qnOUUGBhH27rC\nFf+TZ/faJsHfBSktP9LdmpZicGDo5PdxwTe/ESMLnsp6wLYGTPqWLbALo8bVdRua\nwcSwXcmfY6y5P89JWOFx1gPq/nhx1otcs+C5CrI4tTiJ1UT5isTnbZLVPQCD/bx0\nKN54Ds1v5yptgPZeJmwTGtVEkEKNCJ+S1CDKqzm+5KEesavI2QCjsxbwg7pjCRh8\n6XLzIZC2BH3Iv79fnPCSPRm8COBVazlBMUYDg7rrh1byTfe0UsRuLtt63OvlfwFx\n0BCcUxHQprIsZWNyj+uNFP3R6rra+8fXZuh3tmKkIpPxMXHrykcRhtrQaoCjoyTw\nJ57vgJjuzhcoKPI03KpOkb18EIjHjF8zK2pZRf/2byIfFpGuipaVb+XGfr3wnB6k\nsHLHMSpZIcFV1VM6YDSl7pKKBabuzRj70GD4EWwkT8SdwVahyslPSE85mlYpqjU7\nK7KglivuV8gYdJvXuc73\n=lBqP\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T10:10:34Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/eb77caa2206d464b3e8957b6604d144fdc7bcb97","node_id":"C_kwDOTl7dJtoAKGViNzdjYWEyMjA2ZDQ2NGIzZTg5NTdiNjYwNGQxNDRmZGM3YmNiOTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/ac3e2c602a776ea73a8f2fda2a3b6f39324a33ed","sha":"ac3e2c602a776ea73a8f2fda2a3b6f39324a33ed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/ac3e2c602a776ea73a8f2fda2a3b6f39324a33ed"}],"sha":"eb77caa2206d464b3e8957b6604d144fdc7bcb97","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/eb77caa2206d464b3e8957b6604d144fdc7bcb97"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/301748190?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AndrejK666","id":301748190,"login":"AndrejK666","node_id":"U_kgDOEfxP3g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/ac3e2c602a776ea73a8f2fda2a3b6f39324a33ed/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T07:31:43Z","email":"Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech","name":"ANDREI KUCHMA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T07:31:43Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(desktop): a macOS build for Apple Silicon beside the Windows one (#636)\n\n## What\n\nThe desktop Studio for Apple Silicon Macs: a `.dmg` (and the zip the\nupdater uses) from CI, next to the Windows installer.\n\n- `desktop-windows.yml` → **`desktop.yml`** (\"Desktop build\"): matrix\n`windows-2022` / `macos-15`, one release job publishing both;\n`latest-mac.yml`/`beta-mac.yml` + the mac zip go into the rolling\n`desktop-updates` feed. Manual runs may pick `platforms: windows | macos\n| both`.\n- `studio-cli.yml` builds `darwin-arm64` too (cfs.json already pinned\nits Python).\n- `gearbox-engine.yml` builds the engine on `macos-15` too; publishing\nmoved into one job, so the two platforms never race to create the\nrelease, and a platform missing from an existing release is added to it.\n\n## What changes in the app (Mac only, Windows and the web session\nuntouched)\n\n- **Executable bit kept on unpack** (`unpackVsix`): without it\n`gearbox`, the CLI''s `python3` and `cfs` would not run on macOS. Test\nincluded (runs on Linux CI; checked by hand in a `node:22` container).\n- **PATH from the login shell** in `desktop-main.js`: a Finder/Dock\nstart gets launchd''s PATH (no Homebrew), as VS Code works around.\n- **Cold-start `cfstudio://` link**: macOS delivers it as `open-url`,\npossibly before Theia listens; it is kept where Theia''s start reads it.\n- **Signing**: ad hoc unless `MAC_CSC_LINK`/`MAC_CSC_KEY_PASSWORD` exist\n(+ `APPLE_API_KEY*` for notarization). An ad-hoc app can''t update in\nplace (Squirrel.Mac checks signatures), so such a build is marked\n`updates: manual`: it still checks the feed but offers the release page\ninstead of downloading (`UpdateCheck` state `manual`).\n\n## Not verified\n\n- Nobody has run the result on a Mac yet; this PR''s `build (macos)` job\nis the first build. Until this merges, the CLI and engine releases have\nno `darwin-arm64` VSIX, so the PR''s dmg ships without them (the manifest\nstep warns).\n- Intel Macs are not built.\n\nDocs: `docs/desktop-studio.md` (CI, *Installing on a Mac*, Updates,\nKnown limits), release notes, TASKS.md (Developer ID task).\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","tree":{"sha":"f57936ea2d4e077feb47192209aec8b4fe1cb870","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/trees/f57936ea2d4e077feb47192209aec8b4fe1cb870"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/commits/ac3e2c602a776ea73a8f2fda2a3b6f39324a33ed","verification":{"payload":"tree f57936ea2d4e077feb47192209aec8b4fe1cb870\nparent 060bbcf6b2964c12711de9e9b6c9e94141a04868\nauthor ANDREI KUCHMA <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech> 1791358303 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791358303 +0200\n\nfeat(desktop): a macOS build for Apple Silicon beside the Windows one (#636)\n\n## What\n\nThe desktop Studio for Apple Silicon Macs: a `.dmg` (and the zip the\nupdater uses) from CI, next to the Windows installer.\n\n- `desktop-windows.yml` → **`desktop.yml`** (\"Desktop build\"): matrix\n`windows-2022` / `macos-15`, one release job publishing both;\n`latest-mac.yml`/`beta-mac.yml` + the mac zip go into the rolling\n`desktop-updates` feed. Manual runs may pick `platforms: windows | macos\n| both`.\n- `studio-cli.yml` builds `darwin-arm64` too (cfs.json already pinned\nits Python).\n- `gearbox-engine.yml` builds the engine on `macos-15` too; publishing\nmoved into one job, so the two platforms never race to create the\nrelease, and a platform missing from an existing release is added to it.\n\n## What changes in the app (Mac only, Windows and the web session\nuntouched)\n\n- **Executable bit kept on unpack** (`unpackVsix`): without it\n`gearbox`, the CLI''s `python3` and `cfs` would not run on macOS. Test\nincluded (runs on Linux CI; checked by hand in a `node:22` container).\n- **PATH from the login shell** in `desktop-main.js`: a Finder/Dock\nstart gets launchd''s PATH (no Homebrew), as VS Code works around.\n- **Cold-start `cfstudio://` link**: macOS delivers it as `open-url`,\npossibly before Theia listens; it is kept where Theia''s start reads it.\n- **Signing**: ad hoc unless `MAC_CSC_LINK`/`MAC_CSC_KEY_PASSWORD` exist\n(+ `APPLE_API_KEY*` for notarization). An ad-hoc app can''t update in\nplace (Squirrel.Mac checks signatures), so such a build is marked\n`updates: manual`: it still checks the feed but offers the release page\ninstead of downloading (`UpdateCheck` state `manual`).\n\n## Not verified\n\n- Nobody has run the result on a Mac yet; this PR''s `build (macos)` job\nis the first build. Until this merges, the CLI and engine releases have\nno `darwin-arm64` VSIX, so the PR''s dmg ships without them (the manifest\nstep warns).\n- Intel Macs are not built.\n\nDocs: `docs/desktop-studio.md` (CI, *Installing on a Mac*, Updates,\nKnown limits), release notes, TASKS.md (Developer ID task).\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxfVfCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA5fYQAAwlBLhMFsdI9TR5F24OabY8\nqDIpxG53XRPMEdCJajNkT3xonecx6UslNpfyv6Iy1+zAn4f+55JQIEYhhJlaFUBT\n1WaYSiVp5ASWAS4D38Wr9OU9elOQlivt95dN3tHMaAKT66ibnawohh1ej6viwFFQ\nsRTp0+/BZP/nWV/3IP5xojO/tGbYCxfcIh8SlaWpZ1sldHeUZj1ql+nj2b3/Rs4S\nQs5mtBSvXtj/WraZsJLNfhGD1s4KIuHvpCTum8NSsHuetj3TbAPTlVWL++pE2FDK\nNuIn5xNv+E62A0PFKdxOofZXtUt9aQZk8fCKBbyQy+70F/aje6k6KYsytSmhpLLj\nQEZd+b5RFgguFga+nxZ90ZYbFdTkbiDDdmjzowmYoX5f4kETpYMtHn2IFU+ToB9/\njdrjlO/GZMEEw0M99y4DfHdCXL0QZueJlPEMGJgNFzU623a3BIyvRgqMzKKeT76c\nPt8IRTyPZrnzC/3tjPaj3in5Cwy/1ZPI7SHqBc4GjqE3qtj7AccHlRX1hnThiXu+\nw0D1kiuq9rSpWjfU1y8Em1Mwd9ZYyq0yltgSiNgq52Jl9FG/hRW974mpVFxcM9QL\nPa2tlLOH84QR9BaD9+g0hCt7Z3h141IfTSVlYvpruPxNxRmoDfYtyvJsz4NYnLyT\nmfSRvGjclanr6uiZ9IuV\n=9NQr\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T07:31:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/ac3e2c602a776ea73a8f2fda2a3b6f39324a33ed","node_id":"C_kwDOTl7dJtoAKGFjM2UyYzYwMmE3NzZlYTczYThmMmZkYTJhM2I2ZjM5MzI0YTMzZWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/060bbcf6b2964c12711de9e9b6c9e94141a04868","sha":"060bbcf6b2964c12711de9e9b6c9e94141a04868","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/060bbcf6b2964c12711de9e9b6c9e94141a04868"}],"sha":"ac3e2c602a776ea73a8f2fda2a3b6f39324a33ed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/ac3e2c602a776ea73a8f2fda2a3b6f39324a33ed"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/301748190?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AndrejK666","id":301748190,"login":"AndrejK666","node_id":"U_kgDOEfxP3g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/060bbcf6b2964c12711de9e9b6c9e94141a04868/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T07:30:40Z","email":"Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech","name":"ANDREI KUCHMA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T07:30:40Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(theia): a session''s Claude moves to 2.1.292 (#635)\n\nEvery Claude a browser session carries was weeks old, and each one was\nold by a different amount:\n\n| What | Used by | Was | Now |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `anthropic.claude-code` VSIX | Claude Code panel in the IDE | 2.1.227\n| 2.1.292 |\n| `@anthropic-ai/claude-code` | `claude` in Orca and the terminal |\n2.1.266 | 2.1.292 |\n| `@anthropic-ai/claude-agent-sdk` | `@theia/ai-claude-code` chat |\n0.3.223 | 0.3.292 |\n\nThe desktop is not affected. It already installs the newest version from\nopen-vsx on first start.\n\n**Checked**\n- The VSIX exists on open-vsx for linux-x64, linux-arm64, win32-x64 and\ndarwin-arm64.\n- The CLI package still ships per-platform binaries the same way,\nlinux-x64/arm64 included, so `trim-vendor-binaries.sh` sees the same\nlayout.\n- The new SDK''s `sdk.mjs` loads and exports `query`, which is the entry\n`THEIA_CLAUDE_CODE_PATH` points at.\n\n- The Dockerfile''s install step, run as written on the runtime base\n(`node:22.23.1-bookworm-slim`, same digest) with\n`trim-vendor-binaries.sh amd64`: `claude --version` prints `2.1.292\n(Claude Code)` and `sdk.mjs` exports `query`. The two packages take 536\nMB, against 538 MB for the old pins.\n\n**Not checked:** the full `theia` image and a live session. PR CI skips\n`build-service-images`, so the first full build is the merge run. After\ndeploy, open a new session and try the Claude panel, `claude` in a\nterminal, and Theia''s Claude chat.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","tree":{"sha":"8166461c0df9020903800bc1f5485c94f46e9b95","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/trees/8166461c0df9020903800bc1f5485c94f46e9b95"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/commits/060bbcf6b2964c12711de9e9b6c9e94141a04868","verification":{"payload":"tree 8166461c0df9020903800bc1f5485c94f46e9b95\nparent bbb30efc968d795001718491b920df4f75adc16b\nauthor ANDREI KUCHMA <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech> 1791358240 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791358240 +0200\n\nchore(theia): a session''s Claude moves to 2.1.292 (#635)\n\nEvery Claude a browser session carries was weeks old, and each one was\nold by a different amount:\n\n| What | Used by | Was | Now |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `anthropic.claude-code` VSIX | Claude Code panel in the IDE | 2.1.227\n| 2.1.292 |\n| `@anthropic-ai/claude-code` | `claude` in Orca and the terminal |\n2.1.266 | 2.1.292 |\n| `@anthropic-ai/claude-agent-sdk` | `@theia/ai-claude-code` chat |\n0.3.223 | 0.3.292 |\n\nThe desktop is not affected. It already installs the newest version from\nopen-vsx on first start.\n\n**Checked**\n- The VSIX exists on open-vsx for linux-x64, linux-arm64, win32-x64 and\ndarwin-arm64.\n- The CLI package still ships per-platform binaries the same way,\nlinux-x64/arm64 included, so `trim-vendor-binaries.sh` sees the same\nlayout.\n- The new SDK''s `sdk.mjs` loads and exports `query`, which is the entry\n`THEIA_CLAUDE_CODE_PATH` points at.\n\n- The Dockerfile''s install step, run as written on the runtime base\n(`node:22.23.1-bookworm-slim`, same digest) with\n`trim-vendor-binaries.sh amd64`: `claude --version` prints `2.1.292\n(Claude Code)` and `sdk.mjs` exports `query`. The two packages take 536\nMB, against 538 MB for the old pins.\n\n**Not checked:** the full `theia` image and a live session. PR CI skips\n`build-service-images`, so the first full build is the merge run. After\ndeploy, open a new session and try the Claude panel, `claude` in a\nterminal, and Theia''s Claude chat.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxfUgCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAABokQAHtOdL5kWOHjuSPU6FpPdX1c\nxIVB3BBADRZYk2WLTD9iWWjjtmSs5HXquvlhCpTcnljmjLP3FFmraNtXVC5Llr6s\nGFCjBR0+683uSIavPtnWYClheSlWOSWXoxqSj6ZY9YI2yoXY6eRBF15Op3LZmGZs\nJLdN6vlceWGx1UFlF3JT8bJREPUQTuuEZo8z1ml1TIgc4aw7qOe+87rjHlRUdmGx\ngxeB/NjzAZCdQGmf7A2mGMB+nT6Q7n4npgj3YhfGpH92BbcP6xXbonKq8xkzyh4c\nEaR++OkWEAxJKXxNjZ/3BTw/ZhQ1WysTSMgzxNymnUsNyGWT5oViuRL6+oM0Irz8\nJQq7WO7t/m8IEoyhEmBiOzxjInhe3TINGn1fq3oSOzTEEDdJ98Jt/jKcj3RYl5sD\niLwJ6CT+3ISnRsHT3A0gk0TPg41BXXTIduM1Ri5g4thjiuJ5Zt8zXPq3BHaXcNHI\nGF4OboKRFAZ2O7BRJEkc2Y4B8/TupPByujOFVsjLwo8v48COaTvRE9YQpIE6A61r\niEv/3EiP3hqR4/D+3/0HrDBbJycQ4tleytmrVS8H1OGXOEd0+9ZUQBvCkITMZl2E\nmMYC1UX8XJHU423YKW7fkzkDGeQ8TZvbJ2fSs7l1fFC7m7hZ1o5nmpBejtVfZFwW\nGkRu2vcwc3ani1mx5svU\n=k92E\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T07:30:40Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":