66/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/bbb30efc968d795001718491b920df4f75adc16b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T07:30:24Z","email":"Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech","name":"ANDREI KUCHMA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T07:30:24Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs(prd): a specification maps to gears by contract, then evidence, then gap (#634)\n\nFixes the requirements for mapping a product specification to gears\nbefore building it. Refs #205, #199, #206, #616.\n\n### Requirements (PRD 5.7, all planned)\n- `cpt-studio-fr-spec-gear-mapping`: a capability first matches gears\nthat declare its **contract** with `provide(...)` in `gear.gdl`. The\norganization''s vocabulary translates the capability key into contracts.\nWhat is left is **searched** in gear documentation, and each match cites\nits passage and ranks below every contract match. What is still left is\na **gap**, which is the input of a new gear. The rules are the same for\nevery project.\n- `cpt-studio-fr-mapping-decisions`: a member confirms or rejects each\nmapping. The decision is a graph link from the section through the\ncapability to the gear, carrying who decided, the step that proposed it,\nthe gear version and the document revision. It reopens when the section\nor the gear changes, and it ranks later proposals.\n- `cpt-studio-fr-nfr-to-profile`: non-functional requirements set the\ndeployment profile and `config` in `product.gdl`, never extra gears.\n\n### Also\n- Glossary: **Contract**, **Mapping**; **Capability** now says the\nvocabulary maps keys to contracts.\n- Open questions:\n  - who owns the vocabulary;\n  - requirement-driven resolution in Gearbox (`requires = [...]`);\n- FrontX micro-frontends alongside gears (constructorfabric/gearbox#3).\n- **AC11**: checked on the product projects already on the dev stand.\n- `studio-components-catalog` design: the principle\n`cpt-studio-principle-catalog-contract-first` and the planned driver\nrows.\n\n`node scripts/check-docs.mjs` passes: 121 documents, 671 ids.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Documentation**\n* Added planned guidance for mapping specification capabilities to gear\nthrough declared contracts, then documented evidence, with unmatched\ncapabilities reported as gaps.\n* Documented how mapping decisions retain their context and are reopened\nfor review when relevant specifications or gear change.\n* Clarified that non-functional requirements map to deployment profiles\nand product configuration without adding gear.\n* Expanded acceptance criteria, open questions, and traceability for the\nplanned mapping workflow.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","tree":{"sha":"29ff69063f04207f6bd6a1d3c8a6660aec652466","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/trees/29ff69063f04207f6bd6a1d3c8a6660aec652466"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/commits/bbb30efc968d795001718491b920df4f75adc16b","verification":{"payload":"tree 29ff69063f04207f6bd6a1d3c8a6660aec652466\nparent ea885e7fa745fd9978f120f6f4e3cd619917720f\nauthor ANDREI KUCHMA <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech> 1791358224 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791358224 +0200\n\ndocs(prd): a specification maps to gears by contract, then evidence, then gap (#634)\n\nFixes the requirements for mapping a product specification to gears\nbefore building it. Refs #205, #199, #206, #616.\n\n### Requirements (PRD 5.7, all planned)\n- `cpt-studio-fr-spec-gear-mapping`: a capability first matches gears\nthat declare its **contract** with `provide(...)` in `gear.gdl`. The\norganization''s vocabulary translates the capability key into contracts.\nWhat is left is **searched** in gear documentation, and each match cites\nits passage and ranks below every contract match. What is still left is\na **gap**, which is the input of a new gear. The rules are the same for\nevery project.\n- `cpt-studio-fr-mapping-decisions`: a member confirms or rejects each\nmapping. The decision is a graph link from the section through the\ncapability to the gear, carrying who decided, the step that proposed it,\nthe gear version and the document revision. It reopens when the section\nor the gear changes, and it ranks later proposals.\n- `cpt-studio-fr-nfr-to-profile`: non-functional requirements set the\ndeployment profile and `config` in `product.gdl`, never extra gears.\n\n### Also\n- Glossary: **Contract**, **Mapping**; **Capability** now says the\nvocabulary maps keys to contracts.\n- Open questions:\n  - who owns the vocabulary;\n  - requirement-driven resolution in Gearbox (`requires = [...]`);\n- FrontX micro-frontends alongside gears (constructorfabric/gearbox#3).\n- **AC11**: checked on the product projects already on the dev stand.\n- `studio-components-catalog` design: the principle\n`cpt-studio-principle-catalog-contract-first` and the planned driver\nrows.\n\n`node scripts/check-docs.mjs` passes: 121 documents, 671 ids.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Documentation**\n* Added planned guidance for mapping specification capabilities to gear\nthrough declared contracts, then documented evidence, with unmatched\ncapabilities reported as gaps.\n* Documented how mapping decisions retain their context and are reopened\nfor review when relevant specifications or gear change.\n* Clarified that non-functional requirements map to deployment profiles\nand product configuration without adding gear.\n* Expanded acceptance criteria, open questions, and traceability for the\nplanned mapping workflow.\n\n<!-- end of auto-