s://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/ea885e7fa745fd9978f120f6f4e3cd619917720f","node_id":"C_kwDOTl7dJtoAKGVhODg1ZTdmYTc0NWZkOTk3OGYxMjBmNmY0ZTNjZDYxOTkxNzcyMGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/954deab9a706a22cf7eacdf292ca3dc6804ecbc3","sha":"954deab9a706a22cf7eacdf292ca3dc6804ecbc3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/954deab9a706a22cf7eacdf292ca3dc6804ecbc3"}],"sha":"ea885e7fa745fd9978f120f6f4e3cd619917720f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/ea885e7fa745fd9978f120f6f4e3cd619917720f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/301748190?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AndrejK666","id":301748190,"login":"AndrejK666","node_id":"U_kgDOEfxP3g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/954deab9a706a22cf7eacdf292ca3dc6804ecbc3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T14:00:14Z","email":"Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech","name":"ANDREI KUCHMA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T14:00:14Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(gearbox): move the engine to ea964f9, where a plugin `implements` and every gear has a maturity (#633)\n\n## Why now\n\nGearbox on dev is already broken:\n\n```\ncomponents-catalog: Gearbox facts corpus=MikeFalcon77/gears-rust@feature/gearbox (70a5354) gears=0\n```\n\nThe corpus moved overnight: every `gear.gdl` there now declares\n`maturity` and writes `implements` where it wrote `fills`. The engine we\npin (`55f7015`) knows neither key, so every description fails to\nevaluate. constructorfabric/gearbox#2, merged today as `ea964f9`, is the\nengine that reads them.\n\n## What changes\n\n- **Engine pin.** `STUDIO_GEARBOX_REF` moves to `ea964f9` in\n`studio-backend/Dockerfile`, `Dockerfile.src` and `theia/Dockerfile`.\n- **gearbox-studio''s wire types.** `src/common/generated/`,\n`src/common/extension-points.ts` and `src/browser/ai/generated/` were\nbyte-identical to upstream at `55f7015`. They are now copied verbatim\nfrom `ea964f9`. That brings:\n  - `PluginFill` renamed to `PluginImpl`;\n  - `GearDescriptor.implements` and `GearDescriptor.maturity`;\n  - `DesignGear` and `CatalogueLoadResult.designs`;\n  - `ProductEdit` `remove_source`;\n  - `ExtensionPointDecl.selector`.\n- **Our ported views** read `implements` where they read `fills`: the\nadd-gear dialog, the inspector and the composition. The rename is the\nsame one upstream made.\n- **Two small follow-ups to the new types.**\n  - An empty catalogue load, and its tests, carry `designs: []`.\n  - The edit preview describes `remove_source`.\n\nThe backend already reads `implements` (#630, merged). Other upstream\nchanges since `55f7015`, such as generating into an outside folder and\n`initRepository`, are not ported here.\n\n## Checked\n\n- **Engine `ea964f9` on the live corpus.** Built from source and run as\n`gearbox catalogue --root` against `feature/gearbox` at `70a5354`.\nResult: 49 gears plus 10 at design maturity, from 59 descriptions, with\nno errors.\n- **gearbox-studio.** `tsc --noEmit` is clean. jest: 24 suites passed\nand 1 skipped; 180 tests passed and 1 skipped. That matches\n`upstream/main` exactly. Before the `designs` and `remove_source`\nfollow-ups, tsc failed on 3 errors.\n- **Backend.** fmt, clippy `-D warnings`, and `cargo test\ncomponents_catalog` pass (280 tests).\n\nAfter deploy, the line to look for is `Gearbox facts ... gears=49`.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","tree":{"sha":"4f7c430cce16ce92a00e40bd7558441f0b3054c0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/trees/4f7c430cce16ce92a00e40bd7558441f0b3054c0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/commits/954deab9a706a22cf7eacdf292ca3dc6804ecbc3","verification":{"payload":"tree 4f7c430cce16ce92a00e40bd7558441f0b3054c0\nparent 48b4c075d73a7a36d21a77a6b95d571dad580e99\nauthor ANDREI KUCHMA <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech> 1791295214 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791295214 +0200\n\nfix(gearbox): move the engine to ea964f9, where a plugin `implements` and every gear has a maturity (#633)\n\n## Why now\n\nGearbox on dev is already broken:\n\n```\ncomponents-catalog: Gearbox facts corpus=MikeFalcon77/gears-rust@feature/gearbox (70a5354) gears=0\n```\n\nThe corpus moved overnight: every `gear.gdl` there now declares\n`maturity` and writes `implements` where it wrote `fills`. The engine we\npin (`55f7015`) knows neither key, so every description fails to\nevaluate. constructorfabric/gearbox#2, merged today as `ea964f9`, is the\nengine that reads them.\n\n## What changes\n\n- **Engine pin.** `STUDIO_GEARBOX_REF` moves to `ea964f9` in\n`studio-backend/Dockerfile`, `Dockerfile.src` and `theia/Dockerfile`.\n- **gearbox-studio''s wire types.** `src/common/generated/`,\n`src/common/extension-points.ts` and `src/browser/ai/generated/` were\nbyte-identical to upstream at `55f7015`. They are now copied verbatim\nfrom `ea964f9`. That brings:\n  - `PluginFill` renamed to `PluginImpl`;\n  - `GearDescriptor.implements` and `GearDescriptor.maturity`;\n  - `DesignGear` and `CatalogueLoadResult.designs`;\n  - `ProductEdit` `remove_source`;\n  - `ExtensionPointDecl.selector`.\n- **Our ported views** read `implements` where they read `fills`: the\nadd-gear dialog, the inspector and the composition. The rename is the\nsame one upstream made.\n- **Two small follow-ups to the new types.**\n  - An empty catalogue load, and its tests, carry `designs: []`.\n  - The edit preview describes `remove_source`.\n\nThe backend already reads `implements` (#630, merged). Other upstream\nchanges since `55f7015`, such as generating into an outside folder and\n`initRepository`, are not ported here.\n\n## Checked\n\n- **Engine `ea964f9` on the live corpus.** Built from source and run as\n`gearbox catalogue --root` against `feature/gearbox` at `70a5354`.\nResult: 49 gears plus 10 at design maturity, from 59 descriptions, with\nno errors.\n- **gearbox-studio.** `tsc --noEmit` is clean. jest: 24 suites passed\nand 1 skipped; 180 tests passed and 1 skipped. That matches\n`upstream/main` exactly. Before the `designs` and `remove_source`\nfollow-ups, tsc failed on 3 errors.\n- **Backend.** fmt, clippy `-D warnings`, and `cargo test\ncomponents_catalog` pass (280 tests).\n\nAfter deploy, the line to look for is `Gearbox facts ... gears=49`.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxP7uCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA9OEQABwTzxVmwq0O2tmYIL9nEM2S\n728kquclSQJ5DYQ6k5ouOlBsIqYUx2dTrEUw30f7gK+qYGhtZqvYSzG8xn7J/GwA\nFRMFOGcrqBua0QqbPwIQzwIfQg5UprtEzZTKEDALdq4vBg47K8njv3m0+3KhdQ+B\n8jvrb5PbRgjHohSjjnsqN4EBf0Ejs277mDWHssdwwH9M7JZVanSFH95QLug6Alm7\na0q3aqfaC4RT5G2jcvmisY6bAwFNnr6IGOQ8WcgdIdeRnXjPCd2amKSMIPsJgt9m\nA97OYuCZbh0TyIcNGAHkO4WZpdMZo8beNwERbbRKDXtyqqpnmF7QPJ5KyfYNMycv\n4sfuP25+K+9Q2ozI5COocRFQqe6BHU/5SF7LQ3TWcI3P9n2oGPsBhYEupeazZ/e5\n/wC7YCAClhZUnIQYQK9+CY1kabNoJDJx/8MGxLM6Cw28DXcocvInC+x/yRDruDsT\nbtTILXKBcatdjQkoWWu5Vts5fRD9MDCQFDdMFG49Ed9NrzGy1/4WrNMr95rh5Vag\nwijMXEpl9mRBAK4DzeE82HZeKFeiF6u1oryzDR5lRbi7H5lKKbjJzq2uaPtIVOt3\nHqiEWxn0h0GTZgvH2JXJo3w9SLjqcosEBpZabDgMfXinMCtTgLZnZ9gWZTukAiAe\nYTozKi6//MVmLX18sotu\n=fpCE\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T14:00:15Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/954deab9a706a22cf7eacdf292ca3dc6804ecbc3","node_id":"C_kwDOTl7dJtoAKDk1NGRlYWI5YTcwNmEyMmNmN2VhY2RmMjkyY2EzZGM2ODA0ZWNiYzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/48b4c075d73a7a36d21a77a6b95d571dad580e99","sha":"48b4c075d73a7a36d21a77a6b95d571dad580e99","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/48b4c075d73a7a36d21a77a6b95d571dad580e99"}],"sha":"954deab9a706a22cf7eacdf292ca3dc6804ecbc3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/954deab9a706a22cf7eacdf292ca3dc6804ecbc3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/301748190?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AndrejK666","id":301748190,"login":"AndrejK666","node_id":"U_kgDOEfxP3g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/48b4c075d73a7a36d21a77a6b95d571dad580e99/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T13:23:26Z","email":"Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech","name":"ANDREI KUCHMA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T13:23:26Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"API: the success code says what happened, Idempotency-Key, batches — and code cites current ADRs (#631)\n\nTwo commits, independent of the docs PRs (#625/#627/#628).\n\n## 1. `feat(api)` — status codes, idempotency, batches (`a0fd5c73`)\n\n**Rules** — `docs/api-conventions.md` gains three sections:\n- **H. Status codes**\n  - `GET` 200;\n  - `POST` that creates 201 with the element;\n  - an action 200 (or 204);\n  - started work 202 + `run_id`;\n  - `PUT`/`PATCH` 200;\n  - `DELETE` 204 with no body;\n  - a retried `DELETE` meets 404 and treats it as done;\n- a deletion that can partly fail is a canonical failure, not a report\nin a body.\n- **I. Idempotency**\n  - `Idempotency-Key` header on every `POST` that starts work;\n- the same key in the tenant gives the same run, stored on the run row\nin its creating transaction;\n  - only a success is remembered;\n  - one key per user intent;\n  - syncs also coalesce;\n  - creates (201) do not take a key yet.\n- **J. Batches**\n  - `{ items }` with the caller''s ids;\n  - a declared limit, refused whole;\n- a long batch is one run with an outcome per item, a short one 200 with\nitems in request order;\n  - never `207`.\n\n**The API brought into line**, with every consumer in the same change\n(G3):\n\n| Change | Operations |\n|---|---|\n| DELETE → 204 | `remove_field`, presence sign-out,\n`delete_organization`, `leave_organization`, `delete_membership` (their\ncounts go to the log; DTOs removed) |\n| create → 201 | workspace/project documents, domain-model objects and\nrelations, organizations, `create-repo` (`compose`/`conformance` persist\nnothing and stay 200) |\n| started work → 202 + `run_id` | artifact-ingest, catalogue and report\nsyncs and `graph-sync` (`task_id` → `run_id`), documents quality,\nspec-quality `analyze/*` and `analyze-batch` (declared 202 but answered\n200) |\n| stays 200 (work done in the request) | `reconcile`, domain-model\n`sync`/`import`, `memberships/backfill`; `graph-sync` with `\"wait\":\ntrue` when the run finished in time |\n\n- **`idempotency.rs`**:\n- parses the header (1–255 visible ASCII, else 400 `invalid_argument`)\nand declares it in OpenAPI;\n  - every 202 route passes it to studio-tasks;\n  - notify''s body field `idempotency_key` is replaced by the header;\n  - scheduler run-now scopes the key per schedule.\n- **`tasks::service`**:\n  - attaches a key to the unkeyed queued run it coalesces into;\n  - does not coalesce into a run held under a different key;\n  - 3 Postgres tests in `tasks/service_tests.rs`.\n- **Consumers**:\n- projects-mfe adds the header through a `RestPlugin` and reads\n`run_id`;\n- the prototype sends it on notify, analyze, syncs and run-now, and\ntypes the 204s as `void`;\n- theia''s analyze client sends it, falling back to `getRandomValues`\nwhere `randomUUID` is missing;\n- the desktop `/studio-api` proxy forwards it (the only header\nallow-list found; CORS is off in every profile, and nginx passes headers\nthrough).\n\n## 2. `chore` — code cites current ADR numbers, stale comments fixed\n(`6ad9e0a1`)\n\n- **Old numbers.** After the ADR trees were unified, code still cited\nold numbers. Each citation was read in context:\n  - Theia bridge → ADR-0022 (41 sites);\n  - canonical user → ADR-0023 (9);\n  - person resolver → ADR-0025 (12);\n  - push channel → ADR-0026 (1).\n- **Wrong citations.** Citations of records that never said what the\ncomment claims were re-targeted (access config/PDP → ADR-0009, project\nwizard → ADR-0028) or dropped. gearbox-studio''s own ADRs now carry their\ncpt ids.\n- **Comments that drifted from the code:**\n  - presence notes wait for the next heartbeat;\n  - an event''s `seq` is a durable per-tenant cursor;\n- the default Theia sink is `StudioEventsSink`, in code and in the\nbridge docs;\n- the reports `/sync` description names `organization_id` (ADR-0033\namendment);\n- workbook, `repo_enrich`, `normalize_alias` and the domain-model route\ndocs.\n- **ADR index:** no longer lists ADR-0031 twice.\n- **No behaviour change.**\n\n## Verified\n\nOn commit 1:\n- **Backend:**\n  - `cargo fmt --check`, `cargo clippy --all-targets -D warnings`;\n  - `cargo test --locked` 1286 passed, 0 failed;\n  - `cargo test api_contract` 3 passed;\n  - `api-contract.json` regenerated.\n- **Contract check:** `node scripts/check-api-usage.mjs` OK (156 calls,\n1 known break).\n- **Prototype:** `tsc -b`; vitest 292 passed.\n- **studio-frontend:** `npm run test:unit` green except the known\nlocal-only `overlayContract.test.ts`, which needs built MFE manifests.\n- **Theia:** jest 73 passed in the five touched suites.\n\nAfter the second commit was added on top: clippy clean, check-api-usage\nOK, prototype `tsc -b` OK. The full local test run was cut short by the\nmachine running out of memory, so CI is the authority for the combined\nbranch.\n\n## Not done here\n\n- `theia/studio` `tsc --noEmit` reports four Uint8Array/Buffer typing\nerrors. None is on a changed line; they were not checked against a clean\nmain.\n- `graph-sync`''s body accepts a `tenant` field, which breaks C1 (the\ntenant never comes from the API).\n- Next PR: mechanise H1 in `api_contract.rs`.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n* Background-work requests now support idempotency keys, helping retries\nreuse queued work instead of creating duplicates.\n* Queued sync responses use `run_id` for tracking, and several creation\nand queued-work operations now return more specific HTTP status codes.\n* **Bug Fixes**\n* Deletion and sign-out operations now return empty `204 No Content`\nresponses; membership-removal counts are no longer included in the\nresponse.\n* API guidance and examples now reflect updated response formats and\nretry behavior.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","tree":{"sha":"ed73cf0de71ce41b7ab2139930dfcedb72e67d6a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/trees/ed73cf0de71ce41b7ab2139930dfcedb72e67d6a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/commits/48b4c075d73a7a36d21a77a6b95d571dad580e99","verification":{"payload":"tree ed73cf0de71ce41b7ab2139930dfcedb72e67d6a\nparent 827a33b80b28c05806c03cf240c99732017bcb54\nauthor ANDREI KUCHMA <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech> 1791293006 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791293006 +0200\n\nAPI: the success code says what happened, Idempotency-Key, batches — and code cites current ADRs (#631)\n\nTwo commits, independent of the docs PRs (#625/#627/#628).\n\n## 1. `feat(api)` — status codes, idempotency, batches (`a0fd5c73`)\n\n**Rules** — `docs/api-conventions.md` gains three sections:\n- **H. Status codes**\n  - `GET` 200;\n  - `POST` that creates 201 with the element;\n  - an action 200 (or 204);\n  - started work 202 + `run_id`;\n  - `PUT`/`PATCH` 200;\n  - `DELETE` 204 with no body;\n  - a retried `DELETE` meets 404 and treats it as done;\n- a deletion that can partly fail is a canonical failure, not a report\nin a body.\n- **I. Idempotency**\n  - `Idempotency-Key` header on every `POST` that starts work;\n- the same key in the tenant gives the same run, stored on the run row\nin its creating transaction;\n  - only a success is remembered;\n  - one key per user intent;\n  - syncs also coalesce;\n  - creates (201) do not take a key yet.\n- **J. Batches**\n  - `{ items }` with the caller''s ids;\n  - a declared limit, refused whole;\n- a long batch is one run with an outcome per item, a short one 200 with\nitems in request order;\n  - never `207`.\n\n**The API brought into line**, with every consumer in the same change\n(G3):\n\n| Change | Operations |\n|---|---|\n| DELETE → 204 | `remove_field`, presence sign-out,\n`delete_organization`, `leave_organization`, `delete_membership` (their\ncounts go to the log; DTOs removed) |\n| create → 201 | workspace/project documents, domain-model objects and\nrelations, organizations, `create-repo` (`compose`/`conformance` persist\nnothing and stay 200) |\n| started work → 202 + `run_id` | artifact-ingest, catalogue and report\nsyncs and `graph-sync` (`task_id` → `run_id`), documents quality,\nspec-quality `analyze/*` and `analyze-batch` (declared 202 but answered\n200) |\n| stays 200 (work done in the request) | `reconcile`, domain-model\n`sync`/`import`, `memberships/backfill`; `graph-sync` with `\"wait\":\ntrue` when the run finished in time |\n\n- **`idempotency.rs`**:\n- parses the header (1–255 visible ASCII, else 400 `invalid_argument`)\nand declares it in OpenAPI;\n  - every 202 route passes it to studio-tasks;\n  - notify''s body field `idempotency_key` is replaced by the header;\n  - scheduler run-now scopes the key per schedule.\n- **`tasks::service`**:\n  - attaches a key to the unkeyed queued run it coalesces into;\n  - does not coalesce into a run held under a different key;\n  - 3 Postgres tests in `tasks/service_tests.rs`.\n- **Consumers**:\n- projects-mfe adds the header through a `RestPlugin` and reads\n`run_id`;\n- the prototype sends it on notify, analyze, syncs and run-now, and\ntypes the 204s as `void`;\n- theia''s analyze client sends it, falling back to `getRandomValues`\nwhere `randomUUID` is missing;\n- the desktop `/studio-api` proxy forwards it (the only header\nallow-list found; CORS is off in every profile, and nginx passes headers\nthrough).\n\n## 2. `chore` — code cites current ADR numbers, stale comments fixed\n(`6ad9e0a1`)\n\n- **Old numbers.** After the ADR trees were unified, code still cited\nold numbers. Each citation was read in context:\n  - Theia bridge → ADR-0022 (41 sites);\n  - canonical user → ADR-0023 (9);\n  - person resolver → ADR-0025 (12);\n  - push channel → ADR-0026 (1).\n- **Wrong citations.** Citations of records that never said what the\ncomment claims were re-targeted (access config/PDP → ADR-0009, project\nwizard → ADR-0028) or dropped. gearbox-studio''s own ADRs now carry their\ncpt ids.\n- **Comments that drifted from the code:**\n  - presence notes wait for the next heartbeat;\n  - an event''s `seq` is a durable per-tenant cursor;\n- the default Theia sink is `StudioEventsSink`, in code and in the\nbridge docs;\n- the reports `/sync` description names `organization_id` (ADR-0033\namendment);\n- workbook, `repo_enrich`, `normalize_alias` and the domain-model route\ndocs.\n- **ADR index:** no longer lists ADR-0031 twice.\n- **No behaviour change.**\n\n## Verified\n\nOn commit 1:\n- **Backend:**\n  - `cargo fmt --check`, `cargo clippy --all-targets -D warnings`;\n  - `cargo test --locked` 1286 passed, 0 failed;\n  - `cargo test api_contract` 3 passed;\n  - `api-contract.json` regenerated.\n- **Contract check:** `node scripts/check-api-usage.mjs` OK (156 calls,\n1 known break).\n- **Prototype:** `tsc -b`; vitest 292 passed.\n- **studio-frontend:** `npm run test:unit` green except the known\nlocal-only `overlayContract.test.ts`, which needs built MFE manifests.\n- **Theia:** jest 73 passed in the five touched suites.\n\nAfter the second commit was added on top: clippy clean, check-api-usage\nOK, prototype `tsc -b` OK. The full local test run was cut short by the\nmachine running out of memory, so CI is the authority for the combined\nbranch.\n\n## Not done here\n\n- `theia/studio` `tsc --noEmit` reports four Uint8Array/Buffer typing\nerrors. None is on a changed line; they were not checked against a clean\nmain.\n- `graph-sync`''s body accepts a `tenant` field, which breaks C1 (the\ntenant never comes from the API).\n- Next PR: mechanise H1 in `api_contract.rs`.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n* Background-work requests now support idempotency keys, helping retries\nreuse queued work instead of creating duplicates.\n* Queued sync responses use `run_id` for tracking, and several creation\nand queued-work operations now return more specific HTTP status codes.\n* **Bug Fixes**\n* Deletion and sign-out operations now return empty `204 No Content`\nresponses; membership-removal counts are no longer included in the\nresponse.\n* API guidance and examples now reflect updated response formats and\nretry behavior.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxPZOCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAnYEQAIC+SEzOxJBEAPvzrVUyqd/p\nCXRlE1e3MMUW16EU8z4a0E7i+tlRQ2OdJhvGMl3Gpu0YyvYPrausm/qeBcn+KajL\n5nd0XWtTdSKpeGVS89xnp+3y/AbNxBvlfJD4gUk9TmSwq4K4ArZ254Z+Vg9Qgo5a\nYbAkXcsFFBsIK0fFM+p2I5GJdVeNL005Dc4+4k2AmJ5q6r+15dc6fl5shc919Ihv\n64B2UbCf4A5zpV8vPMJg6c6f1ZJEGiaXSCea1f5oOGMt4smIwSp8MzOVqEwg71kE\nnBmKPw2sNTxwUUwPjobwDfSuFfITYZuNTptw0nPC5ybkrmS47dDG0r9jQs9ivYLw\nBc4Hb2VnNhDzImoy9WyXOmSz4D3iKD5MWJlz/adbQiwFvG7tLopzHqbTk0uWbER1\nPr5nMY6Z1VIq0iSAAEIrOXNCv5+qLB+/vut24gvEXNi2Zf0QItTaRaTOlk0tYKE7\nURb+G+5c1SXqHrGE7RyW5HCiZ6mjyzXbcelnFpYCxqzE+WcznIaVYECG0RDGwd6w\noYZAT3MXuxTzJUgaiCiIIK4gB4WUnqzV49EcJ/HYRkv7WMv2MbAAHztfi3i4lX1a\n4WMxvBMt0Zk9GDaJw4QN68mc+8d1Fg7/znDG4QAU16e1qMoGJv0CEwPFxekWO79d\n4vINdh0Rmf8PFsZ1kdn6\n=3bc4\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T13:23:27Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/48b4c075d73a7a36d21a77a6b95d571dad580e99","node_id":"C_kwDOTl7dJtoAKDQ4YjRjMDc1ZDczYTdhMzZkMjFhNzdhNmI5NWQ1NzFkYWQ1ODBlOTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/827a33b80b28c05806c03cf240c99732017bcb54","sha":"827a33b80b28c05806c03cf240c99732017bcb54","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/827a33b80b28c05806c03cf240c99732017bcb54"}],"sha":"48b4c075d73a7a36d21a77a6b95d571dad580e99","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/48b4c075d73a7a36d21a77a6b95d571dad580e99"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/301748190?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AndrejK666","id":301748190,"login":"AndrejK666","node_id":"U_kgDOEfxP3g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/827a33b80b28c05806c03cf240c99732017bcb54/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T13:00:19Z","email":"Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech","name":"ANDREI KUCHMA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T13:00:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(catalogue): repository gears are found by their gear.gdl, and an engine plugin by `implements` (#630)\n\ngears-rust is retiring its `gear.toml` files into `gear.gdl`\n(constructorfabric/gears-rust#4793), and the Gearbox engine is renaming\n`fills` to `implements` in the same move (constructorfabric/gearbox#2).\nStudio reads both, and in both places the change would have gone silent\nrather than failing:\n\n- **Repository scan.** The catalogue found repository gears only by\n`gear.toml`. After #4793 merges, a scan of gears-rust would find no\ngears,\n  so every repository field (description, category, plugins, documents,\n  owners) would drop out of the catalogue.\n- **Engine catalogue.** `EngineGear.fills` is `#[serde(default)]`. Once\nthe\nengine pin moves past gearbox#2, every plugin would deserialize as a\nplain\n  gear: no host, no grouping, and nothing added by `complete()`.\n\n## What changes\n\n**Gear discovery reads `gear.gdl` as well as `gear.toml`**\n(`repo_enrich.rs`).\n- A gear directory is any directory holding a `gear.toml` or a\n`gear.gdl`.\n- A `gear.gdl` usually sits inside the crate\n(`gears/bss/ledger/ledger/gear.gdl`).\nWhen its directory is named like its parent, the parent is the gear, so\nthe\ngear keeps its docs, its SDK and its directory (same rule\n`primary_crate`\n  already uses).\n- A `gear.gdl` under `src/` is a plugin compiled into its host''s crate\n(mini-chat). It is not catalogued as a component, but its `implements`\nstill\n  counts toward the host''s `plugins`.\n- A `gear.gdl` under `examples/` is skipped, as before.\n- The fields are read from the gdl by a small parser: `description`,\n`category`, `maturity` (new field), `implements` (or `fills`), and every\n  `extension_point(...)` spec. Comments and nested calls are ignored. A\n  `gear.toml` beside the gdl fills whatever the gdl leaves out; Studio''s\n  skeleton still writes both, because the engine''s scaffolded gdl has no\n  description.\n- `plugins` for a gdl gear means another gear in the repository\nimplements one\nof its points. A gdl does not state it itself, the way `has_plugins`\ndid.\n- A gear that declares its own extension point counts as a host even\nwhen it\n  also implements another gear''s point (rate-provider).\n\n**Taxonomy names the file it read.** The reason line says `a gear.gdl at\n…`\ninstead of always `a gear.toml at …` (`manifest` field; older profiles\nwithout it still read `gear.toml`).\n\n**Engine catalogue:** `fills` also accepts `implements`.\n\n**Engine source:** the three Dockerfiles fetch from\n`constructorfabric/gearbox` (Apache-2.0) instead of\n`MikeFalcon77/gearbox`.\nThe pin stays at `55f7015`, which the org repository contains. Moving\nthe pin\npast gearbox#2 is a separate PR, after it merges.\n\n## Checked\n\n- `cargo fmt --check`, `cargo clippy --all-targets -D warnings`,\n`cargo check --no-default-features`, and `cargo test components_catalog`\n  all pass in the CI image.\n- I ran the real discovery and parser (a temporary test, not committed)\n  over the actual tree of gears-rust#4793: 59 `gear.gdl` files and their\n  `Cargo.toml`/docs.\n  - **55 gears.** Every one of the 42 `gear.toml` directories on main is\n    found at the same path; nothing is lost.\n- **13 gained.** github-mirror, graph-storage, and 11 plugins that never\n    had a `gear.toml`.\n  - Every gear has a description, a category and a maturity.\n  - The crate names resolve as before.\n- `plugins: yes` for the 10 hosts with real implementations, mini-chat''s\n    in-crate ones included.\n\n## Known difference after #4793 merges\n\nThirteen gears said `has_plugins = true` in `gear.toml` but declare no\nextension point in their `gear.gdl`, for example chat-engine,\nfile-storage,\ncluster, event-broker, oagw, and the design-only gears. The fact is no\nlonger\nin the repository, so their `plugins` cell will be empty. That is the\nsource\nchanging, not the scan.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n* Component catalogs can now discover gears from either `gear.toml` or\n`gear.gdl`, including nested GDL files alongside a gear’s crate.\n* Catalog entries can use GDL descriptions, categories, maturity, and\nextension-point details, with missing values filled from TOML metadata.\n* Engine gear definitions using `implements` are now recognized, and\nplugin associations are determined from matching extension-point\nspecifications.\n* **Documentation**\n  * Updated Gearbox links to point to the current repository.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","tree":{"sha":"461f8191a9c05fd843d863ee85efe8c1c4ed9917","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/trees/461f8191a9c05fd843d863ee85efe8c1c4ed9917"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/commits/827a33b80b28c05806c03cf240c99732017bcb54","verification":{"payload":"tree 461f8191a9c05fd843d863ee85efe8c1c4ed9917\nparent 4818cbd4ac5f6f7ef90e9d12022f87091b21d39e\nauthor ANDREI KUCHMA <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech> 1791291619 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791291619 +0200\n\nfix(catalogue): repository gears are found by their gear.gdl, and an engine plugin by `implements` (#630)\n\ngears-rust is retiring its `gear.toml` files into `gear.gdl`\n(constructorfabric/gears-rust#4793), and the Gearbox engine is renaming\n`fills` to `implements` in the same move (constructorfabric/gearbox#2).\nStudio reads both, and in both places the change would have gone silent\nrather than failing:\n\n- **Repository scan.** The catalogue found repository gears only by\n`gear.toml`. After #4793 merges, a scan of gears-rust would find no\ngears,\n  so every repository field (description, category, plugins, documents,\n  owners) would drop out of the catalogue.\n- **Engine catalogue.** `EngineGear.fills` is `#[serde(default)]`. Once\nthe\nengine pin moves past gearbox#2, every plugin would deserialize as a\nplain\n  gear: no host, no grouping, and nothing added by `complete()`.\n\n## What changes\n\n**Gear discovery reads `gear.gdl` as well as `gear.toml`**\n(`repo_enrich.rs`).\n- A gear directory is any directory holding a `gear.toml` or a\n`gear.gdl`.\n- A `gear.gdl` usually sits inside the crate\n(`gears/bss/ledger/ledger/gear.gdl`).\nWhen its directory is named like its parent, the parent is the gear, so\nthe\ngear keeps its docs, its SDK and its directory (same rule\n`primary_crate`\n  already uses).\n- A `gear.gdl` under `src/` is a plugin compiled into its host''s crate\n(mini-chat). It is not catalogued as a component, but its `implements`\nstill\n  counts toward the host''s `plugins`.\n- A `gear.gdl` under `examples/` is skipped, as before.\n- The fields are read from the gdl by a small parser: `description`,\n`category`, `maturity` (new field), `implements` (or `fills`), and every\n  `extension_point(...)` spec. Comments and nested calls are ignored. A\n  `gear.toml` beside the gdl fills whatever the gdl leaves out; Studio''s\n  skeleton still writes both, because the engine''s scaffolded gdl has no\n  description.\n- `plugins` for a gdl gear means another gear in the repository\nimplements one\nof its points. A gdl does not state it itself, the way `has_plugins`\ndid.\n- A gear that declares its own extension point counts as a host even\nwhen it\n  also implements another gear''s point (rate-provider).\n\n**Taxonomy names the file it read.** The reason line says `a gear.gdl at\n…`\ninstead of always `a gear.toml at …` (`manifest` field; older profiles\nwithout it still read `gear.toml`).\n\n**Engine catalogue:** `fills` also accepts `implements`.\n\n**Engine source:** the three Dockerfiles fetch from\n`constructorfabric/gearbox` (Apache-2.0) instead of\n`MikeFalcon77/gearbox`.\nThe pin stays at `55f7015`, which the org repository contains. Moving\nthe pin\npast gearbox#2 is a separate PR, after it merges.\n\n## Checked\n\n- `cargo fmt --check`, `cargo clippy --all-targets -D warnings`,\n`cargo check --no-default-features`, and `cargo test components_catalog`\n  all pass in the CI image.\n- I ran the real discovery and parser (a temporary test, not committed)\n  over the actual tree of gears-rust#4793: 59 `gear.gdl` files and their\n  `Cargo.toml`/docs.\n  - **55 gears.** Every one of the 42 `gear.toml` directories on main is\n    found at the same path; nothing is lost.\n- **13 gained.** github-mirror, graph-storage, and 11 plugins that never\n    had a `gear.toml`.\n  - Every gear has a description, a category and a maturity.\n  - The crate names resolve as before.\n- `plugins: yes` for the 10 hosts with real implementations, mini-chat''s\n    in-crate ones included.\n\n## Known difference after #4793 merges\n\nThirteen gears said `has_plugins = true` in `gear.toml` but declare no\nextension point in their `gear.gdl`, for example chat-engine,\nfile-storage,\ncluster, event-broker, oagw, and the design-only gears. The fact is no\nlonger\nin the repository, so their `plugins` cell will be empty. That is the\nsource\nchanging, not the scan.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n* Component catalogs can now discover gears from either `gear.toml` or\n`gear.gdl`, including nested GDL files alongside a gear’s crate.\n* Catalog entries can use GDL descriptions, categories, maturity, and\nextension-point details, with missing values filled from TOML metadata.\n* Engine gear definitions using `implements` are now recognized, and\nplugin associations are determined from matching extension-point\nspecifications.\n* **Documentation**\n  * Updated Gearbox links to point to the current repository.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxPDjCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAuJIQADA4E0WpilWreIVX3NDZBV15\n1ly0pDCzYlivPUM61GXeylu61LnbKYk8DnywwZ5KXskVrU6d1+nQKQ5Bbe8n7iuE\ndoZEpkVTxREDk3Xx0bx5hs4QbhPBcNjqWDefi0dpU+8f1C9f8gEMjqcLyQzwXlfe\n6qKRZZShBXqHkryVxeGEZ836x74CyJ13m4DA/xNj+m6vUxjN5tlSSa3dUhOrB5Pv\n0xqJdhZDqJrTiQ6DWCD0JOxB0Ln0zaQ9Zep1ukYJVF/nQrwSKWqr23Sb9mDN16sr\n6HTXyUwieoaC/ZVp+UStkud7uE1aIC2IpsM4GsW9PwJyH/+I7U8mliNrNA4Bd7Hv\nnqBL8bbFozYHq0fUFpA8OOm+QRD51PvmleoEJ0x8xJpFHEa8Xn/4h71nKlrFdfMA\nrsw2aZ5e9OsDGqGX95wpm/CqfvmM3RxfexhVSWzrpnb+VNQ8252BJZwmr8GBxg7L\nRm10u/cSB56VEDNqeGi6r+da303fRmnFvmSDsat4CpSwhjEWm/7l4XtzHvfZsu0i\ngX6TzSx2D/Sb8L7oIJsQAc0EDH6/8a3KuuKdaOIUY0dOLkDM7rIipIes9wKl0lIt\nG7Sl9m17HXXHwFjTWYoZHAwaJJryuQUOSujX8+zjVzbA31ZOCCU9HzVx/KhKfHes\nHP36znJn9crnbRrT5LMM\n=dAZc\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T13:00:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/827a33b80b28c05806c03cf240c99732017bcb54","node_id":"C_kwDOTl7dJtoAKDgyN2EzM2I4MGIyOGMwNTgwNmMwM2NmMjQwYzk5NzMyMDE3YmNiNTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/4818cbd4ac5f6f7ef90e9d12022f87091b21d39e","sha":"4818cbd4ac5f6f7ef90e9d12022f87091b21d39e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/4818cbd4ac5f6f7ef90e9d12022f87091b21d39e"}],"sha":"827a33b80b28c05806c03cf240c99732017bcb54","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/827a33b80b28c05806c03cf240c99732017bcb54"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/301748190?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AndrejK666","id":301748190,"login":"AndrejK666","node_id":"U_kgDOEfxP3g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/4818cbd4ac5f6f7ef90e9d12022f87091b21d39e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T12:59:45Z","email":"Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech","name":"ANDREI KUCHMA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T12:59:45Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(people): a member row opens into every identity the person holds (#629)\n\n## Why\n\nOn Dev the members screen of Constructor Fabric listed all 11 people as\n`Person <id>`. Every assignment from the identity directory provisioned\nthe person with no name and no e-mail (`record_assignment` passed `None,\nNone`), which is the pitfall `organization-people.md` §7 warns about.\nThe screen also had no way to see how a person signs in, or which\nexternal accounts are attributed to them.\n\n## What\n\n**studio-user**\n- `GET\n/studio-user/v1/organizations/{org_id}/members/{user_id}/identities`\nreturns `{ user_id, logins[], aliases[] }`.\n  - Gated on `people.view`, like the member list.\n  - Answers `404` for somebody who is not in the organization.\n- Reads Studio''s own records only. The IdP reader stays \"about the\nsigned-in person alone\", so an owner cannot use this to enumerate realm\naccounts.\n- `AssignmentRecorder::record_assignment` takes the IdP''s `display_name`\nand `email`. A new person is named with them, and an existing profile\nonly gets its blanks filled; a name the person set themselves is never\noverwritten.\n\n**identity-directory**\n- `assign` reads the name and e-mail off the representation it already\nfetches.\n- The membership backfill passes the directory''s name, so re-running it\nnames the people assigned before this change.\n\n**prototype**\n- The members table''s ▸ unfolds two tables:\n  - **Sign-in identities**: provider, subject, verified, when linked.\n- **Attributed accounts**: kind, account, confidence, whether activity\ncounts as theirs.\n- A platform admin also sees the directory''s account for each Keycloak\nlogin: name, username, e-mail, the broker it came through, and the\ndirectory status.\n\n**Specs**\n- New flow `cpt-studiofrontend-flow-organization-people-identities` and\nacceptance criteria in `organization-people.md`.\n- The route is added to the `studio-user.md` route table.\n- The route breaks C1 `scope-in-path` exactly as its sibling\n`/organizations/{org_id}/members` does, so it joins that sibling in the\nbaseline rather than reshaping the whole group in this PR.\n\n## Verified\n\n- `cargo fmt --check` and `clippy -D warnings` are clean.\n- `cargo test -- user_profile identity_directory api_contract`: 75\npassed, 3 of them new.\n- Prototype: `tsc -b` passes, vitest 290/290, `check-docs.mjs` passes.\n- Standalone stand (postgres profile, static tokens), real requests:\n  - `200` with logins and aliases;\n  - `404` for a non-member;\n  - `403 ORG_OWNER_REQUIRED` for a non-owner.\n- Real UI in headless Chrome against that stand: rows unfold, the inner\nrows are 34 px (I fixed an inherited `.ptable tbody tr { height: 4rem\n}`), and there is no sideways scroll at 1500 or 390 px.\n\n**Not verified:**\n- The directory column for a platform admin: the stand has no Keycloak.\n- Naming through a real Keycloak assignment: covered by unit tests only.\n\n## After deploy\n\nThe 11 people on Dev keep their blank profiles until a platform admin\nruns `POST /cf/studio-identity/v1/memberships/backfill` once.\n\n\n---\n\n## Second commit: the identity directory screen\n\nThree ways the directory misled a platform administrator:\n\n**The Studio Admin row offered \"Update\" into an organization.**\n- What went wrong: the admin''s home is the platform root, and the root\nis not in the picker. The select fell back to the first organization, so\nthe button would have moved the admin there as a member.\n- Fix: the row now says the person administers every organization.\n- Fix: `assign` refuses a platform administrator with `400\nPLATFORM_ADMIN_NOT_ASSIGNABLE`, checked by root membership as in\nADR-0018.\n\n**Re-assigning an admin demoted them.**\n- What went wrong: the role picker offered only Owner and Member.\n- Fix: assignment takes `owner | admin | member`, the same set a\nmembership takes.\n\n**ACCESS showed IdP attributes as if they were access.**\n- What went wrong: the `tenant_id` and `studio_organization_role`\nattributes are never rewritten by a change on the People screen.\n- Fix: each identity carries `memberships[]` from studio-user, read\nthrough the new `OrganizationReader::memberships_of_subject`, which\nnever provisions.\n- Fix: `status` derives from those memberships.\n- Fix: the screen notes where Keycloak still says otherwise.\n- When studio-user cannot be asked, the screen falls back to the\nattributes and labels them \"per Keycloak\".\n\n**Pickers.**\n- They start from where the person belongs, never silently from the\nfirst organization.\n- Update stays disabled until something changes.\n\n### Verified\n- `cargo fmt --check` and `clippy -D warnings` are clean.\n- 76 tests pass, including\n`the_status_is_where_studio_says_somebody_belongs`.\n- `tsc -b` passes, vitest 290/290, `check-docs.mjs` passes.\n- Stand, real requests:\n  - assigning the platform admin → `400 PLATFORM_ADMIN_NOT_ASSIGNABLE`;\n- `role: admin` passes validation and reaches the Keycloak step (`503`\nthere, since the stand has no Keycloak);\n  - `role: boss` → `400`.\n- Real UI in headless Chrome, with `/studio-identity/v1/users` stubbed\nin the new response shape:\n  - the admin row has no controls;\n  - Admin is offered and preselected;\n- drift is shown (\"Keycloak still says Member\", and \"still names … as\nhome\" for a suspended member);\n- a newcomer starts on \"Choose organization…\" with Assign disabled;\nafter picking an organization, Assign posts `{tenant_id, role}`.\n\n**Not verified live:** the directory listing against a real Keycloak\nplus studio-user. The response shape was stubbed.\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","tree":{"sha":"f00926305dd67eea4a94b0a62c76cb465545f0e9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/trees/f00926305dd67eea4a94b0a62c76cb465545f0e9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/commits/4818cbd4ac5f6f7ef90e9d12022f87091b21d39e","verification":{"payload":"tree f00926305dd67eea4a94b0a62c76cb465545f0e9\nparent bd9fe80497ff8c4c62f62cf19617e02d8338db71\nauthor ANDREI KUCHMA <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech> 1791291585 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791291585 +0200\n\nfeat(people): a member row opens into every identity the person holds (#629)\n\n## Why\n\nOn Dev the members screen of Constructor Fabric listed all 11 people as\n`Person <id>`. Every assignment from the identity directory provisioned\nthe person with no name and no e-mail (`record_assignment` passed `None,\nNone`), which is the pitfall `organization-people.md` §7 warns about.\nThe screen also had no way to see how a person signs in, or which\nexternal accounts are attributed to them.\n\n## What\n\n**studio-user**\n- `GET\n/studio-user/v1/organizations/{org_id}/members/{user_id}/identities`\nreturns `{ user_id, logins[], aliases[] }`.\n  - Gated on `people.view`, like the member list.\n  - Answers `404` for somebody who is not in the organization.\n- Reads Studio''s own records only. The IdP reader stays \"about the\nsigned-in person alone\", so an owner cannot use this to enumerate realm\naccounts.\n- `AssignmentRecorder::record_assignment` takes the IdP''s `display_name`\nand `email`. A new person is named with them, and an existing profile\nonly gets its blanks filled; a name the person set themselves is never\noverwritten.\n\n**identity-directory**\n- `assign` reads the name and e-mail off the representation it already\nfetches.\n- The membership backfill passes the directory''s name, so re-running it\nnames the people assigned before this change.\n\n**prototype**\n- The members table''s ▸ unfolds two tables:\n  - **Sign-in identities**: provider, subject, verified, when linked.\n- **Attributed accounts**: kind, account, confidence, whether activity\ncounts as theirs.\n- A platform admin also sees the directory''s account for each Keycloak\nlogin: name, username, e-mail, the broker it came through, and the\ndirectory status.\n\n**Specs**\n- New flow `cpt-studiofrontend-flow-organization-people-identities` and\nacceptance criteria in `organization-people.md`.\n- The route is added to the `studio-user.md` route table.\n- The route breaks C1 `scope-in-path` exactly as its sibling\n`/organizations/{org_id}/members` does, so it joins that sibling in the\nbaseline rather than reshaping the whole group in this PR.\n\n## Verified\n\n- `cargo fmt --check` and `clippy -D warnings` are clean.\n- `cargo test -- user_profile identity_directory api_contract`: 75\npassed, 3 of them new.\n- Prototype: `tsc -b` passes, vitest 290/290, `check-docs.mjs` passes.\n- Standalone stand (postgres profile, static tokens), real requests:\n  - `200` with logins and aliases;\n  - `404` for a non-member;\n  - `403 ORG_OWNER_REQUIRED` for a non-owner.\n- Real UI in headless Chrome against that stand: rows unfold, the inner\nrows are 34 px (I fixed an inherited `.ptable tbody tr { height: 4rem\n}`), and there is no sideways scroll at 1500 or 390 px.\n\n**Not verified:**\n- The directory column for a platform admin: the stand has no Keycloak.\n- Naming through a real Keycloak assignment: covered by unit tests only.\n\n## After deploy\n\nThe 11 people on Dev keep their blank profiles until a platform admin\nruns `POST /cf/studio-identity/v1/memberships/backfill` once.\n\n\n---\n\n## Second commit: the identity directory screen\n\nThree ways the directory misled a platform administrator:\n\n**The Studio Admin row offered \"Update\" into an organization.**\n- What went wrong: the admin''s home is the platform root, and the root\nis not in the picker. The select fell back to the first organization, so\nthe button would have moved the admin there as a member.\n- Fix: the row now says the person administers every organization.\n- Fix: `assign` refuses a platform administrator with `400\nPLATFORM_ADMIN_NOT_ASSIGNABLE`, checked by root membership as in\nADR-0018.\n\n**Re-assigning an admin demoted them.**\n- What went wrong: the role picker offered only Owner and Member.\n- Fix: assignment takes `owner | admin | member`, the same set a\nmembership takes.\n\n**ACCESS showed IdP attributes as if they were access.**\n- What went wrong: the `tenant_id` and `studio_organization_role`\nattributes are never rewritten by a change on the People screen.\n- Fix: each identity carries `memberships[]` from studio-user, read\nthrough the new `OrganizationReader::memberships_of_subject`, which\nnever provisions.\n- Fix: `status` derives from those memberships.\n- Fix: the screen notes where Keycloak still says otherwise.\n- When studio-user cannot be asked, the screen falls back to the\nattributes and labels them \"per Keycloak\".\n\n**Pickers.**\n- They start from where the person belongs, never silently from the\nfirst organization.\n- Update stays disabled until something changes.\n\n### Verified\n- `cargo fmt --check` and `clippy -D warnings` are clean.\n- 76 tests pass, including\n`the_status_is_where_studio_says_somebody_belongs`.\n- `tsc -b` passes, vitest 290/290, `check-docs.mjs` passes.\n- Stand, real requests:\n  - assigning the platform admin → `400 PLATFORM_ADMIN_NOT_ASSIGNABLE`;\n- `role: admin` passes validation and reaches the Keycloak step (`503`\nthere, since the stand has no Keycloak);\n  - `role: boss` → `400`.\n- Real UI in headless Chrome, with `/studio-identity/v1/users` stubbed\nin the new response shape:\n  - the admin row has no controls;\n  - Admin is offered and preselected;\n- drift is shown (\"Keycloak still says Member\", and \"still names … as\nhome\" for a suspended member);\n- a newcomer starts on \"Choose organization…\" with Assign disabled;\nafter picking an organization, Assign posts `{tenant_id, role}`.\n\n**Not verified live:** the directory listing against a real Keycloak\nplus studio-user. The response shape was stubbed.\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxPDBCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAY9wQAFyo4N7acUOWDX1xUN6+/gbt\n5HgjcP3jH3weP7RXLwxkNb8sIplAS042rMcrNdSPpxCg3zo/Wa9AKANo0ncU2XFI\n8hFp51BusH0QvSWY4KSz8Ne/gzZWwpeSbhQruZwVrHC7ni9t2wFFrohld+5VXJsj\ntin6jI4BLVPpMBZZKJ5hJ4qBc9qY+P5wjE2bsX02eEeVga3a6pOGKHNnQMLEvu66\nmgi4LSBd513Ru1ImNW5F8Vi5XCn5tsYQAmr2z/QODMv6XIVNxCoZNBO6Lx2bZV2t\nRVbuq6lqnFwFVJh5zH3lV2S5rLR4P8FpwEAPHMqFX+o96t5/Bsr9tnO3+LtvIcrN\nLXxM9Qm/HB2Jg7f4qPDZZ9BBrLn8dryBlxKl48meGqLSmWEJ1rwf5jPfGSIOQy5y\njz1qMKFL2nG8wGM+CZdice38s85JdbTqhjZXhezYOFNGj7QPVBRmWkGDiTeESuHa\ny01enqqBlA5wSJWnjAlqx/SPwb2tZ1cYkhNFdHLO6rLtIIBM69R6KXyG9wMa+TZv\nwKHOielnjqLsye7/e31ZTtIq3Rpe/2nypJom5S5rJciAnonTGfuseN5NrZDk1jiF\nv62HIoddo9zYEsFV3pZ+ag22DGDxXVFlBFd6XqVXXWQiRXlceaUUKlvBA1nNmM7S\nisaYtiw+xtEtOfiQSNtl\n=DDwB\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T12:59:54Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/4818cbd4ac5f6f7ef90e9d12022f87091b21d39e","node_id":"C_kwDOTl7dJtoAKDQ4MThjYmQ0YWM1ZjZmN2VmOTBlOWQxMjAyMmY4NzA5MWIyMWQzOWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/bd9fe80497ff8c4c62f62cf19617e02d8338db71","sha":"bd9fe80497ff8c4c62f62cf19617e02d8338db71","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/bd9fe80497ff8c4c62f62cf19617e02d8338db71"}],"sha":"4818cbd4ac5f6f7ef90e9d12022f87091b21d39e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/4818cbd4ac5f6f7ef90e9d12022f87091b21d39e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/301748190?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AndrejK666","id":301748190,"login":"AndrejK666","node_id":"U_kgDOEfxP3g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/bd9fe80497ff8c4c62f62cf19617e02d8338db71/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T12:43:30Z","email":"Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech","name":"ANDREI KUCHMA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T12:43:30Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: studio-backend/docs is sorted into what is kept, what is asked and what is history (#628)\n\nStacked on #627 (and #625). Until those merge, the diff includes their\ncommits; review `e93f287a` alone.\n\n`studio-backend/docs/` held 22 documents of four kinds side by side, and\nnothing said which were current. They are now sorted:\n\n| Where | What | Kept current? |\n|---|---|---|\n| `docs/` (in the index) | background work, queued notifications,\nnotification connectors, Theia bridge architecture and local run,\ngraph-storage API/quickstart/handover, Insight quickstart | yes |\n| `docs/upstream/` (new index) | graph-storage and account-management\nrequests, gears-rust and spec-quality issue drafts | yes — the status of\neach ask |\n| `docs/inbox/` (new index) | the graph-storage stand report,\nintegration no. 3 (RU), sent Discord/PR/bug drafts | no — history, cited\nor possibly wanted again |\n| `studio-backend/docs/` | `api-contract.json`, its baseline,\n`gts-types.json`, `architecture/` | read by tests and tools |\n\nEvery reference follows the move: code comments, READMEs,\n`studio-backend/AGENTS.md`, ADR-0019/0020, the gear designs and\n`scripts/insight-smoke.sh`, which re-runs the quickstart''s SQL.\n\n`check-docs.mjs` reads the two new indexes. Its dangling-id rule now\napplies only to the id systems this repository defines, so a citation of\nanother project''s spec (`cpt-cf-evbk-…`) is not an error.\n\nVerified: `node scripts/check-docs.mjs` — 121 documents, 665 ids, clean;\n`bash -n scripts/insight-smoke.sh`.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Documentation**\n* Expanded the documentation index with links to guides, runbooks,\nplatform requests, and archived materials.\n* Added indexes that clarify where to find current platform requests and\nhistorical records.\n* Updated documentation links across project guides and backend\nreferences to point to their current locations.\n* **Chores**\n* Improved documentation checks to recognize additional indexes and\nvalidate citations only for IDs defined in the repository.\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","tree":{"sha":"5ab83667aabd0d7bbced89616b99c1ed21a11139","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/trees/5ab83667aabd0d7bbced89616b99c1ed21a11139"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/commits/bd9fe80497ff8c4c62f62cf1