es, runbooks,\nplatform requests, and archived materials.\n* Added indexes that clarify where to find current platform requests and\nhistorical records.\n* Updated documentation links across project guides and backend\nreferences to point to their current locations.\n* **Chores**\n* Improved documentation checks to recognize additional indexes and\nvalidate citations only for IDs defined in the repository.\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxOzyCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZrUQAKDDFfEpInY3udDkMRqKlMXo\nGy2gkeNQw/86CwdkdWLP0741WC91/SfirgEPB8kcn+hnvS6hp+p37B/QAcqho5W4\nEU2KC5yMxJ6bIWrVj7n7fBnwf5riPCk9onlcdANuTMgDgDFqt/bcQODcLao/XJKO\nzClw8/I2eAveZtXSnbRzsBJwpJ7itO2R9Krz+4SbdUDDGgdz9gZFIDYnPnVcVbys\n1YXgH7NF91jhjHi2CZajxxnqGXbeRbgMlIh4hm08hYmcWGtu4RBd7jj7V1wQa4ju\nTehOHPe7HtpWWDfTffQg60vnBmbo2vvVdmcG3boslWtxAJup010pNsRJdCCH7lTN\ntZ2yzNzCUKZncPq/o2ikjDN3s23pFedhTQTuNAJ7DnFsqBuNHhipRr4IYi4WtgNn\n6f23sHbz2v2lwOOi/ReiRVSAj1X9uhvsLgBrkdos4A7JT3DwQIyMucOw9R3ZbeFG\nbtxYap9144/9bN9iL80gbVMhpGm0CGeUbE749J95NJ6jpH4RM7U6pUB2d5vn25aL\nRyI7WIRw35O5c4lcmCz8Kn3JW3RSBvJKdjlHsdJH/wCSN3ANYHku0TEUtQdblyIm\nCLE3HusS7IYGYFsJylgENh+2zTCqUi+okgvQ98Bq3k27kn+VHaLiquP43oURetZF\nR2oVpH185r7TcaQR1oJP\n=79k2\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T12:43:31Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/bd9fe80497ff8c4c62f62cf19617e02d8338db71","node_id":"C_kwDOTl7dJtoAKGJkOWZlODA0OTdmZjhjNGM2MmY2MmNmMTk2MTdlMDJkODMzOGRiNzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/f0eba201ed4145dcbe0b10d6958f2845b033564e","sha":"f0eba201ed4145dcbe0b10d6958f2845b033564e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/f0eba201ed4145dcbe0b10d6958f2845b033564e"}],"sha":"bd9fe80497ff8c4c62f62cf19617e02d8338db71","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/bd9fe80497ff8c4c62f62cf19617e02d8338db71"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/301748190?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AndrejK666","id":301748190,"login":"AndrejK666","node_id":"U_kgDOEfxP3g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/f0eba201ed4145dcbe0b10d6958f2845b033564e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T07:52:34Z","email":"Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech","name":"ANDREI KUCHMA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T07:52:34Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: every backend gear has its own design, and the product design is an overview again (#627)\n\nStacked on #625 (the docs check). Until that merges, this diff also\nshows its commit; review `54378698` alone.\n\n## What\n\n- **24 gear-level designs** in `docs/design/studio-*.md`, one per\nbackend gear, written against the design template and checked against\nthe code. Routes come from the `OperationBuilder` declarations, tables\nfrom `migrations.rs` and constants from the source.\n- **Gear READMEs** lose the architectural prose, which moved into the\ndesigns and is not copied. Each README keeps what you need to work in\nthe directory (assembly, config, tests, layout) and links to its design.\n`organizations`, `presence`, `reports`, `studio_events` and `git_proxy`\nhad no README and now have one.\n- **The product design** (`constructor-studio.md`):\n  - each §3.2 entry links to its gear design;\n- §3.7 becomes an index: every table is defined once, in its gear''s\ndesign;\n- `studio-git` and `studio-reports`, which were missing, get §3.2\nentries.\n- **PRD rationales** that cited gear READMEs now point at the designs,\nand so does `studio-backend/AGENTS.md`.\n\n## Drift corrected in the product design and PRD\n\nWriting the designs against the code turned these up:\n\n- **presence**: never used the push channel. A note waits in memory for\nthe recipient''s next heartbeat, and a note to someone offline is\nrefused. Fixed in the design and in `cpt-studio-fr-presence`.\n- **scheduler**: only UTC is accepted (`cron.rs` `check_timezone`).\nFixed in `cpt-studio-fr-schedules`.\n- **spec-quality**: routes live under `/studio-spec-quality/v1`, and\nthere is no `/tasks`.\n- **artifact-ingest**: has no `tasks` route; has `reconcile`; owns the\n`studio_artifact_index` database.\n- **documents**: file text is read from the checkout, not from the\ngraph. The \"Classify a repository''s documents\" sequence is redrawn.\n- **insight**: also pushes. Its routes are\n`components/{metrics,pull-requests}`.\n- **identity-directory**: assignment writes to Keycloak and to the\naccess config.\n- **organizations**: also deletes.\n- **authz**: the clamp covers the token''s tenant plus active\norganizations.\n- **events**: the producers are tasks and theia, not presence.\n- **session**: has desktop leases, an idle stop, and reap and readiness\nas runs.\n- **llm-proxy**: has the provider relay on the caller''s credstore key.\n- **connector**: per-connection routes corrected.\n- **notify**: also delivers to the IDE.\n- **kits**: has the desktop `materializations` route.\n- **catalogue**: has the roadmap board and its relations.\n- **§3.3**: endpoint table corrected: git, reports and desktop-sessions\nrows added, identity has no PUT, organizations has DELETE.\n\n## Found in code, not changed here\n\n- Comments in `studio_theia/` and `studio_session/` call the Theia\nbridge \"ADR-0010\"; it is ADR-0022. Old backend-tree numbers ADR-0006 and\nADR-0014 now mean ADR-0023 and ADR-0025.\n- `studio-theia` config fields `control_port` and `s2s_token_env` are\nread nowhere.\n- `studio-backend/src/artifact_ingest/object_store.rs` is not declared\nin `mod.rs`.\n- `reports/rest.rs` (`POST …/sync`) predates the ADR-0033 amendment,\nwhich requires `organization_id` in a schedule''s payload.\n- `components_catalog/repo_enrich.rs` documents `STUDIO_GEARS_CATALOG_*`\nenv vars that nothing reads.\n- `presence/mod.rs` still says notes go over studio-events.\n- `studio_events/dto.rs` still calls `seq` a per-process cursor.\nADR-0026 §4 still says one replica is needed; the `studio_events`\ndatabase supersedes that.\n- `/studio-scheduler/v1` routes are only `authenticated()`, with no role\ncheck.\n\n## Verified\n\n`node scripts/check-docs.mjs`: 91 documents, 665 ids, every spec typed,\nevery id defined once and every cited id defined, every link resolves,\nevery document indexed.\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","tree":{"sha":"cdfbd20de6f0d1691e79566e1ea554b301e54df0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/trees/cdfbd20de6f0d1691e79566e1ea554b301e54df0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/commits/f0eba201ed4145dcbe0b10d6958f2845b033564e","verification":{"payload":"tree cdfbd20de6f0d1691e79566e1ea554b301e54df0\nparent cefe287565b5202266f27a8a9bc19049e3394489\nauthor ANDREI KUCHMA <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech> 1791273154 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791273154 +0200\n\ndocs: every backend gear has its own design, and the product design is an overview again (#627)\n\nStacked on #625 (the docs check). Until that merges, this diff also\nshows its commit; review `54378698` alone.\n\n## What\n\n- **24 gear-level designs** in `docs/design/studio-*.md`, one per\nbackend gear, written against the design template and checked against\nthe code. Routes come from the `OperationBuilder` declarations, tables\nfrom `migrations.rs` and constants from the source.\n- **Gear READMEs** lose the architectural prose, which moved into the\ndesigns and is not copied. Each README keeps what you need to work in\nthe directory (assembly, config, tests, layout) and links to its design.\n`organizations`, `presence`, `reports`, `studio_events` and `git_proxy`\nhad no README and now have one.\n- **The product design** (`constructor-studio.md`):\n  - each §3.2 entry links to its gear design;\n- §3.7 becomes an index: every table is defined once, in its gear''s\ndesign;\n- `studio-git` and `studio-reports`, which were missing, get §3.2\nentries.\n- **PRD rationales** that cited gear READMEs now point at the designs,\nand so does `studio-backend/AGENTS.md`.\n\n## Drift corrected in the product design and PRD\n\nWriting the designs against the code turned these up:\n\n- **presence**: never used the push channel. A note waits in memory for\nthe recipient''s next heartbeat, and a note to someone offline is\nrefused. Fixed in the design and in `cpt-studio-fr-presence`.\n- **scheduler**: only UTC is accepted (`cron.rs` `check_timezone`).\nFixed in `cpt-studio-fr-schedules`.\n- **spec-quality**: routes live under `/studio-spec-quality/v1`, and\nthere is no `/tasks`.\n- **artifact-ingest**: has no `tasks` route; has `reconcile`; owns the\n`studio_artifact_index` database.\n- **documents**: file text is read from the checkout, not from the\ngraph. The \"Classify a repository''s documents\" sequence is redrawn.\n- **insight**: also pushes. Its routes are\n`components/{metrics,pull-requests}`.\n- **identity-directory**: assignment writes to Keycloak and to the\naccess config.\n- **organizations**: also deletes.\n- **authz**: the clamp covers the token''s tenant plus active\norganizations.\n- **events**: the producers are tasks and theia, not presence.\n- **session**: has desktop leases, an idle stop, and reap and readiness\nas runs.\n- **llm-proxy**: has the provider relay on the caller''s credstore key.\n- **connector**: per-connection routes corrected.\n- **notify**: also delivers to the IDE.\n- **kits**: has the desktop `materializations` route.\n- **catalogue**: has the roadmap board and its relations.\n- **§3.3**: endpoint table corrected: git, reports and desktop-sessions\nrows added, identity has no PUT, organizations has DELETE.\n\n## Found in code, not changed here\n\n- Comments in `studio_theia/` and `studio_session/` call the Theia\nbridge \"ADR-0010\"; it is ADR-0022. Old backend-tree numbers ADR-0006 and\nADR-0014 now mean ADR-0023 and ADR-0025.\n- `studio-theia` config fields `control_port` and `s2s_token_env` are\nread nowhere.\n- `studio-backend/src/artifact_ingest/object_store.rs` is not declared\nin `mod.rs`.\n- `reports/rest.rs` (`POST …/sync`) predates the ADR-0033 amendment,\nwhich requires `organization_id` in a schedule''s payload.\n- `components_catalog/repo_enrich.rs` documents `STUDIO_GEARS_CATALOG_*`\nenv vars that nothing reads.\n- `presence/mod.rs` still says notes go over studio-events.\n- `studio_events/dto.rs` still calls `seq` a per-process cursor.\nADR-0026 §4 still says one replica is needed; the `studio_events`\ndatabase supersedes that.\n- `/studio-scheduler/v1` routes are only `authenticated()`, with no role\ncheck.\n\n## Verified\n\n`node scripts/check-docs.mjs`: 91 documents, 665 ids, every spec typed,\nevery id defined once and every cited id defined, every link resolves,\nevery document indexed.\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxKjCCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAYyEQAA4Ro33Z4EP6Z9sHJAX7sSSL\nVFMljybhPbVLdMdyKdES4YJB6YNZWHU6FQi6iNbMX3McXIlExk2LSE7dtMfr0VZt\nEE6qOfF7MypdMg4V9gokxEn7xjkuqA9/gXNrzfv76ukzGilmVsFCDXTYJKb3i77S\nw0388ayIdJ75CKtWSJMxAhXIf72wH9rudM/xl4hCI23Af7VBCP1V8Iyzauxd/z18\nA2BGl4Bw/sWmcQhIGMLNibPGLvflASDnLjw55EtnYR1Rdigvjm/WntjvU+PZvlTT\nSbfZA+Y8V0eq/YGhkvWszHJafCZD1g4ZJBfWrhjU8K6kC5YSdT7ab7ieF8QrbP3q\nhm5ch0QX4G+qykrBUXivpNAJpI5BSMbl/pFooE7Mb6fDjfeILIxvIP7b1PPrkyJx\nB/g4mm8M4AXkcLGiz5waZn4J6vCqoTyrB37Mos6cJ9EE5OtE7dDEnROC6b41feJk\nrsbb9EYdfJ+qJvtakVGnZG9yTzSdKyhwp3k2L9rwWPTWNcwtvRArT03GlriRFaGM\nLV81BDw+aXeWKpKhGcO7/o1ZbjVirL9ySmbulnOXqr2+DSHa9k9/+JhiG0/MkeEp\nni2W0hw/+lReeIT70aOOB93u1ab2b18TiB01NYgXfwOdHTT26sfk3CbHhHCJ2BKU\n1Hu0yHXqtS3a2XZPyvQe\n=TfCD\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T07:52:35Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/f0eba201ed4145dcbe0b10d6958f2845b033564e","node_id":"C_kwDOTl7dJtoAKGYwZWJhMjAxZWQ0MTQ1ZGNiZTBiMTBkNjk1OGYyODQ1YjAzMzU2NGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/cefe287565b5202266f27a8a9bc19049e3394489","sha":"cefe287565b5202266f27a8a9bc19049e3394489","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/cefe287565b5202266f27a8a9bc19049e3394489"}],"sha":"f0eba201ed4145dcbe0b10d6958f2845b033564e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/f0eba201ed4145dcbe0b10d6958f2845b033564e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/301748190?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AndrejK666","id":301748190,"login":"AndrejK666","node_id":"U_kgDOEfxP3g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/cefe287565b5202266f27a8a9bc19049e3394489/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T07:47:30Z","email":"Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech","name":"ANDREI KUCHMA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T07:47:30Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(projects): a product project is created with its product.gdl (#626)\n\n**Goal:** the file a GDL describes exists from the moment a project is\ncreated and lives where the tools look for it; everything after that\nonly changes it.\n\n### What changes\n- **Prototype create plan, `Product from Gears`**: after the repository\nstep, two new resumable steps:\n1. **sources**: the new repository goes into `project.config.sources[]`\n(with its connection and default branch). Before this it was recorded\nonly as the project''s gear repo, and sessions, desktop and git proxy\n(which read `sources[]`) never cloned it. The same step runs for `New\nGears` projects.\n2. **product.gdl**: `POST …/product/preview {gears: [], write: true,\nonto_base: true}` commits the description onto the base branch. Its\ncheck reads `project_product.written`, so Retry does not write twice.\n- **Backend `product/preview`**: `gears: []` is accepted together with\n`write`. `Gearbox::preview` renders it against the pinned corpus and\nskips the engine, because there is nothing to resolve. A preview with no\ngears and no write is still refused.\n- The `written` record gains `path` (`product.gdl`, the root, where both\nthe portal and the IDE''s Gearbox look first). The desktop link opens\nthat path rather than assuming it.\n- Later saves on the Components tab already commit `onto_base` for a\nproduct project, so they rewrite the same file on the same branch.\n\n### Not in this PR\n- The gear constructor/scaffolding (a richer `gear.gdl` flow) is planned\nseparately. `New Gears` still scaffolds onto `scaffold/<slug>`.\n- The FrontX wizard has no project kind yet.\n\n### Verification\n- Backend: `cargo fmt --check`, `cargo clippy --all-targets -D\nwarnings`, `cargo test components_catalog` (267) and `api_contract` (3)\nall pass.\n- Prototype: `tsc -b` passes and `vitest` 282/282 passes.\n- **Not run end to end on a stand.** That needs a GitHub connection that\ncreates a real repository and a Gearbox corpus.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","tree":{"sha":"1b3ff1a6f2eb32f7382ce5afd8cd526432526d92","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/trees/1b3ff1a6f2eb32f7382ce5afd8cd526432526d92"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/commits/cefe287565b5202266f27a8a9bc19049e3394489","verification":{"payload":"tree 1b3ff1a6f2eb32f7382ce5afd8cd526432526d92\nparent 8043e23696e427ff0b0e44aee9c7c067d62df744\nauthor ANDREI KUCHMA <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech> 1791272850 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791272850 +0200\n\nfeat(projects): a product project is created with its product.gdl (#626)\n\n**Goal:** the file a GDL describes exists from the moment a project is\ncreated and lives where the tools look for it; everything after that\nonly changes it.\n\n### What changes\n- **Prototype create plan, `Product from Gears`**: after the repository\nstep, two new resumable steps:\n1. **sources**: the new repository goes into `project.config.sources[]`\n(with its connection and default branch). Before this it was recorded\nonly as the project''s gear repo, and sessions, desktop and git proxy\n(which read `sources[]`) never cloned it. The same step runs for `New\nGears` projects.\n2. **product.gdl**: `POST …/product/preview {gears: [], write: true,\nonto_base: true}` commits the description onto the base branch. Its\ncheck reads `project_product.written`, so Retry does not write twice.\n- **Backend `product/preview`**: `gears: []` is accepted together with\n`write`. `Gearbox::preview` renders it against the pinned corpus and\nskips the engine, because there is nothing to resolve. A preview with no\ngears and no write is still refused.\n- The `written` record gains `path` (`product.gdl`, the root, where both\nthe portal and the IDE''s Gearbox look first). The desktop link opens\nthat path rather than assuming it.\n- Later saves on the Components tab already commit `onto_base` for a\nproduct project, so they rewrite the same file on the same branch.\n\n### Not in this PR\n- The gear constructor/scaffolding (a richer `gear.gdl` flow) is planned\nseparately. `New Gears` still scaffolds onto `scaffold/<slug>`.\n- The FrontX wizard has no project kind yet.\n\n### Verification\n- Backend: `cargo fmt --check`, `cargo clippy --all-targets -D\nwarnings`, `cargo test components_catalog` (267) and `api_contract` (3)\nall pass.\n- Prototype: `tsc -b` passes and `vitest` 282/282 passes.\n- **Not run end to end on a stand.** That needs a GitHub connection that\ncreates a real repository and a Gearbox corpus.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxKeTCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAeegQADcmAz1erh59xqEZJbENetWv\nQ9+GQ/TLLBLhiUUwCsjfMXaLp3wKUaBIVQbCskP/SyrmdBcG6C1S/mPcX2eA5SRA\ngEHsaz7EjXr8IYHb2uNCM4bRVRdRaGeWbIfkTeN7ZNgRfxgFG3e7NmMv7+MIVgj0\nGs3ROSxsgPOTmi6Y4K6cOu4G90PypKpcavLRbX4DSBMYzyKeDtQ9ID7MWs/6cq/h\nGMttmEHJ/+IoSSO0sqdLemFLHK8a2Deqf0StIuNdliTRLMvben+vFRsZPLsjjVBU\n2AP8/y8NLRlarOjvMP0zsVCZTcgfkS6chiC3GGl2HvTais4ycRW4qzJN0fPUnHYm\nG1h0yIhUpVK38OU+92G+OrSxefWxd5zcvXEPzOWg8iCVEga1aXxPd5anIuN4arCK\npp72ORxZK6lx5p94zQROowQCBDB8N/ik78zVQVQbxPL36bjEwRKiZKXv7L4eG5nD\n1cBrc18RNeWImH7laYaoU4FgHdI03dCcCfhDwILxegb17g2lgAVCtD6dydqigHSL\n4JZeOuS+gVa77GusgUDa1ZwUs5MQJ1LvUXufygAwLs8UtvjyN1d0gXHuFh37SN48\n5ZEpCAL8hGyOxrixSLXVoLFP75N430z9IoHI9qJG+OJ58ShJGxJaKNF+ksimOBv4\n9bvzF6xczNrkzd0fqcN8\n=3MOZ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T07:47:31Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/cefe287565b5202266f27a8a9bc19049e3394489","node_id":"C_kwDOTl7dJtoAKGNlZmUyODc1NjViNTIwMjI2NmYyN2E4YTliYzE5MDQ5ZTMzOTQ0ODk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/8043e23696e427ff0b0e44aee9c7c067d62df744","sha":"8043e23696e427ff0b0e44aee9c7c067d62df744","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/8043e23696e427ff0b0e44aee9c7c067d62df744"}],"sha":"cefe287565b5202266f27a8a9bc19049e3394489","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/cefe287565b5202266f27a8a9bc19049e3394489"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/301748190?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AndrejK666","id":301748190,"login":"AndrejK666","node_id":"U_kgDOEfxP3g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/8043e23696e427ff0b0e44aee9c7c067d62df744/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T07:45:43Z","email":"Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech","name":"ANDREI KUCHMA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T07:45:43Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: every spec is typed, cited and indexed, and CI checks it (#625)\n\n## What\n\n`scripts/check-docs.mjs` (Node, no dependencies) holds `docs/` to what\nStudio''s own document pipeline assumes:\n\n- a spec under `docs/<type>/` declares that `type` in its front matter;\n- no template is published unfilled (`{Placeholder}` in the title);\n- every `cpt-` id is defined once (`**ID**:` or `**Contract**:`, as in\nthe templates) and every cited id is defined;\n- every relative link resolves;\n- every document is listed in `docs/README.md` or `docs/adr/README.md`.\n\nIt runs as a step in `test-api-usage`. That job has no path filter, so a\nPR that only touches docs is checked too, and the check costs no extra\nrunner.\n\n## What it found, fixed here\n\n- `docs/design/4444444.md` is an unfilled design template (published in\n4bccebb9) — removed.\n- `docs/design/spec-findings.md` had no type and is a proposal rather\nthan a design — moved to `docs/spec-findings.md` with the notes.\n- `feature/editor-session.md`, `feature/editor-bridge.md` and the three\n`desktop-*.md` documents were missing from the index — added.\n\nCurrent state: 67 documents, 369 ids, clean.\n\n## Verified\n\n`node scripts/check-docs.mjs` exits 0 on this branch. A seeded bad file\n(wrong type, duplicate id, dangling id, broken link, not indexed) is\nreported on all five counts and the script exits 1.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","tree":{"sha":"c3f0d569becc5c7e1a4b3069addc64e1a8631f0d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/trees/c3f0d569becc5c7e1a4b3069addc64e1a8631f0d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/commits/8043e23696e427ff0b0e44aee9c7c067d62df744","verification":{"payload":"tree c3f0d569becc5c7e1a4b3069addc64e1a8631f0d\nparent b5a17d50e4c0d71444818f3f516191cedc505268\nauthor ANDREI KUCHMA <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech> 1791272743 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791272743 +0200\n\ndocs: every spec is typed, cited and indexed, and CI checks it (#625)\n\n## What\n\n`scripts/check-docs.mjs` (Node, no dependencies) holds `docs/` to what\nStudio''s own document pipeline assumes:\n\n- a spec under `docs/<type>/` declares that `type` in its front matter;\n- no template is published unfilled (`{Placeholder}` in the title);\n- every `cpt-` id is defined once (`**ID**:` or `**Contract**:`, as in\nthe templates) and every cited id is defined;\n- every relative link resolves;\n- every document is listed in `docs/README.md` or `docs/adr/README.md`.\n\nIt runs as a step in `test-api-usage`. That job has no path filter, so a\nPR that only touches docs is checked too, and the check costs no extra\nrunner.\n\n## What it found, fixed here\n\n- `docs/design/4444444.md` is an unfilled design template (published in\n4bccebb9) — removed.\n- `docs/design/spec-findings.md` had no type and is a proposal rather\nthan a design — moved to `docs/spec-findings.md` with the notes.\n- `feature/editor-session.md`, `feature/editor-bridge.md` and the three\n`desktop-*.md` documents were missing from the index — added.\n\nCurrent state: 67 documents, 369 ids, clean.\n\n## Verified\n\n`node scripts/check-docs.mjs` exits 0 on this branch. A seeded bad file\n(wrong type, duplicate id, dangling id, broken link, not indexed) is\nreported on all five counts and the script exits 1.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxKcnCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAglIQAADoByDKbfeGDXOg1xwGkNcu\nxWOjnjgr00+yed0pfGcP5JRehKLMJQoaOGG46kPUUm1owoQtfUc9ioaWBSE+YItI\n3e/v5yZS3iFR655u0dMNCpDo1FK2ZONTMFxP7e7dnTmos72m+K++/SPERO/n8O6/\ngijXtOgi+WJTPoCV2qew9VFvolBc8mgxNTRch1Dn62FJkcAgbRRzDY8mB4R14sSA\nXYshYOThRbWDSbceE1bxFZpkffrEHpmvpywJUSGnkgCK95RWoUst2wwniQoPN+n/\nbbvqxbe/1JopLz3YYK1hhgeeYbJuWMH6mvij6mUQ/QpvbiytyWfc7JZCtDhFzt4I\nOxAEDI2QWzehYL2F1os8pplNo1Vn1QDEOIRU0gwiyeYV66i+dQbLaAy5UtHa3rjD\nSMb5Ap6vMUHgr8rgWKfDGdO0Cr1f/SffcRwIyxNhJdWflV4xIfpARZANtKzrCNuL\nGQSWkpUykc3JEfK2vKHlPh6cGEf/tKt31zRxMmpg+4d4NAR2/CCU8WIYK8jkfVwy\nM1YXuXt0J9/JorQ6FywZINlUGhd6RzI8kh7WN2w7mSNWlFBkf0sLaMfueRm+uIC3\nxJhV2HYC4w0ELYtiuaLGf6BGE1EBjsfBEPjmTHuhB4QBYlp+AhDhcRQGWin7UIJE\nUTuJWRGPMx2xMm7SI/sD\n=0MIF\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T07:45:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/8043e23696e427ff0b0e44aee9c7c067d62df744","node_id":"C_kwDOTl7dJtoAKDgwNDNlMjM2OTZlNDI3ZmYwYjBlNDRhZWU5YzdjMDY3ZDYyZGY3NDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/b5a17d50e4c0d71444818f3f516191cedc505268","sha":"b5a17d50e4c0d71444818f3f516191cedc505268","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/b5a17d50e4c0d71444818f3f516191cedc505268"}],"sha":"8043e23696e427ff0b0e44aee9c7c067d62df744","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/8043e23696e427ff0b0e44aee9c7c067d62df744"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/301748190?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AndrejK666","id":301748190,"login":"AndrejK666","node_id":"U_kgDOEfxP3g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/b5a17d50e4c0d71444818f3f516191cedc505268/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T07:45:00Z","email":"Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech","name":"ANDREI KUCHMA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T07:45:00Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Share: a project chooses per repository — commit to the branch, or a pull request (#624)\n\n## Why\n\nShare with the team pushed straight to the working branch. On a\nrepository with GitHub rulesets the push was refused (`GH013: Repository\nrule violations … Changes must be made through a pull request`,\n`Required status check \"DCO\" is expected`). Share did not recognise the\nrefusal, so instead of falling back to review it showed git''s raw error.\n\nNot every team works by committing to the branch. A project now chooses\nthis per repository, in the prototype: when it picks the repository from\na connection, and later on the Sources tab.\n\n## What\n\n**Prototype**\n- **Picking a repository.** The connector picker and the Sources tab\noffer *Changes*: *Commit to the branch* (the default) or *Through a pull\nrequest* (GitHub connections only).\n- **Changing it later.** The Sources tab has a *Changes* column per\nrepository. A change is saved at once, and it rewrites only that entry''s\n`share_mode`.\n- **Storage.** The choice is stored as `share_mode` (`branch` |\n`pull_request`) in the project config''s `sources[]`.\n- **The official portal (studio-frontend) is not touched.**\n\n**Backend (connectors gear)**\n- `project_sources` parses `share_mode`.\n- `GET /studio-connector/v1/sources/{source}/sharing?project_id=&head=`\nreturns the source''s mode, its base branch, whether the provider can\nopen pull requests, and the caller''s open pull request, if any.\n- `POST /studio-connector/v1/sources/{source}/pull-requests?project_id=`\nopens a pull request with the connection''s token, or reuses the one\nalready open.\n- The driver gains `supports_pull_requests` and\n`find_open_pull_request`; only GitHub implements them.\n\n**Theia: Share in pull-request mode**\n- **One commit, one branch.** The documents and their `.studio`\ncompanions become one commit on the person''s branch\n`studio/<person>/share`. The commit is built in a separate index\n(`GIT_INDEX_FILE`), so the shared checkout''s branch, index and files\nnever change. That means no stray local commit to replay after a squash\nmerge.\n- **One open request.** While the person''s request is open, each share\nadds a commit to it. Once it is merged or closed, the branch starts over\nfrom the base.\n- **The dialog.** It reads *Send N documents for review* and links to\nthe pull request with *Open pull request*. Documents already in the\nrequest are listed separately and are not counted as unshared.\n\n**Branch mode**\n- `GH013` rulesets now count as a protected branch, so Share falls back\nto a review branch as it already did for `GH006`.\n- Every Share commit is signed off, so a DCO check accepts the review.\n\n**Docs**\n- `docs/sharing-documents-without-git.md`: new section *Through a pull\nrequest*.\n- `docs/verifying-the-collaboration-work.md`: new check 5j.\n- The connectors README describes the two routes.\n\n## Tested\n- **Theia:** `tsc` is clean. `document-share-service.test.ts` runs\nagainst real git with a bare remote. It checks that a share lands on the\nperson''s branch while the checkout stays untouched, that a second share\nadds to the open request, that the branch starts over after a squash\nmerge, the in-review marking, and the sign-off. `share-model.test.ts`\npasses. In total 29 tests passed.\n- **Backend:** in Docker, `cargo fmt --check` and `clippy -D warnings`\npass. `project_sources` passed 9 tests (2 new), `connectors` 63 (7 new),\n`api_contract` 3, `git_proxy` 9.\n- **Prototype:** 290 tests passed (4 new, for `withShareMode`) and `tsc\n-b` is clean.\n- **Not driven end to end** on a stand against a real GitHub pull\nrequest. The steps for that are check 5j.\n\n## Not done\n- **GitLab and Bitbucket.** Their drivers cannot open pull requests, so\nthe option is disabled for them.\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","tree":{"sha":"84ed3b24918af3574ad1144386e9edb80503bcbf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/trees/84ed3b24918af3574ad1144386e9edb80503bcbf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/commits/b5a17d50e4c0d71444818f3f516191cedc505268","verification":{"payload":"tree 84ed3b24918af3574ad1144386e9edb80503bcbf\nparent e658dcc871f359c58b75751c487ea27ee1f3e233\nauthor ANDREI KUCHMA <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech> 1791272700 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791272700 +0200\n\nShare: a project chooses per repository — commit to the branch, or a pull request (#624)\n\n## Why\n\nShare with the team pushed straight to the working branch. On a\nrepository with GitHub rulesets the push was refused (`GH013: Repository\nrule violations … Changes must be made through a pull request`,\n`Required status check \"DCO\" is expected`). Share did not recognise the\nrefusal, so instead of falling back to review it showed git''s raw error.\n\nNot every team works by committing to the branch. A project now chooses\nthis per repository, in the prototype: when it picks the repository from\na connection, and later on the Sources tab.\n\n## What\n\n**Prototype**\n- **Picking a repository.** The connector picker and the Sources tab\noffer *Changes*: *Commit to the branch* (the default) or *Through a pull\nrequest* (GitHub connections only).\n- **Changing it later.** The Sources tab has a *Changes* column per\nrepository. A change is saved at once, and it rewrites only that entry''s\n`share_mode`.\n- **Storage.** The choice is stored as `share_mode` (`branch` |\n`pull_request`) in the project config''s `sources[]`.\n- **The official portal (studio-frontend) is not touched.**\n\n**Backend (connectors gear)**\n- `project_sources` parses `share_mode`.\n- `GET /studio-connector/v1/sources/{source}/sharing?project_id=&head=`\nreturns the source''s mode, its base branch, whether the provider can\nopen pull requests, and the caller''s open pull request, if any.\n- `POST /studio-connector/v1/sources/{source}/pull-requests?project_id=`\nopens a pull request with the connection''s token, or reuses the one\nalready open.\n- The driver gains `supports_pull_requests` and\n`find_open_pull_request`; only GitHub implements them.\n\n**Theia: Share in pull-request mode**\n- **One commit, one branch.** The documents and their `.studio`\ncompanions become one commit on the person''s branch\n`studio/<person>/share`. The commit is built in a separate index\n(`GIT_INDEX_FILE`), so the shared checkout''s branch, index and files\nnever change. That means no stray local commit to replay after a squash\nmerge.\n- **One open request.** While the person''s request is open, each share\nadds a commit to it. Once it is merged or closed, the branch starts over\nfrom the base.\n- **The dialog.** It reads *Send N documents for review* and links to\nthe pull request with *Open pull request*. Documents already in the\nrequest are listed separately and are not counted as unshared.\n\n**Branch mode**\n- `GH013` rulesets now count as a protected branch, so Share falls back\nto a review branch as it already did for `GH006`.\n- Every Share commit is signed off, so a DCO check accepts the review.\n\n**Docs**\n- `docs/sharing-documents-without-git.md`: new section *Through a pull\nrequest*.\n- `docs/verifying-the-collaboration-work.md`: new check 5j.\n- The connectors README describes the two routes.\n\n## Tested\n- **Theia:** `tsc` is clean. `document-share-service.test.ts` runs\nagainst real git with a bare remote. It checks that a share lands on the\nperson''s branch while the checkout stays untouched, that a second share\nadds to the open request, that the branch starts over after a squash\nmerge, the in-review marking, and the sign-off. `share-model.test.ts`\npasses. In total 29 tests passed.\n- **Backend:** in Docker, `cargo fmt --check` and `clippy -D warnings`\npass. `project_sources` passed 9 tests (2 new), `connectors` 63 (7 new),\n`api_contract` 3, `git_proxy` 9.\n- **Prototype:** 290 tests passed (4 new, for `withShareMode`) and `tsc\n-b` is clean.\n- **Not driven end to end** on a stand against a real GitHub pull\nrequest. The steps for that are check 5j.\n\n## Not done\n- **GitLab and Bitbucket.** Their drivers cannot open pull requests, so\nthe option is disabled for them.\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxKb8CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA5i4QAEnH6RdzmjEFxGl1+yPV/8md\nRK9zWkup6k/K6kyavCwAyzCD0lvartOl553L7+kSEitIvpYsD8ptjzokfsPCw/IJ\n6YU7E8iOdEhTcMRCl7nMtceIdVyZBEHucw/CXjxCpGwF4op+JVy2YmRYiGfG4LIn\nGtGw35aUKrU5H8uYM6+lkkYToB1YKczXaZ8Wo8dhqGBKbXeTtdMHShBc7PPDRmhj\nDYLnKs8R5Hks/pCe8bOG3CUGB2iK4qur5CDHdx5UdkwCU3X8K3LTZz9yi+hm+xH2\nMNABuJwxdOakyPKKBQvPeT0ho59sw3FlyBfQZQ0/S4a0717n7YLNRIFsuPBUmtX2\nY4wQe8/ZgaK78xCEW3n2/EsE4Ij9mYn7knn7F/2sYL6ip6hQ3fkfu5+vT0EPaANu\nPQTP31zKa4sLYyULaOE3QGXU94DyvFPVdYBkVcbDVozbstwApCunKKfG41ULt8yd\ny+YmNh+HU4/X2CygiXpZ0HYNitPW3WoSvnuTI6Q1Bek/PkoQZoKOdRJi4mVkJuik\nAobmDsFmiHVZ1rP8gnB8D6ck7Kvd/zkTeP3psXKrD6QUEih0DVImsGNPj75PZ26y\nu+X+1GzgeFlNj0JM9kKAvI0R7WGTpnkI20XW0pWKUKVXx5RpmjkR2+OG7NDepd2D\nAHaBktvNZT0590OlLIWd\n=O8pC\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T07:45:00Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/b5a17d50e4c0d71444818f3f516191cedc505268","node_id":"C_kwDOTl7dJtoAKGI1YTE3ZDUwZTRjMGQ3MTQ0NDgxOGYzZjUxNjE5MWNlZGM1MDUyNjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/e658dcc871f359c58b75751c487ea27ee1f3e233","sha":"e658dcc871f359c58b75751c487ea27ee1f3e233","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/e658dcc871f359c58b75751c487ea27ee1f3e233"}],"sha":"b5a17d50e4c0d71444818f3f516191cedc505268","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/b5a17d50e4c0d71444818f3f516191cedc505268"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/301748190?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AndrejK666","id":301748190,"login":"AndrejK666","node_id":"U_kgDOEfxP3g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/e658dcc871f359c58b75751c487ea27ee1f3e233/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T07:34:16Z","email":"Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech","name":"ANDREI KUCHMA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T07:34:16Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(share): a GitHub ruleset refusal sends the change for review instead of failing (#623)\n\nSaving with **Share with the team** to a repository whose `main` is\nguarded by a GitHub *ruleset* failed with the raw remote text:\n\n```\nremote: error: GH013: Repository rule violations found for refs/heads/main.\nremote: - Changes must be made through a pull request.\n ! [remote rejected] main -> main (push declined due to repository rule violations)\n```\n\n`failureOf` recognised only classic branch protection (`GH006`) and\nGitLab''s wordings, so a ruleset refusal fell through to `failed`. It is\nnow `protected`, which takes the existing path: push\n`studio/<who>/<stamp>` and offer the review link.\n\nTest: `document-share-service.test.ts` gains the GH013 case. Locally\n13/16 pass; the same 3 integration cases (real git remotes) fail\nidentically on unchanged `main` in the container, so they are\nenvironmental.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n* GitHub repository rule violations that require changes through a pull\nrequest are now correctly identified as protected-branch failures.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","tree":{"sha":"3ddb59464e4a93896fb94fc60f2f506b157e9e33","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/trees/3ddb59464e4a93896fb94fc60f2f506b157e9e33"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/commits/e658dcc871f359c58b75751c487ea27ee1f3e233","verification":{"payload":"tree 3ddb59464e4a93896fb94fc60f2f506b157e9e33\nparent 7348770c09c211800964114a3b335516e786c7cb\nauthor ANDREI KUCHMA <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech> 1791272056 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791272056 +0200\n\nfix(share): a GitHub ruleset refusal sends the change for review instead of failing (#623)\n\nSaving with **Share with the team** to a repository whose `main` is\nguarded by a GitHub *ruleset* failed with the raw remote text:\n\n```\nremote: error: GH013: Repository rule violations found for refs/heads/main.\nremote: - Changes must be made through a pull request.\n ! [remote rejected] main -> main (push declined due to repository rule violations)\n```\n\n`failureOf` recognised only classic branch protection (`GH006`) and\nGitLab''s wordings, so a ruleset refusal fell through to `failed`. It is\nnow `protected`, which takes the existing path: push\n`studio/<who>/<stamp>` and offer the review link.\n\nTest: `document-share-service.test.ts` gains the GH013 case. Locally\n13/16 pass; the same 3 integration cases (real git remotes) fail\nidentically on unchanged `main` in the container, so they are\nenvironmental.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n* GitHub repository rule violations that require changes through a pull\nrequest are now correctly identified as protected-branch failures.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxKR4CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAy2AQABIefJ3TAmJNLtH3boKoKprr\nw/3ZxJMddZrusZOhDkiI7nExTkGuBv554lENdxrcZJMV7zDasWWTpDc01SgpJKNJ\nhj/5bPnnwxLRebPVzbk6RJmO67E/ohw1oeNYka0kN68s5QA7510Ul2CfW1rz32uX\n4RIX1ttNNR1AmJImZlKr/I6v232Yi/OllGIwvqAev90mZUXHslvUq2e2H8eqp2AR\n2joQTPs9GLePXetsf/EcTPl0Z7y1l+YVT1vR0GQ8AeLc56/QChRq0aAp/ZJymjPZ\nsS0ahUvjZqmwJbjT6l3TFiG5g4pfhYiT7ws6RLKSb8DDz4hamhxd3i52Gj9aMclQ\nVvA6JCMeoUVDN0JZXbICF6Ku5rcT1JSUoPiiGS3kGtL07/vgA9+XR1d7UBn1jfeR\n0yD43umpS1gkAH2uKE3FYq1ocGU29potDMbapKqaaqP2SvWyO1HVtQtTUeTRPYZk\nQmSEr5PR03YAay9pHMnrwXiDqms1y2saueaXmeNepqAUFxrcjktMEI44jw0gdyly\n86USvoT+Cq+nxmImzU/IG72IzhHSKGRzNMr8MXiXc93vkRpWILbYDEoPyP7TvCxF\nwERRRD7E5bfquQ/psiKeivR29VicVk26Kro5h1GSeuhlhMPYtvMuWU2rrciXlAB5\nxrb3ZCe5Lf1/dco0o7fk\n=7WmV\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T07:34:16Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/e658dcc871f359c58b75751c487ea27ee1f3e233","node_id":"C_kwDOTl7dJtoAKGU2NThkY2M4NzFmMzU5YzU4Yjc1NzUxYzQ4N2VhMjdlZTFmM2UyMzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/7348770c09c211800964114a3b335516e786c7cb","sha":"7348770c09c211800964114a3b335516e786c7cb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/7348770c09c211800964114a3b335516e786c7cb"}],"sha":"e658dcc871f359c58b75751c487ea27ee1f3e233","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/e658dcc871f359c58b75751c487ea27ee1f3e233"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/301748190?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AndrejK666","id":301748190,"login":"AndrejK666","node_id":"U_kgDOEfxP3g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/7348770c09c211800964114a3b335516e786c7cb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T15:41:32Z","email":"Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech","name":"ANDREI KUCHMA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T15:41:32Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(specs): every document is scanned, tool configuration is not a spec, and the graph keeps no file text (#621)\n\n## Why\nInsight''s Specs screen on dev (2026-10-05):\n- **Not scanned 1**: `inbox/architecture/IDENTITY_RESOLUTION_V4.md` (343\nKB) never left the queue. The checkout walk read text only up to 256 KiB\na file (and 24 MiB a sync, a cap from when the graph store was in\nmemory). The classifier skips a prose file it has no text for, so the\nfile never got a binding. #608''s reader had the same ceiling, so the\nfile could not be opened either.\n- **Needs review 268**: about a third were tool configuration — 47 under\n`.cf-studio/`, 43 under `.claude/`, plus `.github/`, `CLAUDE.md` and\n`AGENTS.md`. A kit''s example ADR showed up as one of the project''s\ndecisions.\n- The graph kept an 8,000-character excerpt of **every text file**,\nsource included: 19,950 `file_content` nodes, about 136 MB with\nembeddings on dev. Only `POST /studio-artifact-ingest/v1/search` read\nthem, and no client (portal, prototype, Theia) calls that endpoint.\nEverything that reads a document gets the text from the checkout\ninstead: the classifier, Spec Quality, and #608.\n\n## What\n- **clone.rs**: no size limits. `walk(dir, read_text)`: the caller names\nwhose text is read. A sync reads documents plus `.studio/comments/` logs\nand lists everything else by path. The repo-files readers still read\nevery text file. Bytes that are not valid UTF-8 are replaced, so a bad\nbyte no longer drops the whole file.\n- **sync**: no more `file_content` nodes and no file-parser extraction.\nThe `file_parser_sdk` and `bytes` deps are removed. The next sync of a\nrepository retires the content nodes earlier syncs wrote. It finds them\nfrom the index through the old file nodes'' `has_text`. File nodes now\ncarry `from_checkout`.\n- **classify**: `.cf-studio/`, `.claude/` and `.github/` dirs, plus root\n`CLAUDE.md` / `AGENTS.md`, are not prose. On such a path a re-sync\noverwrites the classifier''s own verdicts: Detected, Unknown, a\nfront-matter auto-confirm, a Spec Quality guess. A person''s ruling is\nkept: Manual, a Confirm by hand, a Reject.\n- **portal** (projects-mfe): the provenance shown for a file reads\n`from_checkout`, and still reads `has_text` on old nodes.\n\nThe search endpoint stays and searches metadata only.\n\n## Tests\n- `fmt`, `clippy --all-targets -D warnings`\n- `cargo test -- artifact_ingest documents gts_inventory api_contract`:\n317 passed, 6 of them new. They cover: the walk reads only what it is\nasked to and has no size limit; tooling paths never classify; on a sync,\na kit file becomes not-a-document while a Manual ruling is kept; legacy\nexcerpts are found only for this repository and scope.\n- `projects-mfe` `model/artifact.test.ts`: 11 passed.\n\nAfter deploy, re-sync Insight: the 343 KB note leaves \"Not scanned\",\n`.cf-studio`/`.claude` leave \"Needs review\", and its content nodes are\nretired.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","tree":{"sha":"c8026f72a4fa3962b36585147f86e454d83245f3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/trees/c8026f72a4fa3962b36585147f86e454d83245f3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/commits/7348770c09c211800964114a3b335516e786c7cb","verification":{"payload":"tree c8026f72a4fa3962b36585147f86e454d83245f3\nparent f3c67d9f88cfb178209c3bdeae5d4d417ce7fcae\nauthor ANDREI KUCHMA <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech> 1791214892 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791214892 +0200\n\nfix(specs): every document is scanned, tool configuration is not a spec, and the graph keeps no file text (#621)\n\n## Why\nInsight''s Specs screen on dev (2026-10-05):\n- **Not scanned 1**: `inbox/architecture/IDENTITY_RESOLUTION_V4.md` (343\nKB) never left the queue. The checkout walk read text only up to 256 KiB\na file (and 24 MiB a sync, a cap from when the graph store was in\nmemory). The classifier skips a prose file it has no text for, so the\nfile never got a binding. #608''s reader had the same ceiling, so the\nfile could not be opened either.\n- **Needs review 268**: about a third were tool configuration — 47 under\n`.cf-studio/`, 43 under `.claude/`, plus `.github/`, `CLAUDE.md` and\n`AGENTS.md`. A kit''s example ADR showed up as one of the project''s\ndecisions.\n- The graph kept an 8,000-character excerpt of **every text file**,\nsource included: 19,950 `file_content` nodes, about 136 MB with\nembeddings on dev. Only `POST /studio-artifact-ingest/v1/search` read\nthem, and no client (portal, prototype, Theia) calls that endpoint.\nEverything that reads a document gets the text from the checkout\ninstead: the classifier, Spec Quality, and #608.\n\n## What\n- **clone.rs**: no size limits. `walk(dir, read_text)`: the caller names\nwhose text is read. A sync reads documents plus `.studio/comments/` logs\nand lists everything else by path. The repo-files readers still read\nevery text file. Bytes that are not valid UTF-8 are replaced, so a bad\nbyte no longer drops the whole file.\n- **sync**: no more `file_content` nodes and no file-parser extraction.\nThe `file_parser_sdk` and `bytes` deps are removed. The next sync of a\nrepository retires the content nodes earlier syncs wrote. It finds them\nfrom the index through the old file nodes'' `has_text`. File nodes now\ncarry `from_checkout`.\n- **classify**: `.cf-studio/`, `.claude/` and `.github/` dirs, plus root\n`CLAUDE.md` / `AGENTS.md`, are not prose. On such a path a re-sync\noverwrites the classifier''s own verdicts: Detected, Unknown, a\nfront-matter auto-confirm, a Spec Quality guess. A person''s ruling is\nkept: Manual, a Confirm by hand, a Reject.\n- **portal** (projects-mfe): the provenance shown for a file reads\n`from_checkout`, and still reads `has_text` on old nodes.\n\nThe search endpoint stays and searches metadata only.\n\n## Tests\n- `fmt`, `clippy --all-targets -D warnings`\n- `cargo test -- artifact_ingest documents gts_inventory api_contract`:\n317 passed, 6 of them new. They cover: the walk reads only what it is\nasked to and has no size limit; tooling paths never classify; on a sync,\na kit file becomes not-a-document while a Manual ruling is kept; legacy\nexcerpts are found only for this repository and scope.\n- `projects-mfe` `model/artifact.test.ts`: 11 passed.\n\nAfter deploy, re-sync Insight: the 343 KB note leaves \"Not scanned\",\n`.cf-studio`/`.claude` leave \"Needs review\", and its content nodes are\nretired.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqw8UsCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAnRcQAFfBRCYHQ1v3UVmIxF2DNJlZ\nIQTN8CD/NJt+vAY0KajSJKikZtqentIMIvVN4j9905D4QYXt3r9Tm1eyseEVBqQr\nWZJ8lWD/daWXKtczMfQ+/H9Fd7KNeyYNxQC18jhEGrlwWRCucmo2/2otRchCwr+q\nnDAnlPMTbG3DLnSNUBmFYl+rV6sgqk4NsSgp5YilBoD+XEbOP4a01MAZ3bJnLQvx\ncEYtY4GxNbOervndqMmfswsoIh8lrcEgBQeKKVh2kQqqmA9ylIM5NQzOPjzXc4yZ\nj4/aYM21EshFMd0IcPnZxDIqM0bEKYSGAct1NzKv2dWoTpBt0q9+I2tqNkkbRPKE\nNhUMlEEe6TUryxZWmoyu0+wRgiVLhXUqxTp3UaIFfSJd1WPf96r2sT9471MCIZQn\nxaD2dx8IetYpFRFyHDAa+0eIePxA/kBd87pAmBtoR/rfgK6kVa/FdfKQqPhIBiZe\nfYVakGy+nIXc9nY7E7HiScDVti5Enr/1dLuFEnnx6DvWo2NDptLJtX8Wpna+2KLn\nh7CpRMW5eowfesRQpdxmKaoYpJ6yJITWkhdCu8LxsL4HoYfl9GQH9EZgcz6DF6ML\nSp0F9llTq4YqlJeMF+FO2soMHZpeUHJFJKi/dgFmpRuThTOYJ5oWly0Pi3FJEmm/\nn9FlJo1re/LWgFlyP+nC\n=C2U3\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-05T15:41:33Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/7348770c09c211800964114a3b335516e786c7cb","node_id":"C_kwDOTl7dJtoAKDczNDg3NzBjMDljMjExODAwOTY0MTE0YTNiMzM1NTE2ZTc4NmM3Y2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/f3c67d9f88cfb178209c3bdeae5d4d417ce7fcae","sha":"f3c67d9f88cfb178209c3bdeae5d4d417ce7fcae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/f3c67d9f88cfb178209c3bdeae5d4d417ce7fcae"}],"sha":"7348770c09c211800964114a3b335516e786c7cb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/7348770c09c211800964114a3b335516e786c7cb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/301748190?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AndrejK666","id":301748190,"login":"AndrejK666","node_id":"U_kgDOEfxP3g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/f3c67d9f88cfb178209c3bdeae5d4d417ce7fcae/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T15:40:35Z","email":"Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech","name":"ANDREI KUCHMA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T15:40:35Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Documents: rendered comparison, editing together without noise, Share with the team (#620)\n\nDocuments are compared the way a reader sees them, editing together no\nlonger fights itself, and a person who does not know git can get their\nedits into the repository with one button.\n\n## Rendered markdown comparison\nTwo versions of a document are rendered side by side, with added,\nremoved and reworded parts marked on the rendered text. The idea comes\nfrom Markdown Diff Visualiser (MIT); it is adapted to Theia, and the\nunit of comparison is markdown-it''s blocks, not the lines of a git hunk.\n\nIt opens from:\n- a file''s tab and the explorer: against HEAD, or against a branch or\ntag (*Mine ↔ ref* or *What ref changed*);\n- any text diff of two markdown versions;\n- the Documents editor: a conflict, a history entry, a proposal, a\ncolleague''s suggestions, *what changed since you last looked*;\n- the WYSIWYG editor''s conflict banner;\n- on the desktop, *what Sync brought*.\n\nMermaid uses the page''s single copy. Discussions a change touches, or\nleaves orphaned, are noted on the rows.\n\n## Collaboration fixes found along the way\n- The first suggestion or comment in a project now reaches the colleague\nwithout a reload. A watch on a `.studio` folder that does not exist yet\nwas inert, and watches are non-recursive by default.\n- A save changes only what was edited. The two editors'' serialisers now\nwrite the file''s own lines back for every block that renders the same;\none sentence used to rewrite +27/−79 lines.\n- The WYSIWYG editor claims its writes, so a colleague''s Documents\neditor applies them as that person''s save instead of holding them as an\nagent''s.\n- What git writes now belongs to the repository. A pull or checkout\nwhile a document was open used to be held as a proposal and the file put\nback, so the next share committed the old text over the colleague''s\ncommit. Content equal to a commit (HEAD, or the branch it follows) is\nnow applied as that commit author''s edit. An agent''s write is still\nheld.\n\n## Share with the team\nA button in Doc editing''s Team group, with *N documents not shared* in\nthe status bar.\n- It commits only the person''s documents and their `.studio` companions,\nas that person, with co-authors.\n- It fetches, rebases only if behind, and pushes.\n- A protected branch sends the changes to `studio/<person>/<time>` with\n*Ask for review*.\n- A conflict is resolved by comparing, then choosing *Keep my wording*\nor *Keep theirs*.\n\n## The assistant panel does not open by itself\nClaude Code, Codex and AI Chat no longer take the right flank on startup\nor on a mode switch. They open only when asked: a click in the right\nflank, or an assistant command.\n\n## Docs\n- `docs/rendered-markdown-diff.md`\n- `docs/sharing-documents-without-git.md`\n- checks 5a–5i in `docs/verifying-the-collaboration-work.md`\n\n## Checked\n- `theia/product-ext`: `npm test` all passing.\n- `theia/studio`: jest for markdown-diff, markdown-editor, share and the\nguard, 122/122. The git node suites run against real git.\n- On Windows, `markdown-diff-git-service.test.ts` › *lists the refs…*\nfails on `git tag` when the local config demands a tag message. This is\nenvironment-only and unrelated to this change.\n- Live on a session-image stand with two headless browsers driven over\nCDP:\n  - all collaborative scenarios;\n- Alice (Documents) then Bob (WYSIWYG) change one line between them,\nwith 0 proposals;\n  - Share commits as the person and leaves a clean tree;\n- a pull while the document is open shows \"Bob edited this document\"\nwith no proposal, while a hand write is still held.\n\n**Not done:** the desktop Sync notification''s *Show changed documents*\nhas not been clicked in a built electron-app. What it shows is covered\nby tests.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n* Added side-by-side rendered Markdown comparisons for document history,\nconflicts, suggestions, remote edits, and changes since your last visit.\nCompare against the working tree, branches, or tags, with change\nsummaries and navigation.\n* Added “Share with the Team” to share selected documents, review\nchanges, and resolve conflicts.\n* Desktop Sync now lets you open and review Markdown documents brought\nin by a sync.\n* Added a “Changed since you last looked” notice for documents with new\nchanges.\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n* Preserved unchanged Markdown formatting, including table layout and\nline endings, when saving edits.\n* Improved detection of external file changes and handling of missing\nreview data.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","tree":{"sha":"2241b86c0484441f805cf08256cbda0933c036ac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/trees/2241b86c0484441f805cf08256cbda0933c036ac"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/commits/f3c67d9f88cfb178209c3bdeae5d4d417ce7fcae","verification":{"payload":"tree 2241b86c0484441f805cf08256cbda0933c036ac\nparent 49bc5db0c6d3711795851ab847c2249caac2b1b2\nauthor ANDREI KUCHMA <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech> 1791214835 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791214835 +0200\n\nDocuments: rendered comparison, editing together without noise, Share with the team (#620)\n\nDocuments are compared the way a reader sees them, editing together no\nlonger fights itself, and a person who does not know git can get their\nedits into the repository with one button.\n\n## Rendered markdown comparison\nTwo versions of a document are rendered side by side, with added,\nremoved and reworded parts marked on the rendered text. The idea comes\nfrom Markdown Diff Visualiser (MIT); it is adapted to Theia, and the\nunit of comparison is markdown-it''s blocks, not the lines of a git hunk.\n\nIt opens from:\n- a file''s tab and the explorer: against HEAD, or against a branch or\ntag (*Mine ↔ ref* or *What ref changed*);\n- any text diff of two markdown versions;\n- the Documents editor: a conflict, a history entry, a proposal, a\ncolleague''s suggestions, *what changed since you last looked*;\n- the WYSIWYG editor''s conflict banner;\n- on the desktop, *what Sync brought*.\n\nMermaid uses the page''s single copy. Discussions a change touches, or\nleaves orphaned, are noted on the rows.\n\n## Collaboration fixes found along the way\n- The first suggestion or comment in a project now reaches the colleague\nwithout a reload. A watch on a `.studio` folder that does not exist yet\nwas inert, and watches are non-recursive by default.\n- A save changes only what was edited. The two editors'' serialisers now\nwrite the file''s own lines back for every block that renders the same;\none sentence used to rewrite +27/−79 lines.\n- The WYSIWYG editor claims its writes, so a colleague''s Documents\neditor applies them as that person''s save instead of holding them as an\nagent''s.\n- What git writes now belongs to the repository. A pull or checkout\nwhile a document was open used to be held as a proposal and the file put\nback, so the next share committed the old text over the colleague''s\ncommit. Content equal to a commit (HEAD, or the branch it follows) is\nnow applied as that commit author''s edit. An agent''s write is still\nheld.\n\n## Share with the team\nA button in Doc editing''s Team group, with *N documents not shared* in\nthe status bar.\n- It commits only the person''s documents and their `.studio` companions,\nas that person, with co-authors.\n- It fetches, rebases only if behind, and pushes.\n- A protected branch sends the changes to `studio/<person>/<time>` with\n*Ask for review*.\n- A conflict is resolved by comparing, then choosing *Keep my wording*\nor *Keep theirs*.\n\n## The assistant panel does not open by itself\nClaude Code, Codex and AI Chat no longer take the right flank on startup\nor on a mode switch. They open only when asked: a click in the right\nflank, or an assistant command.\n\n## Docs\n- `docs/rendered-markdown-diff.md`\n- `docs/sharing-documents-without-git.md`\n- checks 5a–5i in `docs/verifying-the-collaboration-work.md`\n\n## Checked\n- `theia/product-ext`: `npm test` all passing.\n- `theia/studio`: jest for markdown-diff, markdown-editor, share and the\nguard, 122/122. The git node suites run against real git.\n- On Windows, `markdown-diff-git-service.test.ts` › *lists the refs…*\nfails on `git tag` when the local config demands a tag message. This is\nenvironment-only and unrelated to this change.\n- Live on a session-image stand with two headless browsers driven over\nCDP:\n  - all collaborative scenarios;\n- Alice (Documents) then Bob (WYSIWYG) change one line between them,\nwith 0 proposals;\n  - Share commits as the person and leaves a clean tree;\n- a pull while the document is open shows \"Bob edited this document\"\nwith no proposal, while a hand write is still held.\n\n**Not done:** the desktop Sync notification''s *Show changed documents*\nhas not been clicked in a built electron-app. What it shows is covered\nby tests.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n* Added side-by-side rendered Markdown comparisons for document history,\nconflicts, suggestions, remote edits, and changes since your last visit.\nCompare against the working tree, branches, or tags, with change\nsummaries and navigation.\n* Added “Share with the Team” to share selected documents, review\nchanges, and resolve conflicts.\n* Desktop Sync now lets you open and review Markdown documents brought\nin by a sync.\n* Added a “Changed since you last looked” notice for documents with new\nchanges.\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n* Preserved unchanged Markdown formatting, including table layout and\nline endings, when saving edits.\n* Improved detection of external file changes and handling of missing\nreview data.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqw8TzCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAyKwQADojlBiPqwhA9XKUadGoj1Zs\nzs6lxRM7MAnZNM1MiYr6tY2nSddHUQtU2UUpsDkClrPpasoYCzc6unyG7xR2K4uU\nAwOUZEoc/0DkjUYTYKRXmQ+JUs+Th1/58l4vU0eTl1RkFfrTLEGs9jC3X236OGVS\nIVYpOrkJmx4ZNNbCpzvYhbqIQFFYWzqHYAc4RhvRHPnW8j8X4NuyhgRq4rSqndI0\nWIl+9lOy1qQQ2lRmhIQIEUY3GZlnbBlq5blApHE4By0U94PkFZ3cz+LFxMeME0eh\nVH1NP7uDZaTcDqbp4lEbJgZjEo4EAZb7myNZYbHBXbgD8SPVB6fBgWpPLPw32FnR\nZrfWibyeCe7u8dYxc+X8rggViGJQ/OWlmuprxwj8/Gowi4JYPN0tZLRZRmFacmIq\n73UBoilssGDeOyqTFkQXoWAvZuQNW1qJZB9Ymn0XYQVNM/pbuc7OgnrD5hzOTu+G\nt55Ezzvh77gRwRQCr7gSdTPW4E89ggKC/Cr+pUNHk4zLCnbBMryWAQOdFlw+aodJ\ny1Gq2nPlz7mvMGnos1/j/LzQ8ArdPYrCtqu3UFLdlqBDgmiPvms6zJKAhLhwfASI\niM+B9DOoGxdvdt1Bxoo8K9IPnZba11SfIr/TEGWWRF6qezSC4sPSY6HvIHunb+jG\nKFMcp7UWcf4r334ya5rx\n=dPrK\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-05T15:40:35Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/f3c67d9f88cfb178209c3bdeae5d4d417ce7fcae","node_id":"C_kwDOTl7dJtoAKGYzYzY3ZDlmODhjZmIxNzgyMDljM2JkZWFlNWQ0ZDQxN2NlN2ZjYWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/49bc5db0c6d3711795851ab847c2249caac2b1b2","sha":"49bc5db0c6d3711795851ab847c2249caac2b1b2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/49bc5db0c6d3711795851ab847c2249caac2b1b2"}],"sha":"f3c67d9f88cfb178209c3bdeae5d4d417ce7fcae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/f3c67d9f88cfb178209c3bdeae5d4d417ce7fcae"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/301748190?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AndrejK666","id":301748190,"login":"AndrejK666","node_id":"U_kgDOEfxP3g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/49bc5db0c6d3711795851ab847c2249caac2b1b2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T13:28:52Z","email":"Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech","name":"ANDREI KUCHMA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T13:28:52Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: a README that maps the repository, and its contributing and security policies (#618)\n\n## What and why\n\nThe README answered \"how do I run Compose\" before it answered \"what is\nthis repository\", and the community profile was at 50 %: no\nCONTRIBUTING, no SECURITY, no PR template. This makes the README the\nentry point and adds the missing policies — layered on the\norganization''s\n[governance](https://github.com/constructorfabric/governance) baseline\nrather than repeating it.\n\n- **README.md** — what Studio Web is and for whom; an architecture\ndiagram with a component table tied to the ADRs; the repository layout\nwith a \"start here\" table; a five-step quick start; configuration by\ncapability; published images and their tags; deployment and Studio\nDelivery; development per component; troubleshooting (the `--no-build`,\nsession-image, rate-limit, certificate and mount notes moved here out of\nthe main path); a documentation map. Structure follows `insight`''s\nREADME.\n- **CONTRIBUTING.md** — what is specific here: `.githooks` (fmt + DCO\ntrailer), branching from `upstream/main`, commit/title convention,\nchecks per component as CI runs them, the API ratchet, when an ADR is\nneeded, the desktop rules, CODEOWNERS and how a change reaches a stand.\n- **SECURITY.md** — private vulnerability reporting (already enabled on\nthe repository), supported versions, what is in scope for a multi-tenant\nhost of other people''s code and credentials, and what is not (the\npublished dev credentials).\n- **.github/pull_request_template.md** — what changed and why, how it\nwas verified, contracts and decisions, DCO.\n\n## A fix found on the way\n\nThe old README said an empty database still needs `scripts/dev-up.sh`\nonce. It does not any more: `backend` waits for `backend-bootstrap`\n(`service_completed_successfully`), so a plain `docker compose up` seeds\nthe root tenant. The script itself was broken — it started a `postgres`\nservice that the single-PostgreSQL change renamed to `graph-postgres`.\nIt now starts the one that exists.\n\n## How it was verified\n\n- [x] Every relative link and in-page anchor in the four files resolves\n(scripted check)\n- [x] Every file, script, npm script, workflow operation, tag scheme,\nenv var and service named exists on `main` — checked against `docker\ncompose config --services`, `package.json`, `studio-delivery.yml`,\n`.env.example`, `CODEOWNERS`\n- [x] `bash -n scripts/dev-up.sh`\n- [ ] Not done: a full fresh `docker compose up` on an empty volume\n\n## Contracts and decisions\n\n- [x] No API, event or error contract changes\n- [x] No architectural change\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] One topic\n- [x] Every commit signed off (DCO)\n- [x] No secrets — only the local development credentials the README\nalready published\n\nChanges to `.github/` and `SECURITY.md` need\n`@constructorfabric/studio-leaders` per CODEOWNERS.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Documentation**\n* Added repository-specific contribution guidance covering setup,\ndevelopment checks, pull requests, reviews, and secret handling.\n* Added a security policy outlining vulnerability reporting, disclosure\nexpectations, supported versions, and scope.\n* Updated the README with an overview, local setup, development,\ndeployment, troubleshooting, and documentation guidance.\n* **Chores**\n* Updated the local development startup flow to start `graph-postgres`\nwith Keycloak.\n* **Documentation**\n* Updated the pull request template with prompts for rationale,\nverification, decisions, and a submission checklist.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","tree":{"sha":"e5eb5fa863ff4ad9b4b63dcda1fc96c204e77ee3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/trees/e5eb5fa863ff4ad9b4b63dcda1fc96c204e77ee3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/commits/49bc5db0c6d3711795851ab847c2249caac2b1b2","verification":{"payload":"tree e5eb5fa863ff4ad9b4b63dcda1fc96c204e77ee3\nparent 6a21d527fb1922900b0ae8dfad77aa12eb79ed89\nauthor ANDREI KUCHMA <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech> 1791206932 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791206932 +0200\n\ndocs: a README that maps the repository, and its contributing and security policies (#618)\n\n## What and why\n\nThe README answered \"how do I run Compose\" before it answered \"what is\nthis repository\", and the community profile was at 50 %: no\nCONTRIBUTING, no SECURITY, no PR template. This makes the README the\nentry point and adds the missing policies — layered on the\norganization''s\n[governance](https://github.com/constructorfabric/governance) baseline\nrather than repeating it.\n\n- **README.md** — what Studio Web is and for whom; an architecture\ndiagram with a component table tied to the ADRs; the repository layout\nwith a \"start here\" table; a five-step quick start; configuration by\ncapability; published images and their tags; deployment and Studio\nDelivery; development per component; troubleshooting (the `--no-build`,\nsession-image, rate-limit, certificate and mount notes moved here out of\nthe main path); a documentation map. Structure follows `insight`''s\nREADME.\n- **CONTRIBUTING.md** — what is specific here: `.githooks` (fmt + DCO\ntrailer), branching from `upstream/main`, commit/title convention,\nchecks per component as CI runs them, the API ratchet, when an ADR is\nneeded, the desktop rules, CODEOWNERS and how a change reaches a stand.\n- **SECURITY.md** — private vulnerability reporting (already enabled on\nthe repository), supported versions, what is in scope for a multi-tenant\nhost of other people''s code and credentials, and what is not (the\npublished dev credentials).\n- **.github/pull_request_template.md** — what changed and why, how it\nwas verified, contracts and decisions, DCO.\n\n## A fix found on the way\n\nThe old README said an empty database still needs `scripts/dev-up.sh`\nonce. It does not any more: `backend` waits for `backend-bootstrap`\n(`service_completed_successfully`), so a plain `docker compose up` seeds\nthe root tenant. The script itself was broken — it started a `postgres`\nservice that the single-PostgreSQL change renamed to `graph-postgres`.\nIt now starts the one that exists.\n\n## How it was verified\n\n- [x] Every relative link and in-page anchor in the four files resolves\n(scripted check)\n- [x] Every file, script, npm script, workflow operation, tag scheme,\nenv var and service named exists on `main` — checked against `docker\ncompose config --services`, `package.json`, `studio-delivery.yml`,\n`.env.example`, `CODEOWNERS`\n- [x] `bash -n scripts/dev-up.sh`\n- [ ] Not done: a full fresh `docker compose up` on an empty volume\n\n## Contracts and decisions\n\n- [x] No API, event or error contract changes\n- [x] No architectural change\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] One topic\n- [x] Every commit signed off (DCO)\n- [x] No secrets — only the local development credentials the README\nalready published\n\nChanges to `.github/` and `SECURITY.md` need\n`@constructorfabric/studio-leaders` per CODEOWNERS.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Documentation**\n* Added repository-specific contribution guidance covering setup,\ndevelopment checks, pull requests, reviews, and secret handling.\n* Added a security policy outlining vulnerability reporting, disclosure\nexpectations, supported versions, and scope.\n* Updated the README with an overview, local setup, development,\ndeployment, troubleshooting, and documentation guidance.\n* **Chores**\n* Updated the local development startup flow to start `graph-postgres`\nwith Keycloak.\n* **Documentation**\n* Updated the pull request template with prompts for rationale,\nverification, decisions, and a submission checklist.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqw6YUCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAb+sQAKlLSneo3xGo6KNT8rPBTMCd\nkO53k+F9Qaxn9GrG2cgdKEaO+WHL5ROT0HxyW13cG+6dfVFH9b/LCYD4q0Y3HtEa\nN9aQtGRg4fRJFcRZEjwUOhmmo+q5SirOJOvDTR/vd4Ty01uKZNJ0qBBiyyMRT2yh\n06rnbASPXkef/7iKgh6llxRAco3CT+nQkzjorLSKihwCqw98H9UQLa5X3MUAihSL\nP3e6yNy7voSq7dB5TNjH2y74wX630gpfKy90PdKBBsChEz3PoeieZDGT/eeoLsH3\nWhWZZO196zyLi+yGe2fJvwoVsbqXIfuDny/yf+zkazw4hMAkuTOGTMvn2CFaSjWD\nauB0rWTNqD4aSLNokBYvjZ3fIaZuWpHMOEN+on9rWBfjEm9wsPsoLtvXpADz2ZtM\ng7KcZE1+Fi54mUvodri7ofJTSP4adKKfgqXDA5+aCzahTVHGn78TX43yEVAe4pv6\nVnAbC1TdeFVs4SbO4HwVo8rDOIhg4guPhtbfzBP7HigGWnTLLJn8O9LwBmmVQv4z\nCUJyp/QZm4EDltIkfZFNAAwXGGXIrTajZnhUQg8qeiS4KMn1kVFOS46o/TaNQcTA\n/CHm0NfhIP5ay6zlYr23YM8hewGGxTuDvAtRHv4oBX9gx2MmEOGuUeYAnK6dbgOI\nyNf8spHSTcWYlmAAWwx6\n=dobz\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-05T13:28:53Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/49bc5db0c6d3711795851ab847c2249caac2b1b2","node_id":"C_kwDOTl7dJtoAKDQ5YmM1ZGIwYzZkMzcxMTc5NTg1MWFiODQ3YzIyNDljYWFjMmIxYjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/6a21d527fb1922900b0ae8dfad77aa12eb79ed89","sha":"6a21d527fb1922900b0ae8dfad77aa12eb79ed89","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/6a21d527fb1922900b0ae8dfad77aa12eb79ed89"}],"sha":"49bc5db0c6d3711795851ab847c2249caac2b1b2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/49bc5db0c6d3711795851ab847c2249caac2b1b2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/39742858?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vasylcf/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vasylcf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vasylcf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vasylcf/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/vasylcf","id":39742858,"login":"vasylcf","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5NzQyODU4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vasylcf/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vasylcf/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vasylcf/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vasylcf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vasylcf/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vasylcf","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/6a21d527fb1922900b0ae8dfad77aa12eb79ed89/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T13:06:09Z","email":"39742858+vasylcf@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Vasyl"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T13:06:09Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"build(backend): the graph-storage gear from its official crates (#619)\n\n**The backend now takes the graph-storage gear from its official\ncrates.** constructorfabric/gears-rust#4794 merged on 2026-10-02, and\nrelease-plz published `cf-gears-graph-storage` 0.1.4 and\n`cf-gears-graph-storage-sdk` 0.1.1, with both embedding plugins at\n0.1.0. They replace the interim `weftgraph` / `weftgraph-sdk` 0.1.1\npreview crates (#512). The library names haven''t changed\n(`graph_storage`, `graph_storage_sdk`), so no source file is touched.\n\n## What changes\n\n- **`Cargo.toml`.** The two `package =` lines and the comments that\ndescribed the preview name.\n- **`Cargo.lock`.** The four `weftgraph*` crates are replaced by the\nfour official ones, plus `cf-gears-toolkit-onnx-runtime` 0.1.0, the new\ntoolkit library the ONNX plugin now runs its session through. No other\nlocked version moves. The gear asks for the same toolkit versions the\nbackend already pins (toolkit 0.10.0, toolkit-db 0.16.2,\ntoolkit-security 0.11.0).\n- **Five config profiles.** A comment that cited the \"weftgraph README\"\nnow cites the graph-storage README. The section it quotes is still\nthere.\n\n## What the upgrade from 0.1.1 means for an existing environment\n\n- **No database step.** The gear''s migrations (m0001–m0009), its\nconfiguration fields and the SDK''s public types are unchanged between\nthe `weftgraph-v0.1.1` tag and gears-rust `main`. On the stand the gear\nreports `applied=0 skipped=9`.\n- **The embedding space is the same.** The identity the gear computes is\nthe one already stored (`f6903c4d…`), so vector search stays open and\nnothing has to be re-embedded.\n- **Behaviour that changed in the gear since 0.1.1:**\n- writes, deletes and admin calls are pinned to the caller''s own tenant;\n  - scope membership is checked as payload containment;\n- a stale scope generation now carries a `recorded_generation`\nviolation;\n  - an empty scope replacement is documented as the scope''s erasure.\n  Studio''s consumers compile and pass unchanged.\n\n## Verified locally\n\n- **The CI gates on this branch:**\n  - `cargo fmt --check`;\n  - `clippy --locked --all-targets --features theia-bridge -D warnings`;\n  - `cargo build --locked`;\n  - `cargo check --locked --no-default-features`;\n- the release set `--no-default-features --features graph,theia-bridge`;\n- `cargo test --locked --features theia-bridge`: 1264 passed, 0 failed;\n  - `--list-gears`, which lists `graph-storage`.\n- **The compose stand on the database weftgraph 0.1.1 created** (537k\nnodes, 643k edges), with images rebuilt from this branch:\n  - the backend boots healthy;\n  - the gear''s readiness is healthy on every implemented component;\n- the 44-check REST matrix (`scripts/graph-storage-bench/gs_bench.py\nfunc`) gives 39 pass, 0 fail and 5 notes. The notes are the same\ndocumented limits as on 0.1.1.\n- repository sync of `constructorfabric/insight` through the connector\nwrites 26 nodes and 31 edges the repository gained since the last run,\nand a re-sync converges: 0 and 0, in 2.3 s.\n\n## After this merges\n\nThe `weftgraph*` crates on crates.io get a deprecation release pointing\nto `cf-gears-graph-storage` and are then yanked. A yank leaves existing\nlock files working. From here on, gear updates arrive the same way as\nevery other gears crate: through gears-rust `main` and release-plz.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Chores**\n* Updated the backend’s graph-storage integration to use the officially\npublished components.\n* Updated graph-storage setup references across development and\ndeployment configurations.\n* No changes to configuration values or runtime behavior. These updates\ndo not change the features or behavior available to end users.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\nSigned-off-by: vasylcf <vasylcf@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"2c255b1c0be1b58e13cffa73d9739e9ac7085767","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/trees/2c255b1c0be1b58e13cffa73d9739e9ac7085767"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/commits/6a21d527fb1922900b0ae8dfad77aa12eb79ed89","verification":{"payload":"tree 2c255b1c0be1b58e13cffa73d9739e9ac7085767\nparent 717075a0ddf91e03132c4254a3bab22b2b971a8f\nauthor Vasyl <39742858+vasylcf@users.noreply.github.com> 1791205569 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791205569 +0200\n\nbuild(backend): the graph-storage gear from its official crates (#619)\n\n**The backend now takes the graph-storage gear from its official\ncrates.** constructorfabric/gears-rust#4794 merged on 2026-10-02, and\nrelease-plz published `cf-gears-graph-storage` 0.1.4 and\n`cf-gears-graph-storage-sdk` 0.1.1, with both embedding plugins at\n0.1.0. They replace the interim `weftgraph` / `weftgraph-sdk` 0.1.1\npreview crates (#512). The library names haven''t changed\n(`graph_storage`, `graph_storage_sdk`), so no source file is touched.\n\n## What changes\n\n- **`Cargo.toml`.** The two `package =` lines and the comments that\ndescribed the preview name.\n- **`Cargo.lock`.** The four `weftgraph*` crates are replaced by the\nfour official ones, plus `cf-gears-toolkit-onnx-runtime` 0.1.0, the new\ntoolkit library the ONNX plugin now runs its session through. No other\nlocked version moves. The gear asks for the same toolkit versions the\nbackend already pins (toolkit 0.10.0, toolkit-db 0.16.2,\ntoolkit-security 0.11.0).\n- **Five config profiles.** A comment that cited the \"weftgraph README\"\nnow cites the graph-storage README. The section it quotes is still\nthere.\n\n## What the upgrade from 0.1.1 means for an existing environment\n\n- **No database step.** The gear''s migrations (m0001–m0009), its\nconfiguration fields and the SDK''s public types are unchanged between\nthe `weftgraph-v0.1.1` tag and gears-rust `main`. On the stand the gear\nreports `applied=0 skipped=9`.\n- **The embedding space is the same.** The identity the gear computes is\nthe one already stored (`f6903c4d…`), so vector search stays open and\nnothing has to be re-embedded.\n- **Behaviour that changed in the gear since 0.1.1:**\n- writes, deletes and admin calls are pinned to the caller''s own tenant;\n  - scope membership is checked as payload containment;\n- a stale scope generation now carries a `recorded_generation`\nviolation;\n  - an empty scope replacement is documented as the scope''s erasure.\n  Studio''s consumers compile and pass unchanged.\n\n## Verified locally\n\n- **The CI gates on this branch:**\n  - `cargo fmt --check`;\n  - `clippy --locked --all-targets --features theia-bridge -D warnings`;\n  - `cargo build --locked`;\n  - `cargo check --locked --no-default-features`;\n- the release set `--no-default-features --features graph,theia-bridge`;\n- `cargo test --locked --features theia-bridge`: 1264 passed, 0 failed;\n  - `--list-gears`, which lists `graph-storage`.\n- **The compose stand on the database weftgraph 0.1.1 created** (537k\nnodes, 643k edges), with images rebuilt from this branch:\n  - the backend boots healthy;\n  - the gear''s readiness is healthy on every implemented component;\n- the 44-check REST matrix (`scripts/graph-storage-bench/gs_bench.py\nfunc`) gives 39 pass, 0 fail and 5 notes. The notes are the same\ndocumented limits as on 0.1.1.\n- repository sync of `constructorfabric/insight` through the connector\nwrites 26 nodes and 31 edges the repository gained since the last run,\nand a re-sync converges: 0 and 0, in 2.3 s.\n\n## After this merges\n\nThe `weftgraph*` crates on crates.io get a deprecation release pointing\nto `cf-gears-graph-storage` and are then yanked. A yank leaves existing\nlock files working. From here on, gear updates arrive the same way as\nevery other gears crate: through gears-rust `main` and release-plz.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Chores**\n* Updated the backend’s graph-storage integration to use the officially\npublished components.\n* Updated graph-storage setup references across development and\ndeployment configurations.\n* No changes to configuration values or runtime behavior. These updates\ndo not change the features or behavior available to end users.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\nSigned-off-by: vasylcf <vasylcf@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqw6DBCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZXwQAJK1eGwlEcPge1cHAjXfEEqi\nvqsAtGVzvGU5FlbeGlnjdmxmCnt5p2K6bsPQ6t/NetXcr3u+2fU/hxxPLTSrONUH\n1uBmx8xO3rc+2mu8cUoMHJQYighmFCNzUKrolsDL8odIDHTWIptA3gdSG+WD1WUQ\nY6nO+lMkwKrotv54Vla73ozyh9XtNu4zJMM8xt9NmyO8SmmCsiwIMynZOxZcIquc\nxIkfJtOa7A6gwwvUP+m4VOk0IY/DG5WDQNY+B941Ok5Wjw8DLSmz33LxPl2WXRKB\nWFYS54n7SLTBxHBjSQ8623uss+HNs/DULcQh4Xn0ddD/rVTINndWgQ3rGvSr45yD\nGNzAC8Iw12yRXbADoFCweTLxcF4c8SjtqjEXRrjDZ+CQym72qLTWiyoV1zC+gmLZ\nSPAE7ff8pYQ81v/Cljq4NSNn1PW5j/yAK/Xjdpu/uMUfjWV29wQmmozA3dAiefpS\nZqcTJfOG9VwtI7l4v8fzuQyIl+qllbmCr+4QgqJJoCvixNM1f9HgsEgEpVjoL0xF\n48W9iBZMmE6kglpt+Bcs8sUkJaSF6/D5gsnJjVVdg5tXXp2xvplnAxQEB+HXthZo\nE1lzHAe4z3f8SyQ6dUcdgJBrqwY6jGUpbVBsiqaibkHBOocRhpx+opB8M5aeitxb\n2NskZ/0WEV3zN4R+YCv1\n=Shq4\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-05T13:06:10Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/6a21d527fb1922900b0ae8dfad77aa12eb79ed89","node_id":"C_kwDOTl7dJtoAKDZhMjFkNTI3ZmIxOTIyOTAwYjBhZThkZmFkNzdhYTEyZWI3OWVkODk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/717075a0ddf91e03132c4254a3bab22b2b971a8f","sha":"717075a0ddf91e03132c4254a3bab22b2b971a8f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/717075a0ddf91e03132c4254a3bab22b2b971a8f"}],"sha":"6a21d527fb1922900b0ae8dfad77aa12eb79ed89","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/6a21d527fb1922900b0ae8dfad77aa12eb79ed89"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/301748190?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AndrejK666","id":301748190,"login":"AndrejK666","node_id":"U_kgDOEfxP3g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/717075a0ddf91e03132c4254a3bab22b2b971a8f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T14:30:19Z","email":"Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech","name":"ANDREI KUCHMA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T14:30:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(components): save product.gdl to the project''s repository and open it in the desktop Studio (#617)\n\n## Why\nThe Components tab composes a product, but the two steps after that were\nbroken:\n- **Save product.gdl to the repository** failed with `HTTP 400 · writing\nproduct.gdl failed: no gear repository is connected to this project`.\nThis happened on every project whose repository is connected as a\nsource, Studio-web on dev included.\n- **Build it in Studio-ide** opened a web session, which no longer runs\nGearbox (#605).\n\nThe result is one process: compose in the portal, save `product.gdl`,\nkeep working in the desktop Studio.\n\n## What\n- **backend**: `write_to_project_repo` now picks its target via\n`write_target`. It uses the gear repository when one was connected on\nthe tab. Otherwise it uses the project''s first source read through a\nconnection (`project.config` `sources[]`, the same fallback reading\nalready had). When neither exists, the error says to add a repository on\nthe Sources tab.\n- **link**: `cfstudio://open` takes optional `product=` and `branch=`.\n- `product` is checked as a repository path (no root, no `..`,\nconservative alphabet).\n  - `branch` is checked as a branch name (no leading `-`, no `..`).\n- **desktop**: after cloning and opening the project,\n`DesktopLinkHandler` runs `gearbox.product.openAt(product, branch)`.\nThat is the command a portal session runs for `studio.openProduct`, and\nit brings the saved branch in beside the checkout.\n  - Without Gearbox, the file opens as a plain file.\n  - If that fails too, the person is told where the product is.\n- **portal**:\n  - **Build it in Studio-ide** saves, then launches the desktop link.\n  - **Open in IDE** after a save is now **Open in Studio-ide**.\n- Both are shown without a web session and show the \"install the desktop\napp\" hint when nothing takes the link.\n\n## Checked\n- backend: `cargo test` passes 277 across components_catalog,\nproject_sources and api_contract; `clippy --all-targets -D warnings` and\n`fmt` are clean.\n- theia/studio: jest passes 17/17 on desktop-link and\ndesktop-link-handler. New tests cover: product and branch carried;\nunsafe path or branch dropped; Gearbox command run after open; fallback\nmessage. `tsc` has 0 errors.\n- prototype: `tsc` is clean and vitest passes 282/282 (new: link carries\nproduct and branch).\n- Not on a stand yet. The save fallback writes to a real GitHub\nrepository, so it will be checked by the person clicking Save on dev\nafter deploy.\n\n## Also: unblocks the #615 deploy\nThe first dev deploy of #615 (`sha-fc2021c8`) rolled back. The namespace\nLimitRange refuses containers under 10m CPU / 16Mi memory, so every\nsession pre-pull Pod was rejected and `--wait` timed out. `4b2625ba`\nraises the pre-pull to 10m/16Mi requests and 20m/32Mi limits. Merging\nthis PR ships #615 too.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n* Open a product directly in desktop Studio from the web interface, with\nits project and branch selected when available.\n* If the desktop app is unavailable, the interface displays a hint. If\nopening a product fails, Studio attempts to open its description file\nand shows a message if that also fails.\n* **Improvements**\n* Project scaffold writes now use an available connected repository and\nits configured branch, defaulting to `main` when needed.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","tree":{"sha":"72ef0aa7908db66165ace64f619f59ee02e208bc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/trees/72ef0aa7908db66165ace64f619f59ee02e208bc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/commits/717075a0ddf91e03132c4254a3bab22b2b971a8f","verification":{"payload":"tree 72ef0aa7908db66165ace64f619f59ee02e208bc\nparent fc2021c8238b4754d103921710cc8b37f2dda0e6\nauthor ANDREI KUCHMA <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech> 1790951419 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790951419 +0200\n\nfeat(components): save product.gdl to the project''s repository and open it in the desktop Studio (#617)\n\n## Why\nThe Components tab composes a product, but the two steps after that were\nbroken:\n- **Save product.gdl to the repository** failed with `HTTP 400 · writing\nproduct.gdl failed: no gear repository is connected to this project`.\nThis happened on every project whose repository is connected as a\nsource, Studio-web on dev included.\n- **Build it in Studio-ide** opened a web session, which no longer runs\nGearbox (#605).\n\nThe result is one process: compose in the portal, save `product.gdl`,\nkeep working in the desktop Studio.\n\n## What\n- **backend**: `write_to_project_repo` now picks its target via\n`write_target`. It uses the gear repository when one was connected on\nthe tab. Otherwise it uses the project''s first source read through a\nconnection (`project.config` `sources[]`, the same fallback reading\nalready had). When neither exists, the error says to add a repository on\nthe Sources tab.\n- **link**: `cfstudio://open` takes optional `product=` and `branch=`.\n- `product` is checked as a repository path (no root, no `..`,\nconservative alphabet).\n  - `branch` is checked as a branch name (no leading `-`, no `..`).\n- **desktop**: after cloning and opening the project,\n`DesktopLinkHandler` runs `gearbox.product.openAt(product, branch)`.\nThat is the command a portal session runs for `studio.openProduct`, and\nit brings the saved branch in beside the checkout.\n  - Without Gearbox, the file opens as a plain file.\n  - If that fails too, the person is told where the product is.\n- **portal**:\n  - **Build it in Studio-ide** saves, then launches the desktop link.\n  - **Open in IDE** after a save is now **Open in Studio-ide**.\n- Both are shown without a web session and show the \"install the desktop\napp\" hint when nothing takes the link.\n\n## Checked\n- backend: `cargo test` passes 277 across components_catalog,\nproject_sources and api_contract; `clippy --all-targets -D warnings` and\n`fmt` are clean.\n- theia/studio: jest passes 17/17 on desktop-link and\ndesktop-link-handler. New tests cover: product and branch carried;\nunsafe path or branch dropped; Gearbox command run after open; fallback\nmessage. `tsc` has 0 errors.\n- prototype: `tsc` is clean and vitest passes 282/282 (new: link carries\nproduct and branch).\n- Not on a stand yet. The save fallback writes to a real GitHub\nrepository, so it will be checked by the person clicking Save on dev\nafter deploy.\n\n## Also: unblocks the #615 deploy\nThe first dev deploy of #615 (`sha-fc2021c8`) rolled back. The namespace\nLimitRange refuses containers under 10m CPU / 16Mi memory, so every\nsession pre-pull Pod was rejected and `--wait` timed out. `4b2625ba`\nraises the pre-pull to 10m/16Mi requests and 20m/32Mi limits. Merging\nthis PR ships #615 too.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n* Open a product directly in desktop Studio from the web interface, with\nits project and branch selected when available.\n* If the desktop app is unavailable, the interface displays a hint. If\nopening a product fails, Studio attempts to open its description file\nand shows a message if that also fails.\n* **Improvements**\n* Project scaffold writes now use an available connected repository and\nits configured branch, defaulting to `main` when needed.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqv7/7CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAv0wQAAxzF5h4UELPquzNVVe5iKCm\nDD57me20I7Mu64dUETjzgUD1G0aM8lLyQpOqhFB4bw0yx/DGCLxSCKpNr+p6NgFn\njc5q5agjM+J1NoKGDXMQShShRrvinSMbV6j6wJz7ma5VSDYarKhk25twDbNu04u1\nRx067HD8XO4b1CEpU+r8lNCUx96VT1ttsoX08yDHPuKAlpEedUy6QAyjBH9ju1Z8\n7w3XHtFq8pm1j1eXCx20CUByzw3dYhWIs5U71iSUANg29mXCBk+UkoVGE/sYx2SL\ngs/ak6sinqoDZD1agq5KYuug6HHWDAOcUIE5PHHFxfrIyu3VlBbMY3olu3hHF3pw\n8SK/qnEcFKzHZe5pM274YXpCVR+yrM+1NXIBipTuXdw6DUqesoq2lX5wySAnW5F6\narm2CPib3vCiZp7u/GyNrufc7dIsssbugWPGg0f3CO/Z0TGHSBu9YBlex7SasdLR\n+0H38vsoVYYEfy1qMw34a/6OzhnxJ2XCKNf/wecgYm7bFGSTFX+MmpD6/CgyhmEC\nUYkPmqoY9M72EuJlTzkq74eHvGrTFFzmgFB3+AAvyCxuLbZOGpR944q8J0gzcbQs\nb+uv4eiE4aMd8PMe2x5AZ4Hd4qeg7xriml9406cNz+n2Ekbfn40goCsd43ZcRQ7R\nc0N8MFOHdyS3blw+rp5b\n=0Shr\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-02T14:30:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/717075a0ddf91e03132c4254a3bab22b2b971a8f","node_id":"C_kwDOTl7dJtoAKDcxNzA3NWEwZGRmOTFlMDMxMzJjNDI1NGEzYmFiMjJiMmI5NzFhOGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/fc2021c8238b4754d103921710cc8b37f2dda0e6","sha":"fc2021c8238b4754d103921710cc8b37f2dda0e6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/fc2021c8238b4754d103921710cc8b37f2dda0e6"}],"sha":"717075a0ddf91e03132c4254a3bab22b2b971a8f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/717075a0ddf91e03132c4254a3bab22b2b971a8f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/301748190?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AndrejK666","id":301748190,"login":"AndrejK666","node_id":"U_kgDOEfxP3g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/fc2021c8238b4754d103921710cc8b37f2dda0e6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T12:29:48Z","email":"Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech","name":"ANDREI KUCHMA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T12:29:48Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"perf(session): open a document in the IDE faster — prewarm, idle stop, image pre-pull, Analyze by path (#615)\n\n## Why\nOpening a document in the IDE from the portal was slow. Measured on dev:\n\n| Wait | Time | Fixed by |\n|---|---|---|\n| Session image pull on a node without it (first IDE after a deploy) |\n~61 s | image pre-pull |\n| Pod created, studio-web cloned, Theia up, workbench ready (image\ncached) | ~9 s | prewarm |\n| `studio.init` retry interval | up to 2 s | 300 ms retry |\n| Analyze panel finding the open file''s binding: 5 sequential pages,\n~600 KB | ~3.3 s | `?path=` filter |\n\n## What\n**Prewarm.** `ProjectScreen` calls `studio.prewarm(target)` as soon as a\nproject opens. The session starts in the background, so the click only\nwaits for Theia''s frontend.\n- Creation is idempotent per workspace: a click that arrives later, or\nwhile the prewarm is still in flight, gets the same session.\n- No prewarm when an IDE space is already mounted, since a document\nclick reuses it.\n- At most once per target every 10 min.\n\n**Idle stop.** The reaper (every 5 min) also stops a session no browser\nhas had open for `idle_session_secs` (default 900; 0 turns it off).\n- The session reports its own idle time in `getRuntimeStatus.idleSecs`,\ncounted from Theia''s browser RPC connections. The event forwarder\ndoesn''t count.\n- No replica sees all of a session''s traffic, and the k8s RBAC needs no\nnew verb.\n- Sessions younger than the threshold are never probed.\n- A session that can''t report (older image, unreachable) is left to\n`max_session_secs`.\n\n**Handshake.** `studio.init` retries every 300 ms instead of 2 s. The\nbridge can''t speak first, because it learns the portal''s origin from\nthis message.\n\n**Image pre-pull.** `templates/backend/session-image-prepull.yaml` holds\none idle Pod of the session image on each node.\n- The Pod runs `sleep` as uid 1000 with requests of 5m/8Mi.\n- It is a Deployment, because the deployer Role can''t create DaemonSets.\n- Spread with `ScheduleAnyway`, so it never leaves a Pod Pending under\n`--wait`. `Recreate` strategy, so the deploy pulls the new tag on every\nnode.\n- `backend.sessions.prepull.enabled`: off by default, on in\n`values-dev.example.yaml` (3 worker nodes).\n\n**Analyze by path.** `GET …/projects/{p}/document-bindings` accepts\n`path=` (repeatable) and returns the matches unpaged. The panel now asks\nonly for the open file''s candidate paths.\n- The full list is still read where it''s needed: the set bloat compares\nagainst.\n- The client filters the response too, in case it talks to a backend\nfrom before `path=`.\n\nNot changed: the 26.8 MB frontend bundle. It is already served\nprecompressed (`bundle.js.gz`, 7.4 MB) and revalidated by ETag, so\nrepeat opens don''t download it again.\n\n## Checked\n- backend: `cargo test` passes 248 across documents (on real Postgres,\nincluding the new by-path test), `api_contract` and `studio_session`\n(including 5 new idle tests). `clippy --all-targets -D warnings` and\n`fmt --check` are clean.\n- theia/studio: jest passes 87/87 on the Analyze and endpoint suites;\n`tsc` has 0 errors.\n- prototype: `tsc` is clean and vitest passes 280/280.\n- helm: `lint` passes with the dev values; the template renders; no\nService/PDB selector matches the new Pods. The session image has\n`/usr/bin/sleep` and runs as uid 1000.\n- Not yet on a stand. After merge: deploy backend, then prototype. Then\ncheck that there is one prepull Pod per node, that the session Pod\nexists before the click, `session.await_ready` ~0 s, one bindings\nrequest on open, and that an unopened session stops after ~15–20 min.\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","tree":{"sha":"0ab61c6517c91bb869cc52b5e16e2e23d2098865","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/trees/0ab61c6517c91bb869cc52b5e16e2e23d2098865"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/commits/fc2021c8238b4754d103921710cc8b37f2dda0e6","verification":{"payload":"tree 0ab61c6517c91bb869cc52b5e16e2e23d2098865\nparent 389debb9443679266bef3cc2e1f2975f16d2b36e\nauthor ANDREI KUCHMA <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech> 1790944188 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790944188 +0200\n\nperf(session): open a document in the IDE faster — prewarm, idle stop, image pre-pull, Analyze by path (#615)\n\n## Why\nOpening a document in the IDE from the portal was slow. Measured on dev:\n\n| Wait | Time | Fixed by |\n|---|---|---|\n| Session image pull on a node without it (first IDE after a deploy) |\n~61 s | image pre-pull |\n| Pod created, studio-web cloned, Theia up, workbench ready (image\ncached) | ~9 s | prewarm |\n| `studio.init` retry interval | up to 2 s | 300 ms retry |\n| Analyze panel finding the open file''s binding: 5 sequential pages,\n~600 KB | ~3.3 s | `?path=` filter |\n\n## What\n**Prewarm.** `ProjectScreen` calls `studio.prewarm(target)` as soon as a\nproject opens. The session starts in the background, so the click only\nwaits for Theia''s frontend.\n- Creation is idempotent per workspace: a click that arrives later, or\nwhile the prewarm is still in flight, gets the same session.\n- No prewarm when an IDE space is already mounted, since a document\nclick reuses it.\n- At most once per target every 10 min.\n\n**Idle stop.** The reaper (every 5 min) also stops a session no browser\nhas had open for `idle_session_secs` (default 900; 0 turns it off).\n- The session reports its own idle time in `getRuntimeStatus.idleSecs`,\ncounted from Theia''s browser RPC connections. The event forwarder\ndoesn''t count.\n- No replica sees all of a session''s traffic, and the k8s RBAC needs no\nnew verb.\n- Sessions younger than the threshold are never probed.\n- A session that can''t report (older image, unreachable) is left to\n`max_session_secs`.\n\n**Handshake.** `studio.init` retries every 300 ms instead of 2 s. The\nbridge can''t speak first, because it learns the portal''s origin from\nthis message.\n\n**Image pre-pull.** `templates/backend/session-image-prepull.yaml` holds\none idle Pod of the session image on each node.\n- The Pod runs `sleep` as uid 1000 with requests of 5m/8Mi.\n- It is a Deployment, because the deployer Role can''t create DaemonSets.\n- Spread with `ScheduleAnyway`, so it never leaves a Pod Pending under\n`--wait`. `Recreate` strategy, so the deploy pulls the new tag on every\nnode.\n- `backend.sessions.prepull.enabled`: off by default, on in\n`values-dev.example.yaml` (3 worker nodes).\n\n**Analyze by path.** `GET …/projects/{p}/document-bindings` accepts\n`path=` (repeatable) and returns the matches unpaged. The panel now asks\nonly for the open file''s candidate paths.\n- The full list is still read where it''s needed: the set bloat compares\nagainst.\n- The client filters the response too, in case it talks to a backend\nfrom before `path=`.\n\nNot changed: the 26.8 MB frontend bundle. It is already served\nprecompressed (`bundle.js.gz`, 7.4 MB) and revalidated by ETag, so\nrepeat opens don''t download it again.\n\n## Checked\n- backend: `cargo test` passes 248 across documents (on real Postgres,\nincluding the new by-path test), `api_contract` and `studio_session`\n(including 5 new idle tests). `clippy --all-targets -D warnings` and\n`fmt --check` are clean.\n- theia/studio: jest passes 87/87 on the Analyze and endpoint suites;\n`tsc` has 0 errors.\n- prototype: `tsc` is clean and vitest passes 280/280.\n- helm: `lint` passes with the dev values; the template renders; no\nService/PDB selector matches the new Pods. The session image has\n`/usr/bin/sleep` and runs as uid 1000.\n- Not yet on a stand. After merge: deploy backend, then prototype. Then\ncheck that there is one prepull Pod per node, that the session Pod\nexists before the click, `session.await_ready` ~0 s, one bindings\nrequest on open, and that an unopened session stops after ~15–20 min.\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqv6O8CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjqcQAAaHZzmFOBLJc08Y004VzfCf\nUEi6UFcqbUAtEK7heWe9kpsxKf3rlC8vc5Vamt9f7gb8AgKTyYoIhwh46Hjrcx3u\nOHR85wed9ZeQCM52Auntluq2XPgtab5Uzs0iBaa/Y4YJNeQqM8Z5SKUZIrGap1lM\nXV03t1gf7IQpoKd2oSavXgwjUco0uqNIgkwpU8PbnzicJqVhjrVqzxb7JwDMeIvJ\ndHjCgTkvrLxz0EXcwJ6DXdEoz3UzZ6GtBxj7fh4u0L1mGmSdJtUaD+dy9hpjO+rM\n2N0sR1Xl1S1dGAfbsyda7jxjvyiVhugp6FEmsk2MiXXqIMNUz7k6rZWgayWH9ZDc\nbgn6uBncRCmN8uAZAjhXBtl1PjM/BQr52thEJ8g4tH/3VTmLChKe1HHyqMBxxe75\nIJNBahZ+a4vvV15CLwvG5cOBCfIsxbPYLunDlpS1/y9xlgrrtEdI9sDRn6U6+nc9\nitAS/VEbCjNmqgzVoIXaiaRmydBXi1mxmS0NFy1+JQ3mrbKKKvpGC+CZQwHTsOVy\nSkqLqmixpzvvD1AuKG2zQ4wxGKzYbmgkkfu5hfYqBqvHBpA4Tpsq2SsVgVizMtFt\neJkpCIWDpir5KmhTELq0l/s9sWMzDKuyHi0fJh8iY+1ZL9nlDd7MiAQSxD0yCBiQ\nfa+rQ5Gavf63YZ/zm7P7\n=hWbe\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-02T12:29:49Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/fc2021c8238b4754d103921710cc8b37f2dda0e6","node_id":"C_kwDOTl7dJtoAKGZjMjAyMWM4MjM4YjQ3NTRkMTAzOTIxNzEwY2M4YjM3ZjJkZGEwZTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/389debb9443679266bef3cc2e1f2975f16d2b36e","sha":"389debb9443679266bef3cc2e1f2975f16d2b36e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/389debb9443679266bef3cc2e1f2975f16d2b36e"}],"sha":"fc2021c8238b4754d103921710cc8b37f2dda0e6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/fc2021c8238b4754d103921710cc8b37f2dda0e6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/301748190?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AndrejK666","id":301748190,"login":"AndrejK666","node_id":"U_kgDOEfxP3g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/389debb9443679266bef3cc2e1f2975f16d2b36e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T10:11:40Z","email":"Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech","name":"ANDREI KUCHMA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T10:11:40Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(session): a session whose gate dies comes back, and a dead one is replaced (#614)\n\nFollow-up to #612. That PR stops the session gate from dying when a tab\ncloses. This one makes sure a session recovers if the gate or the\ncontainer dies for any other reason.\n\n## What was wrong\n\nOn studio-dev, `cf-studio-session-349c7f25…` lost its gate at 08:47.\nAfter that:\n\n- The Pod stayed `Running` and `0/1 Ready`. There is no liveness probe\nand `restartPolicy` is `Never`, so nothing restarted the container.\n- `KubernetesDriver::is_running` checked only the phase, so\n`SessionService::create` reused that Pod, and every open of the IDE got\nthe dead address.\n- Even if the Pod had been marked dead, the replacement Pod has the same\nname, which comes from the workspace. `create` would then fail on\n`AlreadyExists`, because nothing removed the old Pod first.\n\n## Change\n\n- **Restart in place.** `restartPolicy: Always`, plus a TCP liveness\nprobe on 3003 (every 10 s, restart after 6 misses). A container restart\nkeeps the Pod, its `emptyDir` `/workspace` and its address. The\nentrypoint skips sources it already cloned (\"already materialized —\nskipping\"). The probe is TCP because during workspace preparation the\nsplash holds the port but answers `/__studio_session_ready__` with 503,\nand an HTTP probe would kill a session that is only cloning slowly.\n- **Don''t reuse a stuck Pod.** `pod_is_live` adds one rule to the phase\ncheck: a `Running` Pod whose `Ready` has been `False` for more than 10\nminutes is not live. `Pending` stays live, and so does a Pod that is\nbriefly unready during preparation or after a restart.\n- **Remove the dead one first.** When `create` finds a listed session\nwithout a live runtime, it calls `driver.destroy` before launching the\nreplacement. Destroy is idempotent, and NotFound is success.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `a_pod_unready_for_too_long_is_not_reused`,\n`a_pod_briefly_unready_or_ready_is_still_live` (k8s.rs).\n- `a_dead_session_is_removed_before_it_is_replaced` (service.rs). The\n`LaunchingRuntime` fake can now mark a handle dead, and records\n`destroy`.\n- `cargo fmt --check`, `clippy --all-targets -D warnings`, and the 60\n`studio_session::` tests pass in the backend-check container.\n\n## To check on a stand\n\nKill the gate in a running session (`kubectl exec … -- pkill -f\ngate.js`). The container should restart within about a minute, and the\nIDE should come back with `/workspace` intact. In particular, check that\norca and Theia start cleanly on a `/workspace` they already used.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","tree":{"sha":"f01e5ddb839f06da63ef13d48b7a4101485eca82","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/trees/f01e5ddb839f06da63ef13d48b7a4101485eca82"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/commits/389debb9443679266bef3cc2e1f2975f16d2b36e","verification":{"payload":"tree f01e5ddb839f06da63ef13d48b7a4101485eca82\nparent 4a2886058c6261cefa3d3764c3471b2c26d0fafa\nauthor ANDREI KUCHMA <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech> 1790935900 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790935900 +0200\n\nfix(session): a session whose gate dies comes back, and a dead one is replaced (#614)\n\nFollow-up to #612. That PR stops the session gate from dying when a tab\ncloses. This one makes sure a session recovers if the gate or the\ncontainer dies for any other reason.\n\n## What was wrong\n\nOn studio-dev, `cf-studio-session-349c7f25…` lost its gate at 08:47.\nAfter that:\n\n- The Pod stayed `Running` and `0/1 Ready`. There is no liveness probe\nand `restartPolicy` is `Never`, so nothing restarted the container.\n- `KubernetesDriver::is_running` checked only the phase, so\n`SessionService::create` reused that Pod, and every open of the IDE got\nthe dead address.\n- Even if the Pod had been marked dead, the replacement Pod has the same\nname, which comes from the workspace. `create` would then fail on\n`AlreadyExists`, because nothing removed the old Pod first.\n\n## Change\n\n- **Restart in place.** `restartPolicy: Always`, plus a TCP liveness\nprobe on 3003 (every 10 s, restart after 6 misses). A container restart\nkeeps the Pod, its `emptyDir` `/workspace` and its address. The\nentrypoint skips sources it already cloned (\"already materialized —\nskipping\"). The probe is TCP because during workspace preparation the\nsplash holds the port but answers `/__studio_session_ready__` with 503,\nand an HTTP probe would kill a session that is only cloning slowly.\n- **Don''t reuse a stuck Pod.** `pod_is_live` adds one rule to the phase\ncheck: a `Running` Pod whose `Ready` has been `False` for more than 10\nminutes is not live. `Pending` stays live, and so does a Pod that is\nbriefly unready during preparation or after a restart.\n- **Remove the dead one first.** When `create` finds a listed session\nwithout a live runtime, it calls `driver.destroy` before launching the\nreplacement. Destroy is idempotent, and NotFound is success.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `a_pod_unready_for_too_long_is_not_reused`,\n`a_pod_briefly_unready_or_ready_is_still_live` (k8s.rs).\n- `a_dead_session_is_removed_before_it_is_replaced` (service.rs). The\n`LaunchingRuntime` fake can now mark a handle dead, and records\n`destroy`.\n- `cargo fmt --check`, `clippy --all-targets -D warnings`, and the 60\n`studio_session::` tests pass in the backend-check container.\n\n## To check on a stand\n\nKill the gate in a running session (`kubectl exec … -- pkill -f\ngate.js`). The container should restart within about a minute, and the\nIDE should come back with `/workspace` intact. In particular, check that\norca and Theia start cleanly on a `/workspace` they already used.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqv4NcCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAHdsQAHChai8YapMbwiWVWGKzx762\nZ8C7Aa13Ydp8oNX9HPFK2UkA6P4L5LKgq5ztJWz2FiRbGk25oBG0fPrqbth11Nec\nYs7Ekh032Wkpkmh+x+UC6pLNZHP7LHafouyMv6LSy/db9E6N8KhbLfOC5XCGdFqp\n/F0x7lo/rUkEEJA4VJmZ6yfoVEjTH9nGkp8WcNf/th+VxtDDcrDPPn9NODCUGPxH\nd9OsQcCWMbDJKN7FuV7x1Yv8soVNXx/B4iiE1PTSb4EV6FZhrODo7AhQP8yGVvbd\nZDEPLD6EW37YTQrNtKGkrSB8SHXMtE8clri/DO3b5DczIRKhEb8ZuB7zzz0TXfNP\npAhVVZsANPcdt0MFt/gfJSdYjKiOeCiNNkZcBy8OlLSC0OEM0n3v6maABLsiC698\nIPJr9HwNb2008wdBA1z0X33gBGHxgZY6ezrwJ9LDTSyQfTMo2ZB9nMEuCyoFstet\n+YGUga1Idp8oJcPRyemKZlaU+MQmQhayoaJA1FfHmlmM0mt9FsFoS3m2vWYXzrgC\n/kxawaV1BxpI0eBoRn3DCaWH+o58/1McffHmsLbM48oThQ0X/2FfOAHkHfMGzl9P\nJmqGE9GMCwMYOeuu8e45gsKdGzirHDciyehzbNJBxTFwWruWcARgWg68D0/5QLZY\nvIJVxSa0nYaXC2dRJBY+\n=fkmB\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-02T10:11:41Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/389debb9443679266bef3cc2e1f2975f16d2b36e","node_id":"C_kwDOTl7dJtoAKDM4OWRlYmI5NDQzNjc5MjY2YmVmM2NjMmUxZjI5NzVmMTZkMmIzNmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/4a2886058c6261cefa3d3764c3471b2c26d0fafa","sha":"4a2886058c6261cefa3d3764c3471b2c26d0fafa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/4a2886058c6261cefa3d3764c3471b2c26d0fafa"}],"sha":"389debb9443679266bef3cc2e1f2975f16d2b36e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/389debb9443679266bef3cc2e1f2975f16d2b36e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/301748190?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AndrejK666","id":301748190,"login":"AndrejK666","node_id":"U_kgDOEfxP3g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/4a2886058c6261cefa3d3764c3471b2c26d0fafa/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T09:25:45Z","email":"Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech","name":"ANDREI KUCHMA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T09:25:45Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(session): a closed tab no longer kills the session gate (#612)\n\n## What happened\n\nOn studio-dev, session `cf-studio-session-349c7f25…` stayed `0/1 Ready`\nafter 08:50. Theia was still running on `127.0.0.1:3004`, but nothing\nlistened on 3003, the gate the browser and the readiness probe go\nthrough. The pod log shows why. At 08:47:28 the user closed the IDE tab,\nand the gate died:\n\n```\nnode:events:497\n      throw er; // Unhandled ''error'' event\nError: write EPIPE ... at Socket.ondata\n```\n\nThree minutes later (180 probes × 1 s) the pod went Not Ready. The pod\nhas no liveness probe and runs with `restartPolicy: Never`, so the\nsession stays dead until someone recreates it. Any session can hit this\non an ordinary tab close.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe `upgrade` handler in `theia/docker/entrypoint.sh` does\n`up.pipe(socket); socket.pipe(up)`, but only `up` had an `error`\nlistener. When the browser side resets first, the write into it raises\nan unhandled `error`, and Node exits.\n\n## Fix\n\n- Both sockets have an `error` listener, and either side closing\ndestroys the other.\n- The two proxy `error` handlers end the response if headers are already\nsent, instead of calling `writeHead` again, which would throw.\n- A last-resort `process.on(\"uncaughtException\")` logs and keeps\nserving.\n\n## Test\n\n`gate.test.mjs` starts a fake upstream on 3004 that keeps writing. It\nthen drops an upgraded connection mid-stream five times, and checks that\nreadiness still answers 204 and the gate process is alive. It fails on\n`main` with the same unhandled `ECONNRESET` and passes with the fix. The\ntest now also fails cleanly, with the gate''s stderr, instead of hanging\nwhen the gate exits.\n\n## Not in this PR\n\nA liveness probe would not help as things stand: with `restartPolicy:\nNever` a failed liveness check just marks the pod `Failed`. Making\nsessions restart their container is a separate decision.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n* Improved service stability when WebSocket connections close\nunexpectedly. The service can continue running and remain available for\nreadiness checks after repeated connection drops.\n* Improved handling of unexpected errors and interrupted HTTP responses,\nhelping prevent failures from disrupting ongoing service.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","tree":{"sha":"52f12129d64a478f37f4045c71bd529d0e096a9b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/trees/52f12129d64a478f37f4045c71bd529d0e096a9b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/commits/4a2886058c6261cefa3d3764c3471b2c26d0fafa","verification":{"payload":"tree 52f12129d64a478f37f4045c71bd529d0e096a9b\nparent 9df98c4f545d8474f16a231fc44c25175323289c\nauthor ANDREI KUCHMA <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech> 1790933145 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790933145 +0200\n\nfix(session): a closed tab no longer kills the session gate (#612)\n\n## What happened\n\nOn studio-dev, session `cf-studio-session-349c7f25…` stayed `0/1 Ready`\nafter 08:50. Theia was still running on `127.0.0.1:3004`, but nothing\nlistened on 3003, the gate the browser and the readiness probe go\nthrough. The pod log shows why. At 08:47:28 the user closed the IDE tab,\nand the gate died:\n\n```\nnode:events:497\n      throw er; // Unhandled ''error'' event\nError: write EPIPE ... at Socket.ondata\n```\n\nThree minutes later (180 probes × 1 s) the pod went Not Ready. The pod\nhas no liveness probe and runs with `restartPolicy: Never`, so the\nsession stays dead until someone recreates it. Any session can hit this\non an ordinary tab close.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe `upgrade` handler in `theia/docker/entrypoint.sh` does\n`up.pipe(socket); socket.pipe(up)`, but only `up` had an `error`\nlistener. When the browser side resets first, the write into it raises\nan unhandled `error`, and Node exits.\n\n## Fix\n\n- Both sockets have an `error` listener, and either side closing\ndestroys the other.\n- The two proxy `error` handlers end the response if headers are already\nsent, instead of calling `writeHead` again, which would throw.\n- A last-resort `process.on(\"uncaughtException\")` logs and keeps\nserving.\n\n## Test\n\n`gate.test.mjs` starts a fake upstream on 3004 that keeps writing. It\nthen drops an upgraded connection mid-stream five times, and checks that\nreadiness still answers 204 and the gate process is alive. It fails on\n`main` with the same unhandled `ECONNRESET` and passes with the fix. The\ntest now also fails cleanly, with the gate''s stderr, instead of hanging\nwhen the gate exits.\n\n## Not in this PR\n\nA liveness probe would not help as things stand: with `restartPolicy:\nNever` a failed liveness check just marks the pod `Failed`. Making\nsessions restart their container is a separate decision.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n* Improved service stability when WebSocket connections close\nunexpectedly. The service can continue running and remain available for\nreadiness checks after repeated connection drops.\n* Improved handling of unexpected errors and interrupted HTTP responses,\nhelping prevent failures from disrupting ongoing service.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqv3iZCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA2bkQADhP36GK88PI0kTa7Jjs6VQi\nKAMruIpaQn+L12Y0SRfvEzjo2lucF2ruJIuXw+2/m2q2gYoKBZ5bXgJcqjGdtM3f\naiTsyJv5qAKM/b9pFA5/L1sPJZtcRrSKPdFv6ibEPH4EvLRhU6wzPDD4smYsPeUe\nyeNF5AO03pzpCkedQJ2KBsQZKpBHhFVsvoDjwzJ6O2QdNRwziIkTH3cjJXIv9kJM\nkYUUDWlLve/hgjMdzDczupNOUWWaZ+8Uv7ZHtCSFVuANuuIF1AwbN216/0uuQNyz\n4lnAgnJjT1c5HXODoltHdIB8XoACkxSAKXgwDWBtk4As/iIWI2TYKaayk5E3et/4\n+eQ8EQFfsuWNgoNmK0iudT2AJ3WlnnAvTvvZLY1EblJmyhmkLR0ba0/+8j/UQnzf\nfztggOymr9slCRTm1VwNg+ekJQDcF1GKtRGq3Akcv7wX8iWmlbHz0YV1WQuIOh2v\nJ1k/3Xh7UMwBFuOFbnY5VBBOHZo+5+NVXJtvZxrqR86RYAJISE6W4aLI0mi5nBly\nXGPVu9isagkgvOzhatoQsVe5fot/JQ45g3G4X6DIiXTHg+zDLfOVd4fGt8Z5WfyR\nv8tGp206knFCgOtHzO3H9zdRPe8lpxrNMP0vKoDIUIVmDQC+CpWAI3Kbnsx0pHT1\nc+2bLiNpiBSQxnLjgwLF\n=vdZn\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-02T09:25:46Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/4a2886058c6261cefa3d3764c3471b2c26d0fafa","node_id":"C_kwDOTl7dJtoAKDRhMjg4NjA1OGM2MjYxY2VmYTNkMzc2NGMzNDcxYjJjMjZkMGZhZmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/9df98c4f545d8474f16a231fc44c25175323289c","sha":"9df98c4f545d8474f16a231fc44c25175323289c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/9df98c4f545d8474f16a231fc44c25175323289c"}],"sha":"4a2886058c6261cefa3d3764c3471b2c26d0fafa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/4a2886058c6261cefa3d3764c3471b2c26d0fafa"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/203880066?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudedigon/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudedigon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudedigon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudedigon/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudedigon","id":203880066,"login":"claudedigon","n