MT17DZQgcEBz+OGA3f92FKQo/k77tbnBJBYrZfMkJSEQ+J2ZZE0btQ8z74tzH\n3SclWN62CxlfueAXPlbphSuB4FAu4fJk5V+bkgPN5tcBYGzHQvrSLrZrDE5qauec\nAkDL8DGP5avGAZ8VGNQSZZmcRlD3T7vxzwDn+5GtJuXZE7TQnDqgeIlkjoFX9Kz4\nA2LFk83qQuFwLj+p/0NN7SEj4E8laPg61NJ9A05W+51QnTPYeX7S9McByHfDUCla\nRJwrpiumNO+5iY9uRXabX50SeFCraHoxvIisdydd1NkeNkrG4QMFn80CKoM9f+N2\nCoPdRxw+Vg7gjP5K/v64V3CLMPE6GiSTT8G5N9OieU1Lnxml+bFz2KqcutWWKN9B\nYJPOUOKuQRmY9fQY+dH7nwRR8ilN473EzREbwXrxitZ7LMgFY3jKKnpS3gIP9Q52\ndHfpMfrtU2VP8Gdi1qPS\n=oN7j\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-02T08:39:57Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/9df98c4f545d8474f16a231fc44c25175323289c","node_id":"C_kwDOTl7dJtoAKDlkZjk4YzRmNTQ1ZDg0NzRmMTZhMjMxZmM0NGMyNTE3NTMyMzI4OWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/635a159385689b3573c0989e9ddb977d03e2ca2f","sha":"635a159385689b3573c0989e9ddb977d03e2ca2f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/635a159385689b3573c0989e9ddb977d03e2ca2f"}],"sha":"9df98c4f545d8474f16a231fc44c25175323289c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/9df98c4f545d8474f16a231fc44c25175323289c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/301748190?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AndrejK666","id":301748190,"login":"AndrejK666","node_id":"U_kgDOEfxP3g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/635a159385689b3573c0989e9ddb977d03e2ca2f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T08:37:29Z","email":"Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech","name":"ANDREI KUCHMA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T08:37:29Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(reports): a report''s hourly refresh refreshes its organization, and the screen says when there is no plan (#607)\n\n## Why\n\nTwo problems showed up on dev after #595.\n\n**1. The hourly refresh never refreshed an organization''s report.**\n`studio-scheduler` schedules are platform-level: they live in, and fire\nin, the platform tenant. The `reports.refresh` schedule (`{\"report\":\n\"roadmap\"}`) therefore refreshed the platform''s source every hour. That\nsource was empty, so every run failed with *no board*, and each run\nwrote a source into the platform tenant along the way. Constructor\nFabric''s (`c31da936`) own report was never touched. Seen in\n`studio_scheduler_schedules` and `studio_tasks_runs` on dev.\n\n**2. The report quietly had no People, no team lanes on the Gantt and no\nproject columns.** The board was set and refreshed, but no plan\n(`gears.yaml`) had ever been loaded, and the screen said only \"has not\nbeen read yet\".\n\n## What\n\n**Schedules, per organization**\n- New narrow in-process port on the scheduler:\n`scheduler::port::Schedules`, with `find` and `ensure`.\n- `GET` / `PUT /studio-reports/v1/reports/{report_id}/schedule` manages\nthe schedule through studio-reports. The gear writes the caller''s\norganization into the payload (`{\"report\", \"organization_id\"}`), so a\nclient never names a tenant (rule C1).\n- A `reports.refresh` run that fires in another tenant **hands itself\non**: it queues the same refresh in the organization''s tenant, where the\nworker acts as that organization. The handed-on payload names no\norganization, so it cannot loop.\n- A refresh for an organization that saved no source now fails and\nwrites nothing.\n\n**Plan visibility**\n- `ReportSourceDto.plan` summarises the plan that was read: people,\nteams, projects, and the board it names.\n- The Reports screen says in place when there is no plan, or when the\nplan names no people. Either way People, the Gantt''s team lanes and the\nproject columns stay empty.\n- Refresh is disabled until something can name the board.\n- \"Load gears.yaml…\" is a real button.\n- The hourly switch goes through the new route instead of calling the\nscheduler directly.\n\nADR-0033 §4 is amended to say how schedules and organizations meet.\n\n## Verified\n\n- Backend: `cargo test` 1252/1252. Clippy `-D warnings`,\n`--no-default-features` and `--features theia-bridge` are clean, and the\napi-contract and gts-types snapshots are regenerated.\n- New tests:\n  - scheduler port payload matching;\n- routing and the hand-off, against a recording queue: queued in the\norganization''s tenant and never handed on again;\n  - one schedule per organization, carrying its organization;\n  - a refresh of an unsaved source writes nothing;\n  - the plan summary;\n  - prototype states (`no-plan`, `no-people`) and `canRefresh`.\n- Prototype: `tsc -b`, vitest 280/280, `check-api-usage` OK.\n\n**Not verified on a stand:** the hand-off through the real queue across\ntwo tenants. The local Keycloak has no user outside the platform tenant\nto drive it with. That the queue accepts a run for another tenant, and\nthat the worker runs it as that tenant''s identity, comes from reading\n`tasks/service.rs` and `tasks/dispatch.rs`.\n\n## After deploy, on dev\n\n1. In Reports, load `gears.yaml` → Save → Refresh. People, the Gantt\nlanes and the project columns appear.\n2. The old schedule in the platform tenant, *Refresh the roadmap report*\n(`9cf70e55-…`), fails every hour. Delete it (`DELETE\n/studio-scheduler/v1/schedules/9cf70e55-6704-43a0-8522-ddb3c8bd86b0`).\n3. Switch \"Refresh every hour\" on again. The new schedule names the\norganization, and its run hands itself to it.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n* Manage report refresh schedules directly from each report, with an\nhourly option and next-run time.\n  * View plan summaries with board, people, team, and project details.\n* See warnings when a report needs a plan or people before it can be\nrefreshed.\n* **Bug Fixes**\n* Refreshes now run in the report’s organization, and reports without a\nsaved source are no longer refreshed.\n  * Refresh is unavailable when required report inputs are missing.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","tree":{"sha":"7a07f2edfdf50b66d6a15a129947b890c34c90db","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/trees/7a07f2edfdf50b66d6a15a129947b890c34c90db"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/commits/635a159385689b3573c0989e9ddb977d03e2ca2f","verification":{"payload":"tree 7a07f2edfdf50b66d6a15a129947b890c34c90db\nparent 609cc15b3788e9b5305449dd821f2c4dc4524c4b\nauthor ANDREI KUCHMA <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech> 1790930249 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790930249 +0200\n\nfix(reports): a report''s hourly refresh refreshes its organization, and the screen says when there is no plan (#607)\n\n## Why\n\nTwo problems showed up on dev after #595.\n\n**1. The hourly refresh never refreshed an organization''s report.**\n`studio-scheduler` schedules are platform-level: they live in, and fire\nin, the platform tenant. The `reports.refresh` schedule (`{\"report\":\n\"roadmap\"}`) therefore refreshed the platform''s source every hour. That\nsource was empty, so every run failed with *no board*, and each run\nwrote a source into the platform tenant along the way. Constructor\nFabric''s (`c31da936`) own report was never touched. Seen in\n`studio_scheduler_schedules` and `studio_tasks_runs` on dev.\n\n**2. The report quietly had no People, no team lanes on the Gantt and no\nproject columns.** The board was set and refreshed, but no plan\n(`gears.yaml`) had ever been loaded, and the screen said only \"has not\nbeen read yet\".\n\n## What\n\n**Schedules, per organization**\n- New narrow in-process port on the scheduler:\n`scheduler::port::Schedules`, with `find` and `ensure`.\n- `GET` / `PUT /studio-reports/v1/reports/{report_id}/schedule` manages\nthe schedule through studio-reports. The gear writes the caller''s\norganization into the payload (`{\"report\", \"organization_id\"}`), so a\nclient never names a tenant (rule C1).\n- A `reports.refresh` run that fires in another tenant **hands itself\non**: it queues the same refresh in the organization''s tenant, where the\nworker acts as that organization. The handed-on payload names no\norganization, so it cannot loop.\n- A refresh for an organization that saved no source now fails and\nwrites nothing.\n\n**Plan visibility**\n- `ReportSourceDto.plan` summarises the plan that was read: people,\nteams, projects, and the board it names.\n- The Reports screen says in place when there is no plan, or when the\nplan names no people. Either way People, the Gantt''s team lanes and the\nproject columns stay empty.\n- Refresh is disabled until something can name the board.\n- \"Load gears.yaml…\" is a real button.\n- The hourly switch goes through the new route instead of calling the\nscheduler directly.\n\nADR-0033 §4 is amended to say how schedules and organizations meet.\n\n## Verified\n\n- Backend: `cargo test` 1252/1252. Clippy `-D warnings`,\n`--no-default-features` and `--features theia-bridge` are clean, and the\napi-contract and gts-types snapshots are regenerated.\n- New tests:\n  - scheduler port payload matching;\n- routing and the hand-off, against a recording queue: queued in the\norganization''s tenant and never handed on again;\n  - one schedule per organization, carrying its organization;\n  - a refresh of an unsaved source writes nothing;\n  - the plan summary;\n  - prototype states (`no-plan`, `no-people`) and `canRefresh`.\n- Prototype: `tsc -b`, vitest 280/280, `check-api-usage` OK.\n\n**Not verified on a stand:** the hand-off through the real queue across\ntwo tenants. The local Keycloak has no user outside the platform tenant\nto drive it with. That the queue accepts a run for another tenant, and\nthat the worker runs it as that tenant''s identity, comes from reading\n`tasks/service.rs` and `tasks/dispatch.rs`.\n\n## After deploy, on dev\n\n1. In Reports, load `gears.yaml` → Save → Refresh. People, the Gantt\nlanes and the project columns appear.\n2. The old schedule in the platform tenant, *Refresh the roadmap report*\n(`9cf70e55-…`), fails every hour. Delete it (`DELETE\n/studio-scheduler/v1/schedules/9cf70e55-6704-43a0-8522-ddb3c8bd86b0`).\n3. Switch \"Refresh every hour\" on again. The new schedule names the\norganization, and its run hands itself to it.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n* Manage report refresh schedules directly from each report, with an\nhourly option and next-run time.\n  * View plan summaries with board, people, team, and project details.\n* See warnings when a report needs a plan or people before it can be\nrefreshed.\n* **Bug Fixes**\n* Refreshes now run in the report’s organization, and reports without a\nsaved source are no longer refreshed.\n  * Refresh is unavailable when required report inputs are missing.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqv21JCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAPQ0QAFDXsuKSDkKfgggQ+odSfgdA\njs2ZbYeN/0BQwE1iDk9/JcR91629VQALgQ3h/Z9St32oyW0gAiYEceO9WjBpb5ho\nm9XFDNjVdXQrEcZDCdRbq1Fxl214PO8mzbKpE9S9bILu78B+TB662+fs86lKe7hW\nx9dDNOs8tNz8y7CfyjfKV0x3aRzuDEdQ+g+932QubWZQru4Ax1M+I4PZCovVPnhz\nJjxx3DJKDutyWOqcda6h4wlC2S5soKVdBbOdduPKdeV7iWviSo7tGE5hleqWezhU\nZISAJiTLBeo75tO8XXz39Ba6ayWlGbWn5sWNCJzLe7urKfCYrwSkiUxuK4bq0fYB\nxcv8NeLdl+eVulmqzyGQ28iuVZCThrznOjjzMn4EqNz6Ki9yl35tbxmgdAO1rxPd\nTMCSgDgkgKtg3Na+V1BZUtyK2Lods3+xLa2AB0V98TM0jfcQKf2CKBGvR0Y2e4B6\nEwYzr/UmYrxSr+l9xJ/unxooeRmoAKsYJcavLj1BOLwlMxzDMqSqHs3hiSbXOnQj\nrqaISoJS6v5bJY7IZH0B8xxSmrmCjPjYkQGGhUgnkTaMO2UU2hhzkYf55V1RXr/g\ngRY3/KoPe3FwZLaUpjptqoIIS5iP1zpzv0OayRHMcnKDSRvEyqgGingP0SAmH5VO\ncah24mki5WLYOGyIsSJm\n=ki3N\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-02T08:37:30Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/635a159385689b3573c0989e9ddb977d03e2ca2f","node_id":"C_kwDOTl7dJtoAKDYzNWExNTkzODU2ODliMzU3M2MwOTg5ZTlkZGI5NzdkMDNlMmNhMmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/609cc15b3788e9b5305449dd821f2c4dc4524c4b","sha":"609cc15b3788e9b5305449dd821f2c4dc4524c4b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/609cc15b3788e9b5305449dd821f2c4dc4524c4b"}],"sha":"635a159385689b3573c0989e9ddb977d03e2ca2f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/635a159385689b3573c0989e9ddb977d03e2ca2f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/301748190?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AndrejK666","id":301748190,"login":"AndrejK666","node_id":"U_kgDOEfxP3g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/609cc15b3788e9b5305449dd821f2c4dc4524c4b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T08:32:06Z","email":"Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech","name":"ANDREI KUCHMA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T08:32:06Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(documents): read a bound repository file''s text (#608)\n\n## Why\n\nThe designer prototype lists specs from `GET\n/studio-documents/v1/spec-rows`, but it can''t open a repository row''s\ntext. Only authored documents carry `content`. A repository file''s text\nlives in the session checkout or the sync''s clone, and the graph holds\nonly an 8k excerpt.\n\n## Contract\n\n`GET\n/studio-documents/v1/document-bindings/{id}/text?project_id=<project>`\n\n- `200 { \"text\": string }`: the file as the checkout the Spec Quality\ndetectors read holds it. That is the session''s checkout when there is\none, otherwise the sync''s clone.\n- `404`: there is no such binding in that project, or no checkout holds\nthe file yet.\n- `503`: this deployment has no `RepoFileReader`.\n\nA spec-rows repository row''s `id` is its binding id. The workspace is\nresolved from `project_id` and both are authorized, the same way\n`spec-rows` does it. An earlier draft had `/workspaces/{workspace_id}/…`\nin the path. That fails the `scope-in-path` rule of\n`docs/api-conventions.md`, so the route takes the same `?project_id=` as\nthe list it comes from.\n\n## One file, not the whole checkout\n\n`DocumentsService::binding_text` used to build every file of every\nrepository the project has, then keep one. That is too much to pay each\ntime a reader opens a document. Now:\n\n- `RepoFileReader` gains `read_repo_file` and `read_synced_clone_file`.\nTheir defaults walk, so other implementations keep working.\n- `IngestService` opens the one file with `clone::read_text_file`, under\n`clone::walk`''s rules: no symlinks at any step, nothing under `.git`, a\ntext path, 256 KiB at most, valid UTF-8. A path that is absolute or\ncontains `..` or an empty segment reads nothing.\n- `decide_binding`, the existing caller of `binding_text`, goes through\nthe same path.\n\n## Checked\n\nIn the `rust:1.97` backend-check container: `cargo fmt --check`, `cargo\nclippy --all-targets -D warnings`, `api-contract` regenerated, and the\n`api_contract`, `documents::` and `artifact_ingest::clone` tests (188\npassed). `the_synced_clone_…` also passes, now covering the single-file\nread too. The service-level selection (tenant order, project mismatch)\nhas no test of its own, since there is no `RepoFileReader` or\n`project_sources` fake to drive it.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","tree":{"sha":"16f8c221e5af9595f8ca87475e7b3661ba3348c2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/trees/16f8c221e5af9595f8ca87475e7b3661ba3348c2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/commits/609cc15b3788e9b5305449dd821f2c4dc4524c4b","verification":{"payload":"tree 16f8c221e5af9595f8ca87475e7b3661ba3348c2\nparent b72f4a775baca3336515ff0cceb5fa5fc7c3db6b\nauthor ANDREI KUCHMA <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech> 1790929926 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790929926 +0200\n\nfeat(documents): read a bound repository file''s text (#608)\n\n## Why\n\nThe designer prototype lists specs from `GET\n/studio-documents/v1/spec-rows`, but it can''t open a repository row''s\ntext. Only authored documents carry `content`. A repository file''s text\nlives in the session checkout or the sync''s clone, and the graph holds\nonly an 8k excerpt.\n\n## Contract\n\n`GET\n/studio-documents/v1/document-bindings/{id}/text?project_id=<project>`\n\n- `200 { \"text\": string }`: the file as the checkout the Spec Quality\ndetectors read holds it. That is the session''s checkout when there is\none, otherwise the sync''s clone.\n- `404`: there is no such binding in that project, or no checkout holds\nthe file yet.\n- `503`: this deployment has no `RepoFileReader`.\n\nA spec-rows repository row''s `id` is its binding id. The workspace is\nresolved from `project_id` and both are authorized, the same way\n`spec-rows` does it. An earlier draft had `/workspaces/{workspace_id}/…`\nin the path. That fails the `scope-in-path` rule of\n`docs/api-conventions.md`, so the route takes the same `?project_id=` as\nthe list it comes from.\n\n## One file, not the whole checkout\n\n`DocumentsService::binding_text` used to build every file of every\nrepository the project has, then keep one. That is too much to pay each\ntime a reader opens a document. Now:\n\n- `RepoFileReader` gains `read_repo_file` and `read_synced_clone_file`.\nTheir defaults walk, so other implementations keep working.\n- `IngestService` opens the one file with `clone::read_text_file`, under\n`clone::walk`''s rules: no symlinks at any step, nothing under `.git`, a\ntext path, 256 KiB at most, valid UTF-8. A path that is absolute or\ncontains `..` or an empty segment reads nothing.\n- `decide_binding`, the existing caller of `binding_text`, goes through\nthe same path.\n\n## Checked\n\nIn the `rust:1.97` backend-check container: `cargo fmt --check`, `cargo\nclippy --all-targets -D warnings`, `api-contract` regenerated, and the\n`api_contract`, `documents::` and `artifact_ingest::clone` tests (188\npassed). `the_synced_clone_…` also passes, now covering the single-file\nread too. The service-level selection (tenant order, project mismatch)\nhas no test of its own, since there is no `RepoFileReader` or\n`project_sources` fake to drive it.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqv2wGCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAEEgQAFrMF81MAioDwRzqMqgEJ4cd\nvo2hf5cAAAYhRI1RfGO4br3dQcN0vUbKCECLd/OPpGG7Et8lSeJhuX01sgiy8eLB\nFNDo7Nx0yT7TjnOPuanEQp2E46UUje4q5FkWKFixn5Z7rp2SC6z2Dik/PnaaciOR\niHO7lKQYLGDdafK8znWFOQXhNU6M7qxCG+Sw9/2UdGZkZiJfTEJAZEswS53/hVWq\np/eXGuRA4aPLTGJPGkAx3tXCYFqeqo+AJ64kVUYlOcL7KsektVNz3gAkzMnY9g2e\n1DdNtyVueArI2E148PlmQVsF+X0yUTCdJJo/CYib3mgE3erpe/YdQI7A28qdsbQ/\n0sOP5DFjXv7WWy25r67sfdmEjFmjTAPSSppV6l+LOrRK6oMAna0p8/4+gRoRegji\nXTSpud/kJkoipwcnp0SyTxxyqJz3ddG4Sgx5yHvzbIh7ENR3ux14oPizyZdu4ZG6\nmJMA7xDuAR8Ow1QBpqIYzjp44U1zui+4M5L8qqOaPon0HYsbHSKWkiXDnvjWfAc7\n6wU+R9ncAFGTVeRWYGOqy1mX9KKQUtrS5DD6WdSdsjUU97rYOx7jlKHF0/Aqx2Xc\nnVf618LftiGPUt6rZ71+3fbjqyCGfm8u6Zi9mPIeLDOVFLDDqARG6bJYWkivabR0\nJWwaIOWXH7j8bfMBDH5q\n=mMqZ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-02T08:32:07Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/609cc15b3788e9b5305449dd821f2c4dc4524c4b","node_id":"C_kwDOTl7dJtoAKDYwOWNjMTViMzc4OGU5YjUzMDU0NDlkZDgyMWYyYzRkYzQ1MjRjNGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/b72f4a775baca3336515ff0cceb5fa5fc7c3db6b","sha":"b72f4a775baca3336515ff0cceb5fa5fc7c3db6b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/b72f4a775baca3336515ff0cceb5fa5fc7c3db6b"}],"sha":"609cc15b3788e9b5305449dd821f2c4dc4524c4b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/609cc15b3788e9b5305449dd821f2c4dc4524c4b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/301748190?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AndrejK666","id":301748190,"login":"AndrejK666","node_id":"U_kgDOEfxP3g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/b72f4a775baca3336515ff0cceb5fa5fc7c3db6b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T08:31:35Z","email":"Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech","name":"ANDREI KUCHMA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T08:31:35Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(deploy): an IDE session is back to 2Gi now that the portal''s is light (#609)\n\n#602 raised the session memory limit to 4Gi. A studio-web session with\ntwo repositories, the Orca runtime and the Gearbox engine had been\nOOM-killed at 2Gi three times in a row.\n\nSince #605 a portal session runs none of those. Measured on dev with one\nwindow open (`ps` in the pod), it is **676Mi**, down from 1.33Gi. Each\nfurther window adds its own plugin host (~230MB) and Claude Code\n(~240MB):\n\n| Windows | Approx. memory |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | ~0.7Gi |\n| 2 | ~1.15Gi |\n| 3 | ~1.6Gi |\n\nSo 2Gi holds two or three people at once and frees quota for more\nconcurrent sessions. `STUDIO_SESSION_MEMORY_LIMIT` still overrides it\nper deployment.\n\nGates: `cargo test config` passes (it loads every profile).\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","tree":{"sha":"7f35c0e2cdde0ca321f9175bac08e136418eb5bf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/trees/7f35c0e2cdde0ca321f9175bac08e136418eb5bf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/commits/b72f4a775baca3336515ff0cceb5fa5fc7c3db6b","verification":{"payload":"tree 7f35c0e2cdde0ca321f9175bac08e136418eb5bf\nparent 4cd16a7d2e8ca2d078851d0e5e47e2ee09bb90cd\nauthor ANDREI KUCHMA <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech> 1790929895 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790929895 +0200\n\nfix(deploy): an IDE session is back to 2Gi now that the portal''s is light (#609)\n\n#602 raised the session memory limit to 4Gi. A studio-web session with\ntwo repositories, the Orca runtime and the Gearbox engine had been\nOOM-killed at 2Gi three times in a row.\n\nSince #605 a portal session runs none of those. Measured on dev with one\nwindow open (`ps` in the pod), it is **676Mi**, down from 1.33Gi. Each\nfurther window adds its own plugin host (~230MB) and Claude Code\n(~240MB):\n\n| Windows | Approx. memory |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | ~0.7Gi |\n| 2 | ~1.15Gi |\n| 3 | ~1.6Gi |\n\nSo 2Gi holds two or three people at once and frees quota for more\nconcurrent sessions. `STUDIO_SESSION_MEMORY_LIMIT` still overrides it\nper deployment.\n\nGates: `cargo test config` passes (it loads every profile).\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqv2vnCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAdbsQAKMIKb2RmPhpBU10OQSZ6FtT\nlwnWZA3p5ImMmMnmwt4ko8zmz7JcelntMmohvDXdOPhsaUXxvX6fWjyJ7F9MFKsL\nwT+o9eyi6UncREfFk0Sv609nr7TLttWLt14X+Qfe5gmkVqhbFGS3klWCIg3/L3LS\nfyIDBFwElm4IEGWvPxMNyID0JKBvycAHUuJzu8Q7cNIngD49A4njmB8EiLh5gI3G\noeg1If6pGv1vJiMrfTEcUEwpXyKZthf3IxxJTbc5EuuU0gfdxOCsjNzGyLp71g9q\nlay5e1VzubGnv1kv2oRdUDgyeNUfc2OhVzHgB/ampq40me7myxxZeP5VjHoTaXS8\nXIgxIDGQdFg6dzo91QsRceHG5WuEp/oeofsiVBH/r5kmVkzF7638qZCpE3uy8r3i\nxRJ3quTIgIjnDgb1a5SLUYMUEytLTqH74ltEVRtIZumoE3FM3Tj6ibg45SpqEFpW\nWkvY7fJuE1ZlVoE21lloOGjfLSpNVNrqeHOkEz/LhK1eWzHv3SHbUYLGBB1OceZL\nFrp71j58HCTy6YNqv16yLen278PjOIbpiqfwSfiE9pag2A1JsA4O3oQTjuyUiMRe\nYvOUDn6QqlsiTqQZnEOHSHpXxR/NEaeUFxjSR7/W5dFe/e5dGQc/UssnZzhtlk2M\n9EHkuPa1MHmV83lNiqY3\n=Gg6y\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-02T08:31:36Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/b72f4a775baca3336515ff0cceb5fa5fc7c3db6b","node_id":"C_kwDOTl7dJtoAKGI3MmY0YTc3NWJhY2EzMzM2NTE1ZmYwY2NlYjVmYTVmYzdjM2RiNmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/4cd16a7d2e8ca2d078851d0e5e47e2ee09bb90cd","sha":"4cd16a7d2e8ca2d078851d0e5e47e2ee09bb90cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/4cd16a7d2e8ca2d078851d0e5e47e2ee09bb90cd"}],"sha":"b72f4a775baca3336515ff0cceb5fa5fc7c3db6b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/b72f4a775baca3336515ff0cceb5fa5fc7c3db6b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/301748190?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AndrejK666","id":301748190,"login":"AndrejK666","node_id":"U_kgDOEfxP3g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/4cd16a7d2e8ca2d078851d0e5e47e2ee09bb90cd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T06:46:16Z","email":"Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech","name":"ANDREI KUCHMA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T06:46:16Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(session): the IDE the web portal opens is for documents and code, without Orca, Gearbox or a mode picker (#605)\n\nDecided 2026-10-02: the web portal never opens a heavy session. Orca and\nGearbox are Constructor Studio Desktop''s; the assistants (Claude Code,\nCodex) stay, because asking an agent about a document is part of writing\nit. Measured on dev the day before, Orca was ~530MB of a 1.33Gi session,\nand the gear corpus clone plus the Gearbox engine came on top of that.\n\n- Backend: orca_enabled defaults to false in the k8s and docker profiles\n  (STUDIO_ORCA_ENABLED=true brings it back).\n- Portal: a launch no longer adds the gears-rust corpus, and \"open\n  product\" opens product.gdl as a file instead of in the Gearbox\n  perspective.\n- Session image: STUDIO_GEARBOX_ENABLED defaults to 0; gearbox-studio\n  then starts no engine and no prewarm, and its panel says Gearbox runs in\n  the desktop.\n- IDE: Doc editing''s Agents button opens the Claude Code / Codex picker,\n  not Orca. The mode picker is the desktop''s only; in a web session the\n  portal decides the mode (it already switches to Doc editing when it\n  opens a document).\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","tree":{"sha":"e7ddea85f063e87548bd04ef38f6b702aab1c7c1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/trees/e7ddea85f063e87548bd04ef38f6b702aab1c7c1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/commits/4cd16a7d2e8ca2d078851d0e5e47e2ee09bb90cd","verification":{"payload":"tree e7ddea85f063e87548bd04ef38f6b702aab1c7c1\nparent 11bdeb01adf0f38ff50d750675a4c8bf8879fef4\nauthor ANDREI KUCHMA <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech> 1790923576 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790923576 +0200\n\nfeat(session): the IDE the web portal opens is for documents and code, without Orca, Gearbox or a mode picker (#605)\n\nDecided 2026-10-02: the web portal never opens a heavy session. Orca and\nGearbox are Constructor Studio Desktop''s; the assistants (Claude Code,\nCodex) stay, because asking an agent about a document is part of writing\nit. Measured on dev the day before, Orca was ~530MB of a 1.33Gi session,\nand the gear corpus clone plus the Gearbox engine came on top of that.\n\n- Backend: orca_enabled defaults to false in the k8s and docker profiles\n  (STUDIO_ORCA_ENABLED=true brings it back).\n- Portal: a launch no longer adds the gears-rust corpus, and \"open\n  product\" opens product.gdl as a file instead of in the Gearbox\n  perspective.\n- Session image: STUDIO_GEARBOX_ENABLED defaults to 0; gearbox-studio\n  then starts no engine and no prewarm, and its panel says Gearbox runs in\n  the desktop.\n- IDE: Doc editing''s Agents button opens the Claude Code / Codex picker,\n  not Orca. The mode picker is the desktop''s only; in a web session the\n  portal decides the mode (it already switches to Doc editing when it\n  opens a document).\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqv1M4CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZB0QAGlf6+aLeCufQhOC45SkBbB7\nV6vpXTgqI6BcqelH1Cc1psWL1HVQpRYXkYH3jyG8RfWoCyahTCylfg7gPU/hB46j\nb/gzC09roVNa7n7j1AE2DBuplo82ws26NPtDY2oIp9/+myjOtTgpZ8pWDjQC+Bp1\n3yhVDl1VQnFd2Iq0oHlWcoOQLkivHYiPtkKR3FHSxQWSaTT/kwhNFW1ycM+q6k+k\n42rh4843Kf29VQkOPmpQkP0LAjfXJ1DZKdiR5oLJcoupbt7r1cMlhFmeHlYtXimm\nzIISAiPKYeq+Jni/UMjJcmObfAxw/qUO8OZ5tugth+QI3QjmZ3K3y4rNmfVsc4WL\nRacK9rj4fE5h0Ylkozv3KlbD8TV4wlz7a4jpRpa21T/+WKWXQ/3mSOdcM2r8Gi3z\nYbgj4nnOtp+2Tf9V6NquTB+HoJJMEBtqc3/G4XTcnzlIJUD9N1vYsrYSmQVUsIda\nQYGh0n6xFqN43NEVd/TBNbkMDujcWZjQoXPZflYnxZVQ6VtXsh3Wkr053xJXbCQ7\niBFdzn2f47dt3lepnMYTdD7mFWt8Mr2RONg9emmdBrV0VMX7IJcpxsDFkvGFuq+G\nYVWpQO6I8kxyUE4/pN72mgPNr3JNJC6hcnmnyHbm1x0fE5L+9py86vKnqpqa7kdm\nk5zu/Kbou17AnCBngFyi\n=LSrZ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-02T06:46:16Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/4cd16a7d2e8ca2d078851d0e5e47e2ee09bb90cd","node_id":"C_kwDOTl7dJtoAKDRjZDE2YTdkMmU4Y2EyZDA3ODg1MWQwZTVlNDdlMmVlMDliYjkwY2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/11bdeb01adf0f38ff50d750675a4c8bf8879fef4","sha":"11bdeb01adf0f38ff50d750675a4c8bf8879fef4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/11bdeb01adf0f38ff50d750675a4c8bf8879fef4"}],"sha":"4cd16a7d2e8ca2d078851d0e5e47e2ee09bb90cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/4cd16a7d2e8ca2d078851d0e5e47e2ee09bb90cd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/301748190?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AndrejK666","id":301748190,"login":"AndrejK666","node_id":"U_kgDOEfxP3g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/11bdeb01adf0f38ff50d750675a4c8bf8879fef4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T22:10:19Z","email":"Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech","name":"ANDREI KUCHMA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T22:10:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(theia): the Analyze panel follows a tab picked while it has focus (#604)\n\nSeen on dev: with focus in the Analyze panel, picking another document''s\ntab in the editor area left the panel describing the previous document.\nThe shell''s current widget changed but its active one did not, and the\ncontroller listened only to the active one; with the panel active it also\nreturned the last document outright.\n\nIt now also listens to onDidChangeCurrentWidget, and with the panel\nfocused it describes the tab in front of the editor area, keeping the\nlast document only when no document is there. The new test fails on the\nprevious controller.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","tree":{"sha":"7e29759027a5e9a0ef8b7b10867a9bf48dffa2be","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/trees/7e29759027a5e9a0ef8b7b10867a9bf48dffa2be"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/commits/11bdeb01adf0f38ff50d750675a4c8bf8879fef4","verification":{"payload":"tree 7e29759027a5e9a0ef8b7b10867a9bf48dffa2be\nparent 53dbe0690c218390152679eef66828fe4610c919\nauthor ANDREI KUCHMA <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech> 1790892619 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790892619 +0200\n\nfix(theia): the Analyze panel follows a tab picked while it has focus (#604)\n\nSeen on dev: with focus in the Analyze panel, picking another document''s\ntab in the editor area left the panel describing the previous document.\nThe shell''s current widget changed but its active one did not, and the\ncontroller listened only to the active one; with the panel active it also\nreturned the last document outright.\n\nIt now also listens to onDidChangeCurrentWidget, and with the panel\nfocused it describes the tab in front of the editor area, keeping the\nlast document only when no document is there. The new test fails on the\nprevious controller.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvtpMCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAoF8QAD/8nEFVgfaKn9csQi6LyrKR\nKjoCwGbGQd/zprc/6/eHHXKURIpg3WcZTpVjFKtS5Lk+Kos6KahJMpoUSIRMYsYA\ng/YLHX4jjNu5A40OqL9PWOzLcf/vH34p4Ol1IlllRT5B6KlQi7Ra8iTNsFqtKNH8\ncrK3Vu7JaGOpAzfgHXAvCuQnMU4jThX1uQKvLUiDRWUiReHI6adPhcdV0eYFbT4o\n/hvPfbtGASqBi0VqQw+7hq03rUvPTTIq7bh6Lgar/VTYIaddop/9KD7D8Zx4Z5X3\nST2AuGbyCW3+osK6Xc+3nMlPJN2w95jH8W3tVWj+f9UrCruiuZsJiK1L3z9EErTA\nZjW5y4iAQRAZaQJSr4gJ4HCksxgigNqFrWO4ULA8AXlSqGFghFIOlMNO9omIuExY\nnedKmQ5vQo9T5mnDNfjAFOPOUgm1NDtj3QDYRfnmd2mYwWMEEV2SOEmcuU0u+M6I\nsvZrc3QQhyVI0X3jPNn6uF5T1pDK9czIjhGjO9OP6HfljWP4zTfgaA+kzAGVdwhq\nHyK8TQ9C54TVIiIKKbtqCkmcd1jL2cODgkt7+TPYh4jGL3bI8norvL+/g1sK6jLA\ny6mfZjZszmM+HA5686i58x0i+YdTVx5dg9LjEuMpA9Kj0u2Q8ki11XDBwqQSQQ8c\n+OcdKoC7WIaXavvtw24H\n=DcgR\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-01T22:10:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gis