ents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/2639a6904a874dce98bd0e3c997fb0ecdde41c09/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T18:06:42Z","email":"Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech","name":"ANDREI KUCHMA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T18:06:42Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(spec-quality): Studio''s findings reach the editor without opting into local signals, and the row breakdown stays in its column (#599)\n\nSeen on dev after #596-#598 rolled out:\n\n- The Markdown editor''s quality destination is an optional feature a project\n  turns on (\"Specification signals\"), so on studio-web, which never did, the\n  findings #597 hands the editor had no button to show them under. Studio''s\n  own Spec Quality findings are not the opt-in local heuristics: a document\n  Studio has findings for now offers the destination either way, and the\n  editor no longer closes it for that document.\n- The Specs row''s breakdown (\"5 sections of another kind\") ran over the\n  Updated column. It is now a second line under the count, cut to the\n  column with the full text on hover.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","tree":{"sha":"02fe8a520f62ec4c72ce8e78fc696f8c83c04b21","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/trees/02fe8a520f62ec4c72ce8e78fc696f8c83c04b21"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/commits/2639a6904a874dce98bd0e3c997fb0ecdde41c09","verification":{"payload":"tree 02fe8a520f62ec4c72ce8e78fc696f8c83c04b21\nparent f462f936f75577ea3fcfad9ce44afebffabc4613\nauthor ANDREI KUCHMA <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech> 1790878002 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790878002 +0200\n\nfix(spec-quality): Studio''s findings reach the editor without opting into local signals, and the row breakdown stays in its column (#599)\n\nSeen on dev after #596-#598 rolled out:\n\n- The Markdown editor''s quality destination is an optional feature a project\n  turns on (\"Specification signals\"), so on studio-web, which never did, the\n  findings #597 hands the editor had no button to show them under. Studio''s\n  own Spec Quality findings are not the opt-in local heuristics: a document\n  Studio has findings for now offers the destination either way, and the\n  editor no longer closes it for that document.\n- The Specs row''s breakdown (\"5 sections of another kind\") ran over the\n  Updated column. It is now a second line under the count, cut to the\n  column with the full text on hover.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvqEyCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAc+oQAA7LlaqoS0dMm0PItsDCWICf\nZ5zlTASkv3iaaDowOnzEd9C4EdNw8iaeMCeDt6Zn5iMAafGsAITizC6J+V+CAucX\nogI6Y6phL0UfrDY0Z6mNhDLfYxRoOUetjLXFmkGkK7SpJd2cdw2YBfoi1nCzaR5I\nkZDs0/UKRz7/ORZPPLfcA058tJYxAROfViZnRVMcYX8hVqCMTv2f2EXftFMewle1\nb+0dW64BAh37dqeHfpTUfBiLmKiZrwlzu1Qn5rO5PscrBo0dEzhNGJ5qPW0hR/qT\nTdZtx0QoOw6xCUWwpjVhOgw39VLofatw/CsOWyUdW4un/adgMTJjS66BHaY+DF+q\n8v5GlPCpyDp6J82HOhT0dKT7rGsNvESEOfudagT8n0okL0xaQj2wXOzCKGVeJkcB\nqYkfPLXP8kcyB/vS219f95jAvaXfs75lfIG+QRDbxS8KTO7TjqCN5QQ/9bIsdhqY\nUVeF4YpEblUldlc3WQ13hDi8QNg3jikH2S3AVYzz5FynGn/F1by3u4QJWHy43Dxd\nhpJrUBV+0NnHxxZzDLcyVTvfz+xeEhYuBaYGCZ3MJE9H2fxOjEwiULZIzP4i8U06\nrrL/lHXU5abpI33IfeyBlq2xZEEZV7OVV9peHdYOTeirwR9v2Vpw71gyCfCFDjBR\nB/vJMRjzDe9GSZu2mKBn\n=bQS6\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-01T18:06:43Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login