K666/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/f462f936f75577ea3fcfad9ce44afebffabc4613/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T16:50:36Z","email":"Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech","name":"ANDREI KUCHMA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T16:50:36Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(spec-quality): a sync also analyses the documents nothing ever analysed (#598)\n\nA sync analyses the typed documents whose text changed since the last sync.\nOn a repository that was synced before the sync started analysing, every\ndocument already has its content_sha recorded, so none of them changed and\nnone was ever analysed: dev''s studio-web project had 63 typed documents and\nwould have shown no findings until someone edited each one.\n\nA typed document with no `purpose` verdict now counts too, after the changed\nones and inside the same cap, so such a repository catches up a batch per\nsync. A document the service will not analyse (a type it does not judge) is\nrecorded as a pending gate verdict with the reason, so it is not asked about\nagain on every sync and a stage says why it is not satisfied.\n\nChecked on a local backend: with one document''s verdicts removed, an\nunchanged sync queued purpose and leak for that document only (plus bloat),\nand the next unchanged sync queued nothing.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","tree":{"sha":"697ec8bd039fc2a663ca85136d7607575affc863","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/trees/697ec8bd039fc2a663ca85136d7607575affc863"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/commits/f462f936f75577ea3fcfad9ce44afebffabc4613","verification":{"payload":"tree 697ec8bd039fc2a663ca85136d7607575affc863\nparent 572f2aca50571b7c5a08ecb1225a3c7667a1d4b9\nauthor ANDREI KUCHMA <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech> 1790873436 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790873436 +0200\n\nfix(spec-quality): a sync also analyses the documents nothing ever analysed (#598)\n\nA sync analyses the typed documents whose text changed since the last sync.\nOn a repository that was synced before the sync started analysing, every\ndocument already has its content_sha recorded, so none of them changed and\nnone was ever analysed: dev''s studio-web project had 63 typed documents and\nwould have shown no findings until someone edited each one.\n\nA typed document with no `purpose` verdict now counts too, after the changed\nones and inside the same cap, so such a repository catches up a batch per\nsync. A document the service will not analyse (a type it does not judge) is\nrecorded as a pending gate verdict with the reason, so it is not asked about\nagain on every sync and a stage says why it is not satisfied.\n\nChecked on a local backend: with one document''s verdicts removed, an\nunchanged sync queued purpose and leak for that document only (plus bloat),\nand the next unchanged sync queued nothing.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvo9cCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAKHcQAG5nz4anq/mlRirBsOtl6Sro\n23UDq4WTjemS5pgFUwOgHN8CBPzd9N/cN8Gdqrg09fX1ze/cHQ5l2SXCVi0hhRvz\nXRhpF+CmNQSXtr+424vnRAq83Ogf25XaK+msWvcZsn8LM7lcUYnYT8mFaMdmx7Nm\nFxGDoDdGAKWFv02GOASJSOM5wplQzBUau85M7LnxXishM6hNhaiLMEVsUB7l9FzU\nII/WsXvCWXZfDnjDXM7xY/ubPoVjPMx7DCnjQb7C8oBSqCHBShVLX6g7QlYpEjls\n3VBfzRThmMsjvunppgq1nYRyLmnqhHkKrpvCPThQjqIpFQCHqTAnm/UQkcI/BTrt\nh8soKCgc7IYiN71fC7ag/bHFOKx06q/PR6wjOj68GRsFkvmZHZio/jKrpzDVFkzQ\nLjLr/RyILMFvEkWxCPErabT2hbQdOEB6VPvb8nLvfqQ/T18Ojic8nD4ZIE3t0PzV\nJ25ACbeuuT4yNVgv+RUpuuAfPkY4+WSLWL8Pc2qalBK4kP50Cq4fcxBOfpFAt8nG\nK5Ckl/mdbH3ybZ2RSUs9zUnFCk8KNFiBr1G73at09zY2uiOSReFTpdgTqv4qScWf\nRCh5AIeTxVhJIV+hIb+Q4r7qGmM1X6aTC6vmi5ANfy3Wk0qsSX7cEakO89qz6ivH\nfCFWnXUo+LpRZ69OF/m