ttps://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AndrejK666","id":301748190,"login":"AndrejK666","node_id":"U_kgDOEfxP3g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/572f2aca50571b7c5a08ecb1225a3c7667a1d4b9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T16:25:31Z","email":"Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech","name":"ANDREI KUCHMA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T16:25:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(spec-quality): Studio''s findings in the document editor, and by kind on the Specs row (#597)\n\nTheia: the Analyze panel hands the open document''s recorded findings to the\nproduct''s Markdown editor (setStudioFindings), which shows them through the\nquality pipeline it already has - the rail''s cards with \"jump to\" and the\ntriage controls, and the underline in the text. studio-quality.js turns a\nserver finding back into the detector report entry it came from (a purpose\ngate violation, one bloat cluster; leak as a section violation), so\nfingerprints, trust and anchoring by quote and section are the existing,\ntested code. Local reports on disk still win where they exist, and Studio''s\nfindings are never written into the checkout''s .studio/quality/state.json.\n\nPrototype: the Review column says what a row''s count is made of - \"3\nsections of another kind · 2 duplicates of other docs\" - and a document\nwritten in Studio shows its findings once a detector has looked at it.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","tree":{"sha":"ed5844dfca165c7dd4c065a5d1c055a0a4a9301a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/trees/ed5844dfca165c7dd4c065a5d1c055a0a4a9301a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/commits/572f2aca50571b7c5a08ecb1225a3c7667a1d4b9","verification":{"payload":"tree ed5844dfca165c7dd4c065a5d1c055a0a4a9301a\nparent 49c0dc9c17f656f0c734ffcd44cb7ffaa8dbcee1\nauthor ANDREI KUCHMA <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech> 1790871931 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790871931 +0200\n\nfeat(spec-quality): Studio''s findings in the document editor, and by kind on the Specs row (#597)\n\nTheia: the Analyze panel hands the open document''s recorded findings to the\nproduct''s Markdown editor (setStudioFindings), which shows them through the\nquality pipeline it already has - the rail''s cards with \"jump to\" and the\ntriage controls, and the underline in the text. studio-quality.js turns a\nserver finding back into the detector report entry it came from (a purpose\ngate violation, one bloat cluster; leak as a section violation), so\nfingerprints, trust and anchoring by quote and section are the existing,\ntested code. Local reports on disk still win where they exist, and Studio''s\nfindings are never written into the checkout''s .studio/quality/state.json.\n\nPrototype: the Review column says what a row''s count is made of - \"3\nsections of another kind · 2 duplicates of other docs\" - and a document\nwritten in Studio shows its findings once a detector has looked at it.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvol7CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA7gkQAGCLejHbzXQzrrO23YmV3SZZ\nLUlVcLyPHFoDrAMtOBiM3uOtXgjc92ReSeSKhCsB8KdIRp3SleJF6sN9yhNrmBTp\n4cnY2XcqrBzh1ik5U1jiPli5LX4UEqXUgLhnulB45mka31BysLnwXQhQS0BsIuo5\n6uepUMYqSBFSR9H7ABiPcsg8vbNsbSqhNrrZfmW