c734ffcd44cb7ffaa8dbcee1"}],"sha":"572f2aca50571b7c5a08ecb1225a3c7667a1d4b9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/572f2aca50571b7c5a08ecb1225a3c7667a1d4b9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/301748190?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AndrejK666","id":301748190,"login":"AndrejK666","node_id":"U_kgDOEfxP3g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/49c0dc9c17f656f0c734ffcd44cb7ffaa8dbcee1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T16:15:08Z","email":"Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech","name":"ANDREI KUCHMA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T16:15:08Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(reports): studio-reports — a report is a definition over a source, configured once per organization (ADR-0033) (#595)\n\nThe roadmap workbook (#586) matched the planning team''s script, but it was\nconfigured with workarounds:\n- the plan was a browser upload sent with every catalogue sync;\n- the board and its roots lived in one person''s local source picker;\n- the layout was Rust, with formulas wired to column letters;\n- all of it sat in the components catalogue.\n\nReports are now their own gear, `studio-reports`\n(`/studio-reports/v1/reports/{report_id}/…`):\n\n- A report is drawn by a **definition**: five sheet kinds (summary,\n  timeline, gantt, people, table). A table''s columns name values by key\n  (`impl`, `milestone`, `card.<field>`, `field.<any board column>`), are\n  formulas over other columns by id (`{effort}{row}*(1-{impl}{row})`), or\n  stand for the plan''s consumer projects. The summary, metrics and red\n  cells find their columns by role, never by letter. The planning team''s\n  workbook is the built-in `back_roadmap`; a plan picks it with\n  `report: back_roadmap` or carries its own definition, validated with\n  the offending column named.\n- A report''s **source** is configured once per organization: a GitHub\n  connection and the plan file in its repository (`owner/repo:path@ref`),\n  read through that connection. The plan can carry `board`, `roots`\n  (bare numbers resolved through the board), `consumers` and `report`.\n  Upload stays as the fallback. The plan is kept as text, because its key\n  order is the column/lane/People order, and compressed in the graph to\n  stay under the 64 KB payload cap. It is parsed the way PyYAML reads it.\n- `POST …/sync` queues `reports.refresh`: it reads the plan again, records\n  what it read, and queues a `catalog.sync` of the board. A scheduler\n  schedule on that task keeps a report current; the screen offers hourly.\n\nThe catalogue keeps reading the board (component facts) and exposes only a\nnarrow port (`components_catalog::port::RoadmapCatalog`). The plan is gone\nfrom catalogue syncs, along with the `roadmap_plan` type and the\n`/studio-components-catalog/v1/roadmap-report[/workbook]` routes.\n\nThe prototype gets a Reports screen (source, refresh, hourly schedule,\ndownload, the report''s tables), and the Components page no longer\nconfigures the board. The IDE reads the new routes.\n\nVerified on a stand against board #48:\n- the workbook is identical to `back_roadmap_to_xls.py`''s output for the\n  same day on all 13 sheets, the 118 Roadmap boxes and the 91 Gantt bars;\n- the plan file is read through the connection;\n- a `reports.refresh` schedule fires end to end;\n- the Reports screen renders the live report in headless Chrome.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","tree":{"sha":"03e36a3b8cf9128585a333c5e604d9599ff05a9d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/trees/03e36a3b8cf9128585a333c5e604d9599ff05a9d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/commits/49c0dc9c17f656f0c734ffcd44cb7ffaa8dbcee1","verification":{"payload":"tree 03e36a3b8cf9128585a333c5e604d9599ff05a9d\nparent 3b438d985b25f61f713c6936d953a45030ec43a1\nauthor ANDREI KUCHMA <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech> 1790871308 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790871308 +0200\n\nfeat(reports): studio-reports — a report is a definition over a source, configured once per organization (ADR-0033) (#595)\n\nThe roadmap workbook (#586) matched the planning team''s script, but it was\nconfigured with workarounds:\n- the plan was a browser upload sent with every catalogue sync;\n- the board and its roots lived in one person''s local source picker;\n- the layout was Rust, with formulas wired to column letters;\n- all of it sat in the components catalogue.\n\nReports are now their own gear, `studio-reports`\n(`/studio-reports/v1/reports/{report_id}/…`):\n\n- A report is drawn by a **definition**: five sheet kinds (summary,\n  timeline, gantt, people, table). A table''s columns name values by key\n  (`impl`, `milestone`, `card.<field>`, `field.<any board column>`), are\n  formulas over other columns by id (`{effort}{row}*(1-{impl}{row})`), or\n  stand for the plan''s consumer projects. The summary, metrics and red\n  cells find their columns by role, never by letter. The planning team''s\n  workbook is the built-in `back_roadmap`; a plan picks it with\n  `report: back_roadmap` or carries its own definition, validated with\n  the offending column named.\n- A report''s **source** is configured once per organization: a GitHub\n  connection and the plan file in its repository (`owner/repo:path@ref`),\n  read through that connection. The plan can carry `board`, `roots`\n  (bare numbers resolved through the board), `consumers` and `report`.\n  Upload stays as the fallback. The plan is kept as text, because its key\n  order is the column/lane/People order, and compressed in the graph to\n  stay under the 64 KB payload cap. It is parsed the way PyYAML reads it.\n- `POST …/sync` queues `reports.refresh`: it reads the plan again, records\n  what it read, and queues a `catalog.sync` of the board. A scheduler\n  schedule on that task keeps a report current; the screen offers hourly.\n\nThe catalogue keeps reading the board (component facts) and exposes only a\nnarrow port (`components_catalog::port::RoadmapCatalog`). The plan is gone\nfrom catalogue syncs, along with the `roadmap_plan` type and the\n`/studio-components-catalog/v1/roadmap-report[/workbook]` routes.\n\nThe prototype gets a Reports screen (source, refresh, hourly schedule,\ndownload, the report''s tables), and the Components page no longer\nconfigures the board. The IDE reads the new routes.\n\nVerified on a stand against board #48:\n- the workbook is identical to `back_roadmap_to_xls.py`''s output for the\n  same day on all 13 sheets, the 118 Roadmap boxes and the 91 Gantt bars;\n- the plan file is read through the connection;\n- a `reports.refresh` schedule fires end to end;\n- the Reports screen renders the live report in headless Chrome.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvocMCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAlRsQAF0AbNXkfLzTn67n1pi+bh7H\nvIV3tOt+F7cix2Kb7H3SYkMmbFuuAfCloXsOHjbzGf7DKA8gTmEMMeag4bwQuWBs\nZDCNKUJ6GBN7AdmcLl0qj4VSDFX4649gvGFAWpGYNggjRPNjSVi8BSSPoG/De0nG\nEruwW9nWOpqJlt+VZF7X8YFNm4G5pDLrQx6T65lhechY6yA++g5pfO9Q3BlghKpr\nuUEgiUDWSRSJTwCgZbAEoVqQyKvv0KXH3QR3yymXJxS0kpAynsjgCg8na/Mlytx4\nOGHiEeDLYTgt+O5igTMqfpW7O3bw8dDQdUOYnH3d4lhNlJwbLAIpouXVWEKiGEw7\nUVhH5nDrDrAp+pLGh1/agLb1gCSf05kwbL/edz82hfS3rZAnZHAvZjt3beDot15e\n64pExTD1MCEwU+AGc0ErFmUvPW4I19rk2KJa7X++0O7wV72BiUX0bY42oRcb/FvG\n+Ro8LYfEqVSQ09xdMp7JZZdsNBJDsIpkhX6SlvFU22ko6IAG88zOZEeIeMSJ1X/t\nnDPINBX2NZuvunMDse8l9pzufBoSdxSndCAakRybEuu63pABy3EU46nAaO8cX0nm\nz7jpn6k+4vR+n/FKyBQ/9uP1ZqreA3CePHAZ+slssssXbdzQ4Llp9waosEkdhBFG\nsXsz4Hmbp8YDJ1JtT9CT\n=qCAs\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-01T16:15:09Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/49c0dc9c17f656f0c734ffcd44cb7ffaa8dbcee1","node_id":"C_kwDOTl7dJtoAKDQ5YzBkYzljMTdmNjU2ZjBjNzM0ZmZjZDQ0Y2I3ZmZhYThkYmNlZTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/3b438d985b25f61f713c6936d953a45030ec43a1","sha":"3b438d985b25f61f713c6936d953a45030ec43a1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/3b438d985b25f61f713c6936d953a45030ec43a1"}],"sha":"49c0dc9c17f656f0c734ffcd44cb7ffaa8dbcee1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/49c0dc9c17f656f0c734ffcd44cb7ffaa8dbcee1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/301748190?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AndrejK666","id":301748190,"login":"AndrejK666","node_id":"U_kgDOEfxP3g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/3b438d985b25f61f713c6936d953a45030ec43a1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T14:19:25Z","email":"Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech","name":"ANDREI KUCHMA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T14:19:25Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(spec-quality): a run records its own findings, and a source sync starts one (#596)\n\nThe detectors ran on the server, the verdict was read on the server and the\ngraph writer is on the server, and the only thing that joined them was the\nbrowser: the Specs tab and the IDE''s Analyze panel followed each run, read\nevery verdict and posted a spec_finding node back. Nothing was kept unless a\ntab stayed open, and an analysis nobody watched could not be kept at all.\n\nA spec_quality.analyze_batch run whose payload carries `record` (workspace,\nproject, and per path the graph node, binding or Studio document) now records\nas each document finishes: the spec_finding node per detector per document,\nin the severity/summary words the clients used, with the findings under\n`details.findings`; the gate verdict a stage reads; and for bloat the\n`duplicates` edges. Two new hub ports carry the writes: SpecFindingWriter\n(artifact-ingest) and AnalysisRecorder (documents). The documents\n`/quality/{detector}` route always asks for it, and maps an inline repository\npath (the IDE sends the document on screen as text alone) to its binding.\n\nA source sync starts one: classify_ingested notes the typed documents whose\ntext is new or different and queues purpose and leak for them and bloat over\nevery typed document read. Capped (analyze_on_sync_max_documents, 50), skipped\nwhile Spec Quality has no key, switchable (analyze_on_sync). An unchanged\nre-sync queues nothing.\n\nThe prototype and the Theia panel stop writing results, which would replace\nthe run''s record with one without findings. A Specs row counts the findings\nplaced in the text rather than the detectors that looked, and the expanded\nrow lists each: severity, message, section and lines, evidence, the\nduplicated passage and where else it is.\n\nChecked end to end on a local backend with the graph and the real Spec\nQuality key: one classification pass over three documents recorded 9 nodes\nwith findings and 9 gate verdicts in 25 s; one changed document re-analysed\nonly that document (plus bloat); nothing changed queued nothing.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","tree":{"sha":"10f290d39a76c45093b0c33b04950edf027fcf15","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/trees/10f290d39a76c45093b0c33b04950edf027fcf15"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/commits/3b438d985b25f61f713c6936d953a45030ec43a1","verification":{"payload":"tree 10f290d39a76c45093b0c33b04950edf027fcf15\nparent 8ceb622df7f4f6089c9c192acc9f4594b6bff89b\nauthor ANDREI KUCHMA <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech> 1790864365 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790864365 +0200\n\nfeat(spec-quality): a run records its own findings, and a source sync starts one (#596)\n\nThe detectors ran on the server, the verdict was read on the server and the\ngraph writer is on the server, and the only thing that joined them was the\nbrowser: the Specs tab and the IDE''s Analyze panel followed each run, read\nevery verdict and posted a spec_finding node back. Nothing was kept unless a\ntab stayed open, and an analysis nobody watched could not be kept at all.\n\nA spec_quality.analyze_batch run whose payload carries `record` (workspace,\nproject, and per path the graph node, binding or Studio document) now records\nas each document finishes: the spec_finding node per detector per document,\nin the severity/summary words the clients used, with the findings under\n`details.findings`; the gate verdict a stage reads; and for bloat the\n`duplicates` edges. Two new hub ports carry the writes: SpecFindingWriter\n(artifact-ingest) and AnalysisRecorder (documents). The documents\n`/quality/{detector}` route always asks for it, and maps an inline repository\npath (the IDE sends the document on screen as text alone) to its binding.\n\nA source sync starts one: classify_ingested notes the typed documents whose\ntext is new or different and queues purpose and leak for them and bloat over\nevery typed document read. Capped (analyze_on_sync_max_documents, 50), skipped\nwhile Spec Quality has no key, switchable (analyze_on_sync). An unchanged\nre-sync queues nothing.\n\nThe prototype and the Theia panel stop writing results, which would replace\nthe run''s record with one without findings. A Specs row counts the findings\nplaced in the text rather than the detectors that looked, and the expanded\nrow lists each: severity, message, section and lines, evidence, the\nduplicated passage and where else it is.\n\nChecked end to end on a local backend with the graph and the real Spec\nQuality key: one classification pass over three documents recorded 9 nodes\nwith findings and 9 gate verdicts in 25 s; one changed document re-analysed\nonly that document (plus bloat); nothing changed queued nothing.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvmvtCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAB/0QAAcLuoPNV47Ue5aYztnMhBxm\ncSPxymGzTRxtNGiaJxisUXn1d019zAYMrBZCPQ8MENzQbGLwjEjSNoMbz939tJbY\nz98MXftfr4YNDEyMzWF8iPLkO7Uiuf5Wc6GWUdrOHUoc8OWkp81c6Wq8hfRHMt7U\nbwwbNpsoHNQcwGDrOTjTldWXpw2lSy6QzKD2Zk/UUSv5M88lYVfBPU5e/8AxkoFO\n7LElbGhZRM9Ctknebn5sZ15crp+qLq3ujcOmRAL2Zbud1jKt6iM5VmF3K+FwybVi\nZcCke9HeewAHS4mZgzTBgep5wWIuPmeb4mDExS+1EWQJlytgWCI8C6ynpfBFU7Gc\niqVdd60j1/S9atkIyaBimuDMmjpWmOVWxUA5yqk9ucsm8Pzn9ElHHMikHAYUXxuy\n3CUAzkl0WR00yc99IlrnAxHMMxaEzcm1dlQlv8GiVrZ0RWEsKZkqnPooYmhpfF8R\nEp12mFaI+FQUGo0+/j9t1VCj5VoYaD6758Sd51ehvDmaaNeuy6+ohaM3+KKhcOjZ\nwzgAFfQhmYxodgSDYvTlVSEo3Y7Lsm6zdl+5jQIbG/wRiBDZZ2VX16oM901MbLRV\ngxCkJG7qJfihMIn+zbWwi0v2u/pzmcNMsJhPQco0en2wVo8VUnCj0nJFlK/85laY\nZN05bKjvm4qG/PmoAGYR\n=n3i7\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-01T14:19:26Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/3b438d985b25f61f713c6936d953a45030ec43a1","node_id":"C_kwDOTl7dJtoAKDNiNDM4ZDk4NWIyNWY2MWY3MTNjNjkzNmQ5NTNhNDUwMzBlYzQzYTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/8ceb622df7f4f6089c9c192acc9f4594b6bff89b","sha":"8ceb622df7f4f6089c9c192acc9f4594b6bff89b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/8ceb622df7f4f6089c9c192acc9f4594b6bff89b"}],"sha":"3b438d985b25f61f713c6936d953a45030ec43a1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/3b438d985b25f61f713c6936d953a45030ec43a1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/301748190?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AndrejK666","id":301748190,"login":"AndrejK666","node_id":"U_kgDOEfxP3g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/8ceb622df7f4f6089c9c192acc9f4594b6bff89b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T13:32:23Z","email":"Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech","name":"ANDREI KUCHMA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T13:32:23Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(spec-quality): a verdict says what the detector found, and where (#594)\n\nGET /studio-spec-quality/v1/verdicts now carries `findings[]`: each one a\nrule, a severity, the detector''s own reason and evidence, and where it is in\nthe analysed text (section, lines, and for bloat the passage itself, with the\nother copies as `related`). The detectors already answered all of this;\n`verdict.rs` kept a pass/fail and a share and dropped the rest, so a screen\ncould count findings and never show one.\n\nRules: purpose.foreign_section, purpose.not_a_spec, leak.foreign_content,\nbloat.cross_document, bloat.self_repeat. A finding''s id hashes the rule,\ndocument, section and passage and never the line numbers, so it survives\nedits above it.\n\nChecked against live calls of all three detectors on this repository''s own\ndocuments: line numbers are right every time; bloat''s character offsets are\nnot (one in six matched), so they are not read; bloat reports a paragraph\nand a sentence inside it as duplicates, so overlapping occurrences in one\nfile are one passage; leak names the kind it read as in `reads_as`.\n\nAlso fixes `?path=` on the same route: a derived Query<VerdictQuery> is\nserde_urlencoded, which cannot read a repeated key into a Vec, so every\nbloat and traceability verdict answered 400 for both portals (#593).\n\ndocs/design/spec-findings.md is the plan this is the first step of.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","tree":{"sha":"23a2b0785885d80525adc63e5526c0a86bdb5376","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/trees/23a2b0785885d80525adc63e5526c0a86bdb5376"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/commits/8ceb622df7f4f6089c9c192acc9f4594b6bff89b","verification":{"payload":"tree 23a2b0785885d80525adc63e5526c0a86bdb5376\nparent b1f5f0b4f467b2d22f988fc5787e25b2852f5568\nauthor ANDREI KUCHMA <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech> 1790861543 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790861543 +0200\n\nfeat(spec-quality): a verdict says what the detector found, and where (#594)\n\nGET /studio-spec-quality/v1/verdicts now carries `findings[]`: each one a\nrule, a severity, the detector''s own reason and evidence, and where it is in\nthe analysed text (section, lines, and for bloat the passage itself, with the\nother copies as `related`). The detectors already answered all of this;\n`verdict.rs` kept a pass/fail and a share and dropped the rest, so a screen\ncould count findings and never show one.\n\nRules: purpose.foreign_section, purpose.not_a_spec, leak.foreign_content,\nbloat.cross_document, bloat.self_repeat. A finding''s id hashes the rule,\ndocument, section and passage and never the line numbers, so it survives\nedits above it.\n\nChecked against live calls of all three detectors on this repository''s own\ndocuments: line numbers are right every time; bloat''s character offsets are\nnot (one in six matched), so they are not read; bloat reports a paragraph\nand a sentence inside it as duplicates, so overlapping occurrences in one\nfile are one passage; leak names the kind it read as in `reads_as`.\n\nAlso fixes `?path=` on the same route: a derived Query<VerdictQuery> is\nserde_urlencoded, which cannot read a repeated key into a Vec, so every\nbloat and traceability verdict answered 400 for both portals (#593).\n\ndocs/design/spec-findings.md is the plan this is the first step of.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvmDnCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAeeQQADL1Ibe+V/8bwXahuFx3wGFi\nYZxLeH8ChiysHK0/iTKjUNLJsoBCLk5tM17eY+48yN05uF/3J2F4d7WKSqHGxq86\nigsKDGggWw/JdBKZyeQnN