:"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/b1f5f0b4f467b2d22f988fc5787e25b2852f5568"}],"sha":"8ceb622df7f4f6089c9c192acc9f4594b6bff89b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/8ceb622df7f4f6089c9c192acc9f4594b6bff89b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/301748190?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AndrejK666","id":301748190,"login":"AndrejK666","node_id":"U_kgDOEfxP3g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/b1f5f0b4f467b2d22f988fc5787e25b2852f5568/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T12:31:07Z","email":"Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech","name":"ANDREI KUCHMA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T12:31:07Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor(spec-quality): one prefix, the gear''s own — and the verdict instead of a raw relay (#593)\n\nThe studio-spec-quality gear answered under two prefixes: ten routes under\n/spec-quality/v1 (listed in the contract baseline as rule-A1 violations) and\n/studio-spec-quality/v1/verdicts, the one added after the rule. /api-docs/\nshowed it as two components.\n\n- Every route is now /studio-spec-quality/v1/…, operation ids\n  studio_spec_quality.*; `spec-quality` leaves the domain list.\n- GET /tasks/{task_id} and GET /tasks, the verbatim relay of the upstream''s\n  task view, are removed: no portal or IDE read them, `verdicts` reads the\n  same upstream task and judges it once on the server, and the run is\n  followed on studio-tasks (the last rule-D2 entry). The batch run''s docs now\n  point at /verdicts.\n- Removed at once, without a deprecation window: every consumer moves in this\n  change.\n- The prototype calls /studio-spec-quality/v1/{capabilities,status,analyze/…}\n  as full literals, so scripts/check-api-usage.mjs now sees them (it could\n  not see the old `''/spec-quality'' + path`).\n\nThe baseline loses the ten domain-prefix lines and every `tasks` line; the\nrest move to the new paths.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","tree":{"sha":"1cbc215c34a235c4be452024e465ec92f4ec4869","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/trees/1cbc215c34a235c4be452024e465ec92f4ec4869"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/commits/b1f5f0b4f467b2d22f988fc5787e25b2852f5568","verification":{"payload":"tree 1cbc215c34a235c4be452024e465ec92f4ec4869\nparent d63ba679b99d07af5e7bda15f766c4f5d95f366c\nauthor ANDREI KUCHMA <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech> 1790857867 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790857867 +0200\n\nrefactor(spec-quality): one prefix, the gear''s own — and the verdict instead of a raw relay (#593)\n\nThe studio-spec-quality gear answered under two prefixes: ten routes under\n/spec-quality/v1 (listed in the contract baseline as rule-A1 violations) and\n/studio-spec-quality/v1/verdicts, the one added after the rule. /api-docs/\nshowed it as two components.\n\n- Every route is now /studio-spec-quality/v1/…, operation ids\n  studio_spec_quality.*; `spec-quality` leaves the domain list.\n- GET /tasks/{task_id} and GET /tasks, the verbatim relay of the upstream''s\n  task view, are removed: no portal or IDE read them, `verdicts` reads the\n  same upstream task and judges it once on the server, and the run is\n  followed on studio-tasks (the last rule-D2 entry). The batch run''s docs now\n  point at /verdicts.\n- Removed at once, without a deprecation window: every consumer moves in this\n  change.\n- The prototype calls /studio-spec-quality/v1/{capabilities,status,analyze/…}\n  as full literals, so scripts/check-api-usage.mjs now sees them (it could\n  not see the old `''/spec-quality'' + path`).\n\nThe baseline loses the ten domain-prefix lines and every `tasks` line; the\nrest move to the new paths.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvlKLCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA434QAJN034sjVELoEqQv0ksZpuLO\n7OlwuaNLV2jdO5usqPZyC0zbNd7LxFs7nvRglDMiMt27Lb6ZerkGh2Wzr+D10v9b\nsCm8T+IchpW4Smgo9VC9NK6R1dd99xbJv1O1F/65YF7mv8YZdnIT0NZ/mZomaIIb\nKEUA4DmFYOG/CFtK0H3E9DJqJ+dWwfqPwXbjxsdoy7koxQDVcAsVSAaOxvzh8YgA\nH0qcjbr0vmvXZbYfvWYZTzct19HYXLuVdOp2B+DTQVo19+lyv1HUvIYYSU5j9Mp6\ncvRWdOwJlbnb1/SEfrtlYmVYEp6S7GsUA1xY+rsE8EusjC7Lf60TCJXBRhS2lzcc\nU7cOVH1xpYjPkI63kfpe9g5T6A3R3207smJkjKDiTh+Zmfva7wi+QlWEbJCCQqgl\nOyM656b3ACBSPz0PJ0zltCkidWj26f5zt9FmrzMU8LJjj2ncF9lDnpzjhfCXVMEA\nufDd1wp/Bp3UqV3SA2gdF4O2g4fOMJB26BqRUdVxCieTxerUZrKommpsMFWvDeeK\no8D2i3Z+qfb9MlmW1PKO2UyyEYHz8V4qBV06KLaok91yeEjistYnQO75WKWsPU9M\nIp4yC5TE9dGKuW1VVIS/wgmXDLjUfa8taJDkCh/kW3+p7dqJaACFb2F9mDdK8RFb\nTcsSWJtWHvre0GO7DVFE\n=JF0f\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-01T12:31:07Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/b1f5f0b4f467b2d22f988fc5787e25b2852f5568","node_id":"C_kwDOTl7dJtoAKGIxZjVmMGI0ZjQ2N2IyZDIyZjk4OGZjNTc4N2UyNWIyODUyZjU1Njg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/d63ba679b99d07af5e7bda15f766c4f5d95f366c","sha":"d63ba679b99d07af5e7bda15f766c4f5d95f366c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/d63ba679b99d07af5e7bda15f766c4f5d95f366c"}],"sha":"b1f5f0b4f467b2d22f988fc5787e25b2852f5568","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/b1f5f0b4f467b2d22f988fc5787e25b2852f5568"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/301748190?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AndrejK666","id":301748190,"login":"AndrejK666","node_id":"U_kgDOEfxP3g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/d63ba679b99d07af5e7bda15f766c4f5d95f366c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T12:17:47Z","email":"Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech","name":"ANDREI KUCHMA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T12:17:47Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor: one route for a background run, one record for a person''s preferences (#592)\n\nTwo duplications the /api-docs/ grouping made visible.\n\nBackground runs. Three gears answered \"how is my run doing\" a second time\nunder their own paths, each a thin copy of the studio-tasks run they read:\nGET /studio-artifact-ingest/v1/tasks/{id}, /studio-components-catalog/v1/\ntasks/{id} and /studio-connector/v1/graph-sync/tasks/{task_id} (the last\nstill described its tasks as in-memory). They were already listed as rule-D2\nviolations (\"a private background-status endpoint beside studio-tasks\"). They\nare removed, with their DTOs, `of_result` and the RunView fields only they\nread; the baseline loses six lines. The sync routes now say to poll\nGET /studio-tasks/v1/runs/{id}, whose `result` carries the counts.\n\nThe FrontX portal and Theia already polled studio-tasks. The prototype''s\n`artifactSyncTask` and `componentsCatalogTask` keep their shape but read the\nrun (`runCount`, `runMessage`), so no caller changes.\n\nPreferences. The prototype kept theme and language in the platform''s\nsimple-user-settings gear and every other remembered choice in studio-user''s\n`/me/ui-preferences` — one person''s preferences in two stores with two\nwriters. Theme and language are now `app.theme` / `app.language` in the one\nrecord, through the same store as the views (`usePreference`), so a later\nview toggle cannot write a stale copy over them. The FrontX portal never\nused simple-user-settings. The gear itself is the platform''s and stays\nlinked; Studio no longer calls it. A theme saved there before is not carried\nover: it is cosmetic, and is picked again on the Profile page.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","tree":{"sha":"39591fcc2c298a1e9cdb2fa82f2e62f77ad121f0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/trees/39591fcc2c298a1e9cdb2fa82f2e62f77ad121f0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/commits/d63ba679b99d07af5e7bda15f766c4f5d95f366c","verification":{"payload":"tree 39591fcc2c298a1e9cdb2fa82f2e62f77ad121f0\nparent 08262c34231e9d5a476e3587c01f6c0b958ac7a3\nauthor ANDREI KUCHMA <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech> 1790857067 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790857067 +0200\n\nrefactor: one route for a background run, one record for a person''s preferences (#592)\n\nTwo duplications the /api-docs/ grouping made visible.\n\nBackground runs. Three gears answered \"how is my run doing\" a second time\nunder their own paths, each a thin copy of the studio-tasks run they read:\nGET /studio-artifact-ingest/v1/tasks/{id}, /studio-components-catalog/v1/\ntasks/{id} and /studio-connector/v1/graph-sync/tasks/{task_id} (the last\nstill described its tasks as in-memory). They were already listed as rule-D2\nviolations (\"a private background-status endpoint beside studio-tasks\"). They\nare removed, with their DTOs, `of_result` and the RunView fields only they\nread; the baseline loses six lines. The sync routes now say to poll\nGET /studio-tasks/v1/runs/{id}, whose `result` carries the counts.\n\nThe FrontX portal and Theia already polled studio-tasks. The prototype''s\n`artifactSyncTask` and `componentsCatalogTask` keep their shape but read the\nrun (`runCount`, `runMessage`), so no caller changes.\n\nPreferences. The prototype kept theme and language in the platform''s\nsimple-user-settings gear and every other remembered choice in studio-user''s\n`/me/ui-preferences` — one person''s preferences in two stores with two\nwriters. Theme and language are now `app.theme` / `app.language` in the one\nrecord, through the same store as the views (`usePreference`), so a later\nview toggle cannot write a stale copy over them. The FrontX portal never\nused simple-user-settings. The gear itself is the platform''s and stays\nlinked; Studio no longer calls it. A theme saved there before is not carried\nover: it is cosmetic, and is picked again on the Profile page.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvk9rCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjvAQAIYmEizBvKOUmzQz6GyGQreo\nXYGBbqyCbVb4wDAahiVdLZU9UbzUID1mWwcV76ucj0+4yYZ0I4GHEAyKvCPfaieU\nRgkIo/R3N+Pi9OtLP2gOhaCTTX4dh6Ex0y9PdvpSjQzcKGzQZBR2i2bE1j6fF53a\naA/lLGxpXLdLtgPM8YcjEIYUnL+9heVmWv3RvEaST53t6WjmntOdxdZkTy/4WpPO\nShT7Gf75MDzlp5Gl8TiJVnwEeiBzTwsX03JRzcB03+O4zO3gob8DdiIZy1JBKQi2\nwo1XCq+b6AVtO4I2cA81ZiF++gzlcZUlPsGEw7nzuTA3I8PaEgV0b2AYeo+rIPfa\nHyu65akyqPHAUL6A5wLusDGFOlhExMAptG+d2GAFW/3T1BE5E/VeHE0d+T75FQBZ\nt99GAdFBfXEho12kog5p6RSd/LdIEuiHWBZwO1yOO6s83b0+oESK2vaS64/Wg0sc\nC3s9aK9OnyHwE2QUIG9yqapuikW2UPM5Sl+m+olGVjAWHQtV+K5xkLJcF5HHI64m\nRrPyFfqnNxen8S0osmAJrzRlTmKmgIJ1BBYwrXRqfAuxwvMjevORhQvmwG4G+0H6\nnWXBpt2YpTjPxdpg2DthIBfWyIN1Rhwwjg7QfNUrBR5t+eyrwIn26HXWCg1uKpew\ni+0anBbs00outnHaSx4N\n=rdGi\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-01T12:17:47Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/d63ba679b99d07af5e7bda15f766c4f5d95f366c","node_id":"C_kwDOTl7dJtoAKGQ2M2JhNjc5Yjk5ZDA3YWY1ZTdiZGExNWY3NjZjNGY1ZDk1ZjM2NmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/08262c34231e9d5a476e3587c01f6c0b958ac7a3","sha":"08262c34231e9d5a476e3587c01f6c0b958ac7a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/08262c34231e9d5a476e3587c01f6c0b958ac7a3"}],"sha":"d63ba679b99d07af5e7bda15f766c4f5d95f366c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/d63ba679b99d07af5e7bda15f766c4f5d95f366c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/301748190?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AndrejK666","id":301748190,"login":"AndrejK666","node_id":"U_kgDOEfxP3g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/08262c34231e9d5a476e3587c01f6c0b958ac7a3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T10:56:37Z","email":"Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech","name":"ANDREI KUCHMA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T10:56:37Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(prototype): a project''s repositories are its config''s sources, as the FrontX portal keeps them (stacked on #590) (#591)\n\n* feat(backend): a project''s repositories are one record — project.config sources[]\n\nA project''s repositories were kept twice: the FrontX portal''s wizard wrote\n`project.config` `sources[]` ({connection_id, full_path, clone_url}), the\nprototype wrote the workspace settings'' `repos[]` ({name, url, token_ref}),\nand each reader picked one or merged both. The FrontX portal reads only the\nconfig, so a project attached in the prototype opened in its IDE with no code\n— \"studio-frontend-prototype/src/place-url.ts was not found in the workspace\".\n\n`project_sources` is now the one reader, in the portal''s shape plus an\noptional `branch`:\n\n- parse: the sources in order, each with its checkout directory derived from\n  `full_path` exactly as the portal''s `checkoutDirectory` does;\n- resolve: each with its connection''s `secret_ref`, looked up by id through\n  the tenant''s ancestors (`connectors::connection_by_id`, the catalogue read\n  without drivers), and whether the connection is personal;\n- git_sources: as sessions and the Git proxy clone them — a personal\n  connection''s token is never handed to a shared session.\n\nEvery reader moves to it and stops reading the settings'' `repos[]`:\n\n- studio-session: a launch clones the project''s sources whoever asks; the\n  request''s `repos` add only what is not the project''s (a backend-host\n  folder, the gear corpus), and one the project has is cloned once\n  (`launch_sources::plan`);\n- studio-git: the sources a desktop may clone, and the sync a push queues;\n- components-catalog: whose dependencies to read, now with their branch;\n- documents: which checkout and which synced clone to read;\n- organizations rollups: the repository count, from the config already read.\n\nThe three hand-written config parsers, `sources_in`, `checkout_sources`,\n`repo_path_of` and `by_secret_ref` go with the second path. `root_*` and\n`local` entries stay in the settings: they describe a working copy, not the\nproject''s repositories.\n\nscripts/migrate-project-sources.mjs moves existing `repos[]` into `sources[]`\non the same tenant (dry run by default, `--apply` to write, idempotent). Run\nit on a stand before this backend reaches it.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>\n\n* feat(prototype): a project''s repositories are its config''s sources, as the FrontX portal keeps them\n\nThe prototype kept a project''s repositories in the workspace settings''\n`repos[]`, which the FrontX portal never reads. They now live where that\nportal and the backend read them, `project.config` `sources[]`\n({connection_id, full_path, clone_url, branch?}), through one module,\n`project-sources.ts`:\n\n- attaching from a connector adds sources through the connection by id,\n  a repository already listed once (`withPicked`);\n- the Sources tab, the launcher, Overview, Specs, Secrets and the workspace\n  dashboard read rows derived from the config and the connections\n  (`asRows`), named by the checkout directory the backend clones into;\n- Detach removes the source from the config (`without`);\n- a launch no longer sends the project''s repositories: the backend clones\n  them itself, and only `local` folders, `root_*` and the gear corpus are\n  sent.\n\nThe settings keep `root_*`, `local` folders and automation; nothing else\nwrites `repos[]`. FrontX''s `ProjectSource` gains the optional `branch` the\nbackend reads.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","tree":{"sha":"f417a5999484bbd939ebc983adc31595e9d9c742","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/trees/f417a5999484bbd939ebc983adc31595e9d9c742"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/commits/08262c34231e9d5a476e3587c01f6c0b958ac7a3","verification":{"payload":"tree f417a5999484bbd939ebc983adc31595e9d9c742\nparent ce2297bd67629a18a1a2db96a04e5a62b8d4f043\nauthor ANDREI KUCHMA <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech> 1790852197 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790852197 +0200\n\nfeat(prototype): a project''s repositories are its config''s sources, as the FrontX portal keeps them (stacked on #590) (#591)\n\n* feat(backend): a project''s repositories are one record — project.config sources[]\n\nA project''s repositories were kept twice: the FrontX portal''s wizard wrote\n`project.config` `sources[]` ({connection_id, full_path, clone_url}), the\nprototype wrote the workspace settings'' `repos[]` ({name, url, token_ref}),\nand each reader picked one or merged both. The FrontX portal reads only the\nconfig, so a project attached in the prototype opened in its IDE with no code\n— \"studio-frontend-prototype/src/place-url.ts was not found in the workspace\".\n\n`project_sources` is now the one reader, in the portal''s shape plus an\noptional `branch`:\n\n- parse: the sources in order, each with its checkout directory derived from\n  `full_path` exactly as the portal''s `checkoutDirectory` does;\n- resolve: each with its connection''s `secret_ref`, looked up by id through\n  the tenant''s ancestors (`connectors::connection_by_id`, the catalogue read\n  without drivers), and whether the connection is personal;\n- git_sources: as sessions and the Git proxy clone them — a personal\n  connection''s token is never handed to a shared session.\n\nEvery reader moves to it and stops reading the settings'' `repos[]`:\n\n- studio-session: a launch clones the project''s sources whoever asks; the\n  request''s `repos` add only what is not the project''s (a backend-host\n  folder, the gear corpus), and one the project has is cloned once\n  (`launch_sources::plan`);\n- studio-git: the sources a desktop may clone, and the sync a push queues;\n- components-catalog: whose dependencies to read, now with their branch;\n- documents: which checkout and which synced clone to read;\n- organizations rollups: the repository count, from the config already read.\n\nThe three hand-written config parsers, `sources_in`, `checkout_sources`,\n`repo_path_of` and `by_secret_ref` go with the second path. `root_*` and\n`local` entries stay in the settings: they describe a working copy, not the\nproject''s repositories.\n\nscripts/migrate-project-sources.mjs moves existing `repos[]` into `sources[]`\non the same tenant (dry run by default, `--apply` to write, idempotent). Run\nit on a stand before this backend reaches it.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>\n\n* feat(prototype): a project''s repositories are its config''s sources, as the FrontX portal keeps them\n\nThe prototype kept a project''s repositories in the workspace settings''\n`repos[]`, which the FrontX portal never reads. They now live where that\nportal and the backend read them, `project.config` `sources[]`\n({connection_id, full_path, clone_url, branch?}), through one module,\n`project-sources.ts`:\n\n- attaching from a connector adds sources through the connection by id,\n  a repository already listed once (`withPicked`);\n- the Sources tab, the launcher, Overview, Specs, Secrets and the workspace\n  dashboard read rows derived from the config and the connections\n  (`asRows`), named by the checkout directory the backend clones into;\n- Detach removes the source from the config (`without`);\n- a launch no longer sends the project''s repositories: the backend clones\n  them itself, and only `local` folders, `root_*` and the gear corpus are\n  sent.\n\nThe settings keep `root_*`, `local` folders and automation; nothing else\nwrites `repos[]`. FrontX''s `ProjectSource` gains the optional `branch` the\nbackend reads.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvjxlCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA1GQQAHcvYsLussi/ZQxGOKr8geEq\nPkJpDLaymXX0aOxJfRU7Lqg4HLeJqmE8sPT8f5VP6/p0qDNOn67Q+yMP7R1sKdl5\n5eVjkYQfMHdq4AW/WnVcsqsIjmF/ciuwHH8nhQWQER5Q4tjuw+WhNWerfBEeW/eU\nXS3s8bGYzb8q5NSkKYwAUKBS5GKmqNQLrGDeAq82h4EPdXLNSVSBpjrRX//wMsq7\n6f/h69TPZsPDhEKNybw8BoHYaqAjrD7SSLqA9Mzg530Xm33Gv+cvbi+SMsWQ5tFi\nJF7mT8fMtMxwd8Q5gQkJmIQD0pMf86jen2OloA9jKs06C9tsPtKBcPlCiZxEupfP\nsOcOTiWNCADn3DXytsYo+MIpl56VZQcrvt6kPrxLyZtHcEBif7ypxQzZ2Z23RJ+B\nyJV+Yl7zxoR77rLdHjUgbeJvFUrw+65YQCQnGdqVT76SecRrLk+TsIe9EXhSyCSq\npRVmKEQSWngwaWnt/wtDG173MbIC9BRYi61iv8+RfFwfF+IsvxU9HMK0f40O2Loz\n6eMh3t+2xfK6CWCClRTx1HLq6FqW2D3FvM0FT2x2y5be4PnGRVIubgllleL7RKJa\nyMDFxWk60by0iRY4JIqZNrTa5X1o6s+lD6jM0U1j6fdrJkalY5rsg25ng+nlwdfa\n9w/8zktRj+ksCIdIjTqk\n=4WxB\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-01T10:56:37Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/08262c34231e9d5a476e3587c01f6c0b958ac7a3","node_id":"C_kwDOTl7dJtoAKDA4MjYyYzM0MjMxZTlkNWE0NzZlMzU4N2MwMWY2YzBiOTU4YWM3YTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/ce2297bd67629a18a1a2db96a04e5a62b8d4f043","sha":"ce2297bd67629a18a1a2db96a04e5a62b8d4f043","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/ce2297bd67629a18a1a2db96a04e5a62b8d4f043"}],"sha":"08262c34231e9d5a476e3587c01f6c0b958ac7a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/08262c34231e9d5a476e3587c01f6c0b958ac7a3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/301748190?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AndrejK666","id":301748190,"login":"AndrejK666","node_id":"U_kgDOEfxP3g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/ce2297bd67629a18a1a2db96a04e5a62b8d4f043/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T10:54:21Z","email":"Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech","name":"ANDREI KUCHMA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T10:54:21Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(backend): a project''s repositories are one record — project.config sources[] (#590)\n\nA project''s repositories were kept twice: the FrontX portal''s wizard wrote\n`project.config` `sources[]` ({connection_id, full_path, clone_url}), the\nprototype wrote the workspace settings'' `repos[]` ({name, url, token_ref}),\nand each reader picked one or merged both. The FrontX portal reads only the\nconfig, so a project attached in the prototype opened in its IDE with no code\n— \"studio-frontend-prototype/src/place-url.ts was not found in the workspace\".\n\n`project_sources` is now the one reader, in the portal''s shape plus an\noptional `branch`:\n\n- parse: the sources in order, each with its checkout directory derived from\n  `full_path` exactly as the portal''s `checkoutDirectory` does;\n- resolve: each with its connection''s `secret_ref`, looked up by id through\n  the tenant''s ancestors (`connectors::connection_by_id`, the catalogue read\n  without drivers), and whether the connection is personal;\n- git_sources: as sessions and the Git proxy clone them — a personal\n  connection''s token is never handed to a shared session.\n\nEvery reader moves to it and stops reading the settings'' `repos[]`:\n\n- studio-session: a launch clones the project''s sources whoever asks; the\n  request''s `repos` add only what is not the project''s (a backend-host\n  folder, the gear corpus), and one the project has is cloned once\n  (`launch_sources::plan`);\n- studio-git: the sources a desktop may clone, and the sync a push queues;\n- components-catalog: whose dependencies to read, now with their branch;\n- documents: which checkout and which synced clone to read;\n- organizations rollups: the repository count, from the config already read.\n\nThe three hand-written config parsers, `sources_in`, `checkout_sources`,\n`repo_path_of` and `by_secret_ref` go with the second path. `root_*` and\n`local` entries stay in the settings: they describe a working copy, not the\nproject''s repositories.\n\nscripts/migrate-project-sources.mjs moves existing `repos[]` into `sources[]`\non the same tenant (dry run by default, `--apply` to write, idempotent). Run\nit on a stand before this backend reaches it.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","tree":{"sha":"0c601f6259809a8179c400a9bcfd761f674b1e61","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/trees/0c601f6259809a8179c400a9bcfd761f674b1e61"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/commits/ce2297bd67629a18a1a2db96a04e5a62b8d4f043","verification":{"payload":"tree 0c601f6259809a8179c400a9bcfd761f674b1e61\nparent 08a1e0af1b15448a2018e3870761e76e0421ec2e\nauthor ANDREI KUCHMA <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech> 1790852061 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790852061 +0200\n\nfeat(backend): a project''s repositories are one record — project.config sources[] (#590)\n\nA project''s repositories were kept twice: the FrontX portal''s wizard wrote\n`project.config` `sources[]` ({connection_id, full_path, clone_url}), the\nprototype wrote the workspace settings'' `repos[]` ({name, url, token_ref}),\nand each reader picked one or merged both. The FrontX portal reads only the\nconfig, so a project attached in the prototype opened in its IDE with no code\n— \"studio-frontend-prototype/src/place-url.ts was not found in the workspace\".\n\n`project_sources` is now the one reader, in the portal''s shape plus an\noptional `branch`:\n\n- parse: the sources in order, each with its checkout directory derived from\n  `full_path` exactly as the portal''s `checkoutDirectory` does;\n- resolve: each with its connection''s `secret_ref`, looked up by id through\n  the tenant''s ancestors (`connectors::connection_by_id`, the catalogue read\n  without drivers), and whether the connection is personal;\n- git_sources: as sessions and the Git proxy clone them — a personal\n  connection''s token is never handed to a shared session.\n\nEvery reader moves to it and stops reading the settings'' `repos[]`:\n\n- studio-session: a launch clones the project''s sources whoever asks; the\n  request''s `repos` add only what is not the project''s (a backend-host\n  folder, the gear corpus), and one the project has is cloned once\n  (`launch_sources::plan`);\n- studio-git: the sources a desktop may clone, and the sync a push queues;\n- components-catalog: whose dependencies to read, now with their branch;\n- documents: which checkout and which synced clone to read;\n- organizations rollups: the repository count, from the config already read.\n\nThe three hand-written config parsers, `sources_in`, `checkout_sources`,\n`repo_path_of` and `by_secret_ref` go with the second path. `root_*` and\n`local` entries stay in the settings: they describe a working copy, not the\nproject''s repositories.\n\nscripts/migrate-project-sources.mjs moves existing `repos[]` into `sources[]`\non the same tenant (dry run by default, `--apply` to write, idempotent). Run\nit on a stand before this backend reaches it.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvjvdCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAACDAQAKM9biSRq4Yn62OHhgrzOlxy\nXzFNK5jwmaLilZeLV3PL/n/kLDW2y9LlXGL0Gt3vAzuVpD5L1kJsCjkzrf6ZNpNK\na21qzPf19R3cDppxQ3mb9JQdtJP1avOINYo4KrhSqX6r0zjZS1FzBogF87PfLLwB\n+15ZqIQ9F6Y7lSN4bBVSbfqB0eFlFzWEUze+Tjcu13Yx/Saewoxdr40/mZ9+57Ry\n0NS5FQp3v7cjfbW69ZKHs0DGteSw+4v9fry8dCSaArVDDsfPgMX3zi510/N0Li59\nGfLWqBPmAcUhJZQSqNjwjWOIRx0eyiI5Ztl8HR7fqyxG6zgIKszmyHr/qVkE7Iac\nsMTe8wBzHTIKBo8TGDcqP62SW3W79brFVAKpI2QRq7qOb/yacXxScXnX+jyt5xIr\nb0+aQ7vqzWxUHmPgCcKi0IeDtmsb01pwxvEeFQ9E+vpB9xh1jbLtJ2D8VzuieKI0\nDc8h/oJDeOph8nCzpmWutMGXkL+N1qFDFqOt+zAX9eKIOgn7JUsBkQlc+8YEACV9\nPES/KUH7mbKQaDQLYAD6Z