:"2026-10-01T10:29:42Z","email":"Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech","name":"ANDREI KUCHMA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T10:29:42Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: main is red — the roadmap plan type missing from the GTS snapshot, and API-docs examples read as calls (#588)\n\nTwo merges broke two gates on main (run 36844262498):\n\n- #586 added `gts.cf.studio.catalog.roadmap_plan.v1~` without regenerating\n  docs/gts-types.json, so gts_inventory''s snapshot test failed. Regenerated\n  with `cargo run -- gts-types`; the diff is the one new type.\n- #587''s api-docs test and doc comment spelled made-up paths\n  (`/studio-git/v1/repos`, `/spec-quality/v1/runs`, …), which\n  scripts/check-api-usage.mjs reads as portal calls with no endpoint. They\n  now use real routes, and the comment no longer quotes a path.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","tree":{"sha":"e7e7e9ca2b73259dcc8bc38a5db58fd78430cc20","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/trees/e7e7e9ca2b73259dcc8bc38a5db58fd78430cc20"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/commits/a38f513b115837ec5e30ebbf297d15a87f367cdd","verification":{"payload":"tree e7e7e9ca2b73259dcc8bc38a5db58fd78430cc20\nparent 9ab36fef528e596b58480363052b4527881394e1\nauthor ANDREI KUCHMA <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech> 1790850582 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790850582 +0200\n\nfix: main is red — the roadmap plan type missing from the GTS snapshot, and API-docs examples read as calls (#588)\n\nTwo merges broke two gates on main (run 36844262498):\n\n- #586 added `gts.cf.studio.catalog.roadmap_plan.v1~` without regenerating\n  docs/gts-types.json, so gts_inventory''s snapshot test failed. Regenerated\n  with `cargo run -- gts-types`; the diff is the one new type.\n- #587''s api-docs test and doc comment spelled made-up paths\n  (`/studio-git/v1/repos`, `/spec-quality/v1/runs`, …), which\n  scripts/check-api-usage.mjs reads as portal calls with no endpoint. They\n  now use real routes, and the comment no longer quotes a path.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvjYWCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAUpQQAF5/4KUNYlrL9bi4gITVz5c2\nIHnCt/xTQ3ODFkVKjsQBXUO3dgh34qjwn4JAWAuP5QlOvPfUSI66EPtZFCnkyA4n\noxk6JMwA/6W/nTro6aCaqjwFrtsY4tW4KbszF87Uh0rF8j1mgkAwBlphfZfGW1Wp\nixe/zY+q/QUUJeyq83lm+dL+UbZbUK3YB7UX0ekF9bw8LsVAp1Co1dxeHel8lTNt\ndGwUBi1dytKHJT5Z7rMR3syxZ1S+qNqT8NrTHiDyCEKGBeisLV/drrVaiSlOIdSo\nnSZz8dvWSKI+M97n2dcO4V4nsmQuN7JwdM/gbZxlzecJwoh4BKSIbZnGbsvT0G8Y\njvDsOVVrKZUTGCHbTBhxFKC0agm2p6i3pqp3RgdEi6WZjgU5AeC2rxJ/gMw6XBaa\neYbDb8ceoHPD7pae1ftteUXX3PFQ2/lrdpZ7VPP6YpO2gVzWBmAAYt5EU1PiUb/7\nR1EUu1xBQzb3FHstxg66oOM1sxWmJRo21Whun7N8ogqXSW57Hpa3sObq53zDJ4tt\njY2lTeX93SCxvQFq3eta21sWMo+z++S1ANEFkQaiGNhKz8SBaBRG96UALGgw2Dy+\npDtDtUY3E3zifqmS3gHWiV7HYX/T+syEuWc9Nas2b9Z81tMIypgAZGgJMuXmjXbd\nxmZYTS9hQd2bwh2BAspJ\n=JSUJ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-01T10:29:42Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/a38f513b115837ec5e30ebbf297d15a87f367cdd","node_id":"C_kwDOTl7dJtoAKGEzOGY1MTNiMTE1ODM3ZWM1ZTMwZWJiZjI5N2QxNWE4N2YzNjdjZGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/9ab36fef528e596b58480363052b4527881394e1","sha":"9ab36fef528e596b58480363052b4527881394e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/9ab36fef528e596b58480363052b4527881394e1"}],"sha":"a38f513b115837ec5e30ebbf297d15a87f367cdd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/a38f513b115837ec5e30ebbf297d15a87f367cdd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/301748190?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AndrejK666","id":301748190,"login":"AndrejK666","node_id":"U_kgDOEfxP3g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/9ab36fef528e596b58480363052b4527881394e1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T09:40:33Z","email":"Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech","name":"ANDREI KUCHMA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T09:40:33Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(prototype): an API reference grouped by the component that serves it (#587)\n\n/cf/docs lists forty tags in one flat run: the gateway''s OpenAPI\ndocument declares no tag list and no grouping, and Stoplight Elements\nshows tags on one level only. Which gear an endpoint belongs to is\nnowhere on the page.\n\n/api-docs/ reads the same /cf/openapi.json and groups it on our side.\nA gear mounts its routes under its own first path segment, so that\nprefix is the component: its operations'' tags become its sections\nunder \"Platform · …\" or \"Studio · …\", carried as x-tagGroups to Scalar,\nwhich shows them as a level of their own. An untagged operation takes\nits component''s name, and a gear added later lands in its own group\nwithout an edit here. Nothing in the toolkit changes, and /cf/docs\nstays as it is.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","tree":{"sha":"cf5a48759db221a46d20ec79e24234dcc52a741e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/trees/cf5a48759db221a46d20ec79e24234dcc52a741e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/commits/9ab36fef528e596b58480363052b4527881394e1","verification":{"payload":"tree cf5a48759db221a46d20ec79e24234dcc52a741e\nparent 57384407fe50c5869f71d4215a29e5681ab6bfb9\nauthor ANDREI KUCHMA <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech> 1790847633 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790847633 +0200\n\nfeat(prototype): an API reference grouped by the component that serves it (#587)\n\n/cf/docs lists forty tags in one flat run: the gateway''s OpenAPI\ndocument declares no tag list and no grouping, and Stoplight Elements\nshows tags on one level only. Which gear an endpoint belongs to is\nnowhere on the page.\n\n/api-docs/ reads the same /cf/openapi.json and groups it on our side.\nA gear mounts its routes under its own first path segment, so that\nprefix is the component: its operations'' tags become its sections\nunder \"Platform · …\" or \"Studio · …\", carried as x-tagGroups to Scalar,\nwhich shows them as a level of their own. An untagged operation takes\nits component''s name, and a gear added later lands in its own group\nwithout an edit here. Nothing in the toolkit changes, and /cf/docs\nstays as it is.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqviqRCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAALVQQAFIBzbFIIaedqn5TVNYRHaR8\nOGPEGUVrB53tbY5cIdxE89nQNvirrWjSIkCM4s8HZPWRxhP7cUhsu2zIKHI03Uxl\nPRo6dOWo4BR6DVoG7hh6f6XIn415IABYUHbtEMlHpUuMdtq6lGNnfnC/uUWpsjjH\nOVPQWcPnAT4vRQW/Rukdh3pWb3xsqHlyDLiL1IJczBqPRNmOpF2s2CgkfSKCoiZv\n4A/w0OeOOVCD4ThQtk3cqhIIRGu8x1iSRWA3MAJEX9tk6ifLzkzZ2g1+Lw7TMBwb\n++JwOzNW+TDzDs6o13HYiOeYNOTcsQcDa5/0Pg2YiqT/9SuyHY06RbcPSMqmXc9a\n3ZSjNydxswPMJr+4fpzbUKOPtTLpz7Fv9hRMCYcUT56dLpAQOYRsScU7TybD/dEJ\nNy4CICnZDCYuk8PdhQx2SiEOErJc027EyZh8z9F/rfBnB51XR3YxhouCU+FciXMt\n0eKTlA6Rr3UtNTp2gWhVteHzhptYfLH3fUk6oEKwouPoi3CC/DZ4Y7DOYU23DEyb\na0D7KMZT3YmOgAEKecW6BMqwY0+n79VN4vbLRbw1Gexp8LcZPxqHhiaDG1LhD7cO\nU5YsoRmQ8EQjk/bu1GCuXQ03Nkn1VpHHGnmZN59coEKU1ZZFug6KYWZlOAhoXJex\nITycKun59DFnVxciqcXx\n=GZgR\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-01T09:40:34Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/9ab36fef528e596b58480363052b4527881394e1","node_id":"C_kwDOTl7dJtoAKDlhYjM2ZmVmNTI4ZTU5NmI1ODQ4MDM2MzA1MmI0NTI3ODgxMzk0ZTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/57384407fe50c5869f71d4215a29e5681ab6bfb9","sha":"57384407fe50c5869f71d4215a29e5681ab6bfb9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/57384407fe50c5869f71d4215a29e5681ab6bfb9"}],"sha":"9ab36fef528e596b58480363052b4527881394e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/9ab36fef528e596b58480363052b4527881394e1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48068281?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SysoevAndrey/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SysoevAndrey/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SysoevAndrey/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SysoevAndrey/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/SysoevAndrey","id":48068281,"login":"SysoevAndrey","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4MDY4Mjgx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SysoevAndrey/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SysoevAndrey/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SysoevAndrey/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SysoevAndrey/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SysoevAndrey/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SysoevAndrey","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/57384407fe50c5869f71d4215a29e5681ab6bfb9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T09:07:42Z","email":"48068281+SysoevAndrey@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Andrey Sysoev"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T09:07:42Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(shell): the portal talks to the editor in its frame (#584)\n\n* docs(theia): §6 of the bridge contract says what the editor''s bridge does\n\nThe portal ↔ IDE channel had stopped on 2026-09-18 and missed half the\nmessages. §6 now follows portal-bridge-contribution.ts and its tests:\nevery message both ways, the handshake (the bridge listens only once its\nsession''s origin rules arrive and answers only the first studio.init, so\nany studio.* is the acknowledgement), delivery and re-arming on every\nframe load, the origin rules on both ends, the viewer and token rules,\nand the trust the frame is given: no sandbox, and why. The design''s\nportal ↔ IDE interface lists the same messages and points at §6.\n\nThe bridge''s behaviour does not change; only its header comment, which\nsaid the portal''s queue alone gets early messages through, now says the\nportal repeats studio.init.\n\nPart of #323.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrey Sysoev <andrey@sysoev.ru>\n\n* feat(shell): the portal talks to the editor in its frame\n\nThe IDE in the editor''s frame is told the portal''s theme, the member''s\ntoken and who they are, the project, and the file to open, and its first\nanswer is when the editor is ready.\n\n- mfe/editorBridge.ts: the portal''s half of §6, with no React and no app.\n  It repeats studio.init every two seconds until any studio.* answers,\n  holds the latest of each other message until then, re-arms on every\n  frame load, takes messages only from the frame''s window and the origin\n  of its address, and posts only there.\n- MfeHandlerIframe gains an onFrame hook, told of every frame it makes,\n  and makes a new frame for a new address instead of changing src. The\n  frame is allowed the clipboard and gets no sandbox.\n- The editor''s session attaches the bridge to space-mfe''s frame and feeds\n  it: the token from app.auth (never a shared property), the viewer from\n  the session profile, the project''s name, the theme by id, and the file\n  as <checkout directory>/<path> (checkoutDirectory, from the rule\n  sessionSources names directories by). Ready waits for the IDE''s answer;\n  two minutes of silence after the address fail as \"The editor did not\n  answer\", a late answer still opens the editor, and Try again makes a\n  new frame. studio.openComponent is answered with a notice until the\n  portal has a component page (#583).\n- docs/feature/editor-bridge.md specifies it; editor-session.md carries\n  the new states, and the decomposition the new entry.\n\nCloses #323.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrey Sysoev <andrey@sysoev.ru>\n\n* fix(shell): the editor''s session hears the newest token, and only from its frame\n\nReview round 1 of #584.\n\n- The session read a new frame starts with no longer overrides a renewal\n  heard since, nor reaches the next frame once its own has gone; a read\n  that fails is logged and the IDE starts without a token. A session that\n  ends is not told to the IDE: the bridge cannot take a token back, and\n  the sign-in screen that follows removes the frame.\n- A launch that ends while the editor is hidden sets no deadline; coming\n  back mounts a frame, which sets its own.\n- The light themes are the shell''s DEFAULT_THEME_ID and LIGHT_THEME_ID,\n  mapped in the session; the bridge keeps no theme ids.\n- registerAppContextEffects takes main.tsx''s session and builds none of\n  its own, so the frame hook and the routing cannot hold two.\n- Dropped what could not be observed: the bridge !== mine checks in\n  onAnswer and onReload (a disposed bridge reports nothing) and resetting\n  the file and the sources on a project switch (every shown scope sets the\n  file, and a switch clears the address before a new frame can exist).\n- New tests: a read overtaken by a renewal, a read of a released frame, a\n  failed read, no profile or project name or bearer token, the newest of\n  two frames, the next project''s IDE, the hidden deadline, the theme for\n  every portal theme, the entry id against space-mfe/mfe.json, and the\n  session''s wiring into routing and Try again. Each was checked by\n  removing the line it guards.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrey Sysoev <andrey@sysoev.ru>\n\n* docs: ADR-0021 records what #323 decided about the frame\n\n- ADR-0021 gains an amendment: the handler''s onFrame hook and its release,\n  a new frame for every address, no sandbox and the clipboard allowed. The\n  two consequences that left this to #323 point at it.\n- §6 says which messages wait for the answer: every one in the prototype,\n  the latest of each type in this portal.\n- The theme DoD touches the session, not the bridge.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrey Sysoev <andrey@sysoev.ru>\n\n* test(shell): a session that ends tells the IDE nothing, and no theme is dark\n\nReview round 2 of #584. After the IDE has answered, an unauthenticated\nevent posts nothing, a reload then gets an init without the ended\nsession''s token, and the next renewal goes out with the viewer. The theme\ntable gains the case with no current theme, which maps to dark. Each was\nchecked by removing the line it guards.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrey Sysoev <andrey@sysoev.ru>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrey Sysoev <andrey@sysoev.ru>","tree":{"sha":"19b5eafcebe3df47248d5b13ef8eb8a82af345ee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/trees/19b5eafcebe3df47248d5b13ef8eb8a82af345ee"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/commits/57384407fe50c5869f71d4215a29e5681ab6bfb9","verification":{"payload":"tree 19b5eafcebe3df47248d5b13ef8eb8a82af345ee\nparent a075b6d6be052360ea1c65c4fbcada4624a31e31\nauthor Andrey Sysoev <48068281+SysoevAndrey@users.noreply.github.com> 1790845662 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790845662 +0200\n\nfeat(shell): the portal talks to the editor in its frame (#584)\n\n* docs(theia): §6 of the bridge contract says what the editor''s bridge does\n\nThe portal ↔ IDE channel had stopped on 2026-09-18 and missed half the\nmessages. §6 now follows portal-bridge-contribution.ts and its tests:\nevery message both ways, the handshake (the bridge listens only once its\nsession''s origin rules arrive and answers only the first studio.init, so\nany studio.* is the acknowledgement), delivery and re-arming on every\nframe load, the origin rules on both ends, the viewer and token rules,\nand the trust the frame is given: no sandbox, and why. The design''s\nportal ↔ IDE interface lists the same messages and points at §6.\n\nThe bridge''s behaviour does not change; only its header comment, which\nsaid the portal''s queue alone gets early messages through, now says the\nportal repeats studio.init.\n\nPart of #323.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrey Sysoev <andrey@sysoev.ru>\n\n* feat(shell): the portal talks to the editor in its frame\n\nThe IDE in the editor''s frame is told the portal''s theme, the member''s\ntoken and who they are, the project, and the file to open, and its first\nanswer is when the editor is ready.\n\n- mfe/editorBridge.ts: the portal''s half of §6, with no React and no app.\n  It repeats studio.init every two seconds until any studio.* answers,\n  holds the latest of each other message until then, re-arms on every\n  frame load, takes messages only from the frame''s window and the origin\n  of its address, and posts only there.\n- MfeHandlerIframe gains an onFrame hook, told of every frame it makes,\n  and makes a new frame for a new address instead of changing src. The\n  frame is allowed the clipboard and gets no sandbox.\n- The editor''s session attaches the bridge to space-mfe''s frame and feeds\n  it: the token from app.auth (never a shared property), the viewer from\n  the session profile, the project''s name, the theme by id, and the file\n  as <checkout directory>/<path> (checkoutDirectory, from the rule\n  sessionSources names directories by). Ready waits for the IDE''s answer;\n  two minutes of silence after the address fail as \"The editor did not\n  answer\", a late answer still opens the editor, and Try again makes a\n  new frame. studio.openComponent is answered with a notice until the\n  portal has a component page (#583).\n- docs/feature/editor-bridge.md specifies it; editor-session.md carries\n  the new states, and the decomposition the new entry.\n\nCloses #323.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrey Sysoev <andrey@sysoev.ru>\n\n* fix(shell): the editor''s session hears the newest token, and only from its frame\n\nReview round 1 of #584.\n\n- The session read a new frame starts with no longer overrides a renewal\n  heard since, nor reaches the next frame once its own has gone; a read\n  that fails is logged and the IDE starts without a token. A session that\n  ends is not told to the IDE: the bridge cannot take a token back, and\n  the sign-in screen that follows removes the frame.\n- A launch that ends while the editor is hidden sets no deadline; coming\n  back mounts a frame, which sets its own.\n- The light themes are the shell''s DEFAULT_THEME_ID and LIGHT_THEME_ID,\n  mapped in the session; the bridge keeps no theme ids.\n- registerAppContextEffects takes main.tsx''s session and builds none of\n  its own, so the frame hook and the routing cannot hold two.\n- Dropped what could not be observed: the bridge !== mine checks in\n  onAnswer and onReload (a disposed bridge reports nothing) and resetting\n  the file and the sources on a project switch (every shown scope sets the\n  file, and a switch clears the address before a new frame can exist).\n- New tests: a read overtaken by a renewal, a read of a released frame, a\n  failed read, no profile or project name or bearer token, the newest of\n  two frames, the next project''s IDE, the hidden deadline, the theme for\n  every portal theme, the entry id against space-mfe/mfe.json, and the\n  session''s wiring into routing and Try again. Each was checked by\n  removing the line it guards.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrey Sysoev <andrey@sysoev.ru>\n\n* docs: ADR-0021 records what #323 decided about the frame\n\n- ADR-0021 gains an amendment: the handler''s onFrame hook and its release,\n  a new frame for every address, no sandbox and the clipboard allowed. The\n  two consequences that left this to #323 point at it.\n- §6 says which messages wait for the answer: every one in the prototype,\n  the latest of each type in this portal.\n- The theme DoD touches the session, not the bridge.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrey Sysoev <andrey@sysoev.ru>\n\n* test(shell): a session that ends tells the IDE nothing, and no theme is dark\n\nReview round 2 of #584. After the IDE has answered, an unauthenticated\nevent posts nothing, a reload then gets an init without the ended\nsession''s token, and the next renewal goes out with the viewer. The theme\ntable gains the case with no current theme, which maps to dark. Each was\nchecked by removing the line it guards.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrey Sysoev <andrey@sysoev.ru>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrey Sysoev <andrey@sysoev.ru>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqviLeCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAH30QAF2O2f3+x3QcgU7xo3tdPsU/\nbxJRt/kzcfofQUPvwXP3JzipAwX2gwNqE8LZwZBS0vVTZfb3YkVk8beNeqwYLWbS\nCq815dOG+L1YjZPmVjj8fVAEn+6dfkHVX50MR3Pz4UiRcV268EA2xzMexJ/SUHO1\nxLi8NHeX2g72hk+q92CogF+7jcuACl9BEtjV0KCFEo27dx0GtZOQQfKa9vWW2DJm\nFhT7hLoT2wHcGFWQH6ikz7FOiMz+WdWkojqpIMLvbZCB+w4jgSP899UoXreI2mQb\nfidHVUjLxbEnoUMn0U2esoISpEnE4sWli3ZkIXGERqaW6fN8pgSX8GznNJgAkF+k\n+cSQBoF4s0kgB5+DcWdX+0/eHLJuootxpPTBMW4n0Y5V1sBfySQr2ru+QRoOggp+\nDJrdtf8L5hZsY6aRj0Qwb+ZRxE2aUpQRvtxer5ugzfMlfS0IAhHTXg5qoJL/IEZL\ny3DPsugzEc3DUXdvfWEbNHJ2PzC8cAFKbPVW0ww5q8vLka34z6+Tt4KlyzDCOld+\noZbrf01xK4kzRK2F9gM9E5e1cidGE7bOjKAh5ICNjzACNTnAJ9mlPj3mP1Hjr8Pl\nEjp2p2QhYu31AI/D+qmGbhgkdiGVwsPJ/kU4zF8Y7gOtoo829UaJej9iQ7xhCUYT\n6rtADBFA4FA6f4EIq7FV\n=46U3\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-01T09:07:42Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/57384407fe50c5869f71d4215a29e5681ab6bfb9","node_id":"C_kwDOTl7dJtoAKDU3Mzg0NDA3ZmU1MGM1ODY5ZjcxZDQyMTVhMjllNTY4MWFiNmJmYjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/a075b6d6be052360ea1c65c4fbcada4624a31e31","sha":"a075b6d6be052360ea1c65c4fbcada4624a31e31","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/a075b6d6be052360ea1c65c4fbcada4624a31e31"}],"sha":"57384407fe50c5869f71d4215a29e5681ab6bfb9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/57384407fe50c5869f71d4215a29e5681ab6bfb9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/301748190?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AndrejK666","id":301748190,"login":"AndrejK666","node_id":"U_kgDOEfxP3g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/a075b6d6be052360ea1c65c4fbcada4624a31e31/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T08:43:53Z","email":"Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech","name":"ANDREI KUCHMA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T08:43:53Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(components): the roadmap workbook is the planning team''s back_roadmap.xlsx, cell for cell (#586)\n\nThe roadmap report''s download was two plain sheets the client laid out. The\nplanning team''s own report -- `back_roadmap_to_xls.py` over board #48 -- is\nthirteen: Summary (formulas over the group sheets), Roadmap (groups as\nswimlanes over nine months, a box per gear at its milestone), Gantt (each\nteam''s remaining work scheduled against its people and power, blockers\nfirst), People, a sheet per group and ALL, with forecasts, data bars and the\ncells it colours red.\n\nThe backend now writes that workbook, its rules ported one for one:\n`GET /studio-components-catalog/v1/roadmap-report/workbook?date=`\n(`roadmap_workbook.rs`, a small OOXML writer in `xlsx.rs`). Against the\nscript''s own output for the same board on the same day it matches on every\nsheet: values, formulas, styles, links, merges, widths, panes, filters,\nconditional formats, and all 118 Roadmap boxes and 91 Gantt bars.\n\nWhat it needs that the board does not carry:\n- the sync reads each issue''s type, blockers and card (`**Description**:`,\n  `**Is Plugin**:` ... in the body), and stores the board''s raw columns on\n  the planned gear;\n- the plan -- the team''s `gears.yaml` (teams, people, power, swimlanes,\n  consumer projects) -- is handed to a sync as `plan_yaml` and kept as text\n  in a `roadmap_plan` node, because its order is the column, lane and People\n  order and JSON keeps none. It is parsed the way PyYAML reads it: a key\n  written twice keeps its first place and last value (the team''s file has\n  one, `''4418''`).\n\nAs the script does, a gear that is a root''s sub-issue but not on the board\nhas no Milestone and sits in the backlog.\n\nThe prototype and the IDE download the server''s workbook instead of building\ntheir own; the prototype''s roadmap source takes the `gears.yaml` file and\ndefaults to the platform''s root issues. Both client-side xlsx writers go.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","tree":{"sha":"bfed98c956fd0f2d47d93ab489e44729de58bfe4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/trees/bfed98c956fd0f2d47d93ab489e44729de58bfe4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/commits/a075b6d6be052360ea1c65c4fbcada4624a31e31","verification":{"payload":"tree bfed98c956fd0f2d47d93ab489e44729de58bfe4\nparent 51b08fa4b8fbe0214d282dd98c3032380a5265bf\nauthor ANDREI KUCHMA <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech> 1790844233 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790844233 +0200\n\nfeat(components): the roadmap workbook is the planning team''s back_roadmap.xlsx, cell for cell (#586)\n\nThe roadmap report''s download was two plain sheets the client laid out. The\nplanning team''s own report -- `back_roadmap_to_xls.py` over board #48 -- is\nthirteen: Summary (formulas over the group sheets), Roadmap (groups as\nswimlanes over nine months, a box per gear at its milestone), Gantt (each\nteam''s remaining work scheduled against its people and power, blockers\nfirst), People, a sheet per group and ALL, with forecasts, data bars and the\ncells it colours red.\n\nThe backend now writes that workbook, its rules ported one for one:\n`GET /studio-components-catalog/v1/roadmap-report/workbook?date=`\n(`roadmap_workbook.rs`, a small OOXML writer in `xlsx.rs`). Against the\nscript''s own output for the same board on the same day it matches on every\nsheet: values, formulas, styles, links, merges, widths, panes, filters,\nconditional formats, and all 118 Roadmap boxes and 91 Gantt bars.\n\nWhat it needs that the board does not carry:\n- the sync reads each issue''s type, blockers and card (`**Description**:`,\n  `**Is Plugin**:` ... in the body), and stores the board''s raw columns on\n  the planned gear;\n- the plan -- the team''s `gears.yaml` (teams, people, power, swimlanes,\n  consumer projects) -- is handed to a sync as `plan_yaml` and kept as text\n  in a `roadmap_plan` node, because its order is the column, lane and People\n  order and JSON keeps none. It is parsed the way PyYAML reads it: a key\n  written twice keeps its first place and last value (the team''s file has\n  one, `''4418''`).\n\nAs the script does, a gear that is a root''s sub-issue but not on the board\nhas no Milestone and sits in the backlog.\n\nThe prototype and the IDE download the server''s workbook instead of building\ntheir own; the prototype''s roadmap source takes the `gears.yaml` file and\ndefaults to the platform''s root issues. Both client-side xlsx writers go.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvh1KCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAATcsQAHBcAQkCM2LyJvl40PbscKGV\nmNyAOLm+PnmN11ViFvApS14DMS0u7i9tVXnif5ghXtORTvSeKnlPvf59VKeifQt4\nA0Z+U/G9CT+cMr0teZhNPCrxlrviQprneyDdIGWmv/5OsYiT4d/jM9ngwv5vGkIm\n6AD0NzXE5/0Wahmy07l18SYtL91tgT5aWjxvVNa9N6wdYk09i5HDmybxYXDBZPNh\n6oSgYevqKxWmyss+DwtXh69BLTaMyiOaIa6qyKT