624a31e31","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/a075b6d6be052360ea1c65c4fbcada4624a31e31"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/301748190?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AndrejK666","id":301748190,"login":"AndrejK666","node_id":"U_kgDOEfxP3g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/51b08fa4b8fbe0214d282dd98c3032380a5265bf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T08:27:55Z","email":"Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech","name":"ANDREI KUCHMA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T08:27:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(prototype): Components on the one list, and a rows-per-page choice on every list (#585)\n\nComponents was the one list #575 left on its own table: it took the\nlist''s address but kept a hand-built <table>, no pager, and a copy of\nthe sortable header. It now renders through DataTable, so the table and\nthe cards page, sort from their headers and open rows the same way as\nevery other list. The catalogue''s own filters (search, category, Hide\nSDKs, type chips) move into the list''s toolbar and keep their address;\nthe graph view is unchanged.\n\nThe shared pager gains \"Rows per page\" (25 / 50 / 100 / 200). The size\nis a preference kept with the person, like table-or-tiles, not part of\nthe address; a new size goes back to page one.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","tree":{"sha":"1a3d78f8411002a91b55ef2daad317a16d1e45ab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/trees/1a3d78f8411002a91b55ef2daad317a16d1e45ab"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/commits/51b08fa4b8fbe0214d282dd98c3032380a5265bf","verification":{"payload":"tree 1a3d78f8411002a91b55ef2daad317a16d1e45ab\nparent c8f982373b03a3b0ccb17d78923ae6ffbc1f1aa2\nauthor ANDREI KUCHMA <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech> 1790843275 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790843275 +0200\n\nfeat(prototype): Components on the one list, and a rows-per-page choice on every list (#585)\n\nComponents was the one list #575 left on its own table: it took the\nlist''s address but kept a hand-built <table>, no pager, and a copy of\nthe sortable header. It now renders through DataTable, so the table and\nthe cards page, sort from their headers and open rows the same way as\nevery other list. The catalogue''s own filters (search, category, Hide\nSDKs, type chips) move into the list''s toolbar and keep their address;\nthe graph view is unchanged.\n\nThe shared pager gains \"Rows per page\" (25 / 50 / 100 / 200). The size\nis a preference kept with the person, like table-or-tiles, not part of\nthe address; a new size goes back to page one.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvhmLCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAd+YQADLHhHCKK0KIU7p/CqA7o0j1\n32Q2oPf695T9gz1B/SngX9LSvgFwhWK0Tsgbq5CYJKDlz0GGl13zA0+OkYM3KW4v\nscOrq9tEfkkuuyDtRMO3gjn3tMty08EHm/9ZOBDxcRD6Aag3u/eCkhALMGGhSKBw\nGcSIkG4kdK9rGGft8y+Tj6W8+IKnQmWjPcClPK82+JB6X31X+++a4HC1hrka4At3\nrJLq/gpr7HgXsA5Fx51N7chJhkP23JET3/vHi