bd510416821f04d6765ea782cf3b1176"}],"sha":"f177f1d1cb36485a0207b738f60892374b76aead","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/f177f1d1cb36485a0207b738f60892374b76aead"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/301748190?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AndrejK666","id":301748190,"login":"AndrejK666","node_id":"U_kgDOEfxP3g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/10ef36bcbd510416821f04d6765ea782cf3b1176/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T13:16:17Z","email":"Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech","name":"ANDREI KUCHMA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T13:16:17Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(components): every gear the roadmap plans is a component, and every record names its sources (#579)\n\nThe catalogue knew a gear only once a crate for it existed, and the roadmap\nreport listed only the gears it could match to one: 23 of the 118 gears the\nBACKEND ROADMAP board plans. The platform team''s own report (back_roadmap)\ncounts all 118 -- the direct sub-issues of eight root issues -- and most of\nthem have no code yet, which is exactly what a consumer waiting for one needs\nto see. It also read the effort estimate from GitHub''s issue fields, which\nour reader never asked for, so Effort was empty for every gear.\n\nBoard:\n- A roadmap source names root issues (`owner/repo#123`); a gear is a direct\n  sub-issue of one, including one nobody has put on the board yet (read from\n  the root). Without roots, every item is one, as before.\n- Each item reads its parent and its issue fields (`Estimated Efforts m*d`);\n  the board''s own fields win where both answer. A host without issue fields\n  is asked again without them.\n- Matching an item to a crate survives a typo (`Chat Egine`), a compound\n  name (`credstore` / `Credentials Store`), and one item planning two crates\n  (`Auth Resolver` → authn- and authz-resolver): 27 matched, up from 23.\n\nCatalogue:\n- Every gear a board plans is stored as a `roadmap_item` node with its plan\n  and the components that implement it; a gear gone from a board that was\n  read is pruned.\n- A planned gear with no code is listed on the Components page as a\n  component of kind `planned` (built-in schema \"Planned gear\": summary and\n  roadmap). Once code for it is catalogued, that component carries the plan\n  and the planned node stops being listed.\n- Every record says where its facts came from: crates.io, the repository,\n  Gearbox, the roadmap board, a person (`sources` on component-values).\n\nReport:\n- One row per board gear, with the repository''s side (lifecycle, release,\n  grade) from the component that implements it; `not_in_code` counts the\n  rest. Effort and what is left of it (estimate × what the implementation\n  axis has not reached), and a summary per group (the title''s `CORE - `\n  prefix): gears, done, in code, each axis averaged, estimated, effort,\n  remaining. The prototype and the IDE show it and write it to the workbook.\n\nChecked against their example workbook on the live board: the same 118\ngears, and effort and implementation agree on 117; the one that differs\nmoved on the board since their run.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","tree":{"sha":"14238f94891e13516ecc1c8111af0ce91c292092","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/trees/14238f94891e13516ecc1c8111af0ce91c292092"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/commits/10ef36bcbd510416821f04d6765ea782cf3b1176","verification":{"payload":"tree 14238f94891e13516ecc1c8111af0ce91c292092\nparent 3b80155c92bbbb62c1c1ac7e8adbd75da01dc862\nauthor ANDREI KUCHMA <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech> 1790774177 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790774177 +0200\n\nfeat(components): every gear the roadmap plans is a component, and every record names its sources (#579)\n\nThe catalogue knew a gear only once a crate for it existed, and the roadmap\nreport listed only the gears it could match to one: 23 of the 118 gears the\nBACKEND ROADMAP board plans. The platform team''s own report (back_roadmap)\ncounts all 118 -- the direct sub-issues of eight root issues -- and most of\nthem have no code yet, which is exactly what a consumer waiting for one needs\nto see. It also read the effort estimate from GitHub''s issue fields, which\nour reader never asked for, so Effort was empty for every gear.\n\nBoard:\n- A roadmap source names root issues (`owner/repo#123`); a gear is a direct\n  sub-issue of one, including one nobody has put on the board yet (read from\n  the root). Without roots, every item is one, as before.\n- Each item reads its parent and its issue fields (`Estimated Efforts m*d`);\n  the board''s own fields win where both answer. A host without issue fields\n  is asked again without them.\n- Matching an item to a crate survives a typo (`Chat Egine`), a compound\n  name (`credstore` / `Credentials Store`), and one item planning two crates\n  (`Auth Resolver` → authn- and authz-resolver): 27 matched, up from 23.\n\nCatalogue:\n- Every gear a board plans is stored as a `roadmap_item` node with its plan\n  and the components that implement it; a gear gone from a board that was\n  read is pruned.\n- A planned gear with no code is listed on the Components page as a\n  component of kind `planned` (built-in schema \"Planned gear\": summary and\n  roadmap). Once code for it is catalogued, that component carries the plan\n  and the planned node stops being listed.\n- Every record says where its facts came from: crates.io, the repository,\n  Gearbox, the roadmap board, a person (`sources` on component-values).\n\nReport:\n- One row per board gear, with the repository''s side (lifecycle, release,\n  grade) from the component that implements it; `not_in_code` counts the\n  rest. Effort and what is left of it (estimate × what the implementation\n  axis has not reached), and a summary per group (the title''s `CORE - `\n  prefix): gears, done, in code, each axis averaged, estimated, effort,\n  remaining. The prototype and the IDE show it and write it to the workbook.\n\nChecked against their example workbook on the live board: the same 118\ngears, and effort and implementation agree on 117; the one that differs\nmoved on the board since their run.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvQuhCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA1bEQAIbZ/wETj6M9W8oDbOvroBn3\nn+AnU/CfspKQgAu6ZOFPobHIVZ7rRlG0wPSX5t6JSZGlz6NEBDxz+MMdGHOwHZhE\nrzrhl2vw+ZbUykyi1MTaG1G1Uy/BrhFKWv9IVOUfQcf6YbeDal9HOrE4zBYwvaE1\n7+tj2zdzMcQvuA8pZc8RBX5El0PtdmBnYJUNQ/aLtH+eFd8OJ8/loAdDAt9UHHBn\nQKmtxlbMxjOHXJmYrYx/RtGT6R53N27PGov33wjDwKsyUO1Q1aXwz61XAMyxbdz3\ntvFvT2OHVleNA7Sps6w+vE3kJ8mbAn/QzPTIma7UVfWQFhkCwsCUnYVf/itZeSOG\nkwPwOBY4/kElAhnvX2v4M1JmzeGMmuhiCRA051hrGNqLhmchDSSWd6z4oSKV4j1j\nclj1QMGWSwtihWGCLokqJ9UO1QQFWhalyPXOODCQat07vF6i0fSgspsExprTK4Vc\nAYMerRWFbIiCYW1jgU/7xR/yRFMtGKVHVo8mpEallCN2p4ollT1RBtwPQXtizWv1\nTxtGi6h4x0+hj6B3VilmbErkNfk8vcsfRS6X2aRcDCYamg5Uglilvs68ltgidV2q\nAp7YGd28A3N3strUTFk86CxIP3+Yk858F13pO+33i0ClihqpG+SFoN81BcCMnkwN\nkow0mH/2Ox/xp3Tny2Db\n=CHN0\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T13:16:17Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/10ef36bcbd510416821f04d6765ea782cf3b1176","node_id":"C_kwDOTl7dJtoAKDEwZWYzNmJjYmQ1MTA0MTY4MjFmMDRkNjc2NWVhNzgyY2YzYjExNzY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/3b80155c92bbbb62c1c1ac7e8adbd75da01dc862","sha":"3b80155c92bbbb62c1c1ac7e8adbd75da01dc862","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/3b80155c92bbbb62c1c1ac7e8adbd75da01dc862"}],"sha":"10ef36bcbd510416821f04d6765ea782cf3b1176","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/10ef36bcbd510416821f04d6765ea782cf3b1176"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/301748190?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AndrejK666","id":301748190,"login":"AndrejK666","node_id":"U_kgDOEfxP3g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/3b80155c92bbbb62c1c1ac7e8adbd75da01dc862/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T12:56:34Z","email":"Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech","name":"ANDREI KUCHMA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T12:56:34Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(prototype): every remaining list on the one list — Workspaces, Components, admin, Chats/Files/Secrets, Activity, Kits, System, Specs (#575)\n\n* feat(prototype): Workspaces on the one list — row opens it, Delete asks through the dialog, the tree is ▸\n\nThe workspaces portfolio moves onto DataTable:\n- **A row click opens the workspace.** Only the name used to.\n- **Open in IDE stays inline.** Open and Delete are in \"…\", and Delete goes\n  through the confirm dialog. The ✕ button and `window.confirm` are gone.\n  The dialog warns that the account system may refuse while the workspace\n  still has projects.\n- **Nested projects expand under the ▸ toggle** and load on first open,\n  each one opening its project.\n- **The list has its own search and a Self-managed / Managed chip filter.**\n  The side panel''s search, self-managed switch and name sort are no longer\n  read here. Workspace and Projects sort from their headers instead.\n- **The heading counts what is shown**: \"Workspaces in Default\n  Organization · 1\".\n\nVerified over CDP against the local stack. The columns read Workspace |\nProjects | People. ▸ lists the three projects under \"Test Worksoace\". The\nmenu reads Open / Delete (danger).\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>\n\n* feat(prototype): the pager sits under the list at its right edge, range first\n\nOne place for it everywhere, the Specs lists included: under the list,\nright-aligned, with \"51–100 of 2,446\" before the page buttons. It used to\nstart at the left edge, where the eye has already moved on to the next\nsection. Measured on the rebuilt bundle: the pager''s top edge is at the\ntable''s bottom, its right edge is flush with the table''s, and the range\nsits before the first button. The standard says so too.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>\n\n* feat(prototype): Components follows the list rules, and the side panel stops offering filters nothing reads\n\n**Components**\n- **The catalogue''s search, category, \"Hide SDKs\" and kind are its own**,\n  above the list and in the address (`?q=`, `?f.category=`, `?f.sdk=`,\n  `?f.kind=`). They used to live in the shell''s side panel, one screen away\n  from the list they filtered. A no-match state now has Clear filters.\n- **\"Component and purpose\" and Downloads sort from their headers**, the\n  same way as DataTable''s, into `?sort=`.\n- **The open component is in the address as `?component=`.** Opening one is\n  pushed, so Back closes it and returns to the list with its search and\n  sort. A link opens it directly. Before this, nothing about an open\n  component could be shared, and Back left the section.\n- **Table rows open with Enter and Space**, and a control inside a row no\n  longer opens the row as a side effect.\n\n**The side panel.** Lists that now own their filters (Workspaces and\nProjects, People, Connections, Background work, Components) have nothing\nfor the panel to offer. It says so (\"This list has its own search and\nfilters, above it.\") instead of showing controls nothing reads, and its\nbadge stops counting them. Connections were filtered twice, once by the\npanel''s query and again by the list, and now only by the list.\n\nVerified over CDP against the local stack, on 115 components:\n- The search narrows the list and writes `?q=`.\n- Downloads writes `?sort=downloads`.\n- Opening a row adds `?component=…`.\n- Back returns to the list with the same `?q=` and `?sort=`.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>\n\n* feat(prototype): the admin lists on the one list — members, organizations and identities\n\n**Organizations**\n- **A row opens the organization**, the same as Manage.\n- **Manage and Members are in \"…\".**\n- **The list has its own search**, over name, id and workspace names.\n\n**Members**\n- **Remove asks through the dialog.** It used to use `window.confirm`.\n- **Suspend / Resume** is in \"…\". The last active owner cannot be demoted,\n  suspended or removed, exactly as before.\n- **Standing** is a chip filter, and **Joined** is relative with the full\n  date on hover.\n- **Withdraw asks first.** Withdrawing a pending invitation used to happen\n  on a single click.\n\n**Identity directory**\n- **The list has its own search and an Access chip filter**: Waiting for\n  access / Assigned / Platform admin.\n- **First seen** is relative, and the Assign controls stay inline.\n\n**Across all three**\n- **The shell''s side-panel query is no longer read.**\n- **A failed read shows once**, in the table, with Retry. It used to also\n  show as a page banner. The banner is now only for a failed action on\n  rows that are there.\n\n`DataTable`: while the list failed to load, a chip count reads \"—\"\n(unknown) instead of 0.\n\nVerified over CDP against the local stack:\n- **/admin/tenants** reads \"All organizations · 1\", with the columns\n  Organization | Workspaces | Owners | Members.\n- **/admin/people** lists the 2 members, with the columns Person | Role |\n  Standing | Joined.\n- **/admin/identities**: the stand''s identity directory answers 503. The\n  page shows that error once, with Retry, and the chips read \"—\".\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>\n\n* feat(prototype): Chats, Files and Secrets on the one list — delete asks, Rotate is a form, not a prompt\n\n**Chats**\n- **A row opens the chat.** Open and Delete are in \"…\".\n- **Delete asks first.** It used to delete on a single click.\n- **The model filter is the list''s own select**, fed by the models the gear\n  reports, instead of the side panel''s. The list has its own search.\n- **Messages and Updated sort**, and Updated is relative.\n\n**Files**\n- **The list has its own search.**\n- **A failed read shows once, as a failure.** It used to show as the\n  \"Nothing stored yet\" text.\n\n**Secrets**\n- **Check stays inline.**\n- **Rotate opens a password field under the row.** It used to open\n  `window.prompt`, which showed the new secret value in plain text and\n  could not be styled or dismissed with Escape.\n- **Delete goes through the confirm dialog**, which says what happens to\n  launches. It replaces `window.confirm`.\n- **The ✕ button is gone.** Delete is the menu''s last item, in danger\n  style.\n\nThe side panel says \"This list has its own search and filters, above it.\"\nfor Chats and Files, as it already does for the other migrated sections.\n\nVerified over CDP against the local stack:\n- **Chats** lists \"Portal assistant\" with the Every model select, and the\n  columns Chat | Model | Messages | Updated.\n- **Files** shows the stand''s 400 once, as a failure.\n- **Secrets** shows its empty state, because the stand has no references in\n  its project settings.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>\n\n* feat(prototype): Activity, Kits, System and GTS entities follow the list rules\n\n**Activity**\n- **DataTable.** Checks and Comments are a chip filter instead of a popover\n  of checkboxes that never closed. The list has its own search and a\n  sortable Recorded column.\n- **Recorded is now relative, with the full timestamp on hover**, the same\n  as every other list. This screen was the only one that showed the date\n  and put \"4h ago\" on hover, the reverse of the rest. The full date is still\n  one hover away, and the column sorts.\n\n**Kits** keep their cards, because each kit carries its own install\ncontrols, which a table row would flatten.\n- **Remove asks first**, and says what stays behind: the files already\n  written into the repositories. It used to remove on a single click.\n- **Requested and materialized times** use the one relative format.\n\n**System: Gears, Permissions and GTS entities**\n- **Each is a DataTable with its own address prefix** (`gears.`, `perm.`,\n  `gts.`), because three lists share one page.\n- **The shared pager and sortable headers** replace a 460 px scroll box\n  per table.\n- **Filters are chips or selects.** Gears filter by deployment mode,\n  Permissions by action, and GTS entities by category.\n- **A GTS entity row opens its schema dialog** from a click, Enter or\n  Space. Before, only the mouse could open it.\n\nVerified over CDP against the local stack. System shows \"Permissions ·\n42\", \"Gears · 58\" (1–50 of 58) and \"Registered entities · 312\" (1–50 of\n312), each with its own pager.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>\n\n* feat(prototype): hand-added files are read past the first page and listed on the one list\n\n\"Added by hand\" read the first page of the project''s file nodes and then\nkept only the manual ones. A project with a synced repository has\nthousands of files, so a hand-added file sorted past that page was not\nlisted at all, with nothing to say so. It now reads every page (offset and\ntotal, 200 at a time, up to 20,000) before keeping the manual ones.\n\nThe list is a DataTable under the `files.` prefix. It has its own\nsearch, File and Size sort from their headers, and loading, failed and\nempty are three states. A failed read shows once, with Retry.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>\n\n* feat(prototype): who is in Studio is a DataTable\n\nThe presence list moves onto the one list:\n- It gets a search and sortable Person / Here since / Last seen headers.\n- Its times use the one relative format with the full time on hover.\n- Message stays inline and is still not offered on your own row.\n- A failed read shows once, with Retry. It no longer also shows the error\n  above an empty list.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>\n\n* feat(prototype): Specs keeps its view in the address, opens on a queue with work, and shows one IDE button\n\nThe Specs screen keeps its own rows, with their inline review actions and\nthe detail that unfolds under a row. It now follows the list rules for\nthe rest:\n- **Queue, type, origin, search and page are in the address** (`?f.queue=`,\n  `?f.type=`, `?f.origin=`, `?q=`, `?page=`). A reload, a shared link or\n  Back lands on the same view of the same page. Before, every visit started\n  over on \"Needs review\", page 1.\n- **It opens on a queue with something in it.** Absent a choice, it opens\n  on Needs review when that has work, and on All otherwise. A freshly\n  synced project used to open on an empty \"Needs review\", which read as if\n  the sync had found nothing.\n- **It has a search**, over path, name and type.\n- **Nothing matches** now comes with Clear filters.\n- **One IDE button per row.** A repository row nothing had bound showed two\n  \"IDE ↗\" buttons, one of which opened a document editor for a file that is\n  not a document.\n- **A document written in Studio shows its detail when its tile is picked**\n  in the tiles view. Before, nothing appeared.\n\nVerified over CDP against the local stack, on a project with 2,853 files:\n- It opens on \"Needs review 286\".\n- Every row carries at most one IDE button.\n- \"All\" plus \"readme\" gives `?q=readme&f.queue=all` and \"1–50 of 59\".\n- A reload restores the queue and the search.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","tree":{"sha":"e6f7f3115e4a099a3bb664e1b12cd63a7fab22a1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/trees/e6f7f3115e4a099a3bb664e1b12cd63a7fab22a1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/commits/3b80155c92bbbb62c1c1ac7e8adbd75da01dc862","verification":{"payload":"tree e6f7f3115e4a099a3bb664e1b12cd63a7fab22a1\nparent a5f56ebdbb3145218ceb5d8e289b7cd706250de3\nauthor ANDREI KUCHMA <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech> 1790772994 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790772994 +0200\n\nfeat(prototype): every remaining list on the one list — Workspaces, Components, admin, Chats/Files/Secrets, Activity, Kits, System, Specs (#575)\n\n* feat(prototype): Workspaces on the one list — row opens it, Delete asks through the dialog, the tree is ▸\n\nThe workspaces portfolio moves onto DataTable:\n- **A row click opens the workspace.** Only the name used to.\n- **Open in IDE stays inline.** Open and Delete are in \"…\", and Delete goes\n  through the confirm dialog. The ✕ button and `window.confirm` are gone.\n  The dialog warns that the account system may refuse while the workspace\n  still has projects.\n- **Nested projects expand under the ▸ toggle** and load on first open,\n  each one opening its project.\n- **The list has its own search and a Self-managed / Managed chip filter.**\n  The side panel''s search, self-managed switch and name sort are no longer\n  read here. Workspace and Projects sort from their headers instead.\n- **The heading counts what is shown**: \"Workspaces in Default\n  Organization · 1\".\n\nVerified over CDP against the local stack. The columns read Workspace |\nProjects | People. ▸ lists the three projects under \"Test Worksoace\". The\nmenu reads Open / Delete (danger).\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>\n\n* feat(prototype): the pager sits under the list at its right edge, range first\n\nOne place for it everywhere, the Specs lists included: under the list,\nright-aligned, with \"51–100 of 2,446\" before the page buttons. It used to\nstart at the left edge, where the eye has already moved on to the next\nsection. Measured on the rebuilt bundle: the pager''s top edge is at the\ntable''s bottom, its right edge is flush with the table''s, and the range\nsits before the first button. The standard says so too.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>\n\n* feat(prototype): Components follows the list rules, and the side panel stops offering filters nothing reads\n\n**Components**\n- **The catalogue''s search, category, \"Hide SDKs\" and kind are its own**,\n  above the list and in the address (`?q=`, `?f.category=`, `?f.sdk=`,\n  `?f.kind=`). They used to live in the shell''s side panel, one screen away\n  from the list they filtered. A no-match state now has Clear filters.\n- **\"Component and purpose\" and Downloads sort from their headers**, the\n  same way as DataTable''s, into `?sort=`.\n- **The open component is in the address as `?component=`.** Opening one is\n  pushed, so Back closes it and returns to the list with its search and\n  sort. A link opens it directly. Before this, nothing about an open\n  component could be shared, and Back left the section.\n- **Table rows open with Enter and Space**, and a control inside a row no\n  longer opens the row as a side effect.\n\n**The side panel.** Lists that now own their filters (Workspaces and\nProjects, People, Connections, Background work, Components) have nothing\nfor the panel to offer. It says so (\"This list has its own search and\nfilters, above it.\") instead of showing controls nothing reads, and its\nbadge stops counting them. Connections were filtered twice, once by the\npanel''s query and again by the list, and now only by the list.\n\nVerified over CDP against the local stack, on 115 components:\n- The search narrows the list and writes `?q=`.\n- Downloads writes `?sort=downloads`.\n- Opening a row adds `?component=…`.\n- Back returns to the list with the same `?q=` and `?sort=`.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>\n\n* feat(prototype): the admin lists on the one list — members, organizations and identities\n\n**Organizations**\n- **A row opens the organization**, the same as Manage.\n- **Manage and Members are in \"…\".**\n- **The list has its own search**, over name, id and workspace names.\n\n**Members**\n- **Remove asks through the dialog.** It used to use `window.confirm`.\n- **Suspend / Resume** is in \"…\". The last active owner cannot be demoted,\n  suspended or removed, exactly as before.\n- **Standing** is a chip filter, and **Joined** is relative with the full\n  date on hover.\n- **Withdraw asks first.** Withdrawing a pending invitation used to happen\n  on a single click.\n\n**Identity directory**\n- **The list has its own search and an Access chip filter**: Waiting for\n  access / Assigned / Platform admin.\n- **First seen** is relative, and the Assign controls stay inline.\n\n**Across all three**\n- **The shell''s side-panel query is no longer read.**\n- **A failed read shows once**, in the table, with Retry. It used to also\n  show as a page banner. The banner is now only for a failed action on\n  rows that are there.\n\n`DataTable`: while the list failed to load, a chip count reads \"—\"\n(unknown) instead of 0.\n\nVerified over CDP against the local stack:\n- **/admin/tenants** reads \"All organizations · 1\", with the columns\n  Organization | Workspaces | Owners | Members.\n- **/admin/people** lists the 2 members, with the columns Person | Role |\n  Standing | Joined.\n- **/admin/identities**: the stand''s identity directory answers 503. The\n  page shows that error once, with Retry, and the chips read \"—\".\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>\n\n* feat(prototype): Chats, Files and Secrets on the one list — delete asks, Rotate is a form, not a prompt\n\n**Chats**\n- **A row opens the chat.** Open and Delete are in \"…\".\n- **Delete asks first.** It used to delete on a single click.\n- **The model filter is the list''s own select**, fed by the models the gear\n  reports, instead of the side panel''s. The list has its own search.\n- **Messages and Updated sort**, and Updated is relative.\n\n**Files**\n- **The list has its own search.**\n- **A failed read shows once, as a failure.** It used to show as the\n  \"Nothing stored yet\" text.\n\n**Secrets**\n- **Check stays inline.**\n- **Rotate opens a password field under the row.** It used to open\n  `window.prompt`, which showed the new secret value in plain text and\n  could not be styled or dismissed with Escape.\n- **Delete goes through the confirm dialog**, which says what happens to\n  launches. It replaces `window.confirm`.\n- **The ✕ button is gone.** Delete is the menu''s last item, in danger\n  style.\n\nThe side panel says \"This list has its own search and filters, above it.\"\nfor Chats and Files, as it already does for the other migrated sections.\n\nVerified over CDP against the local stack:\n- **Chats** lists \"Portal assistant\" with the Every model select, and the\n  columns Chat | Model | Messages | Updated.\n- **Files** shows the stand''s 400 once, as a failure.\n- **Secrets** shows its empty state, because the stand has no references in\n  its project settings.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>\n\n* feat(prototype): Activity, Kits, System and GTS entities follow the list rules\n\n**Activity**\n- **DataTable.** Checks and Comments are a chip filter instead of a popover\n  of checkboxes that never closed. The list has its own search and a\n  sortable Recorded column.\n- **Recorded is now relative, with the full timestamp on hover**, the same\n  as every other list. This screen was the only one that showed the date\n  and put \"4h ago\" on hover, the reverse of the rest. The full date is still\n  one hover away, and the column sorts.\n\n**Kits** keep their cards, because each kit carries its own install\ncontrols, which a table row would flatten.\n- **Remove asks first**, and says what stays behind: the files already\n  written into the repositories. It used to remove on a single click.\n- **Requested and materialized times** use the one relative format.\n\n**System: Gears, Permissions and GTS entities**\n- **Each is a DataTable with its own address prefix** (`gears.`, `perm.`,\n  `gts.`), because three lists share one page.\n- **The shared pager and sortable headers** replace a 460 px scroll box\n  per table.\n- **Filters are chips or selects.** Gears filter by deployment mode,\n  Permissions by action, and GTS entities by category.\n- **A GTS entity row opens its schema dialog** from a click, Enter or\n  Space. Before, only the mouse could open it.\n\nVerified over CDP against the local stack. System shows \"Permissions ·\n42\", \"Gears · 58\" (1–50 of 58) and \"Registered entities · 312\" (1–50 of\n312), each with its own pager.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>\n\n* feat(prototype): hand-added files are read past the first page and listed on the one list\n\n\"Added by hand\" read the first page of the project''s file nodes and then\nkept only the manual ones. A project with a synced repository has\nthousands of files, so a hand-added file sorted past that page was not\nlisted at all, with nothing to say so. It now reads every page (offset and\ntotal, 200 at a time, up to 20,000) before keeping the manual ones.\n\nThe list is a DataTable under the `files.` prefix. It has its own\nsearch, File and Size sort from their headers, and loading, failed and\nempty are three states. A failed read shows once, with Retry.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>\n\n* feat(prototype): who is in Studio is a DataTable\n\nThe presence list moves onto the one list:\n- It gets a search and sortable Person / Here since / Last seen headers.\n- Its times use the one relative format with the full time on hover.\n- Message stays inline and is still not offered on your own row.\n- A failed read shows once, with Retry. It no longer also shows the error\n  above an empty list.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>\n\n* feat(prototype): Specs keeps its view in the address, opens on a queue with work, and shows one IDE button\n\nThe Specs screen keeps its own rows, with their inline review actions and\nthe detail that unfolds under a row. It now follows the list rules for\nthe rest:\n- **Queue, type, origin, search and page are in the address** (`?f.queue=`,\n  `?f.type=`, `?f.origin=`, `?q=`, `?page=`). A reload, a shared link or\n  Back lands on the same view of the same page. Before, every visit started\n  over on \"Needs review\", page 1.\n- **It opens on a queue with something in it.** Absent a choice, it opens\n  on Needs review when that has work, and on All otherwise. A freshly\n  synced project used to open on an empty \"Needs review\", which read as if\n  the sync had found nothing.\n- **It has a search**, over path, name and type.\n- **Nothing matches** now comes with Clear filters.\n- **One IDE button per row.** A repository row nothing had bound showed two\n  \"IDE ↗\" buttons, one of which opened a document editor for a file that is\n  not a document.\n- **A document written in Studio shows its detail when its tile is picked**\n  in the tiles view. Before, nothing appeared.\n\nVerified over CDP against the local stack, on a project with 2,853 files:\n- It opens on \"Needs review 286\".\n- Every row carries at most one IDE button.\n- \"All\" plus \"readme\" gives `?q=readme&f.queue=all` and \"1–50 of 59\".\n- A reload restores the queue and the search.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvQcCCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAxrQQAEniymBizX9ps+mWh6d9tFFV\nBaqzQMd4ysEZshoTNEzfJuRX0eRmrjsy/J77USC0BerDXV+02xH1pCw4MWwIQqUK\nfHDgMeTQW2oyDDgC3g4zSUa79fF+xUpwnVxO7xjGofflDLIwan517nevcxjni4w2\nXv4Q0n0A91aLbyWAWua5EhiFo0y0wdQBGbUzzqppcalx+JMglK7r90Wp7DgJi8Ez\nVh+ID9VeO/aSyD0Xk/KsSKH4lxvoeMiPshmyodhahkFlkNCKn87RZrZc8j/+H9TN\nSQCmoUBnsWkXGovjs6I540o2A/dRjte9fr+8nuZ8phGHZtNrevI+BO5wHEzW2sgq\nJQNnoX9w/T7kYT1jBgQCVhVo7zSD4gUDTdrpW9eT5a8uce/Eqs6APUmxV/Bt9a/Q\no+2Gs1nRlI9GQH2BZ8pVkww935+mK/wAT4J9Q6mc7/0nRzxRF7TFPKhbEF0id7/7\n6wHzQtDosqrez+lMbzqa2gJxC+lo2doMccZyhcPQadJoFIib0EA26g3JWt/au66B\nJIg4QHCP+/fj7bJbC2VNxan09Jc8/SFKUBTx76GzT5ZlhDt8vcfXslwJLy2ancpC\nVxPrqferXt1n1dyJUu628BqgaXYnYnCjDyLCYduvZu2u6xLfuQnhz4Envex5+HOE\n4zFXQmrYG7HNE5JVuOhE\n=hHz0\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T12:56:35Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/3b80155c92bbbb62c1c1ac7e8adbd75da01dc862","node_id":"C_kwDOTl7dJtoAKDNiODAxNTVjOTJiYmJiNjJjMWMxYWM3ZThhZGJkNzVkYTAxZGM4NjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/a5f56ebdbb3145218ceb5d8e289b7cd706250de3","sha":"a5f56ebdbb3145218ceb5d8e289b7cd706250de3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/a5f56ebdbb3145218ceb5d8e289b7cd706250de3"}],"sha":"3b80155c92bbbb62c1c1ac7e8adbd75da01dc862","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/3b80155c92bbbb62c1c1ac7e8adbd75da01dc862"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/301748190?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AndrejK666","id":301748190,"login":"AndrejK666","node_id":"U_kgDOEfxP3g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/a5f56ebdbb3145218ceb5d8e289b7cd706250de3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T12:43:58Z","email":"Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech","name":"ANDREI KUCHMA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T12:43:58Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(desktop): the left rail is one toolset in every mode, like VS Code''s (#578)\n\n* feat(desktop): the left rail is one toolset in every mode, like VS Code''s\n\nExplorer, Search, Source Control, Run and Debug, Extensions and Testing,\nthen Collaboration, Quality where a project turns it on, one Assistants\nentry, and the Studio view at the foot. A mode changes its ribbon and its\nstart page, not the rail.\n\n- RAIL replaces the per-mode MODE_VIEWS; the guarantor places it in every\n  mode and never sets it aside, and RAIL_TABS/railTabsCss draw it.\n- One search: Theia''s, and Ctrl+Shift+F opens it in every mode; the\n  product''s Search keeps the ribbon''s Find and the palette.\n- One Assistants entry offering Claude Code and Codex replaces the two\n  vendor buttons.\n- A mode''s own views leave the rail: Orca sits on the right in every mode\n  (Agent development mirrored: Source Control left, agents right), the\n  Gearbox Catalogue has no tab (OFF_RAIL); their ribbons open them.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>\n\n* fix(desktop): the Studio view stays visible at the rail''s foot, and the rail keeps its order\n\nMeasured on the local desktop: the foot tab was hidden as overflowing\n(Theia''s hideOverflowingTabs), the tab list was only as tall as its tabs,\nand Agent development''s first visit put Source Control above Search.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","tree":{"sha":"5e462da0085eebdefb0e5ccdc08b82020b82dc12","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/trees/5e462da0085eebdefb0e5ccdc08b82020b82dc12"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/commits/a5f56ebdbb3145218ceb5d8e289b7cd706250de3","verification":{"payload":"tree 5e462da0085eebdefb0e5ccdc08b82020b82dc12\nparent c2f366a12e0d8a289b2e0444a44fef9378193ad1\nauthor ANDREI KUCHMA <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech> 1790772238 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790772238 +0200\n\nfeat(desktop): the left rail is one toolset in every mode, like VS Code''s (#578)\n\n* feat(desktop): the left rail is one toolset in every mode, like VS Code''s\n\nExplorer, Search, Source Control, Run and Debug, Extensions and Testing,\nthen Collaboration, Quality where a project turns it on, one Assistants\nentry, and the Studio view at the foot. A mode changes its ribbon and its\nstart page, not the rail.\n\n- RAIL replaces the per-mode MODE_VIEWS; the guarantor places it in every\n  mode and never sets it aside, and RAIL_TABS/railTabsCss draw it.\n- One search: Theia''s, and Ctrl+Shift+F opens it in every mode; the\n  product''s Search keeps the ribbon''s Find and the palette.\n- One Assistants entry offering Claude Code and Codex replaces the two\n  vendor buttons.\n- A mode''s own views leave the rail: Orca sits on the right in every mode\n  (Agent development mirrored: Source Control left, agents right), the\n  Gearbox Catalogue has no tab (OFF_RAIL); their ribbons open them.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>\n\n* fix(desktop): the Studio view stays visible at the rail''s foot, and the rail keeps its order\n\nMeasured on the local desktop: the foot tab was hidden as overflowing\n(Theia''s hideOverflowingTabs), the tab list was only as tall as its tabs,\nand Agent development''s first visit put Source Control above Search.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvQQOCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAbCEQAElXdSJ3tVeD9U9XGd8aqMVT\nk4RmenCiEthzskPU/LE4WiUrY1OZ1+HyCFXgx6qYDqgstqiy7i2l1oHg+PXbkUPX\n1cuvdlTm2bdxPRtSOQCl+i5ySXpHokaPPTdrZmG+3VrBAwaRnGPTAY57aVnSdu2b\n0u8MDOOLDsQ0K9Hi1m++G7XexEs2q0Mvl+vUkQwI3MUYPmMSJh4xwW3RG3driQ39\nuZT15zIootqCMny09nMmaB/4QcX6LXVTryFOEkihTgi5Yk8l7Fjo2KmyDTlqwQWl\niWaBcU/WFKsWXHNxAIoqN4mRLO6QMRgbtGgVE9/hOSLM/KXqJfGLwUw86SrlnJr3\niucnXxaUkrzrOfn7/BMw/+dheM2G2qp/jVA4JSrQPb8oYgGRiP25FaxN42SnNBew\nXDQkxoA144g5Uga3xoXvOBPVIX0OfAPHPLThldIAWe6Zr51YxzCTZ7FBkCB+UYUI\njGHr7Nsq6PhwlwI1q6ePbN4brt3aYSvMkNv6mhQBVnZ1MnIXgfUO/ZnS4F8OQo46\nzLVGSVCxT+RD6EAVsOewO366bWDCg6dbw4MXIdr39VL50A8AnXmp+xuX9oBi1OQU\nWhItSHi3+twI+ev0pJ9gex0IhP79fPxOwYK0VRaQkXGTiaIa2yG+O9ZCrvPWkMZR\nYWWI1kAEnJCc1t6BEo59\n=933+\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T12:43:59Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/a5f56ebdbb3145218ceb5d8e289b7cd706250de3","node_id":"C_kwDOTl7dJtoAKGE1ZjU2ZWJkYmIzMTQ1MjE4Y2ViNWQ4ZTI4OWI3Y2Q3MDYyNTBkZTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/c2f366a12e0d8a289b2e0444a44fef9378193ad1","sha":"c2f366a12e0d8a289b2e0444a44fef9378193ad1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/c2f366a12e0d8a289b2e0444a44fef9378193ad1"}],"sha":"a5f56ebdbb3145218ceb5d8e289b7cd706250de3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/a5f56ebdbb3145218ceb5d8e289b7cd706250de3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/301748190?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AndrejK666","id":301748190,"login":"AndrejK666","node_id":"U_kgDOEfxP3g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/c2f366a12e0d8a289b2e0444a44fef9378193ad1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T12:37:23Z","email":"Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech","name":"ANDREI KUCHMA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T12:37:23Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(prototype): Background work and Connections on the one list (stacked on #573) (#574)\n\n* feat(prototype): Background work on the one list — every run reachable, paged by the backend\n\nRuns asked for `limit=200` and showed whatever came back, so the list was\nsilently cut. On the local stack that was 200 of 2,245 runs. It now pages\nthrough studio-tasks'' own `offset/limit/total`, and the pager reads\n\"1–50 of 2,245\".\n\n- **State and task type go to the backend** and live in the address\n  (`?f.state=`, `?f.type=`). The state chips used to count only the 200\n  rows already fetched, and those rows were already filtered by the server,\n  so every count was wrong. The server does not count per state, so the\n  chips carry no count (\"—\") rather than a wrong one.\n- **No text search.** The backend has none, and searching one page of 2,245\n  would have told nobody anything. The shell''s side-panel query is no\n  longer read here.\n- **Details open from the ▸ toggle.** Cancel is in the \"…\" menu, asks first,\n  and says what a cooperative stop does and does not do. Retry is there for\n  failed and cancelled runs.\n- **Live refresh still works.** studio-events reloads the page on screen,\n  and a 4 s poll runs while that page has queued or running work\n  (`onLoaded`). It no longer re-reads 200 runs every 4 seconds.\n- **Schedules is a list of its own, under `sch.` in the address.** Next and\n  Last are relative with the full time on hover, and Run now is inline.\n\n`DataTable` gains `onLoaded`, which tells a screen each page as it arrives.\nA background reload keeps the rows on screen and clears a previous error\nonly when it succeeds.\n\nVerified over CDP against the local stack. The page reads \"Runs · 2,245\",\nand the first request is `limit=50`. The succeeded chip gives\n`?f.state=succeeded` and requests `state=succeeded&limit=50`. The ▸ toggle\nexpands the run''s details.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>\n\n* feat(prototype): Connections on the one list — one table, its own search, Remove asks through the dialog\n\nConnections were a table per category, filtered by provider chips that\nsat above all of the tables at once. They are now one DataTable:\n- **Kind** (the category) is a column and a chip filter, and the connector\n  is a select filter.\n- **The list has its own search**, over label, account, URL and connector.\n- **The state is in the address, under `conn.`.**\n\nWhat each row does:\n- **Test stays inline**, as the row''s primary action.\n- **Edit and Browse repositories are in \"…\"**, and each opens its panel\n  under the row. For that, `DataTable` gains `detail(row)`, a panel the\n  screen opens from an action, beside the ▸ `expand`.\n- **Edit is disabled for inherited connections**, which are edited where\n  they are defined.\n- **Remove asks through the confirm dialog** instead of `window.confirm`. For\n  a connection shared with the other projects, the dialog says that\n  removing it removes it there too, token included.\n\nVerified over CDP against the local stack. The columns read Connector |\nKind | Account | Label | URL | Health | Scope. The menu is Edit / Browse\nrepositories / Remove (danger), and the editor opens as a panel under its\nrow.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","tree":{"sha":"ee6e8f406c7954575863239dbe6dd89323d94f10","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/trees/ee6e8f406c7954575863239dbe6dd89323d94f10"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/commits/c2f366a12e0d8a289b2e0444a44fef9378193ad1","verification":{"payload":"tree ee6e8f406c7954575863239dbe6dd89323d94f10\nparent c29a77e6553bae3a152da52f1c39a6343758dffe\nauthor ANDREI KUCHMA <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech> 1790771843 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790771843 +0200\n\nfeat(prototype): Background work and Connections on the one list (stacked on #573) (#574)\n\n* feat(prototype): Background work on the one list — every run reachable, paged by the backend\n\nRuns asked for `limit=200` and showed whatever came back, so the list was\nsilently cut. On the local stack that was 200 of 2,245 runs. It now pages\nthrough studio-tasks'' own `offset/limit/total`, and the pager reads\n\"1–50 of 2,245\".\n\n- **State and task type go to the backend** and live in the address\n  (`?f.state=`, `?f.type=`). The state chips used to count only the 200\n  rows already fetched, and those rows were already filtered by the server,\n  so every count was wrong. The server does not count per state, so the\n  chips carry no count (\"—\") rather than a wrong one.\n- **No text search.** The backend has none, and searching one page of 2,245\n  would have told nobody anything. The shell''s side-panel query is no\n  longer read here.\n- **Details open from the ▸ toggle.** Cancel is in the \"…\" menu, asks first,\n  and says what a cooperative stop does and does not do. Retry is there for\n  failed and cancelled runs.\n- **Live refresh still works.** studio-events reloads the page on screen,\n  and a 4 s poll runs while that page has queued or running work\n  (`onLoaded`). It no longer re-reads 200 runs every 4 seconds.\n- **Schedules is a list of its own, under `sch.` in the address.** Next and\n  Last are relative with the full time on hover, and Run now is inline.\n\n`DataTable` gains `onLoaded`, which tells a screen each page as it arrives.\nA background reload keeps the rows on screen and clears a previous error\nonly when it succeeds.\n\nVerified over CDP against the local stack. The page reads \"Runs · 2,245\",\nand the first request is `limit=50`. The succeeded chip gives\n`?f.state=succeeded` and requests `state=succeeded&limit=50`. The ▸ toggle\nexpands the run''s details.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>\n\n* feat(prototype): Connections on the one list — one table, its own search, Remove asks through the dialog\n\nConnections were a table per category, filtered by provider chips that\nsat above all of the tables at once. They are now one DataTable:\n- **Kind** (the category) is a column and a chip filter, and the connector\n  is a select filter.\n- **The list has its own search**, over label, account, URL and connector.\n- **The state is in the address, under `conn.`.**\n\nWhat each row does:\n- **Test stays inline**, as the row''s primary action.\n- **Edit and Browse repositories are in \"…\"**, and each opens its panel\n  under the row. For that, `DataTable` gains `detail(row)`, a panel the\n  screen opens from an action, beside the ▸ `expand`.\n- **Edit is disabled for inherited connections**, which are edited where\n  they are defined.\n- **Remove asks through the confirm dialog** instead of `window.confirm`. For\n  a connection shared with the other projects, the dialog says that\n  removing it removes it there too, token included.\n\nVerified over CDP against the local stack. The columns read Connector |\nKind | Account | Label | URL | Health | Scope. The menu is Edit / Browse\nrepositories / Remove (danger), and the editor opens as a panel under its\nrow.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvQKDCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAloMQAGCO3bjDdvIPaQ5+8bxIaOXD\ntf3AP7mJIs3wnx23OGuUyomnsR6ryrugjkQFqPta5XZk8gTn5hZdoHpYWmL+xSMh\nBWWWDIhRM5brGJU0eqNTymjJRHK4Kgb+yPgnQHmipIFp9YmzpI3L+8snu+7qjBVV\nlFNNC9GO68W1ObTHfaMRcvokobO2y28cG54CO0b8yeAPlAVoAyRfkshzFdx9w8Gl\nOV0Ts4rNDBKXza01xZmEgNS6IDX36n0o1u2UjPIj+QVEjugEZQKEX1ulRt7fCsAF\nOeHi2je+iaiDH0Jv/VlVfzPb8n/GHhg1LuWS2eulr3Xwn2L3TbiEzGhyuFqs/CMm\ni7L44lQzBRLuWOpsLHtM2K6x21UUspVcsY9lk6a5RJrI0jH1WyzOwXhbwNtdnfzC\n6f9P7qzE1ZiYag8DESR5vxfQhZv6jk9lGcPdPTanmaMbptjrwgnuUAitrZB+ozFN\n1rf1vCkcEQyo1RE1euVwQiErNwm5ScgpSZq9iumVoXI11fs/pW6wwQPH7oDWsFeG\nKtOd520fc2GfipIEPQXHRh/DXj3jrG4cqh6JPJqXj45RdPTIgP+Er5wEgz70rnHt\nHICY2C5mP4ALvKbVjJ65+1yFrFR1HPQlXy3BJG4P6BopdPxGA0aOIYpgGcd4Sj2w\nKd4bMScV+dk5ReVzD4WI\n=6ZDn\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T12:37:28Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/use