le Studio backend is said so, with Retry, instead of \"No gear.gdl\" (#558)\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvMiLCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAsCkQAEpQ9Duz5Ccal4kjO7qCq5Uf\nSLuMV8GdhJyD4q9P2QQdJAR1cClcwa22ekTLo5f/hEUvJFiz0DCx02SGNyowo2qn\nKU9zP5rRON23vI+pwMVPu9VEiC7K8Z/nqlNVLlDCXXQf2ogXJ6/RAspQk0Lxv3qH\n6SQcuNfQMB8aIb8shTI52b7Joqh5MXrL8R4RjimYlysTfd5/BdEvJDjsxertnx+a\nsambPnhkrXqeoL07jCxu5p6dTXGQywYiUrpn76GGkTLkLcq4lj9Be/sjsbcXVLbs\nYUeSzP1yUAMNTdUi1lIu3hyQN9mAvrsPusQ58x4dqNz2x1sFTqK0hDp77BsCZ3m4\n61C77LNpuy3r52+pzAXUyVTOpNprs6Fh4fpJQSenr/FxPBDxppwxCCn0qMBEK88P\nllKq09TrvxKlfAKVdSowS2NZIjQMtkLfAz9rG+H+FS7bfNsjeHkosiSGIehJM9fc\nxhMY32/eCIrBWRiuPa1xXnNAclSosvdLMvlwMVYOUw6FHTOVVDjrRuLcf1DZxNa7\nljlE24Zxbom8IWS35uCqvHueOCXK6EK5TCYWcRb/avdopxUvPeT8No2bTbIQap1c\nMRDIJ6vMPnU6QQhYl7uFRcw3EvuwskPKgH6gltGYFcG4j38ebpTouIQWf4LTca4X\nuL8kkmSO1h4AIxNlpfdw\n=15/l\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T08:30:04Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/f9950d053226ddf74349b90a98524229e7025a19","node_id":"C_kwDOTl7dJtoAKGY5OTUwZDA1MzIyNmRkZjc0MzQ5YjkwYTk4NTI0MjI5ZTcwMjVhMTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/365af3c71a2b45f93eccaa181121b946a584ccae","sha":"365af3c71a2b45f93eccaa181121b946a584ccae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/365af3c71a2b45f93eccaa181121b946a584ccae"}],"sha":"f9950d053226ddf74349b90a98524229e7025a19","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/f9950d053226ddf74349b90a98524229e7025a19"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/301748190?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AndrejK666","id":301748190,"login":"AndrejK666","node_id":"U_kgDOEfxP3g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/365af3c71a2b45f93eccaa181121b946a584ccae/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T07:54:45Z","email":"Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech","name":"ANDREI KUCHMA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T07:54:45Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(artifact-ingest): a detached or re-attached repository stops listing its files twice (#556)\n\nOn studio-dev the Specs tab listed every file of studio-web three times,\nthe Spec pipeline named each document three times, and Sources said \"Last\nsync: never\" for a repository synced minutes earlier.\n\nThe graph keys a repository and everything synced from it by attachment\nscope, connection (`secret_ref`) and path. A sync only ever adds, and\nDetach only edited the workspace settings. So each attachment the project\never had kept its whole node set: the fork attached once\n(AndrejK666/studio-web), and studio-web attached twice through two\nconnections. Specs, pipeline and Sources dedupe by node id only, so all\nthree copies showed, and Sources read \"Last sync\" off whichever repo node\nit found first.\n\n- `POST /studio-artifact-ingest/v1/reconcile` forgets every repository\n  synced into one attachment scope that is not in `keep`. That covers its\n  issues, pull requests, files, comments and commits, and the bindings of\n  its files. It reuses #403''s machinery: bindings go first, then file\n  content, then the nodes. `delete_nodes` retires rather than tombstones,\n  so a repository detached and attached again syncs over the same keys.\n  The scope is matched exactly, so a workspace-level call never reaches\n  into its projects. A call with no scope is refused.\n- After every sync, the same repository synced into the same scope through\n  another connection is forgotten. Re-attaching through a new connection\n  no longer leaves the old copy standing. The step is best-effort, like\n  #403''s prune.\n- The prototype calls reconcile on Detach, and before a sync with the\n  current repository list, which also cleans up an environment that\n  already has leftovers. It skips the call when any attached repository\n  cannot name its graph (no token, unsupported URL). Sources and Overview\n  match a repository node by connection and path, not path alone.\n- Overview: the Specs card counts what the pipeline counts, authored and\n  bound alike, instead of saying \"none yet\" next to 118 bound documents.\n  The Team card''s subtitle names the team instead of the installed kits.\n\nVerified on a standalone backend with the graph gear. Two real GitHub\nrepositories were synced through two connections, re-attached through the\nother connection, detached, attached again through the same connection\n(which a tombstoning delete would make fail for good), and switched back.\nEach step left exactly one copy of each attached repository, and bindings\nfollowed. Four unit tests cover the same cases against the in-memory\nstore.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","tree":{"sha":"e1657dd433f2a5cf56504fbd5f7709e328853c8f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/trees/e1657dd433f2a5cf56504fbd5f7709e328853c8f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/commits/365af3c71a2b45f93eccaa181121b946a584ccae","verification":{"payload":"tree e1657dd433f2a5cf56504fbd5f7709e328853c8f\nparent ee0191eb4856dd16e3450f9769feb2331b39bbb2\nauthor ANDREI KUCHMA <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech> 1790754885 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790754885 +0200\n\nfix(artifact-ingest): a detached or re-attached repository stops listing its files twice (#556)\n\nOn studio-dev the Specs tab listed every file of studio-web three times,\nthe Spec pipeline named each document three times, and Sources said \"Last\nsync: never\" for a repository synced minutes earlier.\n\nThe graph keys a repository and everything synced from it by attachment\nscope, connection (`secret_ref`) and path. A sync only ever adds, and\nDetach only edited the workspace settings. So each attachment the project\never had kept its whole node set: the fork attached once\n(AndrejK666/studio-web), and studio-web attached twice through two\nconnections. Specs, pipeline and Sources dedupe by node id only, so all\nthree copies showed, and Sources read \"Last sync\" off whichever repo node\nit found first.\n\n- `POST /studio-artifact-ingest/v1/reconcile` forgets every repository\n  synced into one attachment scope that is not in `keep`. That covers its\n  issues, pull requests, files, comments and commits, and the bindings of\n  its files. It reuses #403''s machinery: bindings go first, then file\n  content, then the nodes. `delete_nodes` retires rather than tombstones,\n  so a repository detached and attached again syncs over the same keys.\n  The scope is matched exactly, so a workspace-level call never reaches\n  into its projects. A call with no scope is refused.\n- After every sync, the same repository synced into the same scope through\n  another connection is forgotten. Re-attaching through a new connection\n  no longer leaves the old copy standing. The step is best-effort, like\n  #403''s prune.\n- The prototype calls reconcile on Detach, and before a sync with the\n  current repository list, which also cleans up an environment that\n  already has leftovers. It skips the call when any attached repository\n  cannot name its graph (no token, unsupported URL). Sources and Overview\n  match a repository node by connection and path, not path alone.\n- Overview: the Specs card counts what the pipeline counts, authored and\n  bound alike, instead of saying \"none yet\" next to 118 bound documents.\n  The Team card''s subtitle names the team instead of the installed kits.\n\nVerified on a standalone backend with the graph gear. Two real GitHub\nrepositories were synced through two connections, re-attached through the\nother connection, detached, attached again through the same connection\n(which a tombstoning delete would make fail for good), and switched back.\nEach step left exactly one copy of each attached repository, and bindings\nfollowed. Four unit tests cover the same cases against the in-memory\nstore.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvMBFCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAkoIQAJjL7sCxfeY4y8H4Kn4BEdbB\n29yVfC6wIilSmP8a+Ov2Uj5IuAgZJYPTGe/IjH2rU68oEDpa2/AyAXUOTy+OriFR\nmq0v06z5+U7G0ty3svbIYk0ye1zXZoOZzTdWr1ExlyJzrzBkSGNBBQ5QxgLCy96k\nifszgp1eiWf95gCKm+Xg3Jw0vGwVRL0x6uQ/pWP2YkjxZCWeihDqgjT+mywSxoQw\neaB65O3Jv2QUwvLdV5cqnL0M3KNGcHBaAOMugzF7lXNoiIoaCJIRAHCKEe3A9b0H\nnRSkedzgO/aEn6anjouZdqlB7b4zYJobTJauJ8q7T//vVu/cL0w1N5K7Q5ahNqtk\nCY9AKDqzWu98RgyqmiaNDmcoAjF9mKP58GnLdVqGuyvdBPA55VnOzk/RrLSTYpS4\n2xFF+drKLalXmB3M0B5VVX55GN10T41l0gClZCB6wYiQKgA/ZI8VtSJGVv4rIVfE\n7IHvB7LtbgSwjMTpcq0SvfRHMv9UpBiX++s8rsN+FMPjRXR/s7j+vc3LSAyqMcaV\nSGzDD5hjXdx9He9r6v6sNEo3F7BwKB5T4+Xwa7P4CZ1T1TSvDGEsSmwfO7YC+HmB\npwrMYsB0d+LD6Hju9pFWjUsKFAKLlHH6Lb6JfMxH/zf+hvcFQBXkL6TVJOWRCy/R\niPQGvpGQMCeC6SPaoP0X\n=QBut\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T07:54:46Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/constructorfabric/studio-web/commit/365af3c71a2b45f93eccaa181121b946a584ccae","node_id":"C_kwDOTl7dJtoAKDM2NWFmM2M3MWEyYjQ1ZjkzZWNjYWExODExMjFiOTQ2YTU4NGNjYWU"