 rails, the right panel''s width rule, and\nthe release note.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>\n\n* fix(desktop): Doc editing reaches a commit — Analyze sees the document, Changes and New document on the ribbon\n\n- Analyze: the product''s Markdown editor (product-ext MarkdownEditorWidget)\n  is neither a TextEditor nor a Saveable, so the panel said \"No active\n  document\" with a spec open. The widget now offers readDocumentText() and\n  onDocumentTextChanged(); the controller reads it as a StudioDocumentWidget,\n  unsaved edits included.\n- Doc editing ribbon: a Document group (New document) and a Git group\n  (Changes -> Source Control, Pushes & PRs where registered).\n- File: New document at the top of the \"new\" group. New/Open Product and\n  New/Open Gear only in Building (gearbox.*) and Full (studio.full), keyed on\n  Theia''s activePerspectiveId context key.\n- Traceability: the desktop proxy''s signed-out 503 carries reason\n  \"signed-out\"; StudioApi.fetchAllPages throws StudioApiError with it, and\n  the graph says to sign in instead of \"Failed to load: HTTP 503\" above a\n  \"no ingested artifacts\" hint.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>\n\n* fix(desktop): Push in the ribbon, Sync as git, and Sources lists the clones\n\nThe ribbon''s \"Pushes & PRs\" (Development, Agent development, Full) named\nstudio.git-operations:toggle. Nothing has registered it since #304 folded Git\nOperations into the Operations panel, so ribbonAction dropped the button on\nevery host and the desktop had no push but Source Control''s own menu.\n\nSync on the desktop ran the session''s canonical-config sync and always failed\nwith \"Workspace sync is unavailable until a valid canonical config is active\".\nThe rejection was reported twice. Sources showed \"Missing canonical config\",\nCreate Config and Edit Raw TOML for a folder that has no TOML: a desktop\nproject is a folder of clones of the repositories set in the project''s\nsettings in Studio (workspace.settings repos[]).\n\nNow, on the desktop only:\n- Push (the ribbon''s GIT_OPS, studio.desktop.git:push) pushes the current\n  branch of the clone Source Control selected, else the only one, else the one\n  picked. A new branch gets its upstream on origin. When the host prints a\n  pull-request link, the notification offers \"Open pull request\".\n- Sync fetches every clone and fast-forwards the ones that are only behind. A\n  diverged branch is left alone and reported. One notification, and the\n  command never rejects, so the ribbon does not add a second.\n- Sources lists the clones: branch, what there is to push and pull,\n  uncommitted files, the remote without credentials. It has Sync and Push.\n\nnode/desktop-git.ts runs git behind /studio-desktop/git/{repositories,sync,push}.\nThose routes are mounted only when a Studio is configured, like the rest of\n/studio-desktop/*. The frontend pieces are bound by the electron frontend\nmodule only. The Sources controller and widget are rebound there, and each\nfalls back to the session''s behaviour when studio-desktop/status is not\nenabled. A session keeps its Sync, Sources and Operations panel, and gets no\nribbon Push, as before.\n\nWhy not restore the Git Operations view: its queue is the session''s autosave\njournal (StudioRuntime), which a desktop does not feed. It would be an empty\npanel there. A session already reaches it as View > Operations.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>\n\n* fix(theia): a top-level menu with nothing to show is hidden\n\nWith no product open, Building showed a Gearbox menu that opened as an empty\nbox. Every entry in it waits for gearbox.context == ''product''. menus.ts\nexpected Theia to omit such a submenu, but Theia 1.75''s menu bar adds every\nlabelled top-level node (BrowserMainMenuFactory.fillMenuBar), empty or not.\n\nThe mode bar already hides the menus a mode does not keep. It now also hides\nthe ones whose entries are all hidden right now, asking Theia''s own\nCompoundMenuNode.isEmpty with the context keys. It checks again when a context\nkey changes, so the Gearbox menu comes back when a product opens. This is\nshared with the session, where an empty top-level menu is just as useless.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>\n\n* fix(theia): the collaboration strip names other people, not you\n\nThe project roster (collab-registry everyone()) includes this window''s own\nauthor. The strip read it as company. Alone and signed out, it said \"You is\nhere\", because \"You\" is identity.js''s placeholder name. With two colleagues it\nsaid \"3 others here\".\n\ncollab-scan''s presenceText leaves out the current identity. A colleague who\nnever set a name also arrives as \"You\", so the strip calls them \"Somebody\".\nThe collaboration panel''s roster is unchanged. Shared with the session, where\nthe same miscount happened.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>\n\n* fix(desktop): Push stays enabled while its notification is open\n\nThe live check found the ribbon''s Push greyed out after a push whose\nnotification offered \"Open pull request\". reportPush awaited the\nnotification''s answer, which arrives only when the notification closes, and\nPush counted itself as running until then. The answer is now handled on its\nown, and Push is enabled again as soon as git returns.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>\n\n* fix(desktop): Doc editing keeps a Source Control tab\n\nThe ribbon''s Changes opens Source Control from Doc editing, and without the\nview among the mode''s rails it took the side bar with no icon to come back\nto it. MODE_VIEWS names it for Doc editing, so the tab shows and the view is\nnot set aside on entering the mode.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>\n\n* fix(desktop): the code modes'' Explorer shows every file, and a toggle is kept per mode\n\nDevelopment, Full, Agent development and Building open the Explorer on all\nfiles (src/ included); Doc editing keeps the document list titled by H1.\nThe Explorer toggle is stored per perspective (studio.explorer.mode.<id>).\nShared with the portal session, whose Workbench is the same mode.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>\n\n* fix(desktop): the code modes keep branch, Problems and the bell in the status bar\n\nThe product hid every Theia status entry in every mode. The code modes now\nname the few they need back (scm.*, problem-marker-status, notifications,\nprogress, connection status, bottom-panel toggle, cursor position), keyed by\nbody[data-studio-perspective]; Doc editing keeps the quiet line.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>\n\n* docs(desktop): the Explorer and the status bar per mode\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>\n\n* fix(desktop): Files shown is applied once, so \"every file\" shows the sources\n\nproduct-ext patched the navigator filter with the project''s Files shown in\nevery presentation, on top of the studio Explorer filter that already applies\nit in the documents presentation. In a code mode src/ was listed and empty.\nThe studio filter now says it applies Files shown (appliesFilesShown) and the\npatch steps aside for it; a build without the studio extension is unchanged.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>\n\n* docs(desktop): Files shown is applied by the Explorer''s own filter\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvKwpCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAGW8QAImgT0qT/hTtORM6Po+5kerm\nn0aOhj99X0uyH4YTtYsVsN3O06qZaXw2GwKQpk1EIALcCr3MbXXIgde4QpQxfIvo\nWCMHNRPaWGSa1ATYzhiImxSzEjFAP/b6fs+co6B+xG6qBrBIL24pmGYStHAud9GS\nVZ7TWC6PKnI+5TW49rOuYXNpn1VSwpFZwnmAs9NZpEGfctY