uctorfabric/studio-web/commit/789c3ed76ec625436ef4aa3fb52aaa6c017598be","sha":"789c3ed76ec625436ef4aa3fb52aaa6c017598be","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/789c3ed76ec625436ef4aa3fb52aaa6c017598be"}],"sha":"8474dfa8ccb31f08a6ea84b891af2f11a451a443","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/8474dfa8ccb31f08a6ea84b891af2f11a451a443"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/301748190?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AndrejK666","id":301748190,"login":"AndrejK666","node_id":"U_kgDOEfxP3g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrejK666","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/commits/789c3ed76ec625436ef4aa3fb52aaa6c017598be/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T20:46:39Z","email":"Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech","name":"ANDREI KUCHMA"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T20:46:39Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(prototype): a Review column — the check to look at first, and missing data told apart (#546)\n\nThe Components table gets a Review column: the first check of the\nquality grade to look at, \"N to review · M without data\", and, opened in\nplace, each failed check with what to do. A check that failed on an\nanswer (work on the component) comes before one that failed for want of\none (data to connect or record).\n\nThe grade counted both as failed -- unknown fails -- and said nothing\nelse. Each part now carries `known`: whether its field had an answer, or\nits derived input could be worked out. The grade itself is unchanged.\nThe gear page''s quality panel marks an unanswered check amber with\n\"No data\", instead of red like a failure.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","tree":{"sha":"a67a42d567b5d8a91b524bd7c1e930ef72b04efc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/trees/a67a42d567b5d8a91b524bd7c1e930ef72b04efc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/constructorfabric/studio-web/git/commits/789c3ed76ec625436ef4aa3fb52aaa6c017598be","verification":{"payload":"tree a67a42d567b5d8a91b524bd7c1e930ef72b04efc\nparent ffcb53b472096850b1595363584fef820ecb3da1\nauthor ANDREI KUCHMA <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech> 1790714799 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790714799 +0200\n\nfeat(prototype): a Review column — the check to look at first, and missing data told apart (#546)\n\nThe Components table gets a Review column: the first check of the\nquality grade to look at, \"N to review · M without data\", and, opened in\nplace, each failed check with what to do. A check that failed on an\nanswer (work on the component) comes before one that failed for want of\none (data to connect or record).\n\nThe grade counted both as failed -- unknown fails -- and said nothing\nelse. Each part now carries `known`: whether its field had an answer, or\nits derived input could be worked out. The grade itself is unchanged.\nThe gear page''s quality panel marks an unanswered check amber with\n\"No data\", instead of red like a failure.\n\nSigned-off-by: Andrej Kuchma <Andrej.Kuchma@constructor.tech>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvCOvCRC1a