-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-20T07:01:19Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Prem-Duvvapu/lld-with-ui/commit/c62e0313925bc9355b4727c4d0aca17198b6077d","node_id":"C_kwDOTmX-H9oAKGM2MmUwMzEzOTI1YmM5MzU1YjQ3MjdjNGQwYWNhMTcxOThiNjA3N2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Prem-Duvvapu/lld-with-ui/commit/00b16a6709fd286146276ceeaed83e6a36695d49","sha":"00b16a6709fd286146276ceeaed83e6a36695d49","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Prem-Duvvapu/lld-with-ui/commits/00b16a6709fd286146276ceeaed83e6a36695d49"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/Prem-Duvvapu/lld-with-ui/commit/a70bbe90b4f7327b378534867f37397e5093a143","sha":"a70bbe90b4f7327b378534867f37397e5093a143","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Prem-Duvvapu/lld-with-ui/commits/a70bbe90b4f7327b378534867f37397e5093a143"}],"sha":"c62e0313925bc9355b4727c4d0aca17198b6077d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Prem-Duvvapu/lld-with-ui/commits/c62e0313925bc9355b4727c4d0aca17198b6077d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Prem-Duvvapu/lld-with-ui/commits/a70bbe90b4f7327b378534867f37397e5093a143/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-19T12:14:48Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-19T12:14:48Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"fix(mobile): finish the airline seat-map and linkedin overflow follow-up\n\nBoth were flagged as \"needs a real redesign\" in the previous PR, but\nturned out to be the same bare-fr grid-track trap already fixed\nelsewhere, just with plain ''NfR Mfr'' declarations instead of a fixed\npx or minmax() column -- a bare `fr` track''s minimum size still\ndefaults to `auto` (its content''s min-content width), so `1fr 2fr`\nis exactly as unresponsive as `1fr 340px` once a child is wide enough.\n\n- Airline: the flight-list + seat-map two-column grid\n  (gridTemplateColumns: ''1fr 2fr'') and the simulation tab''s cabin\n  visualizer grid (''1fr 1fr'') both get .responsive-two-col-grid. Once\n  collapsed to one column, the seat grid itself (repeat(6, 44px) =\n  304px) already fits at 390px on its own -- no redesign needed after\n  all. Also added flexWrap to the flight-search form row, which was\n  a second, independent overflow source once the grid stopped hiding it.\n- LinkedIn: the profile+network tab grid (''1fr 2fr'', which is also\n  where the \"Discover & Search Professionals\" panel that looked\n  unrelated actually lives -- it''s just a nested section of the same\n  grid) and the messaging tab''s contacts+thread grid (''1fr 2fr'') both\n  get the same class.\n\nVerified with the same Playwright/scrollWidth methodology as the\nprevious PR across both pages'' every tab, plus a full re-sweep of\nthe 9 other pages already fixed to confirm no regression.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01J45fJ5ygqtgkKRiKD8JdfD","tree":{"sha":"52047d54ae5a20708a3466ef3abd09b5948673cf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Prem-Duvvapu/lld-with-ui/git/trees/52047d54ae5a20708a3466ef3abd09b5948673cf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Prem-Duvvapu/lld-with-ui/git/commits/a70bbe90b4f7327b378534867f37397e5093a143","verification":{"payload":"tree 52047d54ae5a20708a3466ef3abd09b5948673cf\nparent 00b16a6709fd286146276ceeaed83e6a36695d49\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789820088 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789820088 +0000\n\nfix(mobile): finish the airline seat-map and linkedin overflow follow-up\n\nBoth were flagged as \"needs a real redesign\" in the previous PR, but\nturned out to be the same bare-fr grid-track trap already fixed\nelsewhere, just with plain ''NfR Mfr'' declarations instead of a fixed\npx or minmax() column -- a bare `fr` track''s minimum size still\ndefaults to `auto` (its content''s min-content width), so `1fr 2fr`\nis exactly as unresponsive as `1fr 340px` once a child is wide enough.\n\n- Airline: the flight-list + seat-map two-column grid\n  (gridTemplateColumns: ''1fr 2fr'') and the simulation tab''s cabin\n  visualizer grid (''1fr 1fr'') both get .responsive-two-col-grid. Once\n  collapsed to one column, the seat grid itself (repeat(6, 44px) =\n  304px) already fits at 390px on its own -- no redesign needed after\n  all. Also added flexWrap to the flight-search form row, which was\n  a second, independent overflow source once the grid stopped hiding it.\n- LinkedIn: the profile+network tab grid (''1fr 2fr'', which is also\n  where the \"Discover & Search Professionals\" panel that looked\n  unrelated actually lives -- it''s just a nested section of the same\n  grid) and the messaging tab''s contacts+thread grid (''1fr 2fr'') both\n  get the same class.\n\nVerified with the same Playwright/scrollWidth methodology as the\nprevious PR across both pages'' every tab, plus a full re-sweep of\nthe 9 other pages already fixed to confirm no regression.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01J45fJ5ygqtgkKRiKD8JdfD\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQD7P6xbC\nB0YDwTh2dyJIxpvZCdG/GGNhFskjo3N2wK6GZrXuRKLOFUvUrUKIGTqDh4bb1j3C7I9iAxSLlych\nEwQ=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-19T12:14:53Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.githu