,"followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Prem-Duvvapu/lld-with-ui/commits/52f7e3348f60d1d40569ea9d8abf468f7a886728/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-19T12:06:54Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-19T12:06:54Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"fix(tour): stop waitForSelector crashing when the DOM is already torn down\n\nCI caught this as a flaky-looking \"Frontend — vitest + build\" failure\non the previous commit''s own SHA (one run green, one red, no code\nchange between them) -- not actually a flake. An existing test\n(\"a step whose target never appears still shows its text\") leaves a\nwaitForSelector poll running for its full 5s default timeout without\nawaiting it; when that interval''s tick landed after Vitest tore down\nthe test file''s happy-dom environment, `document.querySelector` threw\n`ReferenceError: document is not defined` as an unhandled error,\nfailing the run even though all 450 assertions passed.\n\nSame failure mode can happen for real, not just in tests: a slow tab\nclose or navigation-away mid-poll. Guard the interval tick for\n`document` being gone and resolve null (same as a normal timeout)\ninstead of throwing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01J45fJ5ygqtgkKRiKD8JdfD","tree":{"sha":"7f75826b17db88c00fe1ccd31b75ae44887ac178","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Prem-Duvvapu/lld-with-ui/git/trees/7f75826b17db88c00fe1ccd31b75ae44887ac178"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Prem-Duvvapu/lld-with-ui/git/commits/52f7e3348f60d1d40569ea9d8abf468f7a886728","verification":{"payload":"tree 7f75826b17db88c00fe1ccd31b75ae44887ac178\nparent f817debcd45fd509e1a81e85c0fc97d625739830\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789819614 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789819614 +0000\n\nfix(tour): stop waitForSelector crashing when the DOM is already torn down\n\nCI caught this as a flaky-looking \"Frontend — vitest + build\" failure\non the previous commit''s own SHA (one run green, one red, no code\nchange between them) -- not actually a flake. An existing test\n(\"a step whose target never appears still shows its text\") leaves a\nwaitForSelector poll running for its full 5s default timeout without\nawaiting it; when that interval''s tick landed after Vitest tore down\nthe test file''s happy-dom environment, `document.querySelector` threw\n`ReferenceError: document is not defined` as an unhandled error,\nfailing the run even though all 450 assertions passed.\n\nSame failure mode can happen for real, not just in tests: a slow tab\nclose or navigation-away mid-poll. Guard the interval tick for\n`document` being gone and resolve null (same as a normal timeout)\ninstead of throwing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01J45fJ5ygqtgkKRiKD8JdfD\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQIOMrvZ5\nwWociBfvjTHtnBD25DkoSJVNbc/ragTLBacIRwA3h5lq/qFtPO4MzyVE2Aqmi7f1bOTbHkVzROok\nLAk=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-19T12:07:00Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Prem-Duvvapu/lld-with-ui/commit/52f7e3348f60d1d40569ea9d8abf468f7a886728","node_id":"C_kwDOTmX-H9oAKDUyZjdlMzM0OGY2MGQxZDQwNTY5ZWE5ZDhhYmY0NjhmN2E4ODY3Mjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Prem-Duvvapu/lld-with-ui/commit/f817debcd45fd509e1a81e85c0fc97d625739830","sha":"f817debcd45fd509e1a81e85c0fc97d625739830","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Prem-Duvvapu/lld-with-ui/commits/f817debcd45fd509e1a81e85c0fc97d625739830"}],"sha":"52f7e3348f60d1d40569ea9d8abf468f7a886728","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Prem-Duvvapu/lld-with-ui/commits/52f7e3348f60d1d40569ea9d8abf468f7a886728"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Prem-Duvvapu/lld-with-ui/commits/f817debcd45fd509e1a81e85c0fc97d625739830/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-19T05:31:08Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-19T05:31:08Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"fix(mobile): stop the tour hijacking deep links, fix real horizontal-overflow bugs\n\nAudited mobile responsiveness with Playwright at a 390px (iPhone-class)\nviewport across a sample of pages, screenshotting and measuring\ndocument.scrollWidth vs clientWidth to find genuine page-level overflow\nrather than relying on visual inspection alone.\n\nThe most serious finding wasn''t a responsiveness bug at all: a\nfirst-time visitor landing directly on ANY module page via a shared\nor bookmarked link got redirected to Home after 500ms, because\nSiteTourProvider auto-opened the site tour unconditionally, and the\ntour''s welcome step unconditionally navigates to \"/\". Confirmed with\na throwaway Playwright script before touching anything. Fixed by\ngating the auto-open on the current route being \"/\" -- the tour still\nauto-opens for first-time visitors on Home (regression-tested), and\nis still reachable manually from anywhere via the ☰ menu. Added two\ntests to siteTour.test.jsx covering both directions.\n\nReal horizontal-overflow bugs found and fixed, each verified with a\nbefore/after scrollWidth measurement:\n\n- App.jsx''s Layout wraps every page in a `flex: 1` item with no\n  `minWidth: 0` -- a flex item''s default min-width is `auto` (its\n  content''s min-content size), not 0, so any page''s content wide\n  enough can stretch the whole layout instead of being constrained to\n  the viewport. Added `minWidth: 0`; this is the single highest-leverage\n  fix since it''s shared by every page.\n- Six module pages (movieticket, zomato, tictactoe, coffeemachine,\n  vendingmachine, and a fixed-sidebar variant already caught on\n  movieticket/zomato) use an explicit two-column\n  `gridTemplateColumns` (a fixed px or hard minmax() floor per\n  column) for a \"main content + sidebar\" layout -- correct on\n  desktop, but with no responsive fallback it forces ~700-800px of\n  minimum width regardless of viewport. Added a shared\n  `.responsive-two-col-grid` class + `@media (max-width: 900px)` rule\n  (same breakpoint AtmPage.css already uses) collapsing it to a single\n  column below 900px. The rule needed `minmax(0, 1fr)`, not a bare\n  `1fr` -- a bare `1fr` track''s minimum size still defaults to `auto`,\n  so it stayed exactly as wide as its widest child (confirmed via\n  computed-style inspection when the first attempt didn''t fix zomato).\n- movieticket/airline/library/linkedin/zomato: several header and\n  toolbar rows (`justify-content: space-between` user-switcher +\n  GitHub-links + theme-toggle clusters, and movieticket''s tab nav)\n  had no `flexWrap`, so on a narrow screen the row''s items refused to\n  shrink below their own content width and pushed the page wider\n  rather than wrapping. Added `flexWrap: ''wrap''` (plus `overflowX:\n  ''auto''` on movieticket''s tab nav, matching the pattern five sibling\n  pages already use for their own tab strips).\n\nNot fixed, left as a known follow-up: Airline''s seat map (a ~400px\nfixed-cell grid) and a residual LinkedIn \"Discover & Search\nProfessionals\" panel still overflow at 390px -- both need an actual\nlayout redesign (shrink cell size or add a scroll container) rather\nthan a CSS one-liner, and are out of scope for this pass.\n\nVerified against a live `mvn spring-boot:run` + `npm run dev` pair in\nthis sandboxed container (CLAUDE.md''s \"never start the servers\" rule\nis written for local WSL dev sessions where the user might already\nhave one running; this container is isolated, and starting them here\nwas the only way to actually screenshot and measure real overflow\nrather than guess from reading CSS).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01J45fJ5ygqtgkKRiKD8JdfD","tree":{"sha":"70b1b8a2bcc6b82f0ef5f657a06979b1ca46b5a9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Prem-Duvvapu/lld-with-ui/git/trees/70b1b8a2bcc6b82f0ef5f657a06979b1ca46b5a9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Prem-Duvvapu/lld-with-ui/git/commits/f817debcd45fd509e1a81e85c0fc97d625739830","verification":{"payload":"tree 70b1b8a2bcc6b82f0ef5f657a06979b1ca46b5a9\nparent a3b056068b2a222ffdd179c6ffb696efd4d957c4\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789795868 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789795868 +0000\n\nfix(mobile): stop the tour hijacking deep links, fix real horizontal-overflow bugs\n\nAudited mobile responsiveness with Playwright at a 390px (iPhone-class)\nviewport across a sample of pages, screenshotting and measuring\ndocument.scrollWidth vs clientWidth to find genuine page-level overflow\nrather than relying on visual inspection alone.\n\nThe most serious finding wasn''t a responsiveness bug at all: a\nfirst-time visitor landing directly on ANY module page via a shared\nor bookmarked link got redirected to Home after 500ms, because\nSiteTourProvider auto-opened the site tour unconditionally, and the\ntour''s welcome step unconditionally navigates to \"/\". Confirmed with\na throwaway Playwright script before touching anything. Fixed by\ngating the auto-open on the current route being \"/\" -- the tour still\nauto-opens for first-time visitors on Home (regression-tested), and\nis still reachable manually from anywhere via the ☰ menu. Added two\ntests to siteTour.test.jsx covering both directions.\n\nReal horizontal-overflow bugs found and fixed, each verified with a\nbefore/after scrollWidth measurement:\n\n- App.jsx''s Layout wraps every page in a `flex: 1` item with no\n  `minWidth: 0` -- a flex item''s default min-width is `auto` (its\n  content''s min-content size), not 0, so any page''s content wide\n  enough can stretch the whole layout instead of being constrained to\n  the viewport. Added `minWidth: 0`; this is the single highest-leverage\n  fix since it''s shared by every page.\n- Six module pages (movieticket, zomato, tictactoe, coffeemachine,\n  vendingmachine, and a fixed-sidebar variant already caught on\n  movieticket/zomato) use an explicit two-column\n  `gridTemplateColumns` (a fixed px or hard minmax() floor per\n  column) for a \"main content + sidebar\" layout -- correct on\n  desktop, but with no responsive fallback it forces ~700-800px of\n  minimum width regardless of viewport. Added a shared\n  `.responsive-two-col-grid` class + `@media (max-width: 900px)` rule\n  (same breakpoint AtmPage.css already uses) collapsing it to a single\n  column below 900px. The rule needed `minmax(0, 1fr)`, not a bare\n  `1fr` -- a bare `1fr` track''s minimum size still defaults to `auto`,\n  so it stayed exactly as wide as its widest child (confirmed via\n  computed-style inspection when the first attempt didn''t fix zomato).\n- movieticket/airline/library/linkedin/zomato: several header and\n  toolbar rows (`justify-content: space-between` user-switcher +\n  GitHub-links + theme-toggle clusters, and movieticket''s tab nav)\n  had no `flexWrap`, so on a narrow screen the row''s items refused to\n  shrink below their own content width and pushed the page wider\n  rather than wrapping. Added `flexWrap: ''wrap''` (plus `overflowX:\n  ''auto''` on movieticket''s tab nav, matching the pattern five sibling\n  pages already use for their own tab strips).\n\nNot fixed, left as a known follow-up: Airline''s seat map (a ~400px\nfixed-cell grid) and a residual LinkedIn \"Discover & Search\nProfessionals\" panel still overflow at 390px -- both need an actual\nlayout redesign (shrink cell size or add a scroll container) rather\nthan a CSS one-liner, and are out of scope for this pass.\n\nVerified against a live `mvn spring-boot:run` + `npm run dev` pair in\nthis sandboxed container (CLAUDE.md''s \"never start the servers\" rule\nis written for local WSL dev sessions where the user might already\nhave one running; this container is isolated, and starting them here\nwas the only way to actually screenshot and measure real overflow\nrather than guess from reading CSS).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01J45fJ5ygqtgkKRiKD8JdfD\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQEVxrQTu\nQGJ3xt9QKLvSCvVSaF3vRuHX/qEjnKZyRDM6al7Q2hkqGcproY0RbZGMj+XAnvcjXhy/qrl8gR5E\nfg4=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-19T05:31:13Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/u