ithub.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Prem-Duvvapu/lld-with-ui/commits/4994f43931b9166a4199a4b610dfecb353cd2c38/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T16:45:39Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T16:45:39Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"feat(home): add a suggested learning order for the 60 modules\n\nEach card now carries an `order` (1-60) reflecting a beginner-to-advanced\ncurriculum: OOP fundamentals and simple state machines first, then\npatterns/strategy-heavy modules, concurrency primitives, and finally the\nhard platform-scale and concurrency-race modules, capped by Workflow as\nthe capstone that combines Chain of Responsibility, a state machine, a\nstrategy, and a per-instance lock race.\n\nA new \"Suggested learning order\" toggle on the home page sorts the\n(already-filtered) grid by that position and stamps a \"Step N\" tag on\neach card, so a first-time visitor has a path through the portfolio\ninstead of 60 undifferentiated cards. Existing search/difficulty/pattern\nfilters compose with it unchanged.\n\nrouting.test.js gained a guard asserting every card has a unique order\ncovering 1..N, so a future new module can''t ship without a position.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01J45fJ5ygqtgkKRiKD8JdfD","tree":{"sha":"38af0203f2340942c29b13b4aaeee3428d57dc96","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Prem-Duvvapu/lld-with-ui/git/trees/38af0203f2340942c29b13b4aaeee3428d57dc96"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Prem-Duvvapu/lld-with-ui/git/commits/4994f43931b9166a4199a4b610dfecb353cd2c38","verification":{"payload":"tree 38af0203f2340942c29b13b4aaeee3428d57dc96\nparent 1ea9000705de2d7f2ac9d5565c6ba30c7f9b000a\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789490739 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789490739 +0000\n\nfeat(home): add a suggested learning order for the 60 modules\n\nEach card now carries an `order` (1-60) reflecting a beginner-to-advanced\ncurriculum: OOP fundamentals and simple state machines first, then\npatterns/strategy-heavy modules, concurrency primitives, and finally the\nhard platform-scale and concurrency-race modules, capped by Workflow as\nthe capstone that combines Chain of Responsibility, a state machine, a\nstrategy, and a per-instance lock race.\n\nA new \"Suggested learning order\" toggle on the home page sorts the\n(already-filtered) grid by that position and stamps a \"Step N\" tag on\neach card, so a first-time visitor has a path through the portfolio\ninstead of 60 undifferentiated cards. Existing search/difficulty/pattern\nfilters compose with it unchanged.\n\nrouting.test.js gained a guard asserting every card has a unique order\ncovering 1..N, so a future new module can''t ship without a position.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01J45fJ5ygqtgkKRiKD8JdfD\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQPmudlOC\nkDNgcxqzO84vHArEdcMkc8Fi6RdR9RCbml5CEiSzQ8DhZP2Azp5Perq7AB4C9oZWBhMmqUAK2hHP\nyw0=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-15T16:45:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","