:"https://github.com/Prem-Duvvapu/lld-with-ui/commit/01faeb2bd906742397d02f273888a073539fb9ed","sha":"01faeb2bd906742397d02f273888a073539fb9ed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Prem-Duvvapu/lld-with-ui/commits/01faeb2bd906742397d02f273888a073539fb9ed"}],"sha":"1ea9000705de2d7f2ac9d5565c6ba30c7f9b000a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Prem-Duvvapu/lld-with-ui/commits/1ea9000705de2d7f2ac9d5565c6ba30c7f9b000a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Prem-Duvvapu/lld-with-ui/commits/01faeb2bd906742397d02f273888a073539fb9ed/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T04:59:17Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T04:59:17Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"feat(tour): walk the module tabs, not just the home page\n\nThe tour stopped at the home grid, which skipped the things the site is\nactually for. It now continues into a real module (elevator) and walks the\noperational tab, the simulation, the class diagram, the sequence diagram,\ndesign details with its sub-tabs, and the source links -- 13 steps.\n\nThis needed the tour to survive navigation, which it could not: it was\nmounted inside Home and unmounted the moment it routed away, and its steps\nqueried for their target once, immediately. A module page''s tab buttons do\nnot exist until the route change AND that page''s lazy chunk have both\nlanded. So:\n\n- SiteTourProvider owns the tour above the router; Home just calls\n  startTour().\n- Steps gained an optional prepare({ navigate, reveal, isRevealed }) that\n  runs before the step is shown, and the step then waits for its target\n  rather than querying once. A target that never appears still shows its\n  text instead of breaking the tour.\n- Steps drive the real tab buttons by clicking them. LldPage owns its tab\n  in local state and DesignDetails owns its sub-tab separately, so clicking\n  is both simpler than threading state and exercises the path a visitor\n  actually takes.\n\nOn the reveal gate: the tour explains it, then unlocks this one module so\nthe next step shows a real class diagram, and says so. A \"class diagram\"\nstep displaying only a padlock undersells the site; silently bypassing the\ngate would waste the feature the previous step just explained.\n\nAlso fixes test isolation properly. PR #128 claimed to fix it by calling\ncleanup() from vitest.setup.js -- that never worked. The setup file\nresolves its own instance of React Testing Library, whose container\nregistry is a different object from the one test files populate, so it\ncleaned an empty set while every render leaked into the next test. A\ntwo-test probe (render a marker, assert the next test''s body is empty)\nfails with that version. The real fix is test.globals: true, which lets RTL\nregister its own cleanup. Verified with the same probe.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01J45fJ5ygqtgkKRiKD8JdfD","tree":{"sha":"a7a6c0f03b5852098ba5ec3822f04729803c0338","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Prem-Duvvapu/lld-with-ui/git/trees/a7a6c0f03b5852098ba5ec3822f04729803c0338"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Prem-Duvvapu/lld-with-ui/git/commits/01faeb2bd906742397d02f273888a073539fb9ed","verification":{"payload":"tree a7a6c0f03b5852098ba5ec3822f04729803c0338\nparent bb9c315c07b0aab6144ff7629972b876ab66baa5\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789448357 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789448357 +0000\n\nfeat(tour): walk the module tabs, not just the home page\n\nThe tour stopped at the home grid, which skipped the things the site is\nactually for. It now continues into a real module (elevator) and walks the\noperational tab, the simulation, the class diagram, the sequence diagram,\ndesign details with its sub-tabs, and the source links -- 13 steps.\n\nThis needed the tour to survive navigation, which it could not: it was\nmounted inside Home and unmounted the moment it routed away, and its steps\nqueried for their target once, immediately. A module page''s tab buttons do\nnot exist until the route change AND that page''s lazy chunk have both\nlanded. So:\n\n- SiteTourProvider owns the tour above the router; Home just calls\n  startTour().\n- Steps gained an optional prepare({ navigate, reveal, isRevealed }) that\n  runs before the step is shown, and the step then waits for its target\n  rather than querying once. A target that never appears still shows its\n  text instead of breaking the tour.\n- Steps drive the real tab buttons by clicking them. LldPage owns its tab\n  in local state and DesignDetails owns its sub-tab separately, so clicking\n  is both simpler than threading state and exercises the path a visitor\n  actually takes.\n\nOn the reveal gate: the tour explains it, then unlocks this one module so\nthe next step shows a real class diagram, and says so. A \"class diagram\"\nstep displaying only a padlock undersells the site; silently bypassing the\ngate would waste the feature the previous step just explained.\n\nAlso fixes test isolation properly. PR #128 claimed to fix it by calling\ncleanup() from vitest.setup.js -- that never worked. The setup file\nresolves its own instance of React Testing Library, whose container\nregistry is a different object from the one test files populate, so it\ncleaned an empty set while every render leaked into the next test. A\ntwo-test probe (render a marker, assert the next test''s body is empty)\nfails with that version. The real fix is test.globals: true, which lets RTL\nregister its own cleanup. Verified with the same probe.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01J45fJ5ygqtgkKRiKD8JdfD\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJZ4dSU5\nqWAmlDhpCvNYkISp/uYfT4wYPjAbjaGwu0SXUYLZdKiXtoiTkr3wtpb9fbojTej+63Hhv0OZ5ALQ\n2AY=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-15T04:59:19Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"http