,"gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Prem-Duvvapu/lld-with-ui/commits/723f2ebe854c070076710d09468897cb42e4a3aa/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T15:29:59Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T15:29:59Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"fix(elevator): rework the App tab''s UI/UX -- theme-token colors, legend, layout\n\nThe whole module''s styling used literal hex colors throughout instead of\nthis app''s theme tokens (var(--accent), var(--success), var(--danger),\netc.) -- fine by coincidence in light mode, but badges, the building\nheader, car states, and the request-status pill all clashed or went\nmuddy/illegible in dark mode, and none of it matched the rest of the\nsite''s palette. Every color in the module (building header, floor call\nbuttons, car states, shaft indicator dots, status badges, request status\npill, load-meter fill, buttons, error banner) now resolves through theme\ntokens, so both themes render correctly -- this also improves the shared\nSimulationTab for free, since it reuses the same ShaftHeaderRow/\nShaftOverlay/ElevatorCard components and CSS classes.\n\nAlso, specific to the App tab:\n- Added a car-state + call-button legend (Idle/Moving/Doors open/Out of\n  service, call-up/call-down) -- the four+ colors in the building view had\n  no key anywhere explaining what they meant.\n- Replaced the solid-red \"#d64545 block with white text\" error banner\n  with the softer bg/color pattern used elsewhere in the app (e.g.\n  circuit-breaker''s .cb-error).\n- Replaced ad-hoc inline `style={{ width: 220 }}` / `style={{ flex: 1 }}`\n  layout divs with real CSS classes (.el-building-body/.el-floor-list/\n  .el-shaft-area), and added `overflow-x: auto` on the building body so a\n  wide multi-car shaft row scrolls within its own box on narrow screens\n  instead of forcing the whole page to scroll horizontally.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01J45fJ5ygqtgkKRiKD8JdfD","tree":{"sha":"03f8b1fb892a29a809bf69e4b39ef79ca631c87e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Prem-Duvvapu/lld-with-ui/git/trees/03f8b1fb892a29a809bf69e4b39ef79ca631c87e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Prem-Duvvapu/lld-with-ui/git/commits/723f2ebe854c070076710d09468897cb42e4a3aa","verification":{"payload":"tree 03f8b1fb892a29a809bf69e4b39ef79ca631c87e\nparent df6bc59de28448ad9ceb07a44273bb263ee48e1b\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789313399 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789313399 +0000\n\nfix(elevator): rework the App tab''s UI/UX -- theme-token colors, legend, layout\n\nThe whole module''s styling used literal hex colors throughout instead of\nthis app''s theme tokens (var(--accent), var(--success), var(--danger),\netc.) -- fine by coincidence in light mode, but badges, the building\nheader, car states, and the request-status pill all clashed or went\nmuddy/illegible in dark mode, and none of it matched the rest of the\nsite''s palette. Every color in the module (building header, floor call\nbuttons, car states, shaft indicator dots, status badges, request status\npill, load-meter fill, buttons, error banner) now resolves through theme\ntokens, so both themes render correctly -- this also improves the shared\nSimulationTab for free, since it reuses the same ShaftHeaderRow/\nShaftOverlay/ElevatorCard components and CSS classes.\n\nAlso, specific to the App tab:\n- Added a car-state + call-button legend (Idle/Moving/Doors open/Out of\n  service, call-up/call-down) -- the four+ colors in the building view had\n  no key anywhere explaining what they meant.\n- Replaced the solid-red \"#d64545 block with white text\" error banner\n  with the softer bg/color pattern used elsewhere in the app (e.g.\n  circuit-breaker''s .cb-error).\n- Replaced ad-hoc inline `style={{ width: 220 }}` / `style={{ flex: 1 }}`\n  layout divs with real CSS classes (.el-building-body/.el-floor-list/\n  .el-shaft-area), and added `overflow-x: auto` on the building body so a\n  wide multi-car shaft row scrolls within its own box on narrow screens\n  instead of forcing the whole page to scroll horizontally.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01J45fJ5ygqtgkKRiKD8JdfD\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQPc/EGm/\nI3Oc20w6VCFc9wdwZRW2EOSYyJWF0TfRcrxATNTSN+rvpdo2CIHj5T5XFGnmGjp2TiX+g2JPZdEZ\ntQk=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-13T15:30:04Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Prem-Duvvapu/lld-with-ui/commit/723f2ebe854c070076710d09468897cb42e4a3aa","node_id":"C_kwDOTmX-H9oAKDcyM2YyZWJlODU0YzA3MDA3NjcxMGQwOTQ2ODg5N2NiNDJlNGEzYWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Prem-Duvvapu/lld-with-ui/commit/df6bc59de28448ad9ceb07a44273bb263ee48e1b","sha":"df6bc59de28448ad9ceb07a44273bb263ee48e1b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Prem-Duvvapu/lld-with-ui/commits/df6bc59de28448ad9ceb07a44273bb263ee48e1b"}],"sha":"723f2ebe854c070076710d09468897cb42e4a3aa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Prem-Duvvapu/lld-with-ui/commits/723f2ebe854c070076710d09468897cb42e4a3aa"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Prem-Duvvapu/lld-with-ui/commits/547868be4bb7221455347b03584c65fac8827087/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T15:29:16Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T15:29:16Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"fix(backend): Swagger UI \"Failed to load API definition\" behind Render''s proxy\n\nRender (and most PaaS free tiers) terminate TLS at a reverse proxy in front\nof this app and forward the original scheme/host via X-Forwarded-* headers.\nWithout server.forward-headers-strategy set, Spring has no way to know\nthat -- it thinks every request arrived over plain http on the proxy''s\ninternal port, so springdoc builds the OpenAPI document''s \"servers\" URL\n(and any redirect Location header, e.g. /swagger-ui.html ->\n/swagger-ui/index.html) as http://... An https page then refuses to fetch\nthat as mixed content, and Swagger UI shows \"Failed to load API\ndefinition\" with no clearer explanation. Trusting forwarded headers fixes\nthe scheme.\n\nAlso widen CORS to cover /v3/api-docs/** and /swagger-ui/** (previously\nonly /api/**), so the same failure can''t recur if the docs are ever\nfetched cross-origin instead of through the frontend''s same-origin proxy.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01J45fJ5ygqtgkKRiKD8JdfD","tree":{"sha":"6f937ddafd7fe1783403afdd4164c50d4ce84815","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Prem-Duvvapu/lld-with-ui/git/trees/6f937ddafd7fe1783403afdd4164c50d4ce84815"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Prem-Duvvapu/lld-with-ui/git/commits/547868be4bb7221455347b03584c65fac8827087","verification":{"payload":"tree 6f937ddafd7fe1783403afdd4164c50d4ce84815\nparent df6bc59de28448ad9ceb07a44273bb263ee48e1b\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789313356 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789313356 +0000\n\nfix(backend): Swagger UI \"Failed to load API definition\" behind Render''s proxy\n\nRender (and most PaaS free tiers) terminate TLS at a reverse proxy in front\nof this app and forward the original scheme/host via X-Forwarded-* headers.\nWithout server.forward-headers-strategy set, Spring has no way to know\nthat -- it thinks every request arrived over plain http on the proxy''s\ninternal port, so springdoc builds the OpenAPI document''s \"servers\" URL\n(and any redirect Location header, e.g. /swagger-ui.html ->\n/swagger-ui/index.html) as http://... An https page then refuses to fetch\nthat as mixed content, and Swagger UI shows \"Failed to load API\ndefinition\" with no clearer explanation. Trusting forwarded headers fixes\nthe scheme.\n\nAlso widen CORS to cover /v3/api-docs/** and /swagger-ui/** (previously\nonly /api/**), so the same failure can''t recur if the docs are ever\nfetched cross-origin instead of through the frontend''s same-origin proxy.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01J45fJ5ygqtgkKRiKD8JdfD\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQBS1r3m+\n9ctpKy/9JxBB07SkNfZF2PPUNxkRYijylh/XnDpXlSthDbxaLWR9ZntKB+5VYmnevvcn/sVVEB1V\nlgM=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-13T15:29:21Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Prem-Duvvapu/lld-with-ui/commit/547868be4bb7221455347b03584c65fac8827087","node_id":"C_kwDOTmX-H9oAKDU0Nzg2OGJlNGJiNzIyMTQ1NTM0N2IwMzU4NGM2NWZhYzg4MjcwODc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Prem-Duvvapu/lld-with-ui/commit/df6bc59de28448ad9ceb07a44273bb263ee48e1b","sha":"df6bc59de28448ad9ceb07a44273bb263ee48e1b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Prem-Duvvapu/lld-with-ui/commits/df6bc59de28448ad9ceb07a44273bb263ee48e1b"}],"sha":"547868be4bb7221455347b03584c65fac8827087","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Prem-Duvvapu/lld-with-ui/commits/547868be4bb7221455347b03584c65fac8827087"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Prem-Duvvapu/lld-with-ui/commits/aec7acbe06a5bdf9e5d1df2982450bfce0670c95/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T15:22:31Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T15:22:31Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"fix(circuit-breaker): unstyled Services tab on first visit, shared busy state\n\nThe Services tab is the module''s default/first tab, but the <style> block\ndefining every .cb-* class was only rendered inside SimulationTab -- so a\nvisitor landing on Services (the common case) saw raw, unstyled markup\nuntil they happened to click into Simulation first, which mounted the\nstyle tag. Inject the CSS in ServicesTab too.\n\nAlso scope the \"busy\" flag per service name instead of one shared\nboolean: calling Simulate Success/Failure on one breaker no longer\ndisables the buttons on every other card in the grid. And add a\nsame-card hint plus a highlighted rejected-call count when a breaker\nis OPEN, so it''s clear from the Services tab alone -- without needing\nthe Simulation tab -- that calls are being rejected.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01J45fJ5ygqtgkKRiKD8JdfD","tree":{"sha":"5ba6691ae65bdac798b164e3850e87a02c746e16","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Prem-Duvvapu/lld-with-ui/git/trees/5ba6691ae65bdac798b164e3850e87a02c746e16"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Prem-Duvvapu/lld-with-ui/git/commits/aec7acbe06a5bdf9e5d1df2982450bfce0670c95","verification":{"payload":"tree 5ba6691ae65bdac798b164e3850e87a02c746e16\nparent df6bc59de28448ad9ceb07a44273bb263ee48e1b\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789312951 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789312951 +0000\n\nfix(circuit-breaker): unstyled Services tab on first visit, shared busy state\n\nThe Services tab is the module''s default/first tab, but the <style> block\ndefining every .cb-* class was only rendered inside SimulationTab -- so a\nvisitor landing on Services (the common case) saw raw, unstyled markup\nuntil they happened to click into Simulation first, which mounted the\nstyle tag. Inject the CSS in ServicesTab too.\n\nAlso scope the \"busy\" flag per service name instead of one shared\nboolean: calling Simulate Success/Failure on one breaker no longer\ndisables the buttons on every other card in the grid. And add a\nsame-card hint plus a highlighted rejected-call count when a breaker\nis OPEN, so it''s clear from the Services tab alone -- without needing\nthe Simulation tab -- that calls are being rejected.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01J45fJ5ygqtgkKRiKD8JdfD\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQPScQj0S\nnfgphoB84x0KSuarK5slXWpRupcwpctpcHOPRIvIyrbbTUu80QHHUcHSa3kkFBFXTyMUH/ZRzWj4\nLgQ=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-13T15:22:36Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Prem-Duvvapu/lld-with-ui/commit/aec7acbe06a5bdf9e5d1df2982450bfce0670c95","node_id":"C_kwDOTmX-H9oAKGFlYzdhY2JlMDZhNWJkZjllNWQxZGYyOTgyNDUwYmZjZTA2NzBjOTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.co